$info=240in1ar
$mame
0.227 [David Haywood, Team Europe]

Mini Arcade Machine (Thumbs Up, 240IN1ARC), Thumbs Up, 201?

Two models of the Thumbs Up machine were produced, both with different gamelists despite being in the same plastic case. The first model of the system is very similar to the Multicade 230, featuring the same exact menu, but includes ten extra games. This seemingly predates the Multicade 230's software, but the handheld itself came out after the 230 had already released. It runs on a VT369 NOAC (NES-on-a-Chip) and its SPI ROM could possibly be read / reprogrammed using a CH341A (source: https://bootleggames.fandom.com/wiki/Thumbs_Up!_Mini_Arcade_Machine).

DRIVER:
nintendo/nes_vt369_vtunknown.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
