$info=386sc2c
$mame
0.214 [rfka01]

386 motherboard using the Symphony chipset, <unknown>, 199?

The 386 motherboard based on the Symphony chipset is a type of motherboard developed in the 1990s for systems based on the Intel 80386 (i386) processor . The Symphony chipset, produced by companies such as C&T (Chips and Technologies) or other specialized companies at the time, was an integrated solution designed to reduce costs and improve integration in entry-level or industrial computers. The Symphony chipset was one of the first attempts to integrate on a single chip many of the functions traditionally handled by separate components in an IBM-compatible PC. It was part of a trend toward simplification and miniaturization of hardware, especially for markets where system cost was crucial.

