68k Single Board Computer, Wichit Sirichote, 2002

One of my experiment needs the computing power between 8-bit and 32-bit cpu.For 8-bit applications I used MCS51 and AVR. Whereas the 32-bit applications,I used embbeded PC running linux. So I chose the cheap 32-bit CPU fromMotorola, the 68HC000. The chip is quite old but there are many chip makersstill produce it. I like the addressing modes of 68000 cpu. So I spentmy hobby time a couple of month to design the hardware and develop a simplemonitor program (soruce: http://www.kmitl.ac.th/~kswichit/68k/68k.html).

