$info=7951om
$mame
0.201 [Robbbert]

7951om, Mera-Elzab, 1987

This device was probably designed to be compact, simple and cheap, as it uses only 74 logic and no (V)LSI circuits. It was used in Polish Railways to communicate points of sale with computer systems. Its features aren't high-end: 40 characters in a line and 12 lines could be displayed, the only port is one serial port, keyboard is not much comfortable, and case is made of quite thin plastic covered in white paint. Speaker was built-in and made a sound each time key was pressed. Fortunately, there was a volume trimmer. There were also some versions with amber CRT, but my unit is the most popular device with green one (source: ).

