TM 990/189 University Board microcomputer, Texas Instruments, 1978

The TM990/189 is a very unusual contraption. About the only reason why it's present in my calculator collection is its unusual keypad: it is clearly recognizable as the keypad of a TI-59, simply relabeled. The TM990/189 is not a calculator, but an experimental computer. It was, apparently, used for educational and development purposes (source: http://www.rskey.org/CMS/index.php/exhibit-hall/118).

