Amiga 1200 (NTSC), Commodore, 1992

The Amiga 1200, or A1200 (code-named 'Channel Z'), was Commodore International's third-generation Amiga computer, aimed at the home market. It was launched on October 21, 1992, at a base price of 399 GBP in the United Kingdom and 599 USD in the United States (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amiga_1200).

