$info=a4000
$mame
0.154 [Dirk Best]

Amiga 4000/040 (PAL), Commodore, 1992

The Commodore Amiga 4000, or A4000, is the successor of the A2000 and A3000 computers. There are two models, the A4000/040 released in October 1992 with a Motorola 68040 CPU, and the A4000/030 released in April 1993 with a Motorola 68EC030. The Amiga 4000 introduced the Advanced Graphics Architecture (AGA) chipset with enhanced graphics and continued the A3000's system architecture. However, the SCSI peripheral interface was replaced by lower cost IDE. The A4000 is housed in a white desktop box with a separate keyboard. Later Commodore released an expanded tower version called the A4000T (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amiga_4000).

