$info=aa4
$mame
0.180 [Nigel Barnes]

Acorn A4, Acorn Computers, 1992

The Acorn A4 was the laptop version of the Acorn Archimedes and was one of the first RISC laptops (and by the way, one of the most powerful - five times faster than a 50 MHz 486 for some operations). The operating system (RISC OS 3.10) was located in the 2 MB ROM. The 9'' LCD screen could only display 14 shades of grey, but used a clever dithering system to make more shades apparent. The A4 could be used for about 3 hours with its internal batteries (source: http://www.old-computers.com/museum/computer.asp?c=31&st=1).

