$info=aa5000
$mame
0.180 [Nigel Barnes]

Acorn A5000, Acorn Computers, 1991

The A5000 was launched in September 1991. Naturally there was a Learning Curve package for eduction to go with it. A year later the A5000 was boosted with additional models (including discless Econet and Ethernet terminals) and bigger hard discs. In July 1993 Acorn finally released the FPA10 Floating Point Accelerator for the A540, A5000 and R260 which boosted floating point performance by a factor of 50. The Acorn A5000 and A540 FPA upgrade kit installation instructions  provides more information about installation and use of the FPA10. In September 1993 a improved A5000  (alpha version) was launched with a faster 33MHz ARM3 and the capability to expand memory beyond 4MB. The A5000 included a number of significant changes from the previous Acorn computers (source: http://chrisacorns.computinghistory.org.uk/Computers/A5000.html).

