In early 1982, Franklin released the Franklin Ace 100, and in March of the same year, the Franklin Ace 1000; they were very close copies of the Apple II Plus computer, respectively. The motherboard design is nearly identical and Franklin also copied Apple's ROMs. Two months later, Apple Computer sued Franklin for copyright violation. Franklin initially won / See Apple Computer, Inc. v. Franklin Computer Corp. (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Franklin_Electronic_Publishers).

