$info=ace500
$mame
0.239 [R. Belmont]

Franklin ACE 500, Franklin Computer, 1986

The last of the Franklin ACE computers - the ACE 500. The first Franklin computers, the 100 and 1000 were rip-offs of their Apple equivalent, and Franklin paid the price for it. They were sued by Apple and forced to develop their own operating system rather than just copy someone elses. The resultant LEGAL Franklin computer systems were the 2000 and 500, which are still clones of similar Apple computer systems, but have no illegal code in them. The ACE 500 is most similar to the Apple IIc, with characteristics such as a one-piece case with a handle, an external power supply, and a built-in floppy drive on the right side of they system, but they look quite different physically. The Franklin ACE 500 has 256K of memory installed, with room to add an additional 256K for 512K total RAM. Other options include a battery-backed clock and calendar (source: https://oldcomputers.net/ace500.html).

DRIVER:
apple/apple2e.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
