$info=acorn_fdc
$mame
0.200 [Nigel Barnes]

Acorn Floppy Disc Controller Board, <unknown>, ????

The Acorn fdc is a standard eurocard which connects to the standard Acorn bus and provides an interface to 1 or 2 drives. It is capable of controlling 4 drive surfaces on 2 double sided drives. Single or double track density drives may be used. A 34-way flat ribbon cable connects to the drives after the shugart interface standard. The intelligent device used is the Intel i8271 (source: http://chrisacorns.computinghistory.org.uk/8bit_Upgrades/Acorn_fdc.html).

