$info=acorn_vib
$mame
0.200 [Nigel Barnes]

Acorn Versatile Interface Board, <unknown>, ????

This device has 2 i/o ports which are each 10 bit parallel, TTL level (i.e. 8 individually proogrammable data bits plus 2 control bits) and a pair of interval timers for providing real time interrupts. One port connects to side B of the bus connector, the other via a high current buffer to the front of the board, wher a 26-way connector may be fitted. This connector is pin compatible with Centronics, Anadex and other printers (source: http://chrisacorns.computinghistory.org.uk/8bit_Upgrades/Acorn_UIB.html).

