0.200 [Nigel Barnes]

Acorn System 3 (6502 CPU), Acorn Computers, 1980

The Acorn System 3 added 'a floppy disk controller card, floppy disk drive, and disk operating system ROM, replacing the cassette interface card and cassette operating system of the System 2 machine. The System 3 became the standard workhorse for development in the Acorn lab: the Acorn Atom has been called a cut-down version of the System 3; and it was based on the System 3 that much of the development work for the BBC Micro was done. In 1982 this was being offered for ?775, or ?1075 with power supply, casing, and two further 8K RAM cards; plus, again, an additional ?136 for a keyboard (source: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acorn_Eurocard_systems#System_3).

