Monochromatic alphanumeric video terminal designed for interacting with 1970s computer systems, featuring a 12-inch CRT display, an integrated keyboard, and a serial interface for communication with mainframes or minicomputers. It supports fixed text modes (typically 24 lines × 80 columns) and is renowned for its robust construction and reliability in professional environments.

