Adventure Vision, Entex, 1982

The Adventure Vision is a self-contained (no external monitor is required) cartridge-based video game console released by Entex Industries in 1982. The Adventure Vision was Entex's second generation' system. Their first console was the Entex Select-A-Game, released a year earlier in 1981 (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Entex_Adventure_Vision).

