$info=ai1000
$mame
0.142 [Sandro Ronco]

AI-1000, Casio, 1989

Unlike many other machines from the late 80's, which only store a defined number of BASIC programs at a time (typically one to ten), the PB-1000 uses its memory as a virtual disk to store BASIC programs, machine-code executables and text files. This feature, combined with other CASIO good ideas, and a real ease of programming and its very cool sensitive screen, all of this makes it one of the coolest machine ever conceived! Just imagine CASIO had even released a disk drive for it! Some people would die for this unit (source: http://cdecas.free.fr/computers/pocket/pb1000.php).

