The Alphatronic P30 is a CP / M machine with two office floppies, with an 8-bit 8085 CPU, along with another 16-bit Intel 8088 cpu. As with many manufacturers of the time, this dual-cpu solution from Triumph-Adler allowed to increase the performance of the machine while safeguarding compatibility with past applications. It is not DOS compatible, and this greatly limited its diffusion;  it was sold mainly in Germany, but also in France and Italy (source, traslated from Italian: http://museo.dagomari.prato.it/singolo.php?cod=175&ord=1).

