$info=amico2k
$mame
0.133 [Fabio Priuli, Curt Coder]

Amico 2000, A.S.E.L., 1978

Starting from the December 1978, the historic electronics magazine "Experiment" of JCE publishing group, began publishing a long series of articles describing a new microcomputer. This is the Friend 2000 (Advanced Micro Computer), designed and built by a small company in Milan, the ASEL Joseph Ferraroli. The original project consists of a minicomputer on a single board, with a numeric keypad for entering programs and a 7-segment display with 6 digits. The card is designed for connection of an external bus that allows you to expand your system with additional cards and turn it into a real computer. The project's main entry is published in the third article of the series, on the issue of March 1979. The user is given detailed instructions now appear overly detailed, but you have to think that those who rode this machine hardly had never ridden one! On the same card two different configurations are possible: a car "base" and expanded with an optional peripheral (source, traslated from italian: http://www.computerhistory.it/index.php?option=com_content&task=view&id=82&Itemid=115).

DRIVER:
trainer/amico2k.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Good
Color: Good
Sound: Good
Graphics: Good
Save State: Unsupported

SOFTWARE LIST:
-

RESOURCES:
Snap, Title, Icon, machine picture (in "Cabinet" collection), Control Panel, Flyer, Marquee and PCB.

WIP:
- 0.142u3: Implemented keyboard and display; fixed LED flickering [Curt Coder].
- 0.133: MESS Team added 'ASEL Amico 2000 skeleton' system.

ROMSET:
1024 bytes in 3 files / 0.45Kb packed

$end
