$info=ampex210p
$mame
0.201 [Robbbert]

Ampex 210 plus Terminal (v3.0), Ampex, 1988

Very popular terminal, with monochrome display and RS-232 port, with software configuration (battery-backed), RTC, memory buffer "window mode" and many configuration options. It has a wide range of baud rates and is quite durable. Ampex terminals were used in industrial systems as well as in office ones, in Poland usually with PC machines as servers. The unit is built around Z80A CPU, it has dedicated 3515260 PLA chip and MC2672B4P CRT driver. Connection is made with AMI18828MHD serial driver chip, but it can be modified using installable module in a socket (source: http://oldcomputer.info/terminal/amp210/index.htm).

