$info=amu880
$mame
0.136 [Curt Coder]

Ausbaufaehiger Mikrocomputer mit dem U 880, Militaerverlag der DDR, 1983

This is an educational kit published in East Germany (DDR) for building and using a microcomputer based on the U880 processor, a cloned version of the Zilog Z80. Aimed at students, electronics enthusiasts and hobbyists, the manual illustrates step-by-step how to assemble, expand and program a do-it-yourself computer system, often in school or technical settings. With a hands-on, didactic approach, it introduces assembler programming, computer architecture, and the use of discrete electronic components. A symbol of technological self-reliance in the socialist environment, it is a significant example of how computer science was taught in Eastern Europe during the Cold War period.

