$info=amust
$mame
0.153 [Robbbert, Chickenman]

Amust Executive 816, Amust, 1983

An unusual-looking CP/M computer. There are no manuals or schematics known to exist. The entire driver is guesswork. The board has LH0080 (Z80A), 2x 8251, 2x 8255, 8253, uPD765A and a HD46505SP-2. The videoram is a 6116 RAM. There is a piezo beeper. There are 3 crystals, X1 = 4.9152 (serial chips?), X2 = 16 (CPU), X3 = 14.31818 MHz (Video?). There are numerous jumpers, all of which perform unknown functions. The keyboard is a plug-in unit, same idea as Kaypro and Zorba. It has these chips: INS8035N-6, F74145, 74LS373N, SN75451BP, 2716 ROM with label KBD-3. Crystal: 3.579545 MHz (source: MAME amust.cpp driver).

