0.147u3 [Al Kossow, Angelo Salese]

APC, NEC, 1982

The N.E.C. Advanced Personal Computer is one of those machines which is hard to catagorize. It does run MS-DOS, which might qualify it as a "PC" however it also runs CP/M-86, and it uses 8" diskette drives, a media format practically unheard in IBM clone machines. This is a large/heavy and very reliable business computer. It runs CP/M-86 and MS-DOS. It is one of the very few machines which runs MS-DOS from 8" floppy disks (source: http://www.classiccmp.org/dunfield/nec/index.htm).

