WIP:
- 0.284: Fix FLASH timing (#14554). The 555 timer in the original Apple II is replaced in the IIe and later, by IOU video counter overflow bits; this slightly slows the FLASH blinking rate from every ~15 frames to exactly every 16 frames [arekkusu42].
- 0.283: Enable use of romcardfp in slots [AJR]. Fix -ramsize crash (#14486). Ensure IIc memory expansion variables are initialized, mimicking device_reset() from a2bus_memexp_device.  This fixes a crash booting ProDOS with -ramsize; also followup 9deea88: initialize all of m_migram. Fix IIc mouse regression (#14465). Remove the incorrectly propagated is_device_connected() checks, which should not apply to the IIc mouse; fixes #14463 [arekkusu42].
- 0.282: Fix regression in 85e73ca reintroducing #12468. Only the mirror is required to fix double-lo-res: ROM@F3CB reads C079. IOUDIS and RDDHIRES only exist on the IIc: Followup 6a4854b: hardware testing shows that IOUDIS and RDDHIRES don't exist on the IIe (despite what Apple copy-pasted into the IIe Technical Reference); replace the implementation with documentation and an assert, to inform future developers [arekkusu42].
- 0.270: Apple //c mouse fixes (#12720): Initialize //c mouse related variables: last_mx/y, count_x/y, m_x0/1, m_y0/1. Set Y0 interrupt flag on //c mouse Y-axis movement even if X-axis movement is still being processed. Increase //c mouse port sensitivity to match that of the //e mouse (found in a2bus/mouse.cpp) [as-tb-dev].
- 0.255: IIe does not have IOUDIS, only IIc/IIc Plus [R. Belmont, TomCh].
- 0.243: Fix Zip Chip emulation so it can't be reenabled while locked [R. Belmont].
- 0.233: Match dot clock to CPU clock for PAL machines. PAL/SECAM models now have the correct CPU speed. Always allow writing to cards in slots 1-3, matches our previous behavior for 4-7 [R. Belmont].
- 0.208: Added Focus IDE and Vulcan/Vulcan Gold IDE [R. Belmont].
- 0.200: Updates: Added debugger guards to avoid accidentally banking out ROM. Fixed floating bus reads - synchronizes Talbot Fantasy Seven credits screen [R. Belmont].
- 0.190: Don't update 80-column screen immediately on page switch [Peter Ferrie].
- 0.178: Made write-only soft-switches write-only [Peter Ferrie].
- 0.173: BugFIX #06163 [Misc.] (apple2e.c) apple2e: XPS Diagnostic IIe test failed! [R. Belmont]. Fix C800 internal ROM reading [R. Belmont].
- 0.170: Fix $c800 arbitration, fixes IDE and SCSI cards among others [R. Belmont].
- 0.166: Fix raster parameters, French Touch "Scroll Scroll Scroll" demo now syncs on apple2e driver [R. Belmont].
- 0.157: Fix LC save states and don't enter double modes if 80COL isn't set [R. Belmont, Peter Ferrie].
- 0.142u4: Add location for the two code roms of the Apple IIe enhanced; restored the ROM IC type information inadvertently removed by the addition of the locations for the Apple IIe enhanced roms [Lord Nightmare].
- 0.142u3: Added keyboard ROMs [Curt Coder].
- 0.2b4: Mike Balfour added 'Apple IIe' system.

