$info=aprfte
$mame
0.144u7 [Kaylee]

Apricot FT//ex 486 (J3 Motherboard), Apricot, 1991

As more organisations discover the benefits of workgroup computing, a strong demand has emerged for solid, high power systems that measure up to the role of a localised server. Drawing on considerable experience in networked systems, Apricot has produced the FT//ex to meet the new demand. This impressive floor standing tower system offers top level performance and cavernous fault tolerant storage capacity at a price to suit the cost conscious buyer. The FT//ex is offered with three choices of processor ranging from the Intel 486DX2-66 to the Pentium-90 so that the correct cost/ performance mix can be matched to the job in hand. As you would expect, the initial choice of processor is not a limiting factor as each model can be upgraded at any time using the modular processor system (source: http://insight.actapricot.org/insight/common/infact/ftex.htm).

