Automatic Products Vending Machine model 110 (set 1), Mars Electronics, 1990

This is a vintage vending machine designed for selling packaged products such as snacks, candies, or beverages. The model, crafted from metal with industrial-style finishes, incorporates a mechanical or electromechanical system for product selection and dispensing—often featuring display windows and buttons or levers for customers to make their choices. Powered by electricity and built for continuous use in public spaces, it combines durability with functional simplicity. As part of a larger collection, it stands as an example of automated retail technology from the 1960s and '70s, now also cherished as a vintage or collectible item.

