Apricot VX FT server, Apricot, 1989

In 1989, a cover story by Byte magazine announced the Apricot VX FT Server as the world's first machine to incorporate the intel 486 micro processor. This machine, designed by Bob Cross, was a fault tolerant file server based on Micro Channel architecture, incorporating an external RAM cache and its own UPS. The VX FT line consisted of Series 400 and Series 800, with four different models each. These (and their other systems) were manufactured in their state of the art factory in Glenrothes, Fife, Scotland (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apricot_Computers#1980s).

