$info=ar140
$mame
0.238 [Nigel Barnes]

Acorn R140, Acorn Computers, 1989

The Acorn R140 workstation represents a major price breakthrough for UNIX systems. Acorn has exploited the performance of its award-winning 32-bit RISC processor to produce the first in a series of personal workstations running the UNIX operating system at a price below that of any comparable product. The RISC processor designed and developed in the UK by Acorn Computers Limited is an outstanding example of pioneering technology leading to radical cost savings. By launching the R140 workstation Acorn has transformed the economics of making UNIX available to users in all fields (source: http://www.computinghistory.org.uk/det/3639/Acorn-R140/).

