0.238 [Nigel Barnes]

Acorn R260, Acorn Computers, 1990

The R260 is functionally identical to the A540. The R260 was fitted with 8 Mb of RAM and a 100 Mb SCSI hard disc drive as standard, while the R225 came with 4 Mb of RAM and no hard drive, and was intended as a cheap networked UNIX workstation. Both machines were supplied with ARM3 chips and built-in Ethernet interfaces (source: http://www.computinghistory.org.uk/det/4475/Acorn-R260/).

