$info=arb
$mame
0.207 [hap, Berger]

Auto Response Board, AVE Micro Systems, 1980

This is an electronic board designed for automation and control applications, capable of managing automatic responses to specific signals or inputs. Used in industrial, educational, or experimental settings, it allows programming logical sequences or reactions to external events—such as sensors, buttons, or electrical signals. Often employed in alarm systems, access control setups, or simple educational robotics, it’s intended to be integrated into larger circuits and programmed with flexibility. It serves as a valuable tool for learning and prototyping in the fields of digital electronics and automation, commonly found in educational kits from the 1980s and 1990s.

