$info=arb605
$mame
0.286 [TeamEurope]

AR Game Console (Model B605, YRPRSODF), Shen Zhen Shi Fei Xun Hu Dong Technology, 202?

Affordable console TV game manufactured by an OEM company from Shenzhen (China), marketed around the 2010–2020 period. Compact device with built-in games based on simplified hardware (often derived from ARM chipsets or NES clones), featuring limited AR (augmented reality) functionality via an optional external webcam for basic interactions with physical cards or markers. Model B605 comes with composite video/HDMI output, two wired controllers integrated into the inexpensive plastic chassis, and power supplied by an external adapter. The games are simplified variations of casual or sports titles with reduced 2D graphics. Targeted at discount markets and low-cost online sales, this product exemplifies the typical offering of China’s OEM industry—entry-level electronic devices without a globally recognized brand name.

