0.188 [hap, Sean Riddle]

Arrange Ball, A-One LSI, 1980

This is a retro-themed handheld console with a built-in display, designed for instant play and on-the-go fun. It comes with a single pre-installed arcade or puzzle game—often a clone or variation of classic titles centered around matching mechanics or quick reflexes. Featuring simple physical controls like a joystick and buttons, it operates independently without the need for a TV or external accessories. Powered by a battery, it’s compact and lightweight, making it perfect for kids or anyone looking for a casual, nostalgic pastime. Its minimalist design and emphasis on straightforward gameplay make it a quintessential product among budget-friendly mini-consoles geared toward occasional retro gaming.

