$info=asr10
$mame
0.152 [R. Belmont]

ASR-10, Ensoniq, 1992

The Ensoniq ASR-10 was a sampling keyboard produced by Ensoniq between 1992 and 1998. It is the keyboard model of the ASR-10R rackmount module. It was a follow up product to the very popular Ensoniq EPS and Ensoniq EPS-16+ performance samplers, and was also available with a piano style weighted keyboard (ASR-88) and a rackmount version. At the time, the machine was one of the most powerful samplers available (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ensoniq_ASR-10).

