0.285 [AJR]

ASSIST05, Motorola, 1980

Debug monitor firmware developed by Motorola for MC6805 microcontrollers in the 1980s. Integrated into the MCM65516 ROM chip, it provided engineers with basic functionalities for embedded development: memory inspection, register modification, and controlled program execution. Primarily used during hardware prototyping and testing of industrial electronic systems, instrumentation, and microcontroller-based devices prior to final product validation.

