0.256 [The Retro Web]

Terminator P-3 "Cusc" (SiS630 chipset), Asus, 2001

The Asus Terminator P3 "Cusc" (featuring the SiS630 chipset) is a dated motherboard designed for Intel Socket 370 processors, such as the Celeron and Pentium III. Introduced in the early 2000s, it integrates graphics, audio, and LAN onto a single SiS630 chip, offering excellent value for its time. Primarily intended for budget and entry-level systems, it supports up to 2 GB of SDRAM RAM and includes an AGP slot for dedicated graphics cards. The name "Cusc" likely refers to a specific version or revision of the board.

