$info=atakaast
$mame
0.239 [algestam, Milan Galcik]

Ataka asteroidov, bootleg (Elektronika), 1992

Soviet video game from the 1980s, developed for microprocessor-based systems like the DVK or UKNC. Based on Atari's classic Asteroids, it replicates the game mechanics: players control a spaceship in a two-dimensional space, firing at asteroids while fending off enemy UFOs. Featuring simple, black-and-white graphics, it stands as an example of a localized adaptation of a Western title within the Soviet educational and computing context.

