$info=ataripc4
$mame
0.218 [rfka01]

PC4, Atari, 1987

Introduced at COMDEX '87 along with the PC2, the PC4 was the last in the Atari PC series to have an Atari designed motherboard and no longer featured an Atari Mouse port. In a further move away from using Atari components, both the Keyboard and Mouse were a generic Mitsumi model which were also found in other brand name IBM Compatibles at the time such as the Commodore PC series (source: http://www.ataripc.net/pc4-286/).

