PC5, Atari, 1988

With the first 386 from Atari, the customer could choose the clock frequency between 6, 16 and 20 MHz, and the operating system (MS-DOS 5.0 or EURIX, a UNIX version) was also available. In contrast, the drives were tried and tested, either a 5? ? or a 3? ? HD drive is used as the floppy disk drive and a 60 MB RLL disk as the hard drive. The interfaces for an external floppy disk drive and for a digital monitor available with the other PC models are omitted with the PC5 (source, traslated from German: http://www.atari-computermuseum.de/pc5.htm).

