The Otrona Attaché was introduced in 1982, with the 8:16 available in 1983 with an 8086 coprocessor board and 256KB RAM. This model also has the optional GPIB interface. The system will boot CP/M 2.2.5 running on the Z80A, and MSDOS 2.11 on the 8086. In CP/M mode, the coprocessor RAM is available as a 248KB RAMDISK (source: http://q7.neurotica.com/Oldtech/Otrona/).

