$info=avrmax
$mame
0.223 [hap]

AVR-Max Chess Computer (English), Elektor, 2009

We congratulate you on building the SHAH chess computer, the latest development from our company. SHAH is characterized by its nostalgic charm, the power supply with two Mignon batteries is particularly remarkable. The chess program is Micro-Max 4.8 by Harm-Geert Müller in a port by Andre Adrian. In order to fully utilize the capabilities of your new SHAH chess computer, we recommend that you read the following instructions carefully. Set up the chessboard, switch on SHAH. The SHAH display appears. Press the 'CL' key, the display goes dark, then enter trains according to the internationally known coordinate system, e.g. E2 E4 (source, traslated from German: https://www.schach-computer.info/wiki/index.php/AVR-Max-Schachzwerg).

