$info=ax200
$mame
0.250 [openMSX]

AX-200 (MSX1, Arabic/English), Sakhr, 1986

Sakhr Computers was a Kuwaiti company that was selling MSX computers imported from Japan in Egypt and the Persian Gulf States. These MSX were localized by Al Alamiah (the parent company at that time) and rebranded for the Arabic market. The AX-200 is the Yamaha YIS-503II adapted for Arabic countries. The not usable mini-slot has been removed. The power supply is built-in. It has an Arabic QWERTY keyboard, but is also available in an Arabic/French version (with AZERTY keyboard), where the English Word Processor is replaced by a French Word Processor. It seems that this computer was sometimes sold with a Yamaha musical module SFG-05 and the indication AX-200M on the underside, similar to the Yamaha YIS-503MII (source: https://www.msx.org/wiki/Sakhr_AX-200).

