$info=ax350iif
$mame
0.250 [openMSX]

AX-350 II F (MSX2, Arabic), Sakhr, 1987

The Sakhr AX-350 II F is an electronic typewriter produced by Sakhr in the 1980s, primarily designed for the Arab market. It allows typing in both Arabic and English thanks to an automatic keyboard layout conversion system. Equipped with a liquid crystal display (LCD) for previewing text before printing, it features internal memory to store short documents and offers basic correction and editing functions. Robust and reliable, it was widely used in administrative and governmental contexts in Arab countries. The "F" version includes an Arabic keyboard with cursive characters and support for formatting that adheres to Arabic linguistic standards.

