$info=b16
$mame
0.142u5 [Angelo Salese]

B16, Hitachi, 1982?

Like all Japanese PC families, this Hitachi-owned computer family has special hardware facilities to render Japanese in text mode. The graphics are integrated on the motherboard and allow 16 colors from a 4096-color palette at a resolution of 640 × 400 pixels. With the B32 DX seen above 640 × 475 pixels are also possible, if one uses as operating system MDOS 2.1. The B16 and B32 computers are incompatible with all other Japanese computer families for MSDOS applications because the BIOS is different. By default, the B16 / 32 computers support the Japanese 1232 KiB floppy format, but for the model shown above, an optional trimodal drive was also available that can also read the 1440 KiB format used by the IBM-compatible ones (source, traslated from German: http://www.duensser.com/pc_famb16.htm).

