0.231 [rfka01, Dirk Best]

7120, BASF, 1982

The BASF 7000 systems are professional computers from Germany. There were several models in the 7000 serie. The computer was based on a DigiLog (USA) Personal Computer (Microterm II Intelligent Terminal), which had an additional printer built in (the paper came out on the top), but was to faulty to be sold (power supply, monitor control, mechanical construction and more). The operating system was an "Enhanced commercial BASIC" interpreter and/or an Assembler. .Later on, a CP/M version was released. The CPU frequency was 4.000 MHz and the memory was 64 kByte + FDC (source: https://www.old-computers.com/museum/computer.asp?st=1&c=1301).

