$info=basic31
$mame
0.136 [Robbbert]

MCS BASIC 31, Intel, 1985

There are 2 version of MCS51 basic architecture on the net at all. First is BASIC52 system, run on 8052 and its varian. Secondly is BASIC31 version. This is a modified version from BASIC52 that run this basic from external memory device for such as 8031/32 or 8051/52' system. With the limited of MCS31/51 architecture, then some feature must be cut off. Then someone changed it to run for this external device and for 80XX' system. With this ability, we can run BASIC31 from an EPROM or another device like EEPROM or flash ROM to 8031 or 8032 and also 8051 or 8052' system. So I start to build my own BASIC31 board to accomodate this version (source: http://dsaprojects.110mb.com/electronics/8031-ah/8031-bas.html).

