$info=basic52
$mame
0.136 [Robbbert]

MCS BASIC 52, Intel, 1985

The MCS BASIC-52 interpreter, developed by Intel, is still very popular, but in its 15th year it needs a thoroughgoing facelift.The MCS BASIC-52 V1.0 interpreter was specially developed by Intel in 1985 for the 8052-AH microcontroller. With its code size of only 8 kB, it fitted into the internal ROM storage of this controller. Unfortunately, the 8052-AH has gone out of production. Nonetheless, the interpreter still enjoys considerable popularity in its final 'official' version (1.1), in spite of a few errors. Nowadays, the 8052 family, with its many derivative versions, has become the most widely used microcontroller family (source: http://www.elektor.com/magazines/2001/february/mcs-basic-52-vi-3.54356.lynkx).

DRIVER:
