$info=basis108
$mame
0.201 [Robbbert]

Basis 108, Basis Microcomputer GmbH, 1982

This professional computer was compatible with most of the hardware and software designed for the Apple II. It could run under DOS 3.x, but thanks to its second CPU, a Z80 processor, it could also run under CP/M. The Basis 108 had 128 KB RAM, (two switchable memory banks of 64k). Two 5"1/4 disk-drives (Apple compatible) could also be mounted inside the computer. In the picture, these are Apple Disk II drives. The Basis 108 was a good Apple II compatible machine with a lot of options built-in (80 columns, disk-drives controller, CP/M, high-resolution graphics), and was cheaper than the equivalent Apple' system. A year after introduction, the Basis Junior was presented at various different electronic shows. It was basically the same computer but with only 64 KB RAM (with optional expansion to 128k) (source: http://www.old-computers.com/museum/computer.asp?c=92).

DRIVER:
apple/apple2.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Preliminary
Color: Good
Sound: Good
Graphics: Imperfect
Save State: Supported

SOFTWARE LIST:
apple2_flop_clcracked.xml, apple2_flop_orig.xml, apple2_flop_misc.xml, apple2_cass.xml

RESOURCES:
Snap and Title.

WIP:
- 0.284: Changed description to 'Basis 108' and manufacturer to 'Basis Microcomputer GmbH'.
- 0.283: Demote to imperfect graphics; also demote basis108 to not working [AJR].
- 0.201: Robbbert added 'Basis 108' system.

ROMSET:
36864 bytes in 10 files / 14.80Kb packed

$end
$info=bassmate
$mame
0.223 [algestam, Mr. Do]

Bassmate Computer, Telko / Nintendo, 1984

The?Bassmate?I saw was sold under the name of a brand called "Probe 2000" and dated from 1984. At first glance, it seemed like a regular sporting aid, be it one that was quite advanced for its time. However, when checking out the image on the back of the box, something dawned on me. That shape seemed rather familiar! It looked just like a?Game & Watch Multi Screen! (source: http://blog.beforemario.com/2013/06/bassmate-computer-new-member-on-game.html?m=1).

DRIVER:
