$info=bbc_tube_6502e
$mame
0.241 [Nigel Barnes]

Acorn Extended 6502 2nd Processor, <unknown>, ????

Pre-production Iss.C and Iss.F boards have been seen running earlier versions of the Tube OS. The boards are different in that they map the Tube ULA at &FF78-&FF7F instead of the usual &FEF8-&FEFF. They also require an earlier version of the Tube Host which can be found in NFS 3.34, the usual DNFS 1.20 will hang at the Tube startup banner.

DRIVER:
devices/bus/bbc/tube/tube_6502.cpp

