$info=bbcmaiv
$mame
0.151 [Nigel Barnes]

BBC Master AIV, Acorn Computers, 1986

In 1983, the BBC decided to celebrate the 900th anniversary of the Domesday Book with a new survey of Britain. Up to 1 million people, mainly in schools, participated by collecting the data which was published as the Domesday Project. Rather than use paper the BBC decided to produce a multimedia product. At this time CDs were still at an early stage in their development and CDROMs did not exist, so the BBC selected Laser discs as a suitable medium. The Domesday Project was published in 1986 on 2 Laser discs (LV-ROM) - the National Disc and the Community Disc (source: http://acorn.chriswhy.co.uk/Computers/Domesday.html).

