0.151 [Nigel Barnes]

BBC Master (ARM Evaluation), Acorn Computers, 1986

The Acorn ARM Evaluation System for the BBC Micro was one of the first production RISC processors. The ARM Evaluation System was part of the development programme leading to the Acorn Archimedes and its early Arthur operating' system. The system was supplied in the standard BBC "cheese wedge" case and connects to the BBC Micro via the TUBE connector port on the base of the BBC (source: http://www.computinghistory.org.uk/det/4617/Acorn-ARM-Evaluation-System/).

