$info=bbcmc
$mame
0.151 [Nigel Barnes]

BBC Master Compact, Acorn Computers, 1986

The Master Compact was launched in September 1986. It is quite different from the rest of the Master series having a 2 box design (3 if you count the monitor) like a modern PC. But what appears to be the system unit is, in reality, only the disc drive/monitor stand, while the motherboard is under the keyboard! The disc unit only contains a 3?" drive and power supply. Like the Acorn Electron Plus 3, the Master Compact has a 3?" disc drive and ADFS as standard, with room for a second 3?" drive in the disc unit. Unlike the rest of the Master series, the Master Compact does not have cartridge slots. Only the operating system (MOS5.10), BASIC IV and ADFS are in ROM. Instead software like View is on the Welcome Disc disc. The Master Compact cost ?451.25 (inc VAT) (source: http://acorn.chriswhy.co.uk/Computers/MasterCompact.html).

