0.254 [hap, Sean Riddle]

Bingo Bear, Hasbro / Tiger Electronics, 1986

Electronic teddy bear-shaped toy designed to teach young children numbers and the basics of bingo in an interactive and fun way. Equipped with buttons, lights, and animated voice features, it randomly calls out numbers, encourages participation with catchy songs and motivational phrases, and recognizes when a child completes a row or covers a full card. Made from soft, safe materials, this toy fosters early learning, social interaction, and group play. Perfect for preschool-aged kids, it combines classic tabletop gameplay with educational technology in a sweet, engaging format.

