$info=berl32t8p
$mame
0.218 [hap, anonymous]

Mephisto TM Berlin (prototype), Hegener + Glaser, 1991

Electronic chessboard prototype developed by Hegener + Glaser in the 1980s in collaboration with Richard Lang, based on the powerful chess engine "The Machine" (TM). Designed to combine high software performance with a portable hardware unit featuring a sensitive chessboard, it was produced in very few units and never mass-produced. Today, it is an extremely rare object, considered a legendary piece among collectors of chess computers, symbolizing the ambition to bring the level of world chess championship electronics into an autonomous device.

