$info=berlinpl
$mame
0.143u8 [Cowering]

Mephisto Berlin Professional 68020 (London upgrade), Richard Lang, 1996

The Berlin Professional was developed by the German manufacturer Hegener & Glaser as a direct alternative to the successful Saitek Risc 2500. Like the Genius module set, this compact chess computer contains the world championship program from 1993, Genius 2.0 by Richard Lang. The chess program is supported by a very powerful hardware, the proven 68020 from Motorola, a 32-bit processor that is clocked at 24 MHz. 1 MB RAM is available for hash tables. The clock frequency has been doubled compared to the Mephisto Berlin 68000 (source, traslated from German: https://www.schach-computer.info/wiki/index.php?title=Mephisto_Berlin_Professional_68020).

