$info=bert
$mame
0.206 [Volker Pohlers]

BERT, VGS Verlagsgesellschaft, 1987

Modular educational system developed by a German publisher specializing in technical manuals, used in the 1980s and 1990s for vocational training in electronics. Composed of interchangeable modules with basic circuits (amplifiers, digital logic, power supplies), it was employed in technical schools to teach analog and digital electronics in a practical way. Designed for safety and ease of use, it included detailed instructional guides and was intended for simulations of faults and measurements. Although now obsolete, it remains a significant example of analog technical education.

