$info=beta
$mame
0.135 [Curt Coder]

Beta, Pitronics, 1984

The Beta computer is a small but fully functional 6502' system. Ideal for controlling applications! The base, called 'controller', is a PCB with 6502 CPU, a 6532 RIOT and a 2716 EPROM. A really minimal 6502 system with lots of I/O and a minimal IC count. This standard controller is meant to be inserted in a PCB called 'terminal' on which specific hardware can be placed, depending on the application (source: http://retro.hansotten.nl/index.php?page=beta-computer).

