The HT12 286 motherboard is one of the last 286 motherboards, manufactured in April 1991. It is based on Headland's highly integrated single chip HT12.  Due to the high degree of integrated components in a superchip, a lot of space could be saved, which enables the board to have a very good layout and good performance.  To the right of the Headland chip is the soldered-on AMD processor, a 286 with a whopping 16MHz, typical of the late days of 286 technology (even though AMD followed in small quantities with a 20MHz variant and the competitor Harris even with a 25MHz variant) (source, traslated from German: http://www.amoretro.de/2012/07/bi-025c-ht12-286-headland-ht12-286-motherboard.html).

