$info=biathlon
$mame
0.240 [algestam, Milan Galcik]

Biathlon, bootleg (Elektronika), 1989

Soviet portable console from the 1980s, inspired by winter biathlon competitions, simulating the combination of cross-country skiing and target shooting. Featuring a monochromatic LCD screen and physical controls, players must alternate between running phases (by rapidly pressing a button) and shooting phases (precisely aiming at stationary or moving targets). The gameplay is simple yet engaging, with scores based on speed and accuracy. Built with a rugged design and battery-powered operation—typical of electronic devices from the USSR—it was intended for home entertainment and reflex-training purposes. This compact device seamlessly blends sports, strategy, and competition into a pocket-sized format.

