$info=bit90
$mame
0.216 [Frank Palazzolo]

Bit90, Bit Corporation, 1983

The Bit Corporation Bit90 is a computer which is?ColecoVision?compatible. It is available in two colors (white with black keys or silver with green keys). The power supply is external. The expansion bus at the back can host RAM packs (memory expansions) or interfaces for different peripherals: disk drive, printer (Centronics parallel), RS-232C. The keyboard has a BASIC key, allowing to type directly a BASIC instruction by pressing just a dedicated key. This computer doesn't support software for Coleco Adam. An adapter for Atari VCS/2600 cartridge was sold separately, too (source: https://www.msx.org/wiki/Bit_Corporation_Bit90).

