$info=bml3
$mame
0.139 [Angelo Salese, Jonathan Edwards, Christopher Edwards]

Basic Master Level 3 (MB-6890), Hitachi, 1980

This japanese computer seems quite powerful. The main board is located into the main case, under the monitor. Inside this main case there are 6 expansion slots which is quite enough ! Thus a lot of expansion boards were available (disk, printers, 8088, Z80 boards, etc). An interesting feature is that there's a little trap-door on the keyboard which reveals some cool control switches : a power switch, a text mode switch (80 / 40 columns), a reset button and volume control knob (source: http://www.old-computers.com/museum/computer.asp?st=1&c=2).

