The Brandt 8641 is an electronic banknote-counting machine designed for use in banking, commercial, or cash-handling environments. Equipped with a power supply, it quickly identifies, counts, and verifies banknotes of various denominations thanks to precise optical sensors and advanced traction mechanisms. It features a digital display for counting visualization, along with functions for accumulation and value selection, and is constructed from durable materials to ensure reliability and security when processing cash. Ideal for managing large amounts of money swiftly and accurately.

