$info=bruc100
$mame
0.132 [Miodrag Milanović]

Bruc 100-1 (MSX1, Italy), Frael, 1987

This is a rare case of a home computer planned and produced in Italy. This somewhat obscure computer is "almost" a MSX 1 machine without bearing any MSX logo. The only difference seems to be that instead of MSX Basic it has a "MCL extended Basic". MSX-1 modules are known to be usable on this machine without problems. The computer looks very much like an ordinary keyboard. It seems that this machine has a very tight relation to the courses of the "2f" computer school. The manufacturer, Frael (Florence, Italy) belongs to the same company as "2f" and both are still existing today (source: http://www.old-computers.com/museum/computer.asp?c=1285&st=1).

DRIVER:
