$info=bt473
$mame
0.277 [R. Belmont]

Brooktree Bt473 True-Color RAMDAC, <unknown>, ????

The Brooktree Bt473 True-Color RAMDAC is an integrated circuit (chip) used in computer systems in the 1980s and 1990s, mainly as part of graphics cards. The term "RAMDAC" stands for Random Access Memory Digital-to-Analog Converter, and denotes a key component in video cards that enables the conversion of digital image data into analog signals, which were necessary for the operation of CRT (Cathode Ray Tube) monitors, which were popular at the time.

