$info=bubltea
$mame
0.282 [David Haywood, TeamEurope]

Mazemaze Mix! Puni Tapi-chan (Japan), Bandai, 201?

It’s a plug-and-play console released in Japan in the 2010s, inspired by the *Puni Puni Poemy* franchise. Designed to connect to a television, it offers educational and interactive mini-games based on matching, visual recognition, and simple logic challenges. The integrated controller is a button-equipped mouse used to interact with animated characters and environments. Audio and video are output via composite connection, targeting preschool-aged children with a colorful, soft experience centered on identifying shapes and familiar objects.

