$info=bup
$mame
0.212 [CB-Emu, Sandro Ronco]

Mephisto Blitz- und Problemlösungs-Modul (set 1), Hegener + Glaser, 1985

The Mephisto flash and problem-solving module, Mephisto B&P module for short, came onto the market in the mid-80s and stood in direct contrast to the selectively calculating Mephisto III program, which came onto the market two years earlier. The Mephisto B&P program by Ulf Ratsmann is said to be particularly good for blitz and, at higher levels, for solving problem chess tasks thanks to the sophisticated brute force calculation. The tactical skills of the module were put in the foreground and to test that, I played a "Blitz" game on level 5, which corresponds to 20 minutes of rapid chess (source, traslated from German: https://schach.computer/partie-gegen-das-mephisto-bp-modul/).

