$info=c2717
$mame
0.128 [Miodrag Milanović]

Consul 2717, Zbrojovka Brno, 1989

ZBA is the abbreviation of Zbrojovka Brno. The Consul 2717 was a clone of the Tesla PMD 85.2 but had a very different design. The mainboard was located in the display case and the keyboard had a more professional look. The machine was only sold to Czech schools. In its basic version it was used with the built-in BASIC-G interpreter which had some graphic commands. Programs could be stored through an external tape recorder (source: http://www.old-computers.com/museum/computer.asp?st=1&c=1130).

