$info=c286lt
$mame
0.210 [rfka01]

Laptop C286LT, Commodore Business Machines, 1990

In 1990, Commodore also launched a PC notebook called the Commodore Laptop C286LT. In Germany it was sold for about 4300 DM (in the US for about 4495 US $). There were also built notebooks with 386SX (16 MHz) with additional optional co-processor Intel 80387SX-16 and 486SX processor in 1991. These differ except for the processor with higher clock rates and a slightly larger hard drive with 40 MB but not. In addition, Windows 3.x can be installed on the 386 and 486 'Commodore LTs, Windows up to version 3.1 also runs on the 286'er. Also includes the somewhat later LTC series instead of the gray scale display a color display. The original price of a 386SX LT in 1991 was approximately $ 4,599. However, the Commodore laptop was just a slightly different Sanyo MBC-17NB (80286) or MBC-18NB (386SX). He was a pure OEM product manufactured by Sanyo (source, translated from German: https://www.c64-wiki.de/wiki/Commodore-Laptop_C286LT).

