$info=c2color
$mame
0.207 [zhongtiao1]

C2 Color (China), Baiyi Animation, 201?

The C2: Card & Color is short-lived handheld released in China in 2015. Published by Baiyi Animation (????), the C2 wanted to bank on the popularity of Roco Kingdom as did the console Monon Color in 2014. The C2 has a similar concept to the Monon Color, but pushes the concept physical card a bit further by integrating the card reader directly in the console itself instead of using the game cartridge to do so. The cards allow the player to interact with the various games. The console came bundled with a few cards and a built-in game. Other games and cards were sold separately. The consoles are very rare, but can still be found brand new in some store in China, but the games are extremely difficult to find (source: http://videogamekraken.com/c2-color-card-by-baiyi-animation).

