$info=c8002
$mame
0.150 [Al Kossow, Robbbert]

C8002, Onyx Systems, 1982

The C8002 is one of the earliest minicomputers to use Unix as an operating' system. The system consists of a main CPU (Z8002), and a slave CPU for Mass Storage control (Z80). The Z80 board contains a 19.6608 and 16 MHz crystals; 2x Z80CTC; 3x Z80SIO/0; Z80DMA; 3x Z80PIO; 2 eproms marked 459-3 and 460-3, plus 2 proms. The Z8002 board contains a 16 MHz crystal; 3x Z80CTC; 5x Z80SIO/0; 3x Z80PIO; 2 eproms marked 466-E and 467E, plus the remaining 7 small proms. The system can handle 8 RS232 terminals, 7 hard drives, a tape cartridge drive, parallel i/o and be connected to a RS422 network (source: 'onyx.c' driver).

