$info=cbm610
$mame
0.36 [Curt Coder]

CBM 610, Commodore Business Machines, 1983

The Commodore CBM 610 is part of the series 600/700, the new powerful line of professional equipment developed and produced by Commodore starting in 1982, also known as CBM-II series. Computers in this series were equipped with MOS 6509 CPU compatible with the 6502 to 2MHz, 80-column display modes, Basic 4.0, SID sound chip (the same as the C64), a serial RS-232 interface and the usual IEEE-488 floppy disk drives and printers (source italian traslated: http://myretrocomputing.altervista.org/commodorecbm610/index.php).

