CBM 8096, Commodore Business Machines, 1981

The CBM 8000 series of included a new display chip which drove an 80x25 character screen, but this resulted in a number of software incompatibilities with programs designed for the 40 column screen, and it appears to have been unpopular as a result. The machine shipped with 32 kB standard as the 8032, but allowed another 64 kB to be added 'externally. Later the upgrade was installed from the factory, creating the 8096 (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Commodore_PET#PET_4000_series_.2F_CBM_8000_series).

