$info=ccs300
$mame
0.150 [Robbbert]

CCS Model 300, California Computer Systems, 1981

There's no info available on this system, however the bankswitching appears to be the same as their other systems. Early on, it does a read from port F2. If bit 3 is low, the system becomes a Model 400. Since IM2 is used, it is assumed there are Z80 peripherals on board.
There's unknown usage of ports 11 thru 1B, 34, and F0 thru F2 (source: MESS driver).

