721 Display Terminal, Control Data Corporation, 1981

Monochromatic cathode-ray tube alphanumeric terminal designed for interaction with mainframes or minicomputers in professional environments. It features a 12- or 24-line display, a functional keyboard with dedicated control keys, an RS-232 serial interface, and support for standard terminal protocols (such as VT52 or similar). Built for reliability and heavy-duty use in business or academic settings during the 1970s–1980s.

