0.211 [zzemu]

China Education Computer 2000, Shaanxi Province Computer Factory, 1991

An 8-bit educational computer developed for school use in China, based on the Z80 architecture or a derivative thereof, featuring an operating system stored in ROM and a built-in BASIC environment. Designed to teach programming and computer science in schools, it includes a video interface for connecting to monitors or TVs, as well as ports for cassette drives and potential expansion options. Characterized by its functional keyboard and straightforward design, this device promotes digital literacy even in resource-constrained environments.

