$info=centurion
$mame
0.268 [hap, Berger]

Kasparov Centurion, Saitek, 1998

With the Centurion in 1998, the company had gathered the experience of three leading chess computer manufacturers ( SciSys, Fidelity and Mephisto ) and maintained their production until 2007 ( Novag continued to manufacture computers for two more years, until 2009). The Saitek Kasparov Centurion had a small LCD display and featured 64 levels (in seven categories), an extensive opening library and 20 classical games for learning. The Centurion is very comprehensive and includes, for example, learning options in the form of saved master games. At interesting points in the game, the player is asked for suggested moves. Depending on the quality of the answers, the chess calculator attempts to evaluate the player's strength in ELO at the end of the course (source: https://www.schach-computer.info/wiki/index.php/Saitek_Centurion).

DRIVER:
saitek/gk2000.cpp

