$info=cf2700g
$mame
0.143u3 [Wilbert Pol]

CF-2700 (MSX1, Germany), Panasonic, 1985

Apart from a nice metallic finish case, the same as Philips and Sony MSX machines, and an unusual arrows keypad, the Panasonic CF-2700 was a pure MSX 1 machine. It featured a dual cartridge slot but, oddly, no RGB video output, only composite and RF jacks. The CF-2700 was also sold under the brand National in some countries with 32 KB RAM instead of 64 for the Panasonic version (source: http://www.old-computers.com/museum/computer.asp?st=1&c=1012).

