$info=cncchess3
$mame
0.242 [hap, Berger]

Computer Chess (Conic, model 7013), Conic, 1981

Conic X, (Conic Experimental, Conic 7013, Conic Korchnoi) an experimental dedicated chess computer by correspondent Hong Kong manufacturer Conic, with a program by Stephen Chen. Conic X played the WMCCC 1981 in Travemünde and became 6th of 8 with 2/7. While the tournament report by Björn Schwarz mentioned Conic Experimental running on a Z 80 A CPU, the soon later released Conic 7013 endorsed by Victor Korchnoi, with magnetic sensory board and apparently a similar program, was shipped with a 6502 processor (source: https://www.chessprogramming.org/Conic_X).

