Electronic Football (Conic, TMS1000 version), Conic, 1979

A console dedicated to an electronic soccer game, powered by the TMS1000 microcontroller. It features an LED or light-matrix display that simulates the field and players' movements, along with simple controls for managing offense and defense. The design is compact and rugged, typical of the 1970s–1980s era, and it runs on battery power. Offering an immediate and intuitive gaming experience, it’s perfect for casual entertainment or as a collectible piece for vintage technology enthusiasts.

