0.137 [Robbbert]

Codata, Contel Codata Corporation, 1982

Intelligent terminal from the 1970s–1980s, designed for accessing mainframe and host systems in corporate or government environments. It combines a monochromatic CRT display, a functional keyboard, and the ability to emulate proprietary or standard terminal protocols (such as IBM 3270). Featuring a robust, modular design with dedicated serial connectivity, it was optimized for data entry tasks, database management, or legacy telecommunications operations.

