0.78 [Per Ola Ingvarsson, Tomas Karlsson]

Compis, Telenova, 1985

The Telenova Compis computer was designed to be used in swedish schools. It featured a 80186 CPU and used CP/M 86. The name "compis" would be a synthesis of the word Computer and the swedish word "kompis", meaning Buddy or mate. It was also a shorting for 'computer i skolan' (computer in school). The Compis was called Scandis in Norway (source: http://www.old-computers.com/museum/computer.asp?c=358&st=1).

