$info=comportiii
$mame
0.192 [rfka01]

Portable III, Compaq, 1987

The Portable III is a very handy, IBM compatible portable computer. Attractive and easy to lug around, it has a bright and easy-to-read gas plasma screen. The screen pivots for a comfortable viewing angle, and the keyboard attaches to the system during transportation. The built-in 20Meg hard drive means no floppy disks are required to run it. Sorry, there are no batteries, you have to plug it into a 110VAC power outlet. An optional internal 1200 baud modem and additional memory are the only internal expansion capabilities. Originally listed for $199, an external expansion chassis (model 2662A) capable of holding two full-length expansion cards can be attached to the back of the Portable III for additional capabilities (source: http://oldcomputers.net/compaqiii.html).

