Constellation Quattro, Novag Industries / Intelligent Heuristic Programming, 1986

The naming of a product is always a delicate thing, especially if this is intended for the international market, such as chess computer. At an early stage, manufacturers used terms such as Super, Turbo, Mega, Star to emphasize the special quality and performance. Another way was to specify a clear product line so that the consumer could assign the chess computer directly to a company. Known were city names at Mephisto, well-known grandmaster at Applied Concepts and gems at Novag (source traslated from German: http://chess-computer.blogspot.com/2016/10/novag-quattro-forte-symphonie.html).

