$info=copspa
$mame
0.244 [hap, Sean Riddle]

COPS Pocket Assistant, National Semiconductor, 1982

A handheld device based on National Semiconductor's COPS (Controller-Oriented Processor System) architecture, designed as a portable personal assistant. It integrates an embedded microprocessor, an alphanumeric LCD display, a numeric keypad, and non-volatile memory for storing notes, contacts, or reminders. Powered by batteries, it features compact dimensions and a simple interface for quick management of personal data. Designed for mobile professionals in the 1980s, before the rise of modern PDAs.

