Kasparov Corona (ver. D+), Saitek / Heuristic Software, 1990

Electronic chessboard with an integrated LCD display and keypad, featuring an advanced chess engine developed in collaboration with Heuristic Software. It offers multiple difficulty levels, tactical analysis, a digital stopwatch, and save/resume game functions. Sleek and compact design, with dual power options (battery or mains). Includes physical pieces—either magnetic or electronically contact-based—for direct interaction with the board. The "D+" version indicates a firmware update with improvements in calculation and strategic responsiveness.

