$info=cpc300
$mame
0.81 [Jirou Kaneda]

IQ-2000 CPC-300 (MSX2, Korea), Daewoo, 1986

The Daewoo CPC-300 was a home computer based on the MSX standard, and produced by a Korean company Daewoo Electronics Co. Ltd. as one of several models of series of MSX computers. It also has the logo IQ 2000 on top of the case. The computer was made in the form of a keyboard. All the circuits of the computer are in the keyboard case. Two possible color versions exist / black with gray keys, and white with gray and blue keys. Both have a built-in power-supply. This version of an MSX computer does not have a floppy drive, and only one slot for cartridges on the top of the case (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daewoo_CPC-300).

