$info=crvisioj
$mame
0.132 [Wilbert Pol, Curt Coder]

CreatiVision (Japan), Cheryco, 1982

The Creativision was distributed in major areas with PAL television system like Europe (Italy, Germany, Switzerland, Austria and Sweden), Australia, New Zealand and South Africa. The only NTSC version which is known to exist is that the Japanese, who obtained a limited sales success, but it is now highly sought by collectors. In all countries where it was marketed retained its name, except in Australia and New Zealand where it was sold by Dick Smith Electronics, as the Wizzard. Here he obtained a great success selling to the point of bringing the DS Publishing (the editorial department of the Dick Smith) to the publication of books on programming the BASIC Creativision and game production and utility tape. Creativision was distributed in Japan by Cheryco (source, traslated from italian: http://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/CreatiVision#Versioni).

