SL 286-16, Commodore Business Machines, 199?

The Commodore SL 286-16 is a PC with a fairly flat desktop case. For reasons of space, the expansion cards had to be installed horizontally in the five ISA interfaces, as the height of the housing is too low. The 286 AMD processor clocks with a frequency of 16Mhz and 1Mb of RAM are installed ex works. A 3.5 "floppy disk drive and a 40Mb IDE hard disk are also available. A VGA monitor can be connected to the ISA graphics card (source, traslated from German: https://mingos-commodorepage.com/sammlung/systemedetail.php?id=41&rubtable=sammlung&path=sammlung&detailf=systemedetail&title=Commodore%20SL%20286-16).

