$info=ct6vta2
$mame
0.288 [The Retro Web]

CT-6VTA2 (VIA Apollo Pro+ chipset), Chaintech, 1999

ATX motherboard for Intel Pentium III processors (Socket 370), manufactured by Chaintech in 1999. Based on the VIA Apollo Pro+ chipset (VT82C694X + VT82C686A), it supports a 133 MHz FSB, up to 1 GB of PC133 SDRAM, and a 4x AGP slot for graphics cards. Includes an IDE Ultra DMA/66 controller, integrated AC'97 audio, optional LAN, and USB 1.1 ports. Economical design with manual CPU voltage adjustment via jumper. Designed for desktop users and small offices as a stable platform for Windows 98/ME/2000 systems on compact and affordable hardware. Represents a mainstream solution of the VIA era, known for good compatibility but occasional limitations in drivers and multiprocessor support compared to Intel alternatives.

