$info=ctk2100
$mame
0.238 [Devin Acker]

CTK-2100, Casio, 2009

The CTK-2100 from Casio is a portable electronic keyboard with 61 piano-style keys. It features step-by-step built-in music lessons that were designed to gradually help you learn how to play. The CTK-2100 comes with a huge library of 400 playable tones, 150 beats and rhythms, and 110 songs. It's an inexpensive, feature-rich instrument that's great for learning, serious playing, and for just having fun with music. There are multiple reverb effects built into the CTK-2100 to sweeten the sound. A built-in sampler lets you record 1 second of audio that can be played back on dedicated trigger pads. 10 additional sound effects are included to spur creativity with sampling. A standard mini-plug stereo input lets you plug in an MP3 player so you can jam out with your favorite music. A large, easy-to-read display is prominently placed on the CTK-2100, so you will know what mode the keyboard is in at all times. The integrated USB port can be connected to a computer to transfer MIDI data. The CTK-2100 can operate via AC power or by 6 standard zinc-carbon or alkaline AA batteries (AC adapter and batteries not included) (source: https://www.bhphotovideo.com/c/product/651460-REG/Casio_CTK2100_CTK_2100_61_Key.html/overview).

