$info=cx5f
$mame
0.155 [Wilbert Pol]

CX5F w/SFG05 (MSX1, Japan), Yamaha, 1984

The Yamaha CX5, CX5F, CX5M, CX5MII and CX5MII/128 computers were specifically targeted at music and sound production, and as such were regarded by many as non-standard MSX machines. However, they are in fact standard MSX1 computers and can be used as such. The CX5F is similar to the CX5M but was aimed at the Japanese market and features a Japanese keyboard. The CX5F is identical to the Yamaha YIS-503, but expands it with the built-in FM synthesizer and MIDI IN and OUT (source: http://www.msx.org/wiki/Yamaha_CX5F).

