0.128 [Wilbert Pol, Miodrag Milanović]

CX5MIIB (MSX1, Italy), Yamaha, 1984

The CX5MII/128 was the third Yamaha MSX computer and was aimed squarely at the music market. It has additional memory, but is very similar in operation to the original CX5M. The main difference is the presence of the SFG-05 sound module offering the ability to use a MIDI controller keyboard instead of the YK-01/10/20 series keyboards (source: http://www.computinghistory.org.uk/det/748/Yamaha-CX5MII-128/).

