$info=cybikov2
$mame
0.132 [Tim Schuerewegen]

Cybiko Classic (V2), Cybiko Inc, 2000

There are two models of the Classic Cybiko. The obvious difference is that version 1 has a switch on the side; version two uses the 'ESC' key for power management. The not-so-obvious differences between the two are the internal memory changes and the location of the firmware. The CPU is a Hitachi H8S/2241 at 11.0592 MHz and it also has an Atmel AT90S2313 co-processor at 4 MHz to provide some support for RF communications. It came with 512 KB ROM flash memory and 256 KB RAM. It came with an add-on slot in the back (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cybiko#Cybiko_Classic).

