0.126 [Curt Coder]

Chuang Zao Zhe 50, Bit Corporation, 1986

The DINA 2 in One, originally known as the Chuang Zao Zhe 50, is a video game console manufactured by Bit Corporation, a Taiwanese electronics company. It is a hybrid console with the ability to play ColecoVision and SG-1000 games. This hybrid was possible due to the fact that the ColecoVision and SG-1000 have nearly identical hardware; the two systems share the same CPU, VDP and sound chip. The DINA was initially released in 1986. The system included a built-in ColecoVision game, Meteoric Shower (source: http://segaretro.org/Dina_2_in_one).

