0.148 [Lord Nightmare, Olivier Galibert]

D-110 Multi Timbral Sound Module, Roland, 1988

The D-110 (a direct descendent of the D-50 keyboard and the D-550 module) is based on Roland's "Linear Arithmetic" (LA) synthesis. The manual goes on to say that, along with the stereo outs, "the D-110 features 6 independent Multi outputs where 6 different sounds can be sent out separately." "The D-110 has 8 Parts which work like conventional synthesizers, and a Rhythm Part which behaves like the sounds of a rhythm machine. Each Part can be controlled by information on a different MIDI channel (source: http://www.synthmuseum.com/roland/rold11001.html).

