$info=d64plus
$mame
0.110 [Phill Harvey-Smith]

Dragon 64 Plus, Dragon Data Ltd / Compusense, 1985

The Dragon Plus was an add-inboard for the Dragon 32 or 64. It provided an additional 64KB of RAM and an 80 column text mode driven by an MC6845 with its own 2KB buffer. The board plugged into the SAM socket on the motherboard, with the SAM being placed on the Dragon Plus board and also required one of the BASIC roms to be moved to the Dragon Plus board with a ribbon cable plugging into the vacated socket. The 80 column display required an additional monitor socket to be provided on the Dragon case as this used its own composite video output circuit (source: http://archive.worldofdragon.org/index.php?title=Dragon_Plus).

