In the early 1980's, I was working with my Mits Altair 8800 as my main computing platform. I had taken on some work with a local company who was using the "new" Motorola 6809 processor. The 6809 was a vastly different architecture, and had many features which were ahead if its time (such as stack relative addressing). In fact, the 6809 still holds the reputation as one of the most powerful general purpose 8-bit processors ever produced (source: http://www.classiccmp.org/dunfield/d6809/index.htm).

