$info=daisy
$mame
0.216 [Nigel Barnes, Centre for Computing History]

Comus Daisy, Comus Instruments Ltd., 1987

This computer was manufactured and sold by Comus Instruments of Kingston Upon Hull as an analogue sampling' device. Internally it used a BBC Master motherboard connected to custom data sampling boards. Little is available online about this computer. It was donated by an ex-Comus employee who mentioned that approximately 200 units were sold in total (source: http://www.computinghistory.org.uk/det/50115/Comus-Instruments-Daisy/).

