$info=dancef2p
$mame
0.286 [TeamEurope]

Dance Factory 2 Player Dance Mat, <unknown>, 202?

Dance mat for video games bundled with the title "Dance Factory" for PlayStation 2 (Codemasters, 2006). The device is made of fabric/polyester and features pressure sensors beneath a printed surface shaped like directional arrows (up, down, left, right), designed for synchronized dance gameplay that matches the rhythm of music. The "2 Player" version includes two distinct gaming areas on the same mat, allowing two users to dance simultaneously in cooperative or competitive modes. The "Dance Factory" game stood out for its ability to automatically generate choreographies from any audio track—whether it was an audio CD or MP3—rather than relying solely on pre-defined tracks. The dance mat connected to the console via a standard controller port, featuring an affordable design typical of rhythm-game accessories from that era, aimed at a young and family-oriented audience seeking active home entertainment.

