$info=daphor32
$mame
0.282 [Nigel Barnes, Alessandro Liberalato]

Daphor 32, Dasit S.p.A., 1983

It is an Italian home computer released in 1983, based on the Zilog Z80 processor and compatible with the CP/M standard. Equipped with 64 KB of RAM, TV video output (RF or composite), a cassette tape drive, and an integrated keyboard, it boots into a ROM-resident BASIC interpreter. Designed for educational and hobbyist use, it was one of the first systems produced in Italy for the local market, offering an affordable alternative to foreign models of the era.

