$info=dcdev
$mame
0.121 [incog]

HKT-0120 Sega Dreamcast Development Box, Sega, 1998

Dreamcast Katana Dev.Box is the official development kit for the Sega Dreamcast. It is the tool used by the majority of Dreamcast developers to produce Dreamcast games. The Katana DB is effectively a computer, but with four Dreamcast controller ports and a GD-ROM disc drive. It has a region switch plus various debugging features, and is compatible with S-Video, RCA and VGA television outputs. The major difference between the Katana DB and a normal Dreamcast is that the Katana DB can interface with a Windows (or Macintosh) computer, as well as various other development components for testing and debugging (source: https://segaretro.org/Dreamcast_Dev.Box).

