$info=dcproto
$mame
0.286 [dragoncity]

Dreamcast (prototype), Sega, 1998

Prototype of the Sega Dreamcast developed between 1997 and 1998 under the codename "Katana," prior to its commercial launch (1998–1999). It featured a bulkier design compared to the final version, additional debug ports for developers, and in some cases lacked the integrated 56k modem that was later included in the retail console. Based on the Hitachi SH-4 CPU and PowerVR2 GPU, it was intended exclusively for internal testing and use by authorized developers—never released to the general public. This prototype represents a crucial stage in the development of the first sixth-generation console with native online connectivity.

