$info=dg10
$mame
0.285 [BCM, Devin Acker]

DG-10 Digital Guitar, Casio, 1987

Hybrid digital guitar produced by Casio in 1983, combining a guitar body with an 8-voice polyphonic synthesizer. The six metal strings served as triggers to generate digitally sampled sounds, including piano, strings, woodwinds, and percussion. It featured a miniaturized 32-key keyboard on the neck for modulation and alternative tunings. Designed for experimental musicians and home studios, it allowed layering of the strings' acoustic sound with digital synthesis via separate audio outputs, anticipating modern MIDI controller concepts in string-instrument format.

