$info=dg20
$mame
0.285 [BCM, Devin Acker]

DG-20 Digital Guitar, Casio, 1987

The advanced digital guitar produced by Casio as the successor to the DG-10 featured an 8-voice polyphonic synthesizer with enhanced sampling capabilities. The six metal strings served as capacitive sensors, triggering digital sounds (piano, strings, bass, percussion) with more precise dynamic response. The neck housed a 32-key keypad for modulation, pitch bending, and non-standard tuning. Designed for electronic composers and home studios, this instrument allowed independent mixing of the acoustic string signal and digital synthesis via separate outputs, offering creative flexibility in sound layering and anticipating the use of string instruments as advanced MIDI controllers.

