0.127 [Curt Coder]

Dina, Telegames, 1988

The videogame crash of 1983 affected Coleco. Texas-based company Telegames eventually purchased the rights to the ColecoVision console, and bought most of Coleco's stock. Rather than selling Coleco's bulky unit, Telegames began manufacturing and distributing the Bit Corporation designed DINA 2-in-1. In 1988 the renamed DINA became the Telegames Personal Arcade. The unit was sold via mail order catalogs. The unit was sold through Telegames, Inc. via mail order for only $40USD (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Telegames_Personal_Arcade).

