$info=dm5620
$mame
0.138 [Lukasz Markowski]

Dreambox 5620, Dream Multimedia, 2004

The Dreambox is a series of Linux-powered DVB satellite, terrestrial and cable digital television receivers (set-top box), produced by German multimedia vendor Dream Multimedia. There was a DM 5600 and also a DM 5620 model. The only difference being that the DM 5620 included an Ethernet port. Otherwise, the DM 56X0 models were a cut down version of the DM 7000 without an IDE interface. They did, however, include an RF modulator allowing them to be used with older TVs that lack a SCART connector (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dreambox#DM_5600.2C_DM_5620).

