$info=dms5000
$mame
0.137 [Miodrag Milanović]

DMS-5000, Digital Microsystems, 1982

The DMS-5000 resumed the concept of the DMS-3/F system, a CP/M based machine that could be used as a stand-alone computer or as a network station for the HiNet local area network. The DMS-5000 was sold in two versions, a Z80 based model with 64 KB of RAM, and a 8086 version with up to 1 MB of RAM (source: http://www.old-computers.com/museum/computer.asp?c=609&st=1).

