$info=dmv
$mame
0.144u5 [rfka01]

Decision Mate V, NCR, 1984

An other CP/M / MSDOS hybrid' system. This computer had no great commercial success. The Decision Mate V came with 128 KB of RAM, but could be upgraded to 256 or 512 KB with expansion cards. The serial and Centronics interfaces were not on the mainboard, but were added 'as expansion cards. An additional card with a 68000 was developed by NCR in order to use CP/M 68 (source: http://www.old-computers.com/museum/computer.asp?c=299).

DRIVER:
ncr/dmv.cpp

