$info=dn3000
$mame
0.145u1 [Hans Ostermeyer]

Apollo DN3000, Apollo, 1988

Apollo/Domain was a range of workstations developed and produced by Apollo Computer from circa 1980 to 1989. The machines were built around the Motorola 68k family of processors. The model naming convention was DN (for Domain Node) with a model number. If the system had no display, it was a DSP (for Domain Service Processor) (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo/Domain#Models).

