$info=dolphinm
$mame
0.280 [anonymous]

Dolphin Microcomputer, Hope Computers, 1989

Compact and modular microcomputer system designed in the 1980s for educational and hobbyist use, based on the Z80 architecture with the CP/M operating system. It features an integrated keyboard, expansion slots, serial ports, and the ability to connect to monitors or TVs. Ideal for programming, text management, and lightweight applications, it stands out for its affordable price and software compatibility with other systems of the era. Perfect for schools, small offices, and computer enthusiasts alike, this system exemplifies the entry-level desktop computers of the pre-PC standardization era.

