0.286 [TeamEurope]

Doraemon Hirameki Pad (Japan), Bandai, 2017

Educational tablet for early childhood, produced by Bandai and inspired by the renowned Japanese franchise Doraemon. The name "Hirameki Pad" (ひらめきパッド) derives from "hirameki" (intuition/bright flash of genius), highlighting its focus on developing logical thinking and creative problem-solving skills. This device features a touch-sensitive LCD screen and offers interactive educational activities designed for children aged 3 to 6 (including logic quizzes, shape/pattern recognition, and simple puzzles) featuring characters from Doraemon and Nobita. It includes sounds, music, and voice feedback to encourage learning through play. The tablet boasts a durable design made of colorful plastic (blue and yellow inspired by Doraemon), is battery-powered, and is specifically crafted to stimulate children’s intelligence and creativity in a playful way, preparing them for their first formal school experiences.

