$info=drpcjr
$mame
0.132 [Brad Oliver, Matt Conte]

Doctor PC Jr, Bung, 1996

For those that don't know a Rom copier is a neato little device that lets tech-savvy individuals enter the exciting world of video game piracy. With one of these units you can rip the ROM off of a cartridge, mess with the source code (like change around graphics,) and if you have a burner you can even compile it back into another cartridge, slap a label on it and sell your "game" as your own. Most people who use them though do it for educational purposes, and units like these are not designed to be used in a Chinese factory to slog out tem million multicarts for the latest piece of garbage Famiclone. These machines also allow you to take a ROM from the internet and burn it into a cart as well (if you have the right equipment). Most Rom copiers are merely add-ons that fit into the cartridge slot of a particular console, but this one is unique in that it has a Famicom built right in (source: http://ultimateconsoledatabase.com/famiclones/doctor_pc_jr.htm).

