$info=ds2000
$mame
0.282 [Olivier Galibert, Al Kossow]

DS 2000 KSR, HAL Communications Corp, 1981

It is an intelligent teleprinter terminal released in 1981, designed for data communication in professional and industrial environments. Based on an 8-bit CPU, it integrates a impact keyboard, a tape reader, and a modem for transmission over telephone lines. It supports standard serial protocols and functions as a user interface for central systems, offering dot-matrix printing and reliable text input. Characterized by durability and compatibility with contemporary business networks, it is an example of low-cost terminals for automation and remote control.

