Kiratto Pri-Chan Design Palette (Japan), Tomy, 201?

Controller shaped like a makeup palette or design, intended for young girls and inspired by a trendy, idol-driven multimedia franchise—perfect for connecting to a TV or external device. It allows users to create and customize characters, outfits, and accessories using colorful buttons, wheels, and sensors that interact with the software displayed on the TV screen. The controller features glowing effects, sounds, and instant feedback to simulate the experience of a real virtual design studio. It encourages creativity, hand-eye coordination, and role-playing, with content that can be updated regularly and often linked to physical collectible cards. Designed with safety, durability, and high aesthetic appeal in mind—characteristic of Japanese toy design focused on the kawaii world.

