$info=dtc
$mame
0.228 [Plamen Mihaylov, Patrick Mackinlay]

DTC, Facit, 1981

Central unit Faci1t 6506. Box made of sheet metal, dark gray upper part and black lower part. Facit logo made of plastic on the front. Connectors (including for monitor and tape recorder), volume control and reset button on the back. Motherboard is the same as used in Luxor ABC-800. Diskette unit Facit 6553. Light beige plastic cover with ventilation recess on the top. The back consists of a black aluminum profile with heat sinks. Front in black plastic with two 5.25-inch floppy drives, below this a protruding flange of brown aluminum with Facit logo of plastic. Power switch, mains connection plug and connection plug (37-pin D-sub) on the back. Keyboard Facit 6570. Upper part in dark gray plastic and underside in black sheet metal. 77 keys of black and red plastic. Swedish characters and Ü. Numeric part and function keys. Facit logo made of plastic on the upper left upper corner. Gray connection cable with 5-pin DIN connector runs out from the back. Monitor Facit 6565. Housing in light gray aluminum sheet. Monochrome 14-inch cathode ray tube type picture tube. Frame around the picture tube of dark gray molded light metal with Facit logo of plastic as well as LED and controls for contrast and brightness. Black lacquered back with Switch, earthed mains connection, fuse holder and connection socket (15-pole D-sub). The model corresponds to Luxor ABC-815. Matrix printer Ericsson, probably model 4160 (corresponds to Facit 4570). Beige plastic cover. Control panel with four-digit LED display on the right. Opening on the front with the printer paper is driven by tractor feed. Discharge takes place at the bottom of the front. Power switch, grounded mains connection, voltage switch, two fuse holders and connection socket (25-pin D-sub) on the back. Connector with 15 pins for connecting the feeder. Sheet feeder Facit 5060 mounted at the top. Two cassettes of brown plastic (source, translated from Swedish: https://digitaltmuseum.se/021026305488/dator).

