$info=dual68
$mame
0.136 [Peter Trauner, Manfred Schneider, Robbbert]

Dual Systems 68000, Dual Systems Corporation, 1981

Dual systems based their business on the Motorola 68000 line of CPU's. The board ran with a 8MHz clock and could address up to 16MG of RAM address space (24 bits). It met all IEEE-696  S-100 bus specifications. No wait states were requires for 4Mhz type RAM boards. They had a second board called the CPU-68000M which also ran at 8MHz but also included the Motorola MC68451 Memory management Unit LSI chip. This allowed sophisticated segmented memory management. There was also a CPU-68000M-L10 which was identical but ran at 10MHz (source: http://www.s100computers.com/Hardware%20Folder/Dual%20Systems/68000/68000CPU.htm).

