$info=dx100
$mame
0.233 [DBWBP]

DX100 Digital Programmable Algorithm Synthesizer, Yamaha, 1985

It’s a digital synthesizer based on Yamaha’s FM (Frequency Modulation) technology. Designed as a compact and affordable instrument, it inherits the sonic architecture of the renowned DX7 but with a simplified engine: it features 4 operators (instead of 6), 8 fixed algorithms, and 8-voice polyphony. It includes a 49-key unweighted keyboard, editable presets, and the ability to store custom sounds. Although more limited than professional models, it delivers a bright and versatile sound, ideal for synth-pop, electronic music, and home productions of the era. Its compact design and low price made it popular among emerging musicians and FM synthesis enthusiasts.

