$info=ec4913
$mame
0.215 [rfka01]

UC4913 REV:1.1, Elitegroup, 199?

It’s a Socket 7-compatible PC motherboard produced in the 1990s. Based on the VIA VP2 chipset (VT82C591/592), it supports Intel Pentium, Pentium MMX, and AMD K6-compatible processors. It features 30-pin SIMM memory slots (supporting up to 128 MB of RAM), 16-bit ISA and PCI expansion slots, an integrated IDE controller for hard drives and CD-ROMs, and optional audio/video capabilities via riser cards or add-on modules. Designed for budget or business desktop systems of the Pentium era, it blends legacy hardware compatibility with support for contemporary technologies such as the PCI bus and, in some revisions, SDRAM. The presence of jumpers for configuring clock speed and voltage reflects the flexibility typical of transitional motherboards moving toward the Plug and Play era.

