$info=ecircus
$mame
0.245 [algestam, Milan Galcik]

Circus (Elektronika), bootleg (Elektronika), 19??

It is an LCD handheld video game produced in the Soviet Union during the 1980s. Featuring a compact and rugged design, it displays monochrome matrix-based graphics with stylized characters and simple animations. It includes four red directional buttons (two on each side) and two side function keys for selecting game modes or setting the timer. The screen shows Cyrillic text (“НУ, ПОГОДИ!” – “Just you wait!”), referencing the famous Soviet animated series "Nu, pogodi!", on which the gameplay is based. It is not a computer but a dedicated gaming device, typical of Soviet-era industrial production—often built with locally sourced components and designed to be affordable and durable.

