$info=edames
$mame
0.262 [hap, Sean Riddle]

Electronic Dames, Saitek, 1988

It is a dedicated checkers console released in 1988. Featuring a checkerboard grid with buttons or sensors beneath each square, it allows play against a human opponent or an AI engine offering multiple difficulty levels. It includes typical features of the era, such as a game timer, legal-move indicators, error correction, and piece-color selection. Powered by batteries or an external adapter, it stands out for its compact design, rubber keys, and a seven-segment or LCD display showing game status. It exemplifies the category of dedicated handheld electronic devices produced in the 1980s to bring classic board games into portable electronic form.

