$info=egame150
$mame
0.227 [gelotus]

E-Game! 150-in-1, <unknown>, 201?

It is an inexpensive handheld console that bundles 150 retro games, mostly unauthorized clones of classic arcade titles and 8-bit console games from the 1980s and early 1990s. Featuring a color LCD screen, built-in speaker, membrane keypad, and a design inspired by vintage handheld consoles, it offers simple and immediate gameplay—albeit with limited graphics and sound quality. Powered by batteries or via USB, it targets the entry-level market and exemplifies the typical low-cost "multi-game" devices widely produced in Asia and distributed globally.

