$info=ehx20
$mame
0.135 [Curt Coder]

Epson HX-20, Epson, 1983

The Epson HX-20 (also known as the HC-20) is generally regarded as the first laptop computer, announced in November 1981, although first sold widely in 1983. Hailed by BusinessWeek magazine as the "fourth revolution in personal computing", it is generally considered both the first notebook and handheld computer (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Epson_HX-20).

