$info=ekaras
$mame
0.218 [Sean Riddle, ClawGrip]

e-kara (Spain, includes 3 songs), Takara / SSD Company LTD / newgent, 2002

e-kara is a toy to enjoy karaoke that was released by Takara (later Takara Tomy) from 2000 to 2009. Insert a special cartridge into the main unit, turn on the power, connect to the AV terminal input side of the TV using a special cable, it is a system that can do karaoke, and various products are released as sensation games Plug It! (Plug-it) series. In addition, a telop is displayed on the TV screen, and the user can sing while watching the telop. In addition, they enjoyed video games in addition to karaoke. The shape of the e-kara main unit is similar to a vocal microphone, but multiple key switches for operation are arranged in the upper part of the side and near the microphone collecting part. Some models also have a 7-segment display. A connection terminal for a dedicated cable is provided at a lower portion of the main body, and is connected to a television or the like via the connection terminal. You can also enjoy the duet by adding an optional microphone (source, traslated from Japanese: https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/E-kara).

