$info=eks515
$mame
0.286 [TeamEurope]

Karaoke Screen Party (EKS-515), Easy Karaoke, 201?

Affordable karaoke system for home use, manufactured by an Asian OEM brand (likely Chinese) under the name "Easy Karaoke," model EKS-515, marketed around the 2000–2010 period. Compact device with a built-in CD+G player (CD with graphics) that displays song lyrics on a TV via composite/RF video output. Includes two microphone inputs with separate volume and tone controls, a basic audio mixer for echo effects, and voice recording functionality onto cassette tape or flash memory (depending on the version). The term "Screen Party" in the product name refers to its ability to display synchronized lyrics and simple animations on the TV screen during playback. Black/grey plastic design with an LED display on the front showing track information and time; powered by mains electricity. Intended for discount markets and occasional family use, this represents a typical entry-level solution from the Asian OEM industry for home karaoke entertainment—without included music licenses (requires commercially available karaoke CDs).

