$info=elanht286
$mame
0.214 [rfka01]

Elan High Tech 286, Leanord SA, 198?

It is an IBM-compatible desktop computer based on the Intel 80286 processor, targeted at professional and business environments in the latter half of the 1980s. Designed to run operating systems such as MS-DOS and early versions of OS/2, it supports the 286’s protected mode for advanced memory management. It features 16-bit ISA expansion slots, integrated controllers for floppy and hard disk drives (often MFM or IDE), and sometimes includes onboard VGA or EGA video or a dedicated graphics slot. Housed in a compact desktop or tower case and built with an architecture prioritizing reliability over high performance, it represents a typical European clone of the era—often locally assembled from standardized components to provide a cost-effective alternative to branded systems.

