Electronic I.Q., Conic, 1979

Licensed from Grandstand, it's the same game as Grandstand's Solitaire. The object of the game is to turn off all the lights. A 6x5 grid of lights appears when you start the game, and using various combinations of the buttons on the game, certain lights will go off, and others will come on. Your challenge is to get them ALL turned off (source: http://www.handheldmuseum.com/Conic/IQ.htm).

