$info=electrio
$mame
0.271 [hap, Sean Riddle]

Electronic Trio, SciSys / Heuristic Software, 1985

This is the SciSys Electronic Trio: an electronic chess + checkers + tic tac toe computer. It was first introduced in 1986. It has a peg sensory board and shows the moves with LEDs. It has 3 compartments on the side to store the pieces. You can switch modes by pressing the new game button multiple times. This electronic chess computer is made for beginners. It has 8 levels, with level 7 taking 35 minutes on average per move. Trio’s Tic Tac Toe computer plays immediately though. In checkers mode, Trio takes about 10 minutes at level 8 to play (source: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=35ZyCMIJE4Q).

