$info=electron
$mame
0.104 [Wilbert Pol]

Acorn Electron, Acorn Computers, 1983

The Acorn Electron is a budget version of the BBC Micro educational/home computer made by Acorn Computers Ltd. It has 32 kilobytes of RAM, and its ROM includes BBC BASIC along with its operating' system. The Electron was able to save and load programs onto audio cassette via a supplied converter cable that connected it to any standard tape recorder that had the correct sockets. It was capable of basic graphics, and could display onto either a television set, a colour (RGB) monitor or a "green screen" monitor (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acorn_Electron).

