$info=elekscmp
$mame
0.136 [Miodrag Milanović]

Elektor SC/MP, Elektor, 1977

Elektor designed with the SC / MP is a simple and inexpensive microprocessor-learning' system. SC / MP stood for Simple cost-effective microprocessor and called the 8-bit processor ISP-8A/500D in P-MOS technology from National Semiconductor, which was clocked at 1 MHz and in addition to +5 V also has a negative auxiliary voltage 7V required. At the time of publication Elektor already existing N-MOS version ISP-8A/600D needed only 5 V and was faster and more energy efficient, but also much more expensive (source, traslated from german: http://www.elektor.de/jahrgang/2005/april/elektor-sc-mp-computer-(1977).63401.lynkx).

