$info=elt286b
$mame
0.215 [rfka01]

ELT-286B-160B(E), Chaintech, 198?

It is an IBM PC–compatible motherboard based on the Intel 80286 processor, intended for professional desktop systems in the latter half of the 1980s. Designed to run at typical clock speeds of the era (10–12 MHz), it supports up to 16 MB of RAM via 30-pin SIMM slots and features integrated controllers for floppy drives, hard disks (MFM/RLL or IDE, depending on the revision), and serial/parallel ports. It includes an EMS (LIM) memory expansion slot and provides 16-bit ISA expansion slots, but lacks L2 cache and support for advanced local buses. Engineered for reliability and compatibility with MS-DOS and OS/2, it represents a standard solution for business workstations or mid-range clones manufactured in Asia during the transitional period between 8086/8088-based systems and 386 platforms.

