$info=elwro800
$mame
0.134 [Mariusz Wojcieszek]

800-3 Junior, Elwro, 1986

Elwro 800 Junior / 8-bit microcomputer home with CPU Zilog Z-80, presented at the International Fair in Poznan in 1986, and produced since 1986 by companies Elwro intended for schools. The computer was designed by a team of scientists from the Institute of Automation University of Technology, winning with competing models of school computers. Was produced in the Works Electronic ELWRO in Wroclaw for the Ministry of Education, which established that the computer has to be fully compatible with the ZX Spectrum . Used in the production of components or for the first national foreign exchange area. Junior had such ability to operate in a network, which was about exceeding his ministerial guidelines. The production of the computer was taken a year after his presentation, order of the Ministry for the year 1987 allocates production to 3.5 thousand computers. Distribution and Junior schools, as well as training in the use of computers dealt with the Headquarters Procurement Education (source translated from polish: http://pl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elwro_800_Junior).

