$info=elzet80k
$mame
0.231 [Robbbert]

Elzet/K 80, Giesler & Danne GmbH & Co. KG, 1982

The ELZET/P is a luggable CP/M computer that from the outside looks very much like a Kaypro II. The floppy drives could be one under the other like the Kaypro, or could be vertically-orientated side-by-side. The drives are 80 track quad-density with 800KB capacity. Behind the drives is a cage that can hold up to 8 slots that plug into a small motherboard. The ELZET/K is a similar computer but is a slightly smaller form factor (source: MAME driver).

