$info=enmirage
$mame
0.142u1 [R. Belmont]

Mirage DMS-8, Ensoniq, 1984

The Mirage was Ensoniq Corporation's first product, introduced in 1984. Priced below $1700 with features previously only found on more expensive samplers like the Fairlight CMI, it became a best seller. The mirage was one of the earliest affordable sampler synths. The Mirage was an 8-bit sampler featuring a 61 key velocity sensitive keyboard, a two digit LED display, extensive MIDI implementation, analog filters, a 333 note sequencer. It had 128Kb of RAM and a maximum sample rate of 32 kHz and up to 6.5 seconds sample-time at 10 kHz. It included a built-in 3.5 inch SSDD floppy drive, which was used to boot the operating system as well as store samples and sequences. Each disk had a copy of the operating system and could be used as a boot disk, obviating the need for a separate boot disk (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ensoniq_Mirage).

