$info=entrada
$mame
0.287 [The Retro Web]

Classic/PCI LP "Entrada" (Intel I420EX Aries chipset), Intel, 1994

Intel Classic/PCI LP "Entrada" motherboard, based on the Intel I420EX (Aries) chipset, manufactured in the mid-1990s for the embedded and industrial markets. Low-profile form factor, designed for compact systems with high reliability requirements. Supports Pentium processors at 60/66 MHz (Socket 5) with a 66 MHz system bus. Features an integrated S3 Trio32 graphics controller compatible with VGA, optional onboard audio, IDE controller for floppy and hard disk drives, serial and parallel ports, and limited ISA/PCI expansion slots. ATX power supply. Widely used in kiosks, POS systems, automation, and industrial applications thanks to the stability of the Intel chipset and the extended support typical of embedded platforms. Represents a mainstream pre-ATX professional solution focused on longevity and software compatibility with DOS/Windows 95 in non-consumer environments.

