EOS B900, Yamaha, 1999

Yamaha EOS B900 is a digital mixing console designed for live sound reinforcement and studio recording. It has been used by many professional sound engineers and musicians, including the likes of Coldplay, U2, and The Rolling Stones. The console features 24-bit/96kHz audio resolution, 16 analog inputs, 8 analog outputs, and 8 digital inputs/outputs. It also has a built-in effects processor, a built-in compressor, and a built-in EQ. Additionally, the console has a built-in USB port for connecting to a computer, allowing for easy recording and playback (source: https://synthpedia.net/yamaha/eos-b900/).

