$info=eps16p
$mame
0.151 [R. Belmont]

EPS-16 Plus, Ensoniq, 1990

The EPS-16+ was an innovative early sampler workstation designed for the 90's. Its sampler specs are impressive: 16-bit, variable sampling rates from 11.2kHz to 44.6kHz. With a slim 1Mb of memory this gives just about 11.5 seconds of sampling time in mono at 44.6kHz. Editing functions are quite nice: normalizing, sample splicing, merging, phase switching, auto-looping, auto-truncating, sample rate conversion and more (source: http://www.vintagesynth.com/ensoniq/ens_eps16.php).

