$info=epsax2e
$mame
0.217 [rfka01]

PC AX2e, Epson, 198?

It’s an IBM PC/AT-compatible desktop computer produced by Epson in the second half of the 1980s. Based on the Intel 80286 processor, it supports extended memory (up to several megabytes), 16-bit ISA expansion slots, 5.25" floppy drives, and an integrated hard disk. Designed for professional use, it runs MS-DOS and contemporary business applications, featuring a proprietary BIOS and a reliable design typical of mid-to-high-end PC clones. It was well-regarded for its build quality and software compatibility, particularly in the European market.

