$info=epsax3
$mame
0.217 [rfka01]

PC AX3, Epson, 198?

It’s an IBM PC/AT-compatible desktop computer produced by Epson in the second half of the 1980s. Based on the Intel 80286 processor, it offers support for extended memory (up to several megabytes), 16-bit ISA slots, 5.25" floppy drives, and an integrated hard disk. Designed for professional and technical use, it runs MS-DOS and contemporary business applications, featuring a proprietary BIOS and a reliable architecture. Compared to the AX2 model, it introduces improvements in expandability and memory management, reinforcing Epson’s reputation for robust, well-engineered hardware—particularly popular in Europe.

