TV Globe (Japan), Epoch, 201?

It’s a plug-and-play console released in Japan, designed to connect directly to a television. Shaped like a globe, it offers interactive educational games focused on geography, world cultures, and international quizzes. The integrated controller features colored buttons for answering questions or selecting destinations, while audio and video are output via RF or composite connection. Aimed at children and families, it blends learning and entertainment in a playful, instant-play format.

