$info=ergo201
$mame
0.222 [Bitsavers]

ERGO 201 (Special #9233), Micro-Term / Kurzweil Computer Products, 1985

The Micro-Term ERGO-201 is a computer terminal produced in 1983 as part of the ERGO series of computers manufactured by Micro-Term Incorporated, located in St. Louis, MO. It consists of a monitor and a keyboard. The monitor contains the motherboard with a keyboard, printer, and auxiliary port. The computer runs on a SGS Z8400 CPU, a clone of the Zilog Z80A CPU. The Micro-Term Ergo Series can emulate a variety of terminals but the most common terminal emulation is vt100 (source: https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Micro-Term_ERGO-201).

