Erik, <unknown>, 1994

The "Erik" (Эрик) is an 8-bit Soviet personal computer designed and assembled by amateurs and hobbyists, whose complete schematics were published in 1994 in the renowned Russian electronics magazine *Radiolyubitel* (Радиолюбитель). This computer was not conceived as a mass-produced industrial product distributed in state-run stores, but as an advanced DIY project dedicated to the amateur radio community, designed to overcome the technical limitations of earlier homemade machines.

