$info=esqm
$mame
0.148u5 [anonymous]

ESQ-M Digital Wave Synthesizer Module, Ensoniq, 1986

The Ensoniq ESQ-M is a vintage synthesizer, the rackmount version of the ESQ-1, that offers eight voice polyphony. It can do basic splits and layers which can be saved as part of a patch. Each voice features three digital oscillators, an analogue filter (a Curtis chip) three LFO's, four envelopes, and four Digitally Controlled Amplifiers and a very serious modulation routing ability (source: http://www.synthtopia.com/content/2009/07/02/ensoniq-esq-m/).

