$info=eurobeeb1
$mame
0.278 [Nigel Barnes]

EuroBEEB-1, Control Universal, 1984

It’s a Spanish clone of the BBC Micro Model B, produced in 1984 for the educational and home markets. Based on the original architecture with a 2 MHz MOS 6502 CPU, 32 KB of RAM, and the Acorn MOS operating system, it faithfully replicates the British model’s graphics, sound, and I/O capabilities—including cassette, RGB monitor, and peripheral connectors. Designed for teaching computer science in Iberian schools, it featured language adaptations and sometimes a locally localized keyboard layout. Its production responded to demand for BBC Micro–compatible hardware in a context of limited access to original units outside the United Kingdom.

