$info=eurobeeb2
$mame
0.278 [Nigel Barnes]

EuroBEEB-2 (Teletext), Control Universal, 1984

It’s an enhanced version of the Spanish clone of the BBC Micro Model B, released in 1984 with added features for the educational and local broadcast markets. In addition to the base architecture—featuring a MOS 6502 CPU, 32 KB of RAM, and the Acorn MOS operating system—it integrates a teletext chip (typically an SAA5050 or equivalent) that enables native generation of teletext pages compliant with the World System Teletext standard (Level 1). This capability made it especially useful for schools, local broadcasters, and informational applications, allowing users to create and display formatted text content on standard televisions. Like the base model, it included language adaptations and localized keyboard layouts, addressing demand for BBC-compatible hardware with practical enhancements tailored to the Iberian market.

