EuroBEEB-3C (CU-Graph colour), Control Universal, 1984

It’s an advanced variant of the Spanish clone of the BBC Micro Model B, released in 1984 with enhanced graphics capabilities. Based on the original architecture—featuring a MOS 6502 CPU, 32 KB of RAM, and the Acorn MOS operating system—it incorporates a proprietary graphics chipset (CU-Graph colour) that extends the standard BBC Micro’s video capabilities, offering an expanded color palette and additional resolutions via RGB or composite output. Designed for educational use, graphics work, and small-scale multimedia projects, it was especially popular in Iberian schools and hobbyist circles. It included language adaptations and localized keyboard layouts, meeting demand for BBC Micro–compatible hardware enriched for the local market.

