$info=europa
$mame
0.262 [hap, Berger]

Mephisto Europa, Hegener + Glaser, 1988

This is a tabletop chessboard, measuring 23x29x2.7 cm. It can be powered by batteries (4 AA batteries) or by the included power supply. The processor is an 8-bit 6301Y with a clock frequency of 8 MHz; the software resides on a 16 KiB ROM, and it has 256 bytes of RAM available. The library includes 300 variants, the programmer is Frans Morsch, and the estimated ELO score is 1638 for the SSDF list and 1714 for the Aktiv list. There are 50 levels of play, including 16 special levels for beginners (source, traslated from Italian: https://museoscacchi.wordpress.com/2011/11/07/hegener-glaser-mephisto-europa/).

