EURO PC, Schneider Rdf. AG, 1988

The Schneider EURO PC was an MS-DOS-based computer division of the Schneider home computer. He was released after the success of the Amstrad CPC series to also in the emerging market for home PCs that offer inexpensive complete' system. If the CPC series under license from the English manufacturer sold Amstrad, the tailor was a self-production PC. The PC used a Siemens 8088 (the clock in the BIOS or operation using a key combination to 4.77, 7.15 or 9.54 MHz has been set), it had 512 KB of RAM (expandable through plug-in card to 640 KB) and came with MS-DOS 3.3 and Microsoft Works 1.0 (source, traslated from german: http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Schneider_Euro_PC).

