$info=exl100
$mame
0.127 [Raphael Nabet]

EXL 100, Exelvision, 1984

The 'EXL 100 was the first computer produced by Exelvision, a company founded in 1983 by a group of former employees of the French subsidiary of Texas Instruments, which developed the computer almost entirely self-financing. The Exelvision EXL 100 was launched in 1984 and unfortunately had little commercial success, there were more substantial sales in France thanks to a government initiative in 1985 the French schools computers purchased 9000 EXL 100 and Exelvision had the necessary funds to stay in market and develop a new computer. The computer remained relatively unknown in other countries where the absence of a real investment and marketing strategy were sold very few units (source, traslated from italian: http://myretrocomputing.altervista.org/exelvision-exl-100/).

