$info=exp4044
$mame
0.218 [rfka01]

EXP4044, ExpertChip, 199?

It’s a Socket 7-compatible PC motherboard produced in the 1990s. Based on a VIA chipset (likely VP2 or MVP3), it supports Intel Pentium, Pentium MMX, and AMD K6/K6-2 processors. It features 30-pin SIMM and/or 168-pin DIMM memory slots (depending on revision), ISA and PCI expansion slots, an integrated IDE controller, and—in some versions—onboard audio and video. Designed for budget or multimedia desktop systems in the post-Pentium era, it combines legacy hardware compatibility with support for emerging technologies such as AGP bus and SDRAM.

