$info=expert3i
$mame
0.143u3 [Wilbert Pol]

Expert 3 IDE (MSX2+, Brazil), Ciel, 19??

It’s an MSX2+-compatible home computer produced in Brazil in the 1990s. Based on the Zilog Z80 processor, it features advanced graphics (bitmap modes up to 512×212 resolution with 19,230 colors), enhanced audio via the Yamaha YM2413 chip, and built-in IDE hard disk support—a rarity among MSX systems. It includes joystick ports, MSX expansion slots, composite/RF video output, and a localized keyboard with a Brazilian layout. Designed for home and educational use, it runs MSX-DOS2 and supports advanced software, including games and productivity applications, representing one of the most complete evolutions of the MSX platform in the South American market.

