32768 bytes in 2 files / 24.16Kb packed

$end
$info=f1392
$mame
0.137 [Peter Trauner, Manfred Schneider, Robbbert]

Fountain 1392, Fountain, 1979

The "Fountain 1392" is a variation of the Radofin 1392, a programmable video game console from the 1970s that is part of the Radofin 1292 family. It features a Signetics 2636N audiovisual co-processor and was part of an early system that used cartridges, which had ROM sizes of up to 8KB.

