$info=f2
$mame
0.144u4 [Angelo Salese, Robbbert]

Apricot F2, ACT, 1984

Unlike the Apricot F1 which was a kind of bridge between the home-computing and the professional markets, the F2 and the F10 were clearly marketed as business machines. They were quite similar to the F1, but included an extra expansion slot, more memory and larger storage capacity : two disk-drives for the F2 and one disk-drive and a 10MB hard-disk for the F10 (source: http://www.old-computers.com/museum/computer.asp?c=493&st=1).

