0.248 [Dirk Best, Bitsavers]

4431, Facit, 1981

It’s an IBM PC-compatible desktop computer produced in Sweden in 1981 by Facit (a Swedish company known for typewriters and calculators). Based on the Intel 8088 processor, it features 64–256 KB of RAM, 5.25" floppy drives, and the MS-DOS operating system. Designed for professional and administrative use, it has a compact design with an integrated keyboard and a metal chassis. It was one of the earliest European PC-compatible systems, developed in collaboration with IBM and primarily targeted at the Scandinavian.

