$info=facit4440
$mame
0.201 [Robbbert]

4440 Twist (30M-F1), Facit, 1984

In Sweden it was used in tax offices, because of its useful features. Main feature of Facit Twist or Facit xxx0 was its screen which could be rotated 90 degrees to portrait orientation allowing 72 line display at 80 columns. Screen was white, with good contrast and flicker-free. It was useful with table comparison and data managenemt. Twist was a good Swedish machine, rigid and reliable. Casing was made of alluminium alloy painted white and brown. Mainboard was located on the back side, and rear part of case was acting as a huge heatsink (source: http://oldcomputer.info/terminal/facxxx0/index.htm).

