$info=fairicam
$mame
0.286 [TeamEurope]

Rilu Rilu Fairilu Camera (Japan), Sega Toys, 2016

Digital toy camera produced by Sega Toys in collaboration with Sanrio, based on the "Rilu Rilu Fairilu" franchise (2016). Compact device designed for preschool girls, featuring an approximately 2-inch LCD screen, basic resolution (0.3–2 MP), and photo/video recording capabilities enhanced with filters and frames themed around Fairilu—fairy characters inspired by flowers and magical objects. The device boasts a pink/purple design with fairy-like wings, large buttons suited to small children’s hands, and battery-powered operation. Some versions supported microSD cards or USB transfer. This playful and educational tool provides an introductory, creative approach to digital photography and was primarily marketed in Japan from 2016 to 2019.

