$info=falco500e
$mame
0.240 [Bitsavers]

Falco 500e, Falco Data Products, 1991

It’s an IBM PS/2-compatible desktop computer released in 1991. It supports extended memory (up to several megabytes), 16-bit ISA expansion slots (not Micro Channel, despite the PS/2 reference), 3.5" floppy drives, and an IDE hard disk. Designed for professional and technical use, it runs MS-DOS, Windows 3.1, and—in some configurations—UNIX-like operating systems. The system includes a proprietary BIOS, serial and parallel ports, and—in certain versions—an integrated VGA controller. It was marketed in Europe as a cost-effective alternative to IBM workstations, with a strong focus on stability and software compatibility.

