$info=fds
$mame
0.155 [Fabio Priuli]

Famicom (w/ Disk System add-on), Nintendo, 1986

The Family Computer Disk System, sometimes called the Famicom Disk System, the Disk System, the FDS and the FCD, was released on February 21, 1986 by Nintendo as a peripheral for the Nintendo Family Computer console in Japan. It uses proprietary floppy disks (called "Disk Cards") for data storage. It was announced, but not released, for the North American/PAL Nintendo Entertainment System. Through its entire production span, 1986-2003, 4.44 million units were sold (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Family_Computer_Disk_System).

