$info=feagpriv
$mame
0.272 [hap, Berger]

Elite Private Line (EAG 6081 conversion), Fidelity Deutschland, 1986

Private Line, (Fidelity Elite Private Line) a dedicated chess computer of the Elite series by Fidelity Electronics with a 6502 processor and a Sargon based program by Dan and Kathe Spracklen, the computer designed by German representative of Fidelity Electronics, Peter Reckwitz. Along with his "team" members Elite and Elegance, Private Line played the 4th World Microcomputer Chess Championship 1984 in Glasgow. The computer had a wooden sensory board and an external display unit. It was released in small quantities for a few collectors and enthusiasts (source: https://www.chessprogramming.org/Private_Line).

