$info=feagv4b
$mame
0.280 [Berger]

Elite Avant Garde 2265 (model 6114-2/3/4, set 3), Fidelity International, 1989

An electronic device dedicated to chess, designed for intermediate and advanced players, featuring adjustable difficulty levels, position analysis, and multiple game modes (including tournaments and training sessions). Equipped with a physical chessboard equipped with sensors beneath the squares and magnetic or contact-based pieces, it automatically recognizes moves and responds via an LED display or voice prompts—depending on the version. The device also offers features such as move suggestions, a built-in timer, detection of illegal moves, and game storage capabilities. Crafted from high-quality materials with a sleek, elegant design, it’s perfect for those seeking a reliable, sophisticated digital opponent for strategic study or entertainment.

