$info=feap90
$mame
0.201 [Robbbert]

Multitel Fe Ap 90-1.1, Siemens, 1989

Another unit based on Siemens Bitel T3210 design. After some success of "intelligent telephone", Siemens manufactured other types of this terminal, here is a newer version of T3210. This one is known as "Multitel Fe Ap 90-1.1". It was not marked with Siemens logo, but with German Post office logo and stickers so it was probably leased from Post for operation as Bildschirmtext service terminal. It is newer than T3210 - my unit is from 1988 (?89) while Bitel is 2 years older. The construction has been simplified - re-designed mainboard contained only one ROM containing data essential for operating - mostly characters and graphics - and the system ROM has been moved to battery-backed SRAM module. This way it could be upgraded without much disassembly. Lock module ROM is not used at all. DB expansion connector has been replaced with two DIN ones and card reader conector is not soldered in. It was definitely a "cost-reduced" and upgraded version of T3210. Its strange name - "Fe Ap" may come from German "Fernsprech Apparat" - Telephone device, as well as e.g. "Fernschreiber" - a teletype especially that some German telephones had types "FeT Ap ..." (source: http://oldcomputer.info/terminal/multitel/index.htm).

DRIVER:
siemens/bitel.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Preliminary
Color: Good
Sound: Preliminary
Graphics: Good
Save State: Unsupported

SOFTWARE LIST:
-

RESOURCES:
Snap, Title, Icon, machine picture (in "Cabinet" collection), Control Panel and PCB.

