It’s a portable electronic organizer released in 1994, designed for children and teens. Featuring a liquid crystal LCD screen, an integrated keyboard with function buttons, and a stylus pen for handwritten input, it offers agenda, note-taking, educational games, and virtual pet care (raising a puppy). It also includes a small speaker for sounds and feedback. Conceived as both a learning and entertainment tool, it combines logic, creativity, and responsibility in a compact, colorful format typical of 1990s Japanese gadgets.

