$info=fex68km3
$mame
0.188 [CB-Emu]

Excel 68000 Mach III Master 2265 (set 1), Fidelity International, 1988

It’s a dedicated chess computer released in 1988, based on the Motorola 68000 processor and designed for advanced players. It features a powerful chess engine for its time, offering multiple difficulty levels, analysis mode, an integrated opening book, and an LED display to show moves on a physical chessboard. Its elegant design includes a wooden board with pressure sensors and magnetic pieces, delivering a tournament-like experience in a home setting. Intended for training, study, and challenging a high-level artificial opponent, it stands as one of the most advanced chess systems of its generation.

