$info=fex68km4
$mame
0.218 [hap, Berger]

Excel 68000 Mach IV 68020 Master 2325 (set 1), Fidelity International, 1989

The Fidelity Excel Mach IV Master deserves a prominent place in the story of Fidelity's struggles to try to wrest the World Championship from Mephisto. A quest in which Fidelity failed despite Dan and Kathe Spracklen making considerable progress with the strength of their program. You can read about Mephisto's triumph over Fidelity in my piece on the Mephisto Almeria Turniermaschine. At the 1988 World Microcomputer Chess Championships Fidelity used special fan cooled cases and 68030 processors but otherwise their tournament machines were essentially Mach IV Masters (source: http://www.chesscomputeruk.com/html/fidelity_excel_mach_iv_master.html).

