$info=fex68km4a
$mame
0.274 [Berger]

Excel 68000 Mach IV 68020 Master 2325 (set 2), Fidelity International, 1989

It’s a dedicated chess computer released in 1989, based on the Motorola 68020 processor—an upgrade over earlier models—delivering superior performance and a more refined chess engine. Designed for expert players, it includes an extensive opening book, in-depth analysis mode, multiple playing levels (including tournament time controls), and instructional features. The system incorporates a wooden physical chessboard with pressure sensors and magnetic pieces, accompanied by an LED display for showing moves and system messages. It represents one of the high points of the pre-Pentium era in dedicated chess computers, balancing computational power, reliability, and build quality.

