0.184 [yovan]

The Excellence (model EP12, set 1), Fidelity International, 1985

It’s a dedicated chess computer released in 1985, designed for intermediate and advanced players. Based on an 8-bit microprocessor (typically a Motorola 68000 or equivalent), it offers multiple difficulty levels, an extensive opening book, analysis mode, and an LED display for showing moves. It includes a physical chessboard with pressure sensors and magnetic pieces, ensuring direct and precise interaction. Intended for training and study, it represents one of the most advanced solutions of its time for learning chess strategy.

