$info=fingbowl
$mame
0.256 [hap, Sean Riddle]

Finger Bowl, Tiger Electronics, 1981

It’s a manual dexterity game released in 1981, consisting of a transparent bowl with a rotating lid and small balls inside. The player uses only their fingers to guide the balls through paths, holes, or targets within the container. Lacking electronics, batteries, or digital components, it relies entirely on manual skill, coordination, and motion control, representing a simple, analog form of physical entertainment typical of the pre-digital era.

