$info=fl100
$mame
0.205 [Dirk Best]

FL-100, Grundig, 198?

It is a home computer released in Germany in the second half of the 1980s, based on the Zilog Z80 architecture. Designed for home and educational use, it features 64 KB of RAM, TV video output (RF or composite), a cassette tape drive, and an integrated keyboard. It boots into a ROM-resident BASIC interpreter and supports educational software and simple games. Marketed as an affordable alternative to Western models, it was primarily distributed in Central and Eastern Europe.

