$info=flufflav
$mame
0.286 [TeamEurope]

Fuwatcho Uncho Fuwa Fuwa (lavender, Japan), Happinet, 2021

Toy smartwatch for early childhood, produced by Happinet as part of the "Fuwatcho" line. The name "Uncho Fuwa Fuwa" refers to a character designed specifically for young children, paired with the Japanese term "fuwa fuwa" (ふわふわ), which evokes softness and tenderness. This compact device features a soft silicone strap, a monochromatic LCD screen displaying animated characters, a clock with large numerals, an audible timer, and simple interactive games. Large buttons are perfectly suited for small children’s hands; it runs on a button-cell battery (CR2032) and boasts a rounded, durable design. The watch has no real connectivity or advanced smart features—it’s an educational toy intended to introduce children aged 2–5 to the concept of timekeeping and daily routines. It is primarily marketed in Japan as a promotional gadget tied to preschool franchises.

