$info=fm16beta
$mame
0.142u5 [Barry Rodewald]

FM-16β, Fujitsu, 1982

The model number was FM-16β, and it was sold in the USA from about 1983 to around 1985. It had dual processors on daughter boards, one with a Zilog Z-80a and the other with an i8086 on a true 16-bit bus. Hard drives were external, connecting through a SCSI host adapter. The machine could have up to 2MB of RAM on a proprietary expansion card, and ran at 8MHz. It had a 640x480 16 color display and 104 keys keyboard (source: http://www.old-computers.com/museum/computer.asp?st=1&c=382).

