FM-77AV40SX, Fujitsu, 1985

The FM-77AV40SX was the last FM-77 series machine, Audio-Visual expansion of FM-77AV40EX. About this computer, Nomura Hisayuki adds: some people said FM77AV40SX was the ultimate 8 bit computer. Its video-functions were remarkable: a. Displays TV programs on it's video monitor b. TV control from the keyboard c. TV screen capture d. Displays subtitles on TV (these functions were realized in the 80s!). 260,000 color graphics was also marvelous (source: http://www.old-computers.com/museum/computer.asp?c=375&st=1).

