$info=fm77av
$mame
0.133 [Barry Rodewald]

FM-77AV, Fujitsu, 1985

The FM 77 AV was an impressive system in 1985. It's a good example of what was developped in Japan and we never heard of in the rest of the world. The system has great audio and video features, hence the AV for "Audio and Video". It can display 640 x 200 pixels in two colors, or 320 x 200 in 4096 colors ! There is even a multipage mode where you can define two 460 x 200 screens with 8 colors each, or six 640 x 200 monochrome screens! (source: http://www.old-computers.com/museum/computer.asp?c=373).

