FP-1000, Casio, 1982

Casio FP 1000 (FP 1000 / FP 1100) is a professional computer, a product of the company Casio (Casio), which began to be made in Japan in 1983. He used a Zilog Z80 A as the central microprocessor and the RAM memory of the FP 1000 computer had a capacity of 64 KB. CP/M was used as the operating system (source, translated from Serbian: https://sr.wikipedia.org/sr-el/Casio_FP_1000).

