$info=fpresbu
$mame
0.198 [hap, Berger, yoyo_chessboard]

Prestige Challenger (Budapest program), Fidelity Electronics, 1983

It’s a dedicated chess machine released in 1983, designed for advanced players and enthusiasts. Built around an 8-bit microprocessor with an accelerated clock, it offers multiple difficulty levels, in-depth analysis capabilities, an extensive opening book, and an LED display for move visualization. The device features a game engine developed in collaboration with Hungarian experts (the Budapest program), enhancing both strategic depth and tactical precision. Equipped with a physical chessboard featuring pressure sensors and magnetic pieces, it combines accuracy and reliability in a compact design ideal for study, training, and amateur competition.

