$info=froz2dct
$mame
0.286 [TeamEurope]

Frozen 2 Dream Camera Tablet (Japan), Takara Tomy, 2020

Toy tablet-camera produced by Takara Tomy under license from Disney, based on the Frozen 2 franchise (2019). This compact device is designed for girls aged 4 to 8, featuring a design inspired by the film’s icy world: an approximately 3-inch LCD screen with a themed border (blue/silver colors, snowflake motifs), a built-in front-facing camera for taking selfies and photos enhanced with Frozen-themed filters (frames featuring Elsa, Anna, Olaf, and “ice magic” effects). The device includes simple interactive games (memory, matching, virtual glitter drawing), playback of musical tracks from the film ("Into the Unknown," "Show Yourself"), and animated video clips. It’s battery-powered (using AAA batteries or rechargeable batteries), comes with a wrist strap, and features large, intuitive buttons. Some versions support microSD cards for saving photos. While not a fully functional tablet, this electronic educational toy combines photographic creativity, role-playing, and immersion in the Frozen franchise; it was primarily marketed in Japan and Asian markets between 2019 and 2021.

