$info=frxc402
$mame
0.214 [rfka01]

FRX/386DX Cache System, Modula Tech, 199?

This is a PC motherboard compatible with the AT standard, produced in the early 1990s. Built around the FOREX FRX46C402, FRX36C300, or SiS 85C206 chipset, it supports Intel 80386DX/SX processors and features 30-pin SIMM memory slots, a 16-bit ISA expansion bus, integrated controllers for floppy and hard disk drives, and sometimes includes support for L2 cache. Designed for cost-effective desktop or business systems from the pre-486 era, this motherboard combines compatibility with MS-DOS and early Windows environments while offering a reliable design—though notably lacking PCI bus technology or other more advanced features of the time. It’s a quintessential example of second-generation 386 hardware, widely distributed across Europe and Asia for large-scale cloning purposes.

