0.80 [Jirou Kaneda]

FS-1300 (MSX1, Japan), National, 1985

The National FS-1300 is same as the CF-1200 or CF-2700, but has more RAM. It was produced by the Japanese corporation Matsushita Denki for the Japanese market. At that time National was the brand used in Japan and Panasonic was used for the international market. The MSX1 product line from National was called "King-Kong" in Japan. The computer consists out of a single unit with integrated keyboard and power supply. This model has 2 cartridge slots placed in parallel on the top right. The case is dark silver and grey. It was produced after the CF-1200 with a joystick included for a lower price (source: https://www.msx.org/wiki/National_FS-1300).

