$info=fs4600f
$mame
0.81 [Jirou Kaneda]

FS-4600F (MSX2, Japan), National, 1986

It’s a Japanese home computer released in 1986, compatible with the MSX2 standard. Based on a 3.58 MHz Zilog Z80 processor, it features 128 KB of RAM, advanced graphics capabilities (with resolutions up to 512×212 pixels and over 19,000 colors), enhanced audio powered by the AY-3-8910 chip, and support for 3.5" floppy disk drives. The system includes an integrated keyboard with a Japanese layout, RGB/composite video output, and MSX expansion ports. Designed for home use, educational purposes, and lightweight software development, it runs MSX-DOS2 and supports a vast library of games and applications optimized for MSX2—making it a versatile and comprehensive system within the Japanese MSX ecosystem of the 1980s.

