$info=fs5000f2
$mame
0.81 [Jirou Kaneda]

FS-5000F2 (MSX2, Japan), National, 1986

The model FS-5000F2 is based on FS-5500F2. The name of this computer is FS-5000 as indicated on front, but the label on back and on the box specifies its link with the FS-5500F2 model by indicating FS-5000F2. Compared to the FS-5500 series the audio/video control panel, trackball and superimpose/digitize capabilities have been removed but the memory goes up to 128kB. It was aimed at the Japanese market. Only the version with 2 floppy disk drives was released (there is no FS-5000F1). The PSG sound output is stereo on the rear RCA terminals, the RGB21 connector as well as the headphone output. A switch on the back allows to switch to mono, which affects the RCA terminals and the RGB21 connector but not the headphone jack (this remains stereo). Another switch allows a selection between JP50on or JIS keyboard layout (source: https://www.msx.org/wiki/National_FS-5000F2).

