$info=fsa1st
$mame
0.143u3 [Wilbert Pol]

FS-A1ST (MSX Turbo-R, Japan), Panasonic, 1991

The Panasonic FS-A1ST MSX turboR is the second to last MSX computer ever produced and it follows the latest standard for the MSX line. The FS-A1ST has a new PCM sound chip, the R800 CPU and 256Kb of RAM. Panasonic was the only company to build MSX turboR computers, and they were only sold in Japan. The FS-A1ST was succeeded by the A1GT, which featured more RAM and MIDI IN and OUT (source: http://www.msx.org/wiki/Panasonic_FS-A1ST).

