$info=fscc9ps
$mame
0.179 [anonymous]

Sensory 9 Playmatic S, Fidelity Deutschland, 1983

It’s a dedicated chess machine released in 1983, designed for intermediate and advanced players. Built around an 8-bit microprocessor with an accelerated clock speed, it offers multiple difficulty levels, positional analysis, an opening book, and an LED display for move visualization. The system includes a physical chessboard equipped with pressure sensors and magnetic pieces, ensuring precise interaction. The game engine, developed in collaboration with European programmers, emphasizes positional play and solid tactical strategies, making it ideal for study and training at the advanced amateur level.

