$info=ft486f55
$mame
0.217 [rfka01]

486FT55 (SiS 85C496/85C497 chipset), Freetech, 1995

It’s a PC motherboard compatible with the AT standard, manufactured in 1995. Based on the SiS 471/472 chipset or its equivalent, it supports Intel 80486DX2/DX4 processors up to 100 MHz, up to 128 MB of RAM (via 72-pin SIMM slots), as well as 16-bit ISA and PCI expansion slots. It features an integrated IDE controller for hard drives and CD-ROMs, along with serial and parallel ports. While it doesn’t include onboard audio or video, this motherboard offers excellent stability and compatibility with MS-DOS and Windows 3.1/95. Designed for budget desktop systems or upgrade solutions from the post-386 era, it provides a reliable transition option to the 486 architecture before the widespread adoption of Pentium processors.

