0.151 [Al Kossow, Robbbert]

FT-68M, Forward Technology, 198?

It’s a PC motherboard compatible with the AT standard, produced in the second half of the 1980s. Based on the Intel 80286 processor, it supports extended memory (up to several megabytes), features 16-bit ISA expansion slots, and includes a 5.25" floppy drive as well as MFM/IDE hard disk support. Designed for professional and technical use, it runs MS-DOS and business applications of the era, featuring a proprietary BIOS and a highly reliable design. It was marketed as an affordable solution for businesses and laboratories, emphasizing hardware compatibility and operational stability in legacy environments.

