$info=fw600
$mame
0.201 [R. Belmont, rfka01]

FontWriter FW-600, Sharp, 1994

It’s a portable word processor released in 1994, designed for writers, students, and professionals on the go. Featuring a built-in QWERTY keyboard, a high-readability monochrome LCD screen, and battery-powered operation, it offers advanced text formatting features, a spell checker, and an integrated dictionary. Documents can be stored either in internal memory or on PCMCIA cards, and it includes an optional thermal printer or supports external printers via a serial port. Built on a dedicated operating system, it doesn’t run general-purpose software but is optimized for standalone text productivity, making it a professional solution in the pre-widespread notebook era.

