$info=fz20m
$mame
0.278 [BCM, Devin Acker]

FZ-20M Digital Sampling Synthesizer Module, Casio, 1989

The Casio FZ-20M is a digital synthesizer and sampler produced by Casio in 1989, as an evolution of the FZ series that included the FZ-1 and FZ-10M. It is an intermediate step between the FZ-10M and the top-of-the-line FZ-1, offering a balance of advanced features, sound quality, and affordability, aimed at musicians, emerging producers, and semi-professional studios. While not reaching the notoriety of competing models such as the Akai S900 or the E-mu Emulator, the FZ-20M is remembered today as one of the most affordable samplers of the late 1980s, with solid performance for the time.

