$info=ga6vx
$mame
0.288 [The Retro Web]

GA-6VX (VIA Apollo Pro chipset), Gigabyte, 1998

ATX motherboard for Intel Pentium II/III processors (Socket 370), produced by Gigabyte in 1998–1999. Based on the VIA Apollo Pro chipset (VT82C693A + VT82C596B), it supports a 100 MHz FSB, SDRAM PC100 memory up to 768 MB, and an AGP 2x slot. Includes an IDE Ultra DMA/33 controller, integrated AC'97 audio, and USB 1.1 ports. Features an economical design with jumpers for CPU configuration. Targeted at desktop users as a stable platform for Windows 98/NT on affordable hardware. Represents a mainstream VIA-era solution, appreciated for general compatibility but with occasional driver limitations compared to Intel alternatives.

