$info=ga888
$mame
0.262 [azya52, David Haywood]

Block Game & Echo Key GA888, <unknown>, 199?

It’s a handheld electronic game released in the 1990s, based on a Hitachi HT11xx LCD driver chip. Equipped with a fixed-segment monochrome display and buttons for control, it features a "block breaker"-style game (similar to Breakout or Arkanoid), in which the player moves a paddle to bounce a ball against blocks. The game has no sound or dynamic graphics—animations are simulated using pre-defined segments of the display.

