Gaelco DS5002FP Programmer, Gaelco, 1992

Professional programming device for arcade boards, primarily used by technicians and developers to write, modify, or update firmware on DS5002FP chips—cryptographic microcontrollers widely employed in many arcade mainboards from the 1990s and 2000s. Equipped with a serial or USB interface, it allows bypassing hardware protections, loading custom code, and restoring locked or damaged boards. Requires advanced technical expertise and is utilized in the fields of arcade cabinet repair, preservation, and modding. This is not a consumer product but rather an industrial development and reverse-engineering tool.

