$info=gb50_150
$mame
0.279 [Myrtle Shah]

GB-50 Retro Station Pocket System, <unknown>, 2019

This is a portable "plug-and-play" console designed as a tribute to retro aesthetics, featuring a selection of pre-installed video games—primarily classic 8-bit titles or those inspired by early gaming systems. Powered by a built-in battery, it comes with an integrated display and physical controls (buttons and a joystick), allowing you to start playing instantly without needing any external devices. Since it doesn’t connect to a TV, it’s perfect for solo, on-the-go gaming, appealing to enthusiasts seeking nostalgic entertainment with a vintage-inspired look—typical of the budget-friendly mini-consoles manufactured in Asia.

