$info=gbcolor
$mame
0.61 [Anthony Kruize]

Game Boy Color, Nintendo, 1998

The Game Boy Color is Nintendo's successor to the 8-bit Game Boy handheld game console, and was released on October 21, 1998 in Japan, November 19, 1998 in North America, November 23, 1998 in Europe and November 27, 1998 in the United Kingdom. It features a color screen and is slightly thicker and taller than the Game Boy Pocket. As with the original Game Boy, it has an 8-bit processor. The Game Boy and Game Boy Color combined have sold 118.69 million units worldwide (for more info see: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Game_Boy_Color).

DRIVER:
nintendo/gb.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Good
Color: Good
Sound: Imperfect
Graphics: Imperfect
Save State: Supported

SOFTWARE LIST:
gbcolor.xml, gameboy.xml

RESOURCES:
Snap, Title, Icon, machine picture (in "Cabinet" collection), Control Panel, Flyer, pdf Manual, Marquee, PCB and Artwork Preview.

WIP:
- 0.285: (gbcolor.xml) Add South Park prototype ROM (#14809) [Mike Swanson].
- 0.248: Actually fill in CRC for added 'cartridge and put the PCB designations on the right items in 'gbcolor.xml' [Vas Crabb].
- 0.247: Added 'notes on what happens if you bypass the boot check for Rocket Games cartridges in 'gbcolor.xml' [Vas Crabb].
- 0.234: Fixed some parent/clone relationships, and improved some short names in 'gameboy.xml' and 'gbcolor.xml' [kmg].
- 0.175: Documented more Game Boy Color PCBs, based on no-intro pictures in gbcolor.xml [Fabio Priuli].
- 0.161: Added 'some recent dumps of Sachen carts in gbcolor.xml [Tauwasser, BigFred, taizou].
- 0.155: Added 'a configuration setting (off by default) to skip BIOS checks at boot. This allows the recently dumped Rockman World Prototype to be played, and the Rocket Games pirate GBC carts too [Fabio Priuli].
- 0.153: Fixed heavy gfx regression caused by my conversion of the LCD to be a' device. Fixed NVRAM saving [Fabio Priuli].
- 0.148u5: Simplified video code by reducing the number of memory pointers used, and added 'support for save state registration [Fabio Priuli].
- 0.148u4: Added 'PCB documentation to gba, gbcolor and n64 lists, based on nointro pictures [LoganB].
- 0.148u2: Added support for Sintax mapper, promoting a dozen of pirate games to working state [taizou, Fabio Priuli].
- 0.147: Graphics corruption in many sets (commandk, dkongc, zeldaldx) (MTB #05003) [Sandro Ronco].
- 0.145u8: Fixed sprite regression [Alegend45].
- 0.135: Made SVBK readable. RAM bank #0 cannot be selected at d000-dfff. This fixes many  games. Added BIOS [Wilbert Pol]. Updates: Fixed multisession error. Improved handling of palette writes. Fixes bugs #187, #298, and #1699 [Carlos].
- 0.134: Added 'preliminary support for the bootstrap ROM [Wilbert Pol].
- 0.123: Added 'locking of palette data registers [Wilbert Pol].
- 0.110: Added 'double speed mode support (bug #300) [Wilbert Pol].
