$info=gen32l
$mame
0.143u8 [Cowering]

Mephisto Genius 68030 (London upgrade), Richard Lang, 1996

At that time, the first relatively low-cost 32 bit module set with a program of Richard Long. The significantly slower 68020 predecessor modules cost about 2000€. The program was also an EPROM upgrade for some older models. The Genius 2.0 program of the best according to many experts, chess programmer Richard Lang in November 1993 could win the world title. Originally conceived as a pure computer program, decided to make the German manufacturer Hegener + Glaser, this program also tip the owner of the modular boards accessible. The operation of the computer cursor is controlled using a model system, only six buttons (source, traslated from german: http://www.schach-computer.info/wiki/index.php/Mephisto_Genius).

