$info=genitvp
$mame
0.288 [TeamEurope]

Genius TV Progress (VTech, France), VTech, 2006

Educational system for children connected to TV via RF/composite output. Includes a colorful keyboard with large buttons, integrated joystick, and slots for educational software cartridges. Based on proprietary 8-bit hardware (often derived from Z80 or 6502 architectures), it provides literacy, math, logic, and creativity activities. Features simple graphics overlaid on the TV video signal and mono audio via internal speaker or TV. Powered by an external power adapter. Marketed in the 1990s–2000s as a home learning tool for children aged 3–8, representing the pre-digital "edutainment" approach with content aligned to early school programs.

