$info=gfc1080
$mame
0.155 [Wilbert Pol]

GFC-1080 (MSX1, Korea), Goldstar, 1985

The Goldstar GFC-1080 was aimed for the Korean market. It was available in ivory color with colored keys and has a hangul led. Compared to the FC-80, a firmware is included: a spreadsheet named Pasocalc and an assembler/monitor. The same model was available without this firmware, see GFC-1080A. After booting, you access to a menu with 2 options (Pasocalc and Basic). The built-in assembler/monitor can be launched from Basic by CALL A or _A. You need then to press RETURN to get an intro message and the monitor zone at the bottom of the screen. A new pressing on RETURN displays a specific cursor (source: https://www.msx.org/wiki/Goldstar_GFC-1080).

DRIVER:
msx/msx1.cpp

