$info=gfc1080a
$mame
0.155 [Wilbert Pol]

GFC-1080A (MSX1, Korea), Goldstar, 1985

The Goldstar GFC-1080A was aimed for the Korean market. This model is the same as GFC-1080 but without the firmware (Pasocalc + assembler/monitor). The GFC-1080A was available in ivory color with colored keys and has a hangul led. This computer is a MSX1 with a Z80A from Zilog (Z8400A PS) or Goldstar (GSS Z8400A PS) at 3.579545MHz. All features are common to the standard, apart from one: it has a hole at the right of the cartridge slot to store a lightpen when the pen is not in use. A lightpen was planned in option with its dedicated cartridge, but was never released (source: https://www.msx.org/wiki/Goldstar_GFC-1080A).

