$info=gigatron
$mame
0.218 [Sterophonick]

Gigatron TTL Microcomputer, Marcel van Kervinck / Walter Belgers, 2018

The Gigatron TTL microcomputer is a minimalistic retro computer. It is special in its own oddball way, because it has absolutely no complex logic chips in it, not even a microprocessor! Instead, its CPU is built out of a handful of classic 7400-series ICs, colloquially known as the TTL logic series. In the Gigatron these simple chips not only form a CPU, but this CPU in turn performs all tasks that normally require dedicated peripheral chips. Despite its simple and small design, the Gigatron works as an 8-bit single-board microcomputer that you can play video games with (source: https://gigatron.io/).

