GM-1000 GM Sound Module, Suzuki (Hammond license), 1994

half rack module, with 16x2 lines display backlit. General-Midi Expander with traditional (and variation) GM-sounds and Hammond sounds based on VASE (versatile advanved sound technology) developped by hammond-suzuki. Sound plain rompler with 8mb wavetable at 16 bits 44kHz machine, includes 266 sounds (GM 128 voices + 138 variations) + 9 drums sets (102 voices) = 368 voices. Special, and most interesting the 32 hammons variations with dedicated digital leslie emulation. Sounds cannot be really edited, but module a couple of parameters such as envelope attack/decay/release, filter cutoff and resonance, plus LFO modulator vibrato depth, delay and of course rate. Module is fully compliant to sysex editor for advanced editing. Effects: 8 reverbs: like room hall plate and 8 choruses including also echo, and leslie, flanger and delays. Parameters can be adjusted basically on the screen (source: https://www.polynominal.com/hammond-gm1000/).

