$info=gmaster
$mame
0.124 [PeT]

Game Master, Hartung, 1990

The Game Master is a handheld game console developed by the German company Hartung to compete with the Nintendo Game Boy. It was also released in the UK as the Systema 2000 by already well established maker of cheap LCD games Systema. The Game Master has a 64 x 64 monochrome LCD screen capable of displaying graphics on par with the Atari 2600. The design was much like the Sega Game Gear with a D-Pad and 2 action buttons. The cartridges resemble those used by the Watara Supervision mainly that the card edge of the cartridge jutted out past the plastic of the cartridge. The Game Master utilizes a 40-pin cartridge port like the Supervision but is not compatible with Supervision games (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hartung_Game_Master).

