Go Retro Portable 260+ Games (older), Retro-Bit, 2018

Retro-Bit's 2018 retro handheld console features an approximately 3-inch LCD screen and comes with over 260 built-in games inspired by NES/Famicom titles (unofficial clones with slightly modified graphics and names to circumvent copyright restrictions). Its compact design resembles a modernized Game Boy Color, complete with a D-pad, A/B buttons, Start/Select buttons, and power options via AAA batteries or micro-USB. Some versions include composite video output for TVs and come with a hard-shell case. Aimed at casual or nostalgic users as an affordable device for simplified retro entertainment—this is not an officially licensed Nintendo console. It represents a typical entry-level solution in the retro clone market, perfect for occasional gaming experiences without the need for complex setups.

