Goupil G1, SMT, 1979

SMT Goupil (SMT for personal computer and telecommunications company) was a French company specialized in IT, founded in 1979 by Claude Perdrillat, previously a senior employee at the Directorate General of Telecommunications. During the 1980s, the company produced Goupil many computers, mainly to the French authorities. This market, largely provided to the company by the address book of its founder, collapses in the late 1980s with the emergence of drastic budget cuts in the French public sector more competitive and aggressive technological rivals. Its main competitors of the time are IBM, Apple and Olivetti (source, translated from the French: https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/SMT_Goupil).

