$info=gscpm
$mame
0.222 [Frank Palazzolo]

Simple CP/M Machine, Grant Searle, 201?

This project shows how it is possible to construct a Z80 computer running full CP/M 2.2 with disk storage using a minimal chip count. Source code and schematics are included to allow modifications if needed. Several commercial CP/M packages have been tried on this and they work perfectly. A large library of applications are available elsewhere on the web, and these can be loaded onto this machine using my own custom-made transfer software. Also included is a ROM version of BASIC to allow the machine to be programmed without CP/M. A LOT of work has gone into this project, as I have not only designed the hardware, but written the Boot ROM, BIOS, Formatting, System Transfer and File transfer programs. Also, many hours spent in making the ROM BASIC as clean as possible, with extended commands written by myself within it (source: http://searle.x10host.com/cpm/index.html).

