$info=h21
$mame
0.169 [Dirk Best]

Video Computer H-21, TRQ, 1982

Manufactured by Talleres Radioeléctricos Querol (TRQ), based in Vinarós (Spain), is currently engaged in the field of emergency lighting, ie the lights that light up when the power goes out. However, in the early 80s, they tried to get into the gaming world with a console clone of Interton VC-4000 that was very popular in Germany in the early nineties and our H21 TRQ was compatible. Its price was around the current 120 euros, ie 20,000 pesetas back in the 80s (ie a lot of money) and not known for certain whether featured games specific to it, saving copies of games like Space Invaders and PacMan (source, translated from spanish: http://www.retropia.es/posts/consolas-made-in-spain).

