Head to Head: Electronic Baseball, Coleco, 1980

This Coleco (Hartford, Connecticut) game was manufactured in Canada in 1980 and was donated to the Museum in 1982. It includes instructions in both English and French. This hand held electronic game is for two players - a pitcher and a batter - and is shaped somewhat like a baseball stadium. The plastic case is approximately 21.5cm long x 19.5cm wide x 7.3cm high, with a built in speaker. Battery doors accept two 9volt batteries (source: http://www.gamesmuseum.uwaterloo.ca/VirtualExhibits/electronic/handheld/sport/headto.html).

