HB-F1 (MSX2, Japan), Sony, 1986

This MSX 2 system, is basicaly a Sony HB-F1 with a 3?" disk drive built-in the case (2DD, 720 KB). The keyboard is quite complete with a numeric keypad and special keys. There is a hardware PAUSE-button which hangs the computer when pressed. The SPEED-CONTROLLER slider (slow-motion) and the REN-SHA-TURBO slider (auto-fire for both joysticks and spacebar) are nice features for playing games. Sadly this computer was only sold in Japan, so it's pretty hard to find one nowadays (source: http://www.old-computers.com/museum/computer.asp?st=1&c=773).

