0.81 [Jirou Kaneda]

HB-F1II (MSX2, Japan), Sony, 1987

Sony HB-F1II is a cost reduced version of the HB-F1 to better compete against the Panasonic FS-A1, while also adding a REN-SHA-TURBO slider (auto-fire for both joystick and spacebar). The Sony HB-F1II was available only in black. It was aimed at the Japanese market. The computer comes with an external power adapter, it includes a pause button that allows users to pause the system at will and a speed slider to slow down the' system. The Sony HB-F1II is a MSX2 with 2 cartridge slots (one at the top, one at the back). The CPU is a Z80A from NEC (uPD780C-1). A MSX-Engine from Yamaha (S1985) is used. The AC-HB3 power adapter specifications are the same as the Panasonic FS-AA51 adapter for the Panasonic FS-A1 and FS-A1mkII (source: https://www.msx.org/wiki/Sony_HB-F1II).

