$info=hbf900
$mame
0.81 [Jirou Kaneda]

HB-F900 (MSX2, Japan), Sony, 1986

The HB-F900 is a computer aimed at Japanese professional market. It can do superimposing with genlock signal (GENerator LOCK) via a specific video I/F connector on the back. This model is available in black (B) or in white (W) color. The separate keyboard (KBD-13 or KBD13(B)) comes either from the HB-F500 or the HB-T600 rather than a dedicated design. Sold with the MOS-1 mouse and the "Wordship" (Japanese wordprocessor) on floppy disk. The HB-F900 is a MSX2 with a Z80A from Sharp (LH0080A) or NEC (uPD780C) and an MSX-Engine S1985 from Yamaha. The optional AV creator HBI-F900 interface is needed to digitize images, create video effects and even edit video. The AV creator is only available in black (source: https://www.msx.org/wiki/Sony_HB-F900).

