$info=hc5
$mame
0.155 [Wilbert Pol]

HC-5 (MSX1, Japan), Victor, 1983

The first Victor computers were essentially rebranded Yamaha MSX machines without SFG music module. A superimposing adapter module (HC-A602S) was sold as an option. The HC-5 is available in two models: first version is the same as the CX5 or YIS-303 but with only 16kB RAM; second version is the same as the CX5F or YIS-503 but with only 16kB RAM. This machine was aimed at the Japanese market. The power supply is internal. The HC-5 supports all Yamaha modules. The optional superimposing adapter module has a RGB21 connector, mixed video output and audio volume regulator (source: https://www.msx.org/wiki/Victor_HC-5).

DRIVER:
msx/msx1.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Good
Color: Good
Sound: Good
