$info=hcd62121
$mame
0.149u1

Hitachi HCD62121, <unknown>, ????

DRIVER:
devices/cpu/hcd62121/hcd62121.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Good
Color: Good
Sound: Good
Graphics: Good
Save State: Unsupported

WIP:
- 0.274: Register recently added member variables for save states. Add missing save items (#13144) [QUFB].
- 0.273: Implemented timer register updates, fixed instruction 0xC5; casio/pickytlk.cpp: Added six systems [QUFB].
- 0.264: Improved emulation and fixed issues with debugger. Implemented additional move instructions and timer wait. Added an infinite timer variant, (seems to be used with the low power-variant of timer_wait). Fixed timer so that it expires on KO enabled key input. Fixed swap flags - they are always cleared regardless of values. Implemented more instructions tested on hardware. Implemented the TIME register. Fixed register accesses from the debugger [QUFB].
- 0.215: Implemented exclusive OR with indirect addressing. Used by cfx9850 for zoom menu in graph mode [Ricardo Barreira].
- 0.196: Renamed (hcd62121_cpu_device) to (hcd62121) and description changed to 'Hitachi HCD62121' [Angelo Salese].
- 0.192: Made improvements based on experiments with hardware using a CFX-9850G. Fixed mistakes in CL flag calculations, and added 'more unknown instructions. CFX-9850G is now emulated just accurately enough for most of the RUN mode to work well [Ricardo Barreira].
- 0.186: Renamed (hcd62121) to (hcd62121_cpu_device). Improved rotate and shift instructions; identified COM and PORT registers; fixed unidasm configuration [Wilbert Pol].
- 0.149u1: Added 'Hitachi HCD62121' device.

ROMSET:
None required.

$end
