$info=hd61830
$mame
0.143u3

Hitachi HD61830B LCD Controller, <unknown>, ????

DRIVER:
devices/video/hd61830.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Good
Color: Good
Sound: Good
Graphics: Good
Save State: Unsupported

WIP:
- 0.233: Fix cursor in d2 [cracyc]. Fixed character blink mode. When Cursor=Off and Blink=On, the controller is in "Character Blink" mode, according to the data sheet. This means that the character cell at the the position of the cursor is turned fully ON at a 50% blink duty cycle. Verified on a device with a real HD61830 (Atari Portfolio) [Jaen Saul].
- 0.213: Make number-of-characters command to round up to an even number [Nigel Barnes].
- 0.186: Changed description to 'Hitachi HD61830B LCD Controller'.
- 0.143u3: Added 'HD61830 LCDC' device.

ROMSET:
1472 bytes in 1 file / 0.68Kb packed

$end
$info=hd6301v1
$mame
0.150

Hitachi HD6301V1, <unknown>, ????

DRIVER:
devices/cpu/m6800/m6801.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Good
Color: Good
Sound: Good
Graphics: Good
Save State: Unsupported

WIP:
- 0.262: ST IMM opcodes cause a trap interrupt. Save more internal registers to NVRAM. RTI after TRAP returns to the address where the trap error occured. Port output latches are kept intact when in standby mode, x0 does not have ddr4. Instead of skip, zerofill NVRAM when no battery save. Fix timer 2 serial clock [hap].
- 0.261: Fix SLP wakeup from Tin input capture event [AJR].
- 0.220: Renamed (hd6301) to (hd6301v1) and description changed to 'Hitachi HD6301V1'.
- 0.196: Changed description to 'Hitachi HD6301' [Angelo Salese].
- 0.150: Added 'HD6301' device.

ROMSET:
None required.

$end
