$info=hec2hr
$mame
0.136 [JJ Stacino]

Hector 2HR, Micronique, 1983

The 2HR (HR for High Resolution) is the successor of the Victor / Hector 16k models, but this time is conception is entirely french. The machine has been completely redesigned and this new model is then more powerful. This is in fact a completely new machine with more memory and high-resolution. It is still compatible with the 16k models in a "model 1" mode choosen at the start-up menu (source: http://www.old-computers.com/museum/computer.asp?st=1&c=152).

