ROMSET:
4096 bytes in 1 file / 2.75Kb packed

$end
$info=hec2hrp
$mame
0.132 [JJ Stacino]

Hector 2HR+, Micronique, 1983

The Hector 2HR+ is a microcomputer brand Hector created by society and micro-released in 1985. It features an 8-bit Z80 processor. His ROM is 16 KB and it has 48 KB of RAM. Its display capabilities are 8x2 color 243x231 (half brightness) 40x23 text. Sound generator, generator 4 octaves of notes, transfer 1500 baud. It had a tape recorder integrated (source, traslated from french: http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hector_2HR%2B).

