Homelab 3, Jozsef and Endre Lukacs, 1983

The HomeLab computers family was conceived in the People's Republic of Hungary by the famous Lukács brothers. József Lukács, the older brother was the creator of the hardware, and the younger, Endre Lukács was the father of software (a great BASIC language). The HomeLab machines were cheap, well-working and easy-to-use Basic computers. They were neither clones nor licencied, but original Hungarian home computers (source: http://www.old-computers.com/museum/computer.asp?c=1095&st=1).

