HP 3478A Multimeter, HP, 1983

A digital multimeter (DMM) is a test tool used to measure two or more electrical values—principally voltage (volts), current (amps) and resistance (ohms). It is a standard diagnostic tool for technicians in the electrical/electronic industries. The Hewlett Packard 3478A unit is a digital multímeter capable of performing 5 different types of measurements: DC voltage, true RMS AC voltage, 2 and 4 wire resistance, and AC and DC current.

