0.142 [Gabriele D'Antona, F. Ulivi]

HP 9816, Hewlett Packard, 1982

The 9816 was introduced in late 1982. This was the low-cost model in the 200 Series range. It only had two expansion slots and featured a monitor integrated with the system unit and modular keyboard and mass storage (usually a 9121 dual 3.5 inch floppy drive). The monitor was nine inches diagonally with a 400 by 300 dot resolution. The 9816A came standard with 128K RAM. The 9816S came standard with 512K RAM. The 9816 family was also known as the 200 Series Model 16, 9000 Model 216 and 9000/216 (source: http://www.hpmuseum.net/display_item.php?hw=4).

