$info=hp9845b
$mame
0.154 [Curt Coder]

9845B, Hewlett-Packard, 1979

The 9845B was a revised version of the 9845A, announced first in the 9845B sales brochure from 1979 and introduced in the 1980 catalog. The 9845B was HP's top-selling System 45 model. It took a noticable part in HP's revenue of that time. Most of the 9845 systems which are still available today are 9845B models. The 9845B system architecture was the final system architecture for all 9845 systems. Modifications were from then on performed only to single assemblies and most important, the CRT display (source: https://www.hp9845.net/9845/hardware/9845b/).

