$info=hp9k310
$mame
0.158 [R. Belmont, Al Kossow]

HP9000/310, Hewlett-Packard, 1985

The model 310 was the first of the 300 Series computers. It featured a 10MHz 68010 CPU. The basic unit came with 1 MB of RAM and built-in HP-IB, RS-232, monochrome video and HP-HIL interfaces. Bundled versions of the Model 310 included Model 310C (98581A) and Model 310M (98580A). By the time the 310 was discontinued in early 1991, over 65,000 units had been sold (source: http://www.hpmuseum.net/display_item.php?hw=120).

