0.203 [Sven Schnelle]

HP9000/360, Hewlett-Packard, 1988

UNIX workstation system introduced in 1988, based on the Motorola 68020 processor and designed for professional environments that demand high performance in scientific, engineering, and business applications. It runs HP-UX, the proprietary operating system, and features a scalable architecture with support for extended memory, advanced graphics, and network peripherals. Characterized by robustness, stability, and software compatibility, it represented a reliable solution for technical offices and development centers in the late 1980s.

