$info=hr16
$mame
0.138 [Sandro Ronco]

HR-16, Alesis, 1987

Like most digital drum machines from the 90s, the HR-16 is great for circuit bending. However, it can be a bit unstable, even when unbent. Take a look at the service manual- it is a long list of repairs and upgrades. I wouldn't recommend it as a first bending project. If you get into bending HR-16s, you will most likely end up having 3 or 4 HR-16s in various stages of disrepair, scavenged for parts for your one working HR-16 (soruce: http://www.burnkit2600.com/hr-16/).

