$info=ht68k
$mame
0.136 [Miodrag Milanović]

TinyGiant HT68k, Hawthorne Technology, 1987

It's a neat single-board computer from the mid-1980's manufactured by Hawthorne Technologies. This SBC is in a 5-1/4" form factor so it could be bolted to a floppy drive. It's based on an 8MHz 68000 CPU and has a dual serial controller, 256k of RAM and a PC-compatible floppy controller. It came with a floppy-based operating system called K-OS and had an assembler, debugger and Forth language. The setup I got came complete with manuals and disks. The disks include a floppy-based operating system, Forth, a 68000 debugger and a text editor. The basic specs are: 68000 @ 8MHz, two serial ports, one Centronics parallel port, 128k of RAM (expandable to 512k), an expansion bus and a PC-compatible floppy controller enabling the use of 3?", 5?" or 8" drives (OS comes configured for 5?") all in a 5.75" x 8" size. The list price was $395 and it came with a ROM monitor, disk-based operating system, assembler and editor (source: http://www.classiccmp.org/cini/ht68k.htm).

