$info=hunter216
$mame
0.213 [Phill Harvey-Smith]

Husky Hunter 2/16, Husky Computers Ltd, 1990

An improved version of the earlier Hunter 16, launched in the mid-1980s. It retained the Z80 architecture and the CP/M operating system but offered greater memory capacity, a more legible LCD display, and often included a second 5.25-inch floppy drive for enhanced flexibility. Designed for mobile professionals in fields such as logistics, engineering, and administration, this device combined rugged durability, extended battery life, and compatibility with existing business applications, establishing itself as a reliable tool for data processing outside the office during the pre-laptop PC era.

