This machine was aimed at the Japanese market - see HX-20 series for the technical details. As for many machines with the "Pasopia IQ" label, the PSG sound output is stereo, with a switch at the back. An RS-232C interface with its switch can be added 'by soldering the connector on the power supply board, then adding the switch and the same RS-232C board from the HX-22. You also need to add a connector on the power supply board or solder the wires directly. A kit was sold for the HX-20 and HX-21 by Toshiba in Japan at the time. This is the HX-R701 kit. It can also be used on the HX-23, HX-23F and HX-32. The RGB output can also be added 'by soldering several components as on the video decoder board from the HX-21 or HX-22. Launch price for the computer: ?69,800 (source: https://www.msx.org/wiki/Toshiba_HX-20).

