$info=hx21
$mame
0.155 [Wilbert Pol]

HX-21 (MSX1, Japan), Toshiba, 1984

This machine was aimed at the Japanese market. As for many machines with the "Pasopia IQ" label, the PSG sound output is stereo, with a switch at the back. Although it's a MSX1 computer, it can use a part of the MSX memory to create a RAM-Disk or Memory Disk (feature generally reserved for computers with version 2.1 of MSX-BASIC). An RS-232C interface with its switch can be added 'by soldering the connector on the power supply board, then adding the switch and the same RS-232C board from the HX-22. You also need to add a connector on the power supply board or solder the wires directly. A kit was sold for the HX-20 and HX-21 by Toshiba in Japan at the time. This is the HX-R701 kit. It can also be used on the HX-23, HX-23F and HX-32. Launch price for the computer: ?79,800 (source: https://www.msx.org/wiki/Toshiba_HX-21).

