0.250 [openMSX]

HX-21F (MSX1, France), Toshiba, 1985

The Toshiba HX-21F is the adaptation for France of the HX-21 - see HX-21 series for the technical details. It has a QWERTY keyboard, just like the HX-10F. A specific RGB connector (Peritel) replaces the RF, composite video and audio connectors, but these can probably be added 'on the video decoder board. The PSG sound is mono instead of stereo. An RS-232C interface as like that of the HX-20 can be added 'if you replace the IC3 ROM by the one from the HX-22CH, HX-22GB or HX-22I (source: https://www.msx.org/wiki/Toshiba_HX-21F).

