$info=hyu16te
$mame
0.257 [sequoia]

Super 16 TE, Hyundai, 1987

An enhanced version of the Super 16 T, introduced in the late 1980s, it was based on a 12-MHz Intel 80286 processor and featured expanded expandability. It included a built-in floppy controller, hard-disk support, and often an optional VGA video card, as well as improved management of extended memory (XMS). Aimed primarily at the Korean market and small businesses, this model offered more robust performance and greater flexibility than the base model, while maintaining a favorable price-to-performance ratio among PC/AT clones of the era.

