$info=i386
$mame
0.150

Intel I386, <unknown>, ????

DRIVER:
devices/cpu/i386/i386.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Good
Color: Good
Sound: Good
Graphics: Good
Save State: Unsupported

WIP:
- 0.288: Add CPUID brand ID for Pentium 3 and 4 [Angelo Salese]. Migrated to SoftFloat 3 [Patrick Mackinlay].
- 0.287: Adjust cs for ppro+; fix SMM; fix softfloat with gcc 15 optimizer; include the 486; qword ptr also needs the fix; use the correct bits for dpl [cracyc].
- 0.283: Set cpl after all memory reads are done in i386_task_switch [cracyc].
- 0.280: Throw faults from i386_trap so double and triple faults can be handled properly [cracyc].
- 0.278: Check cpl in verr and verw. Check for fault before setting register [cracyc].
- 0.272: Make the sse opcodes generate the #NM exception used to save\restore the fpu state [yz70s].
- 0.268: Disable logging. Fix cycles when leaving rep when out of cycles and count == 0 fmtowns_cd: add note about microcosm [cracyc]. x87 stack top set to 0 when entering MMX state, generate #NM only from TS bit MMX opcodes generate #NM only when TS is set, EM bit generates #UD. Correct various mmx and sse opcodes in pentops.hxx Expecially for the case when the source and destination registers are the same Moved a couple cyrix routines together with the other ones. Correct errors in pentops.hxx caused by bad mmxprolog routine Currently the mmxprolog routine can raise a #NM exception. But the caller will execute the mmx opcode anyway, unfortunately by fetching the bytes from the first instruction in the exception service routine. This adds a bool return value to mmxprolog so the caller can return too without making a mess. Correct buggy fxsave and fxrstor opcodes and let chihiro show 3D again [yz70s].
- 0.264: Handle double and triple faults [cracyc].
- 0.262: Don't handle op/addr size prefixes twice in rep [cracyc]. In the CPU state view show the flags of the x87 status words and some of CR0 add constants for the bits in the CRx registers and start using them. Display cr0 and x87 status registers as before plus more usages for the crx bits constants [yz70s].
- 0.257: tzcnt fall back to bsf for 386 and 486 too [cracyc].
- 0.255: Use logmacro.h granular logging [Luigi30].
- 0.252: Don't change x87 stack pointer until after memory access in case of a page fault. nm fault if ts is set. Add fxsave and fxstor. Emms should trap too [cracyc].
- 0.242: Changed a couple of disassembler helpers to return std::string [Vas Crabb].
- 0.236: When DEBUG_MISSING_OPCODE is defined, log a small backtrace This way together with the full list of bytes that form the non recognized opcode there are the addresses of the previously executed instructions [yz70s].
- 0.221: Handle aliases for fstp st(i) instruction [Carl].
- 0.212: Added 'hardware breakpoint support [MoochMcGee].
- 0.210: Improved splitting of unaligned accesses (excluding program fetches) [AJR].
- 0.204: Signal a privilege change to the debugger when protected mode is enabled or disabled, or CS descriptor flags change [AJR].
- 0.201: Fixed a bug that could cause a common CPU detection check to misidentify a 386 as a 486 [MoochMcGee]. Added Athlon XP processor. Fixed XADD condition codes - should be based on result of addition. Added an enumeration describing CPUID feature information bits [Samuele Zannoli].
- 0.200: Fixed two cppcheck warnings [MoochMcGee].
- 0.196: Changed description to 'Intel I386' [Angelo Salese].
- 0.193: x87 bug fixes and FERR support [Andrey Merkulov].
- 0.184: Save state fixes for i386/pc_vga/cs4031: Save cs4031 emulated A20 state, additional i386 attribute registers/flags, and VGA palette configuration. Fixed broken VGA port reads on state load. Fixed enum range check in i386 [moralrecordings].
- 0.150: Added 'I386' device.

ROMSET:
None required.

$end
