0.259 [smj_crash]

ICM-3216, National Semiconductor, 1985

The ICM-3216 is a complete computer system contained on two 11.02 inch (300 mm) by 9.18 inch (233 mm) printed circuit boards. “This Integrated Computer Module will add the power of the Series 32000 processor chip set to National Semiconductor's line of board level microcomputer products. The CPU cluster, serial ports, printer port, SCSI interface and MiniBus Interface reside on the CPU unit. Memory resides on one printed circuit board which is the same size as the CPU unit. It provides one to eight megabytes of memory and interfaces to the CPU via alocal memory bus with no wait states at 10 MHz (source: original National Semiconductor brochure).

