Z80 SBC (prototype?), Insight Enterprises, 1983

Single-board computer based on the Zilog Z80 processor, manufactured by Insight Enterprises in the 1980s, likely in prototype form or for internal corporate use. This compact board integrates a Z80 CPU, minimal RAM/ROM memory, serial ports for communication, and connectors for bus expansion. It was designed for embedded development, hardware testing, and industrial control applications. The lack of extensive commercial documentation suggests limited production or exclusive OEM/prototype use aimed at enterprise customers—typical of development boards from that era, which were intended for engineers and businesses rather than the consumer market.

