$info=igor
$mame
0.265 [hap, Sean Riddle]

Igor (Excalibur), Excalibur Electronics, 1997

Excalibur Igor, a talking dedicated chess computer by Excalibur Electronics, released in 1997. The computer has a Hitachi H8/3214 controller running at 12 MHz with 32 KiB ROM and 1 KiB RAM, and features a press sensory board along with LCD, button panel and speaker. The Ron Nelson program was a continuation of his H8 programs in the Mirage, Ivan and Grandmaster line, also supported by chess consultant and opening book author Larry Kaufman (source: https://www.chessprogramming.org/Excalibur_Igor).

