$info=imds2
$mame
0.160 [F. Ulivi]

Intellec MDS-II, Intel, 1979

The Intellec Microcomputer Development Systems (MDS) were complete computers intended for the development of Intel microcomputer based products. They included a main unit with CPU, RAM, ROM, I/O and interrupt circuitry, as well as all necessary software: Assembler, linker, debugger. The Intellec MDS was launched in (about) 1975. It featured an 8080 processor and could implement MCS-80 (8080) based computers and Intel Series 3000 systems. The main unit needed a Serial video terminal or an ASR-33 Teletype to be connected, as well as a paper tape puncher/reader and/or floppy drive unit. Siemens sold in Germany a local version of the first Intellec called SME-800 (source: http://www.old-computers.com/museum/computer.asp?c=754&st=1).

