Informer 207/100, Informer Computer Terminals, 1983

Portable terminal manufactured by Informer Technologies in the 1980s for industrial and logistics applications. Based on a 4.77 MHz Intel 8088 processor with 256 KB of RAM, expandable up to 256 KB, featuring a monochromatic 4-line LCD display and an integrated numeric keypad. Designed for data collection in warehouses, inventory management, and point-of-sale environments, it includes RS-232 serial connectivity for synchronization with central systems. Powered by a rechargeable battery for mobile use, it comes with a rugged plastic housing that is impact-resistant. Primarily used in warehouse and retail settings before the advent of modern handheld computers, this device represents one of the earliest portable solutions for field data entry.

