$info=inmotion
$mame
0.282 [David Haywood, TeamEurope]

IN Motion - Motion Controlled Video Games Console (Hot Game 198 in 1), Grafix, 200?

It’s a plug-and-play console released in the 2000s, designed to connect to a television and controlled via a motion sensor. It features 198 preloaded games, primarily sports and action titles, where the player’s movements (gestures, body motions) are detected by an external device. The system uses a wireless controller or infrared sensor, with audio and video output via composite connection. Targeted at a family audience, it promotes an active, physical gaming experience, anticipating mainstream motion-control technology.

