Intelligent Chess, Intelligent Games / SciSys, 1980

Intelligent Chess, (SciSys Intelligent Chess) it's a dedicated chess computer and early forerunner of both chess database and chess display system based on a system called Tolinka by Barry Savage, a 2D Graphics Board displayed on a Television screen with flashing square features. Further, games along with audio commentaries could be stored and retrieved using an integrated Stereo audio cassette tape recorder. Intelligent Chess was developed by Philidor Software, and manufactured by SciSys for the associated Intelligent Games Ltd., forerunner of Intelligent Software, released in 1980 (source: https://www.chessprogramming.org/Intelligent_Chess).

