$info=inteladv
$mame
0.195 [R. Belmont, Sean Riddle, Team Europe, rfka01]

Intelligence Advance E/R (Germany), VTech, 2005

Educational computer for children, manufactured by VTech and primarily aimed at the German and Central European markets. This model belongs to the Intelligence Advance series and focuses on bilingual learning (German/English) through interactive games. It features a monochromatic LCD screen, a simplified QWERTZ keyboard with large, brightly colored keys, and a built-in speaker for audio feedback. The device offers educational activities in mathematics, spelling, logic, and vocabulary, presented in a game-based learning format. Powered by AA batteries for portability, it is designed for children aged 6 to 12, with content tailored to their respective school levels. The device comes in a sturdy, colorful plastic casing typical of VTech products from that era, featuring an ergonomic design suited for small hands and resistant to accidental impacts during everyday home use.

