$info=intelct2
$mame
0.288 [TeamEurope]

Intellectus 2 (France), Yeno, 199?

Yeno's children's educational computer, an evolution of the original Intellectus model. Features a colorful design with a built-in keyboard featuring large thematic keys, a monochrome or color LCD display (depending on the version), includes a mouse and stereo speakers. Based on PC-compatible hardware or embedded SoC, it runs educational activities in literacy, math, logic, music, and creativity, often featuring animated characters or child-friendly licensed content. Includes USB ports, memory card slots, and sometimes Wi-Fi connectivity. Powered by an external adapter. Designed for preschool and school-aged children (4–10 years) as a home edutainment tool, typical of the European approach to toy computers from the 2000s–2010s, which combines structured learning and family entertainment in a safe, self-contained format.

