$info=intlc8m80
$mame
0.275 [AJR]

intellec 8/Mod 80, Intel, 1974

The Intel Intellec 8/Mod 80 is a development and debugging system designed by Intel Corporation in the 1970s. It was part of the Intellec family, a series of tools used for the development and testing of systems based on Intel microprocessors, particularly the Intel 8080 microprocessor, one of the first widely used 8-bit processors. The Mod 80 was specifically dedicated to the development of systems based on the Intel 8080 processor and was used by engineers to write, test, and debug software or hardware for embedded applications, computers, and industrial devices.

