$info=iq502
$mame
0.184 [kazblox]

IQ-502, Micro Genius, 1992

Console Famiclone produced by TXC Corporation under the brand Micro Genius, marketed in the early 1990s primarily in Asia, the Middle East, and emerging markets. This version is compatible with NES/Famicom cartridges and features two wired controllers integrated into the compact chassis. It boasts an economical design with RF/composite video output for connection to a TV, powered by an external adapter. The console offered access to thousands of existing NES titles without any built-in games, providing a low-cost solution for markets where the official Nintendo presence was less established. Its construction is made of basic plastic, typical of clones from that era, with a focus on hardware compatibility rather than premium build quality.

