$info=irisha
$mame
0.128 [Miodrag Milanović]

Irisha, MGU, 1983

Electronic device for children produced by MGU (an Asian OEM brand specializing in electronic toys), model "Irisha." This is a mini portable console or toy tablet featuring a 2- to 3-inch LCD screen, brightly colored plastic design, and intended for preschool-aged children. It comes with simplified built-in games (2D platformers, puzzles, educational activities) running on low-cost hardware (typically unofficial ARM chipsets). Powered by AAA batteries or USB, it features large buttons that are easy for small hands to press. The device does not have official licenses: games feature generic graphics or are inspired by popular franchises but have been modified to avoid copyright infringement. The device is designed to provide an engaging and affordable play experience for young children while avoiding legal issues related to copyrighted content.

