$info=isa_ibm_speech
$mame
0.255 [Luigi30]

IBM PS/2 Speech Adapter, <unknown>, ????

The IBM PS/2 Speech Adapter is a sound card released by IBM similar to the IBM PCjr Speech Attachment. Instead of a PCjr sidecar, it is an ISA card which included a breakout box containing a built in speaker, volume control, headphone connectors, and a microphone input. Sound was produced by TI TMS5220C and Motorola MC3418L chips for LPC speech synthesis and CVSD sound (source: http://www.pixelatedarcade.com/tech_attributes/overview/ibm-ps-2-speech-adapter).

