$info=isa386u30
$mame
0.214 [rfka01]

ISA-386U30 REV.2.2, Asus, 199?

ASUS ISA-386U30 REV.2.2 motherboard for Intel 80386DX (32-bit) processors, manufactured circa 1989–1991. Industrial design featuring a 16-bit ISA slot for expansion, support for 30-pin SIMM modules for DRAM up to 16 MB, integrated floppy and IDE controllers, and onboard serial/parallel ports. Based on the Chips and Technologies chipset (82C301/82C302). Revision 2.2 included improvements in stability and compatibility compared to earlier versions. Typically used with MS-DOS, Windows 3.x, or OS/2 in entry-level workstations and business PCs from the pre-Pentium era. It represents a reliable solution for 386-based systems employing the ISA architecture prior to the adoption of the VLB/PCI slot.

DRIVER:
pc/at.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Preliminary
Color: Good
Sound: Good
Graphics: Imperfect
Save State: Unsupported

SOFTWARE LIST:
ibm5150.xml, ibm5170.xml, ibm5170_cdrom.xml, generic_cdrom.xml, ibm5170_hdd.xml, midi_flop.xml

RESOURCES:
Snap, Title and Marquee.

WIP:
- 0.214: rfka01 added 'Asus ISA-386U30 REV.2.2' system.

ROMSET:
65536 bytes in 1 file / 35.96Kb packed

$end
