iSBC 286, Intel, 19??

Single-board computer Intel based on the 80286 processor (16-bit), produced in the 1980s for embedded and industrial applications. It integrated the CPU, RAM/ROM memory, a controller for floppy disks/hard drives, serial/parallel ports, and expansion slots onto a single compact board. Widely used in industrial automation, control systems, instrumentation, and as a development platform for embedded software. It supported operating systems such as MS-DOS, CP/M-86, and proprietary real-time systems. Featuring a rugged design suited for industrial environments, it included standard connectors for integration into dedicated racks or cabinets. It represented a complete "all-in-one" solution prior to the advent of modern modular industrial PCs.

