$info=itt1700
$mame
0.203 [Al Kossow]

ITT 1700, ITT Courier, 1983

External ITT Courier model 1700 modem, manufactured by ITT Corporation in the 1980s–1990s for dial-up connections over analog telephone lines. Typical speed: 1200/2400 bps, using V.22/V.22bis protocols. Compact design housed in a gray metal chassis with an LED display indicating connection status; external power supply; RJ11 ports for the telephone line and RS-232 port for connecting to a computer. The modem included features such as automatic answering, tone/pulse dialing, and a buffer for reliable data transfers. It was widely used in business environments and BBS systems before the advent of faster modems (9600+ bps). It represented a dependable solution for data communications in the pre-commercial Internet era.

