The JAKKS Pacific Pronto Games 1 vs. 100 is an interactive electronic toy produced by JAKKS Pacific as part of its popular "Pronto Games" line, launched in the early 2000s. This device is inspired by the popular TV game show "1 vs. 100," originally broadcast internationally (as Eén tegen 100 in the Netherlands) and then adapted in the United States by NBC in 2006-2008, with presenters such as Bob Saget. The game is designed for a single player to answer multiple-choice questions, trying to mentally eliminate 100 "virtual opponents"-just as in the TV show-by answering the questions correctly while everyone else "gets it wrong."

