Disney (JAKKS Pacific TV Game) (SPG110 hardware, 28 MAY 2004 A), JAKKS Pacific Inc / HotGen Ltd, 2004

"JAKKS Pacific Inc / HotGen Ltd Disney (JAKKS Pacific TV Game) (SPG110 hardware, 28 MAY 2004 A)" is one of the most famous and widely distributed Plug & Play games developed by the British studio HotGen and marketed by JAKKS Pacific in 2004. The Mickey Mouse-themed Joystick: The device is an all-in-one controller shaped like a game joystick, featuring aesthetic details reminiscent of the Disney mascot. All the computing hardware is housed inside the casing. The heart of the device is a SunPlus SPG110 System-on-a-Chip (SoC). This 16-bit architecture was capable of simultaneously handling smooth 2D scrolling graphics, saturated color palettes (ideal for cartoons), and sound effects in advanced chiptune format.

