The JAKKS Pacific Handheld Games: High School Musical is a handheld electronic toy (handheld LCD) produced by JAKKS Pacific in 2007, coinciding with the extraordinary success of the first and second parts of the Disney Channel High School Musical franchise. It is designed for young fans of the series, especially preteen girls and boys, and combines elements of music, interactive play, and school/romantic themes in a simple and accessible format. It is not a console or PC video game, but a self-contained electronic device with a preinstalled game designed to be played on a small, fixed LCD screen (without backlighting, typical of handheld games of the era). Once turned on, the player enters an experience inspired by the world of East High, with characters such as Troy, Gabriella, Sharpay, Chad, and Taylor, and experiences mini-adventures related to the school, performances, and dancing.

