0.264 [Devin Acker]

Jaminator, Noise Toys Inc., 1990

The "Noise Toys Jaminator" (also known commercially as Jaminator: The Hi-Tech Guitar) is an innovative electronic musical instrument and standalone synthesizer shaped like a guitar, designed in 1990 by Noise Toys Inc. Conceived by renowned programmers and creatives Steve Capps (the well-known designer of Apple’s very first Macintosh interface), Ray DuFlon, and Ed Bogas, the Jaminator was initially distributed by the well-known tech toy company Worlds of Wonder (WOW), and was later marketed in the early 1990s by Yamaha on international markets. It is historically considered a direct and pioneering conceptual precursor to successful modern music video games such as Guitar Hero and Rock Band.

