Jyarajyaland (Japan, PlugIt! version), Takara / SSD Company LTD, 2003

Jara-Ja Land is another Japanese XaviX hardware game from Takara. This one is themed around Japanese redemption titles, and it is fair to say the presentation is through the roof here. You expect these Plug and Play units to generally be cheap throw-away affairs, but the level of detail to some of them defies that, animations here are just superb. This one currently doesn't have controls hooked up (I think it's some kind of analog dial input) but you can run the attract mode for 15 minutes until the machine decides to soft power-off due to inactivity (source: https://mamedev.emulab.it/haze/2020/04/09/under-the-surface-part-9/).

