The Casio Super Picky Talk - My Room Fantasy, released in 1996, is an educational electronic toy by Casio designed for preschool children. Part of the Super Picky series, known for voice interaction and learning activities, this model is themed around fantasy and bedroom play, featuring voices, sounds, and phrases (in Japanese, sometimes English) that guide children through recognition, music, and imaginative games. With colorful buttons and animated characters, it encourages language development, memory, and symbolic play. Designed with a soft, child-safe form, it is an early example of interactive electronic toys for young children in the pre-internet era.

