$info=jpaddp
$mame
0.286 [TeamEurope]

Jewel Pad Diamond Premium (Japan), Sega Toys, 201?

An educational tablet/toy manufactured by Sega Toys (the toy division of Sega Sammy Holdings), part of the "Jewel Pad" line designed for preschool and school-age girls. The "Diamond Premium" model is an advanced version with an elegant, jewelry-inspired design: a transparent/silver plastic chassis with glittery accents, edges decorated with diamond patterns, and a 4- to 5-inch LCD touchscreen. Based on Japanese girls’ franchises (likely linked to Sanrio’s Jewelpet or similar properties), it includes interactive activities such as drawing with virtual glitter, color/shape matching games, simple educational quizzes, and the creation of “precious” digital accessories. It features a built-in speaker for music and voice feedback, large colorful buttons, and battery or adapter power. Some versions support microSD cards for saving artistic creations. A play-based educational tool designed to develop creativity and hand-eye coordination, marketed primarily in Japan between 2015 and 2020 as a safe and simplified device for a first introduction to digital interaction.

