$info=jspodred
$mame
0.286 [TeamEurope]

Kouchuu Ouja Mushiking: Mushitori Battle Zukan (Japan), Sega Toys, 201?

Portable educational device produced by Sega Toys, based on the Mushiking (King of Beetles) franchise, which was popular in Japan from 2003 to 2010. "Mushitori Battle Zukan" (Encyclopedia of Beetle Battles) is a compact gadget featuring a monochromatic LCD screen and a reader for collectible cards. Children scanned physical cards—each bearing a QR code or chip—that depicted real beetles (such as stag beetles and rhinoceros beetles) to engage them in virtual battles or access encyclopedic information about them (species, habitat, size). The device included turn-based battle games, leaderboards, and a "capture" feature to expand the virtual collection. It boasted a sturdy design made of colorful plastic, powered by AAA batteries, and equipped with large buttons suited for children’s hands. Linked to the broader Mushiking ecosystem—including arcade machines in game centers, card trading, and manga/anime—it sparked interest in real entomology through play.

