$info=k1m
$mame
0.220 [DBWBP]

K1m Digital Multi-Dimensional Synthesizer Module, Kawai Musical Instrument Manufacturing, 1988

A variant of the popular K1 in a space-saving desktop form. The K1's were offered as a low-cost option for musicians to get the (back then) must-have Roland D-50 and Korg M1 sounds - The starting portion of a sound was sampled (very short, low-fi samples), and the remaining "bulk" of the waveform was supplied by standard digital waves. This was the new way of designing synthesizers in the late '80s and early '90s. The K1m is a great-sounding little synthesizer that can fill many roles even in a modern studio. From haunting pads, to '80s FM style bass, to "DigitalNativeDance-style" combis, the K1m delivers those types of sounds (source: https://www.synthmania.com/k1m.htm).

