$info=k1rii
$mame
0.220 [DBWBP]

K1rII Digital Multi-Dimensional Synthesizer Module, Kawai Musical Instrument Manufacturing, 1989

The Kawai K1rII rack-mount digital synthesizer module offers 16-voice (max.) polyphonic output from Kawai's VM additive synthesis tone generator. The K1rII built-in sound generator offers a selection of 256 basic waveforms using the two most advanced approaches to sound synthesis: 204 formed by the additive synthesis of the first 128 harmonics; 52 recorded with PCM sampling. You can freely mix up to four of these waveforms to produce an entirely new sound: a crisp digital sound, a rich analog sound, or any combination in between (source: https://encyclotronic.com/synthesizers/kawai/k1rii-r274/).

