K8915, Robotron, 1982

This calculator was manufactured by Robotron Zella-Mehlis and existed in 2 basic versions: the K8915-terminal or a PC. This will be discussed in more detail on the PC version. The proliferation of K8915 was not too great, and the computers were located mostly in industry and in agriculture. The K8915 was an 8-bit machine, which was constructed from components of the K1520' system. Due to the initial development as a terminal was built, the housing is very compact. The floppy drive has been placed next to the computer as a key module. There were also additional units that were equipped with a cassette drive, and contained units, the tape drive and floppy drive (source, traslated from german: http://www.robotrontechnik.de/index.htm?/html/computer/k8915.htm).

