$info=kaypro10
$mame
0.131 [Robbbert]

Kaypro 10 - 1983, Non-Linear Systems, 1983

Kaypro Corporation, commonly called Kaypro, was an American home/personal computer manufacturer of the 1980s. The company was founded by Non-Linear Systems to develop computers to compete with the then-popular Osborne 1 portable microcomputer. Kaypro produced a line of rugged, portable CP/M-based computers sold with an extensive software bundle which supplanted its competitors and quickly became one of the top selling personal computer lines of the early 1980s. The Kaypro 10 followed the Kaypro II, and featured a 10 megabyte hard drive and a single 5 1/4 floppy drive (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kaypro).

