Kaypro 4/84, Kaypro Corporation, 1984

This model of Kaypro, generally referred to as Kaypro 4 Kaypro IV '84 to distinguish it from the 1983, was presented in different versions: Kaypro 4: evolution of the old Kaypro IV, with higher clock used a Z80A (4 MHz Z80 2.5 against the Kaypro IV), had a display of superior quality that allowed you to use fonts with more definition (8x16 pixels against the 5x7 pixels of its predecessor), had an internal clock used by the programs, a comprehensive suite of programs (Wordstar, dBase II, Microplan, Microsoft Basic, S-Basic, SuperCalc, C-Basic as well, of course, the CP / M) (source, traslated from italian: http://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kaypro#I_computer_Kaypro).

