$info=kblades
$mame
0.188 [hap, Sean Riddle]

Blades of Steel (handheld), Konami, 1990

1989 LCD Handheld game which plays a game of Ice Hockey. LCD Electronic games became popular between 1980 and 1987. They use liquid crystal to display black graphics against a grey background, although many variations of this kind of display exist in both handheld and tabletop form, including clear screens, colour displays and multi-screen games. Nintendo may have set the benchmark with their legendary Game & Watch games, but there are 100s of other fantastic LCD games from the era just waiting to be discovered (source: https://www.retrogames.co.uk/039685/Handheld/Blades-of-Steel-by-Konami).

