$info=kc85_3
$mame
0.61 [Kevin Thacker]

KC 85/3, VEB Mikroelektronik "Wilhelm Pieck" Mühlhausen, 1987

The types KC85/2 and KC85/3 do not differ externally. Only within a few changes were made. Thus, in KC85/3 e.g. a BASIC interpreter built, which is loaded with the predecessor model KC85/2 only from cassette or module M006 had to be plugged. Through the integration of the interpreter was the user more memory available. The BASIC interpreter was extended to include some instructions and is broadly compatible with the KC85/2 (source, traslated from german: http://www.robotron-net.de/kc85xx.html#KC85/3).

