$info=kc85_4
$mame
0.61 [Kevin Thacker]

KC 85/4, VEB Mikroelektronik "Wilhelm Pieck" Mühlhausen, 1989

The KC85/4 was unveiled at the Leipzig trade fair in the spring of 1988. The body color is gray now and the keyboard connector with DIN socket replaces the previously used phone jack. The inner workings of the KC85/4 differed significantly from its predecessors. It was separated from the frame buffer memory, and increased to 64kB each, as is the ROM of the operating system, including the BASIC interpreter of 16kB (KC85/3), 20kB (KC85/4) (source, traslated from german: http://www.robotron-net.de/kc85xx.html#KC85/3).

