$info=kc85_5
$mame
0.132 [Kevin Thacker, Sandro Ronco]

KC 85/5, VEB Mikroelektronik "Wilhelm Pieck" Mühlhausen, 1989

The board of KC was 85 quarters prepared for production time already for the use of more powerful types of memory. The use of this memory was not realized, however, until the cessation of the series by the manufacturer. The built-in 64Kbit DRAM can be exchanged but slightly 256Kbit types. The CAOS and BASIC ROMs can be replaced with more advanced versions with larger types without the need for further changes are the original hardware. Such upgraded KC 85/4 is commonly depicted as KC 85/5 (source, traslated from german: http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kleincomputer_KC_85/2-4#KC.C2.A085.2F5).

