$info=kc87_20
$mame
0.133 [Miodrag Milanović, Robbbert]

KC 87.20, Robotron, 1987

For image output of the KC was connected via a 87 coaxial RF antenna connected to a TV. For exclusive use as a computer monitor were due to the low cost and compact size portable black and white TV sets distributed by the Russian type Junost far. In the basic version (KC 87.10, 87.20, and KC KC 87.30) offered the KC 87 only monochrome character display with white characters on black background. Alternatively, were also a color version of the device (KC 87.11, 87.21, and KC KC 87.31) as well as an upgrade option available for the basic version, which is a representation of eight foreground and background colors was possible. The connection to the TV required in this case, an RGB connection (source, traslated from german: http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kleincomputer_robotron_KC_87).

