$info=knd
$mame
0.233 [Sean Riddle, Kamaal Brown, David Haywood]

Codename: Kids Next Door - Operation: P.L.U.G.G.U.H.S., Tech2Go / One Man Band, 2005

The P.L.U.G.G.U.H.S. was a Codename: Kids Next Door plug-'n'-play game developed and distributed by Tech2Go. The product consisted of a controller and cables to plug into a TV. The game featured five missions, each playable with one member of Sector V. The game is a 2-dimensional side-scrolling shooting game with enemies shooting back at the player. Characters are able to jump, crouch and shoot to the left and the right. However, the characters cannot shoot while jumping or shoot upwards. Collecting gold candy replenishes life points. Defeat sends the player back to the mission select screen (source: https://knd.fandom.com/wiki/P.L.U.G.G.U.H.S.).

