0.278 [Antonio Malara]

Triton Music Workstation/Sampler (v2.5.3), Korg, 1999

The Korg Triton Music Workstation/Sampler (v2.5.3), released in 1999, is one of the most influential music workstations of the late 20th century. Combining a synthesizer, sampler, sequencer, and workstation in a single professional instrument, the v2.0.0 firmware update brought significant improvements, including an expanded sound library, enhanced sampling capabilities, and advanced editing and storage features. Widely used by producers, composers, and musicians in studios and live performances, the Triton is renowned for its rich sound quality, intuitive interface, and versatility across genres like pop, rock, jazz, and electronic music. It is a cornerstone of early 2000s music production.

