$info=kr03
$mame
0.140 [Miodrag Milanović]

KR-03, Elektronika, 1986

Electronics KR-02 and KR-03 is a standard 86RK Radio with 2 KB ROM and 16 KB of memory. The printed circuit board a little bit different from publication in the magazine "Radio", whereas in the scheme of significant changes have been made. The kit includes circuit board with components, power supply, keyboard block "Elektronika MS 7007" (completely analogous to that used in computer UKNC, differ only in the inscriptions on some keyboards). To support this keyboard to monitor changes have been made that might cause incompatibilities with some programs. The kit was not part of the PC case, but it was a metal chassis, to which were attached computer's motherboard and power supply and keyboard. On the set could be delivered either an external power supply transformer, or a small pulse to be installed in the chassis (source, traslated from russian: http://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%AD%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%82%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BA%D0%B0_%D0%9A%D0%A0-01/02/03/04).

