$info=las128e2
$mame
0.155 [R. Belmont]

Laser 128ex2 (version 6.1), Video Technology, 1988

The Laser 128 was a clone of the Apple II series of personal computers, first released by VTech in 1984. Unlike the Apple II clones from Franklin, VTech reverse-engineered the Apple ROMs using a clean room design rather than copying them. Apple Computer challenged VTech in court, but unlike its efforts directed at Franklin, Apple was unable to force the Laser 128 off the market. Apple countered the Laser 128 with its upgraded Apple IIc Plus. VTech responded with the Laser 128EX and the Laser EX2 (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laser_128).

