$info=laser_xt3
$mame
0.181 [Miodrag Milanović]

Laser XT/3, VTech, 1989

Computer home VTech Laser XT/3, the European/Spanish variant of the MSX2 standard produced by Video Technology in the late 1980s. Based on a 3.58 MHz Z80A processor with 128 KB of RAM, it features a built-in MSX engine—the Yamaha S-1985—and a Yamaha V9938 VDP for advanced MSX2 graphics (resolution up to 512×212, with 192 simultaneous colors). The system includes two cartridge slots, a built-in cassette port, RGB/composite/PAL video output for European monitors and TVs, and standard MSX joystick ports. It boasts a compact gray plastic design with an integrated membrane keyboard. Primarily aimed at the educational and home markets, it supports MSX-BASIC programming, advanced games, and productivity applications. This represents an OEM implementation of the MSX2 standard, with a focus on European software compatibility and affordable pricing in the Spanish and Portuguese markets.

