$info=lbpc
$mame
0.216 [Don Maslin Vintage Computer Archive]

Little Board/PC, Ampro Computers, 1989

Ampro described their Little Board as the world's simplest and least expensive CP/M computer. It is a complete, miniature single-board computer (SBC) optimized for compatibility with 5 1/4-inch mini-floppy disk drives. Ampro had taken advantage of the latest in semiconductor developements, incorporating all the essential elements of a CP/M computer on one tiny board - CPU, 64K RAM, boot EPROM, battery-backed clock, terminal port, modem port, printer port, and floppy disk controller (source: https://oldcomputers.net/ampro-little-board.html).

