$info=lchicken
$mame
0.183 [hap, Sean Riddle]

I Took a Lickin' From a Chicken, LJN Toys, 1980

I Took A Lickin' From A Chicken was a computerised game from back in the late 70s. It had 3 different modes - Tic-Tac-Toe, Simon, and Addition - but the Tic-Tac-Toe game was the best. You would compete against this little motorized plastic chicken that was housed under a clear plastic dome. When it was the chicken's turn, it would move from side to side as if scanning the game board to figure out his move, while uttering mechanical clucking noises. Then it would lurch forward with a loud cluck and its selection on the game board would become illuminated. If the chicken won the game it would caw loudly as if it was laughing at you. At the beginning of each game it would play a horrible midi rendition of "Old McDonald Had A Farm" (source: http://www.doyouremember.co.uk/memory/i-took-a-lickin-from-a-chicken).

