LeapPad, LeapFrog, 2001

The LeapPad is undoubtedly a product designed for children, it is immediately understood by the colorful and rounded design and by the particularly resistant plastic of which the body is made. The 5-inch screen has a fairly low resolution, but we are talking about a device from a couple of years ago, the brightness is still very good and the touch responds quite well. As for the software, we find many of the more than one hundred applications available preloaded on the device, even if some very interesting ones must be purchased separately and loaded using the appropriate cartridges. However, among the apps already installed there are several Disney programs, such as the Animation Studio, an application with which children can create their own personalized stories and enrich them with images taken directly from the device's camera (source, traslated from Italian: https://www.tabletperbambini.it/leapfrog-leappad-explorer-tablet/).

