$info=loewed
$mame
0.201 [Robbbert]

Multitel D, Loewe, 1992

Another Bildschirmtext terminal from late 1980s/early 1990s. Small, monochrome screen and keyboard are totally enough for device which is used to browse telephone pages. This terminal has also a handset to perform telephone functions. Contrary to Siemens Bitel units this one has no keylock, but has both serial port and printer port in some, Centronics-like format. Technically it's based on 8031 and 8052 microcontrollers with 64kB of dynamic RAM (source: http://oldcomputer.info/terminal/multitel_D/index.htm).

