$info=lviv
$mame
0.56.1 [Krzysztof Strzecha]

PK-01 Lviv, Lviv Polytechnical Institute, 1989

PK-01 Lvov (PK-01 Lviv) was a Soviet-Ukrainian 8-bit personal computer produced from 1986 to 1991. It had KR580VM80A 2.5-MHz microprocessor (a clone of the Intel 8080 CPU), 16-KB ROM, 64-KB RAM (including 16-KB of video memory with resolution of 256x256 pixels) and was able to display 4 colors from 8-color palette. It also had BASIC programming-language interpreter built-in (source: https://github.com/izhaks/PK01LvovEmulator).

