LW-30, Brother, 1991

Portable label printer Brother LW-30, manufactured in the early 2000s. Compact design with power options including AA batteries or an external adapter, a built-in QWERTY keyboard, and a monochrome LCD display. It uses thermal print ribbons in widths of 6/9/12 mm (TZe technology). Basic features include text formatting, frame creation, symbol insertion, and storage of recently used labels. Designed for office, school, and home use to create organizational labels, tags, and identification labels. Simple interface with no PC connectivity—all text is entered directly via the integrated keyboard. This model represents the entry-level offering in Brother’s P-touch series prior to the introduction of models with USB/Bluetooth connectivity.

