LW-350, Brother, 1995

Portable label printer Brother LW-350, a model from the P-touch series launched in the early 2000s. Compact design with power options including AA batteries or an external adapter, an integrated QWERTY keyboard, and a monochrome LCD display. It uses thermal print ribbons TZe in widths of 6/9/12 mm. Compared to the base model LW-30, it offers advanced features such as multi-label storage, additional text styles, decorative frames, pre-defined symbols, and automatic formatting for addresses or phone numbers. Designed for office, school, and home use to create organizational labels, tags, and professional identification labels. It features a standalone interface without PC connectivity—all text is entered directly via the built-in keyboard. This model represents an intermediate step in the P-touch lineup before the adoption of USB/Bluetooth connections in later models.

