0.262 [David Haywood]

Lexibook JG7420 - TV Game Console (200 Games, 32-bits), Lexibook, 201?

Console TV game plug-and-play Lexibook JG7420, marketed as an affordable device featuring "200 games." Compact design with wireless controller, composite/PAL video output for European TVs, and power supplied via an external adapter. The games are simplified variations of classic arcade, puzzle, and sports titles preloaded onto ROM chips—running on embedded 8- or 16-bit hardware that isn't truly 32-bit; the "32-bit" label is purely marketing-driven. Basic 2D graphics, mono audio, and repetitive gameplay. Intended for children aged 5–12 as an entry-level entertainment option for discount markets.

