0.286 [TeamEurope]

Lexibook JG7440 - TV Game Console (250 Games, 32-bits), Lexibook, 201?

Economic console TV game manufactured by Lexibook (a French brand specializing in educational devices for children), model JG7440. Compact device with 250 built-in games based on simplified 32-bit hardware (typically ARM chipsets or unofficial NES/SNES clones). Colorful plastic design with two wired controllers integrated into the chassis, composite video/HDMI output for TVs, and power supplied via an external adapter. The games are simplified variations of classic titles (platformers, puzzles, sports) featuring reduced 2D graphics and basic sampled audio. Does not include official licenses; the game titles feature slightly modified names to circumvent copyright restrictions. Intended for children and discount markets as entry-level casual entertainment, typical of the Asian OEM industry that manufactures for European brands.

