$info=lyon32t
$mame
0.218 [hap, anonymous]

Mephisto Lyon 68030, Hegener + Glaser, 1990

The Mephisto tournament machines (hereinafter referred to as TM) were custom-made and were mainly sold by Hobby Computer Centrale Munich on the occasion of the WMCCC Chess Micro World Cup between 1989 and 1992. The wooden housing was based on the proven ESB board. These special devices differed noticeably from the 32-bit "series modules" (Motorola 68020 with 12 MHz and 1 MB RAM), which calculated much slower than the TM. It is estimated that the TM in the "sales version" (Portorose - Vancouver 68030 with 36 MHz) sold between 25 and 50 devices to solvent customers from 1989 to 1992. The appropriate cooling was provided by two fans built into the device (source, traslated from German: https://www.schach-computer.info/wiki/index.php/Mephisto_Lyon_68030).

