$info=m240
$mame
0.142 [Carl]

M240, Olivetti, 1987

The Olivetti M240 was the successor M24. Was based on a microprocessor i8086 to 10MHz and out of series with the already XT bus (ISA 8bit), had 640KB RAM, the possibility of mounting on the internal controller also drives floppy disk high-density 1.2 and 1.44MB. He ran up to 4 floppy drive and could mount an internal hard disk drive and two external 5?". The keyboard was different from the M24 and not the mouse connector. The video card was for the first models an AT & T compatible CGA then rode a series of EGA. Could mount a drive for bus XT 8-bit 16-bit ISA. The M240 has 2 dip switches on the motherboard (each consisting of 8 microswitch) and 9 jumper (source, traslated from italian: http://informaticaitaliana.blogspot.it/2011/06/computer-olivetti-il-modello-m240.html).

