0.258 [Jo22]

M250E, Olivetti, 198?

In 1989, the Olivetti M250 was at the top of the low-end professional PC range offered by Olivetti. To meet the market needs of the time, this product used 8 MHz 80286 microprocessors, 1 MB RAM and hard disks with two different sizes: 20 MB and 40 MB. Furthermore, Olivetti added some particular innovations such as the compatible VGA graphics controller and quick access to the hard disk. The 16-bit architecture ensured power, speed and complete compatibility with the vast range of XT/AT expansion plates existing on the market (source, traslated from Italian: http://www.itmuseum.it/_App/museumDb/index.php?r=idMain/view&id=1004).

