Olivetti L1 M40, Olivetti, 1981

In 1982, Olivetti was able to announce Linea 1 (L1), based on the Zilog Z8001 microprocessor and the Cosmos IV operating system (trade name: MOS - Multifunctional Operating System), built internally. The development of an operating system for an integrated line of systems poses problems of particular complexity;  the success of the Cosmos project, entrusted to Alessandro Osnaghi, testifies to the maturity and competence achieved by Olivetti at that time also in software. Cosmos IV is developed in a short time and already at the third release (1985-86) it appears stabilized, reliable and with excellent performances (source, traslated from Italian: https://www.storiaolivetti.it/articolo/57-l1-una-nuova-linea-di-sistemi-informatici/).

