$info=m6502
$mame
0.149u1

MOS Technology 6502, <unknown>, ????

DRIVER:
devices/cpu/m6502/m6502.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Good
Color: Good
Sound: Good
Graphics: Good
Save State: Unsupported

WIP:
- 0.287: Modify SBC decimal adjust algorithm for 65C02, which differs from NMOS 6502 in edge cases. Allows 6502test.ssd (from mungre/beeb6502test repository) to pass test BCD-FC on bbcm [AJR]. Route core fetch/data/write paths through interruptible accesses (#15121): Add interruptible access regression test; narrow interruptible access follow-up [Stuart Inglis]. Small refactor to do_sbc_d to make it easier to see the difference between nmos/cmos [hap].
- 0.277: Like z80, around 10% performance gain by checking unset devcb on every opcode [hap].
- 0.274: Use conventional call stack for "SuperXaviX" [David Haywood].
- 0.258: Don't detect edge triggered inputs before the first clockcycle. Don't clear input pins external state at device_reset. Add 6503 CPU [hap].
- 0.256: Return to implicitly using read_arg to read operands at PC (fixes regression in all XaviX games). Side note: this changes the semantics of read_pc to what was formerly known as read_pc_noinc. Now that memory accesses themselves can be interrupted and restarted, updating PC as a side effect is obsolete anyway [AJR]. Make fully wait-states compatible [Olivier Galibert].
- 0.254: Added Yamaha GEW7- and GEW12-based keyboards [Devin Acker]. More this-> for templatey goodness. Template 6502 microcontroller helper on underlying CPU type [Vas Crabb].
- 0.248: Add the missing uses_custom_memory_interface. Avoid multiple instructions on one line for when reads at restartable [Olivier Galibert].
- 0.227: Added 'preliminary ST2205U DMA support [David Haywood].
- 0.222: Changed description to 'MOS Technology 6502'.
- 0.217: Added 'disassembler and basic execution core for Rockwell R65C19 [AJR].
- 0.214: Improved reset sequence emulation (fixes MT06486) [MoochMcGee, hap, smf].
- 0.202: Made SET instruction in Mitsubishi M740 subfamily actually affect execution (fixes MT07091) [AJR].
- 0.201: Added support for microcontrollers and implemented MOS 6500/1 as a device [Vas Crabb, Olivier Galibert].
- 0.196: Changed description to 'MOS Technology M6502' [Angelo Salese].
- 0.195: Fixed tracing and breakpoints for paged variants [Olivier Galibert].
- 0.149u1: Added 'M6502' device.

ROMSET:
None required.

$end
