$info=m6801
$mame
0.150

Motorola MC6801, <unknown>, ????

A microcontroller (or microcomputer) is a CPU, with additional on-board peripherals, usually containing RAM, ROM, and I/O as to serve as a single (or close to single) chip solution for a computer' system. As the program space is typically small, they were designed and used for high volume, low cost, simple applications. Today we would refer to them as embedded applications. The Motorola MC6800, released in 1974 was a decent 8-bit processor. It was however not inexpensive (a fact not lost upon one of its designers, Chuck Peddle, who left to design the 6502). Initial pricing for the MC6800 was $360, dropping to $175 the next year (source: http://www.cpushack.com/2016/08/19/cpu-of-the-day-motorola-mc6801-the-second-first-6800-mcu/).

DRIVER:
devices/cpu/m6800/m6801.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Good
Color: Good
Sound: Good
Graphics: Good
Save State: Unsupported

WIP:
- 0.278: Corrected the ICR read handlers (#13799) [m1macrophage].
- 0.265: Revert changes to serial emulation from a4cf1316fa003f73193c3010984a373015051e02 - not the correct solution, introduces time travel issue unfortunately. Fix new regression with eat_cycles [hap].
- 0.263: Add input ports ddr override mask [hap].
- 0.262: Port data latches are not initialized at reset. Mask unused RAM ctrl reg bits [hap].
- 0.261: Add support for canned NVRAM. Add standby pin. Save RAM control reg upper bits to 'nvram', psion: remove local implementation of m6801 standby pin and RAM control reg. Add setter for NVRAM battery status [hap]. Move RAM, ROM and I/O areas into internal maps for all variants (including a few that lacked their own device types until now). CPU device now saves NVRAM for applicable standby areas, which only include the first part of internal RAM on NMOS variants [AJR].
- 0.256: Remove i/o ports tri-state callback. Add i/o ports tri-state callback, misc: correct some typos [hap].
- 0.255: Fixed HD6303R to use an internal map, removed internal-only handlers from associated drivers [Ryan Holtz].
- 0.220: Fixed a bug that caused the emulation to lock up on WAI/SLP if a timed event had already occurred. Fixed disassembly of SLP instruction for HD6301. Added second timer output comparator and associated status register to HD6301X/HD6301Y [AJR].
- 0.215: Changed description to 'Motorola MC6801'. Added more logging and reduced unnecessary serial transmit output updates [Edstrom].
- 0.196: Changed description to 'Motorola M6801' [Angelo Salese].
- 0.150: Added 'M6801' device.

