Emulation: Good
Color: Good
Sound: Good
Graphics: Good
Save State: Unsupported

WIP:
- 0.278: BugFix09174 [Core] CPU Hitachi HD6309: Timing is incorrect for relative branches in HD6309 native mode [Peer]. Don't reset physical input pins state at device_reset [hap].
- 0.272: Revert speculative change. Remove fake SWI interrupt line, replacing interrupt callback with exception hook for debugging. Mask PCR-mode addresses in disassembly. Add interrupt vector read callback [AJR].
- 0.268: Added sync acknowledge callback [Sven Schnelle].
- 0.266: Fixed invalid escape sequence warnings [Vas Crabb].
- 0.263: Fixed HD6309 indirect W register references in indexed addressing modes [Tim Lindner].
- 0.258: Zerofill more variables at device start, 6840ptm: clear output ports at reset [hap].
- 0.255: Set V flag on undocumented XDEC instruction [Tim Lindner].
- 0.254: Emulated observed behavior of invalid instructions for MC6809 [Tim Lindner]. Read reset vector during execute_run rather than device_reset to facilitate bank switching of vectoro area [AJR].
- 0.252: Fixed HD6309 STBT instruction [Tim Lindner].
- 0.251: Improved emulation to TFR and EXG instructions [Tim Lindner]. Rename *.ops to *.lst [hap].
- 0.246: Simplify disassembly of pushes and pulls of both A and B [AJR].
- 0.245: Add support for stepping out [AJR].
- 0.222: Corrected illegal branch form for HD6309 family [Tim Lindner]. Made $10, $20 an illegal instruction on for the HD6309 family [Tim Lindner].
- 0.208: Disassembler fixes: Fixed program counter increment for indexed addressing with single-byte offset. Changed indexed addressing to print absolute addresses based on current program counter rather than offsets. Added explicit EXT addressing annotation for small offsets. Renamed "indirect" to "indexed" in code [tomctomc].
- 0.201: Improved disassembly. Use FCB directive to represent illegal opcodes, don't print spaces after instructions without operands [AJR].
- 0.196: Changed description to 'MC6809 (legacy)' [Angelo Salese].
- 0.194: Fixed disassembly of relative instructions [AJR].
- 0.193: Started resolving the great MC6809/MC6809E device type/clock divider mix-up [AJR].
- 0.149u1: Added 'M6809' device.

ROMSET:
None required.

$end
