M8120, Motorola, 1991

The M8120 is a nice little shoebox-sized computer build 1991 by Motorola. The case is just big enough to offer the space for the board, optional memory expansions and the power supply. The used CPU is a Motorola 88100, member of the 88k family, clocked at 25MHz. If you take a close look, the mainboard is actually a VME board and a ?raiser card? which offers one SCSI, one network and six serial connectors to the outside world (source: https://www.geekdot.com/m8120/).

