M82 Game Selectable Working Product Display, Nintendo, 1986

The Nintendo M82 is a demonstration unit for the Nintendo Entertainment System to allow customers to try games in-store before purchasing them. The full title on the machine was the M82 Game Selectable Working Product Display. The machine was fundamentally different from the more arcade orientated PlayChoice, because it used consumer NES carts instead of proprietary ROM chips (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nintendo_M82).

