$info=mac3
$mame
0.278 [Nigel Barnes]

Mac III 6502 Microcomputer, L.J.Technical Systems, 1990

The L.J. Technical Systems Mac III 6502 Microcomputer is an educational computing system developed by L.J. Technical Systems, a British company specialized in producing kits and didactic systems for teaching electronics and computer science in schools and technical institutions, particularly in the 1980s. Despite its name suggesting a connection with Apple, it has no relation to the Macintosh. Here, the term "Mac" is likely an acronym or an internal commercial name (possibly from "Microcomputer" or "Machine"), while "III" indicates a system version. The heart of the device is the MOS 6502 microprocessor, the same one used in iconic computers like the Apple II, Commodore 64, BBC Micro, and Nintendo Entertainment System (NES).

