$info=mac512k
$mame
0.115 [R. Belmont]

Macintosh 512k, Apple Computer, 1984

The Macintosh 512K Personal Computer, also known as the "Fat Mac," is the second of a long line of Apple Macintosh computers, and was the first update to the original Macintosh 128K. It was virtually identical to the previous Mac, differing primarily in the amount of built-in memory (RAM), which quadrupled the original's. This large increase earned it the nickname Fat Mac. The additional memory was significant because more ambitious users with computer experience stretched the capacity of the original Mac almost immediately, despite the limited number of applications (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macintosh_512K).

