Macintosh LC II, Apple Computer, 1991

The LC II was a slightly less crippled version of the LC. Still running a 32-bit CPU on a 16-bit data bus and limited by design to no more than 10 MB of RAM, at least the 68030 offered virtual memory and works with RAM Doubler (the LC II is slower than the Mac IIx, even though both use the same 16 MHz 68030 CPU) (source: http://lowendmac.com/lc/macintosh-lc-ii.html).

