Macintosh LC/Performa 475, Apple Computer, 1993

The Macintosh LC 475 was an entry-level 68LC040-based system from Apple Computer. Code-named "Aladdin" or "Primus", it was released on October 21, 1993 as part of the LC series for the educational market and discontinued on July 15, 1996. Its counterparts were the business-oriented Macintosh Quadra 605 and consumer-oriented Performa 475 (source: https://apple.fandom.com/wiki/Macintosh_LC_475).

