Macintosh LC/Performa 575, Apple Computer, 1994

The Macintosh LC 575 was a personal computer from Apple's LC line of computers. It was available from February 2, 1994 until April 3, 1995. It was superseded by the LC 580, which looks very similar, but uses a lower cost display and a re-engineered logic board. A PowerPC 601 upgrade for it was marketed from November 3, 1994 to March 2, 1996 (source: https://apple.fandom.com/wiki/Macintosh_LC_575).

