Macintosh PowerBook 140, Apple Computer, 1991

The PowerBook 140 was released in the first line of PowerBooks. It was the mid-range PowerBook, between the low-end 100 and the high-end 170. As with the PowerBook 170, and unlike the 100, this PowerBook featured an internal floppy drive. Codenames for this model are: Tim Lite, Tim LC, Replacements, and Leary. In 1992, it was replaced by the PowerBook 140, which was essentially a speed bump, though the PowerBook 160 essentially superseded it as the new mid-line model (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PowerBook_140).

