0.143u1 [R. Belmont]

Macintosh PowerBook 145B, Apple Computer, 1993

The PowerBook 145B was a laptop made by Apple Computer. The PowerBook 145B was the same as the PowerBook 140#PowerBook 145 that came before it, but with a lower price and additional 2 MiB of RAM soldered to the motherboard. The only codename for this model is Pikes Peak. Unlike previous Mac models but like the Performas, the 145B did not ship with a full set of system disks. System 7.1 was preinstalled on the internal hard disk, and a single system start-up disk was included. The package also included two utilities that provide basic backup and restore functions. The 145 was superseded by the PowerBook 150 as the next low end PowerBook (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PowerBook_145#PowerBook_145).

