Macintosh Quadra 630, Apple Computer, 1994

The Macintosh Quadra 630 was the last model of Apple Computer's Quadra series of Macintosh systems. It was released on July 18, 1994, replacing the Quadra 610, although the PowerPC-based Power Macintosh line had already been introduced a few months earlier in March. Two reasons were cited for this: One, the older 68040 processors were less expensive; and two, PowerPC-native software was not yet as widely available (source: https://apple.fandom.com/wiki/Macintosh_Quadra_630).

