$info=mathmarv
$mame
0.174 [hap, Sean Riddle]

Math Marvel, Texas Instruments, 1980

This educational toy for youngsters is similar to the futuristic DataMan. The Math Marvel is preprogrammed to teach the basic four mathematic functions through different games. A nice feature of this game is an added 'buzzer to give some noisy feedback. From a technical point of view the toy is in one line with the TI-45 scientific calculator introduced in 1978. Both share a member of the TMS1980 single chip calculator series based on the TMS1000 family (source: http://www.datamath.org/Edu/MathMarvel.htm).

