$info=mato
$mame
0.81 [Krzysztof Strzecha]

Mato, Statny, 1985

The Mato was an 8-bit personal computer produced in the former Czechoslovakia by Štátny majetok Závadka š.p., Závadka nad Hronom. Their primary goal was to produce a personal computer as cheaply as possible, and therefore it was also sold as a self-assembly kit. It was basically modified PMD 85, but without backward compatibility. This, combined with its late arrival to the market, made the MATO a commercial failure (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MA%C5%A4O).

