$info=maxxi
$mame
0.164 [Felipe Corrêa da Silva Sanches]

Maxxi, Polymax, 1982

Due to the success in the US market, many Brazilian manufacturers tried to produce equipment compatible with Apple, allowing the use of one of the largest application software libraries available on the international market. Being equipment that was a long time in the North American market and that initially faced little competition, Apple had developed programs for it in several areas, from leisure to more sophisticated applications such as artificial intelligence. The Maxxi was one of the first national microcomputer compatible with Apple (Apple II and Apple II Plus). It was manufactured by Polymax, a company based in Porto Alegre that manufactured also micros larger, for commercial applications. The Maxxi was considered a home PC or personal use for enterprise applications as a tool and decision support (source, traslated form Portoguese: http://www.cobit.xpg.com.br/micros/maxxi.htm).

