$info=mb1320
$mame
0.286 [The Retro Web]

MB-1320/25C-B.5 (SCATsx chipset), Biostar, 1990

Motherboard Biostar MB-1320/25C-B, based on the SCATsx chipset (SIS 471 + 472), was manufactured in the mid-1990s for Intel Pentium processors running at 60/66 MHz (Socket 5/7). It features an industrial design with a 16-bit ISA slot, support for 30-pin SIMM modules for DRAM up to 128 MB, integrated floppy/IDE controller, and onboard serial and parallel ports. Power supply is AT type (P8/P9 connector). This motherboard was typical of entry-level workstations and corporate PCs from the Windows 95/NT 3.51 era. The SCATsx chipset offered modest performance, featuring a 32-bit data bus and limited support for external L2 cache. It represents an economical solution from the pre-PCI mainstream era, prior to the widespread adoption of the ATX architecture.

