$info=mb87030
$mame
0.203

Fujitsu MB87030 SCSI controller, <unknown>, ????

DRIVER:
devices/machine/mb87030.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Good
Color: Good
Sound: Good
Graphics: Good
Save State: Unsupported

WIP:
- 0.288: Several bugfixes and a massive speedup: DREQ was not always dropping at the end of a SCSI transaction. This was causing data to get blasted to DMA before the chip was set up in some cases; the transfer counter could underflow when SCMD_TERM_MODE was in use; SCMD_RST_OUT wasn't actually resetting anything; several delays were checked against the datasheet and found to be off by an order of magnitude. This was making SCSI-1 perform like floppy disks; mpc2000xl and mpc3000 now have fully working SCSI. Both machines can format a disk, save and load data, and read CD-ROMs error-free. Previously they were struggling to even select a SCSI target, let alone send commands; additional testing: partitioned and formatted a hard disk on x68000 and I was able to load and run utilities from HDD on fz20m [R. Belmont].
- 0.284: Added a BSY line callback suitable for drive LEDs [R. Belmont]. Correct the behaviour when a transfer size 0 is requested [Olivier Galibert].
- 0.263: Fix some bit definitions for the SCMD register [Patrick Mackinlay]
- 0.262: Logging improvements [AJR].
- 0.255: Make DMA transfers go through DREG rather than separate single buffer [AJR].
- 0.254: Improve arbitration/selection handling. Fix hp98265a diagnostic error [Patrick Mackinlay].
- 0.205: Fixed FIFO behaviour (fixes SCSI on HP9000/382) [Sven Schnelle].
- 0.204: Implemented padding mode (allows Pascal 3.24 to boot and run from SCSI on hp9k_3xx) [Sven Schnelle].
- 0.203: Added 'Fujitsu MB87030 SCSI controller' device. Converted to use delegate timers. Emulated Fujitsu MB87030 SCSI controller [Sven Schnelle].

$end
