$info=mbc16lt
$mame
0.219 [rfka01]

MBC-16LT, Sanyo, 198?

Released in late 80s this computer was known as very light, and indeed its weight is smaller than similar Toshiba T1200 or Bondwell units. It has Intel 80C88 CPU and 640kB of RAM, two 720kB floppy disk drives and no expansion capabilities except "expansion connector" not soldered to mainboard. Its non-backlit LCD has only 80x25 text mode compatible with MDA (monochrome graphics card). It was a bit cheaper than similar units of known brands (source: http://oldcomputer.info/portables/sanyo/index.htm).

