$info=mbc200
$mame
0.144 [Matt Dawson, Angelo Salese, Miodrag Milanović]

MBC-200, Sanyo, 1982

Machine MBC-1200 is identicaly but sold outside of Japan. The MBC-200 is a 8-bit CP/M machine intended for business market. They were the first Sanyo business machines to have graphics capability. They feature a high-resolution 640 X 400 dot matrix for graphic displays or a 40 line X 80 character text mode. The auxiliary CPU ensures high speed execution of graphics, while the detachable ergonomic keyboard and coiled cable enhance ease of use (soruce: http://www.old-computers.com/museum/computer.asp?st=1&c=1180).

