2011 Super HiK 105 in 1 Turbo Edition, <unknown>, 200?

An affordable TV game marketed around 2011, this compact device features 105 built-in games based on simplified hardware compatible with NES/Famicom titles. It has a plastic design with two wired controllers integrated into the chassis, composite/RF video output for connecting to a TV, and power supplied via an external adapter. The games are simplified variations of classic 8-bit titles, with reduced graphics and audio compared to the originals.

