$info=mc1200
$mame
0.192 [Robbbert]

MC-1200, Milwaukee Computers, 1980

This is a rectilinear box with solid wood side, perforated metal top, metal bottom, back, and part of front, and front panel with two 5.25" floppy drives. The back has a power switch, a fuse, 3 female DB 25 connects (2 vertical on the right with 8 position knobless rotary switches above each), one horizontal on top center, a D-shell female amphenon connector at the bottom, and a small black push button above a vertical DB-25 connector. There is a label on the right with lettering "MC-1000 SERIES COMPUTER" above the serial number, and "MC-1200" on a DYMO label affixed at the bottom (source: https://www.computerhistory.org/collections/catalog/102757262).

