0.288 [Nigel Barnes]

MC 218, Ericsson, 2000

The Ericsson MC 218 is a handheld device (Mobile Companion) launched in 1999, developed in collaboration with Psion. It is essentially a rebranded Psion 5mx, featuring a full QWERTY keyboard, a flip-up screen, and running on the EPOC operating system (the predecessor to Symbian). Designed for mobile communication, the MC 218 served as a digital assistant and, via infrared modem and cable, connected to Ericsson cell phones of the time (such as the i888) to browse the web, send emails, faxes, and text messages.

DRIVER:
psion/psion5mx.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Preliminary
Color: Good
Sound: Good
Graphics: Good
Save State: Supported

SOFTWARE LIST:
-

RESOURCES:
No resources available.

WIP:
- 0.288: Nigel Barnes added 'Ericsson MC 218' system.

ROMSET:
25165824 bytes in 2 files / 9.55Mb packed

$end
