$info=mc600
$mame
0.283 [Nigel Barnes, anonymous]

MC 600, Psion, 1990

1990 handheld computer with a built-in QWERTY keyboard, a high-resolution monochrome LCD screen, and the SIBO (EPOC16) operating system. Designed for professional users, it offers integrated applications such as a word processor, spreadsheet, calendar, and database, with support for expansion cards for memory and serial communication.

