$info=mcc1
$mame
0.285 [DBWBP, Edward d-tech]

MCC-1 MIDI Control Computer, Dynacord, 1986

MIDI control device released by Dynacord in 1986, designed to manage complex musical setups in recording studios and live performance venues. It functioned as a smart patchbay with one MIDI input, four independent outputs, and a thru port for advanced signal routing. The device enabled automatic program switching across multiple sound modules simultaneously, simplifying the management of extensive sound libraries during performances. Built in Germany with Dynacord’s characteristic rugged durability, it became an essential tool for electronic musicians of the era in organizing multi-device MIDI configurations before the advent of modern software sequencers.

