$info=mcm_roc
$mame
0.278 [Lord Nightmare]

Miuchiz Monsterz Roc, MGA Entertainment, 2006

The MGA Entertainment Miuchiz Monsterz Roc, launched in 2006, is an interactive electronic toy produced by MGA Entertainment, the American company known for franchises like Bratz, L.O.L. Surprise!, and Rainbow High. It is part of the Miuchiz Monsterz line, a sub-series within the popular Miuchiz family, which also includes Miuchiz Pawz (virtual animals) and Miuchiz Cutiez. Unlike the cute puppies of the Pawz series, the Miuchiz Monsterz are inspired by friendly and stylized monsters with eccentric designs, fluorescent colors, and "rebellious" or "rock" personalities, aimed at attracting girls and pre-teenagers who enjoy a bolder, punk, or alternative style. The name "Roc" (a play on "Rock") refers to one of the characters in the series, designed to embody a rock, energetic, and tough identity, in line with the trendy and youthful aesthetic that MGA was promoting at the time.

