Minicom IV (2002-04-19), Ultratec, 2002

This basic TTY is affordable and easy to use. It has an easy-touch keyboard with a bright, tilted 20-character display for hours of comfortable use. Minicom IV includes a printer port to connect an external printer. Turbo Code lets you enjoy "real-time" conversations with other Turbo Code TTYs. Auto ID lets everyone you call know you are using a TTY. Available options include an extended warranty, a dust cover and a soft carrying case. For basic communication features in a reliable TTY, Minicom IV is right for you (source: http://www.ultratec.com/ttys/non-printing/minicom.php).

DRIVER:
ultratec/minicom.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Preliminary
Color: Good
Sound: Preliminary
Graphics: Imperfect
Save State: Unsupported

SOFTWARE LIST:
-

RESOURCES:
Snap, Title, Icon and machine picture (in "Cabinet" collection).

WIP:
- 0.162: Felipe Corrêa da Silva Sanches added 'Ultratec Minicom IV (2002-04-19)' system.

ROMSET:
8192 bytes in 1 file / 5.49Kb packed

$end
$info=mcompgin
$mame
0.171 [hap, Kevin Horton]

Computer Gin, Mattel Electronics, 1979

Apparently only a fair rendition of the card game. There are things you can do in real Gin that aren't implemented in this handheld game. Mattel had designed a Computer Gin II to come out the following year that played Gin more or less perfectly, but it was never released (source: http://www.handheldmuseum.com/Mattel/Gin.htm).

DRIVER:
handheld/hh_ucom4.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Good
