$info=md2
$mame
0.136 [Miodrag Milanović]

Micro Decision MD-2, Morrow Designs, 1982

The Morrow Micro Decision is a solidly designed single-board Z-80 microcomputer. Although it looks something like an IBM PC clone (the IBM PC had been released more than a year earlier), it's actually a CP/M machine that requires an external serial terminal (which was generally sold as a bundle) (source: http://www.computercloset.org/MorrowMicroDecisionMD-2.htm).

