$info=md4duv
$mame
0.288 [bitsavers]

MD-4DUV (UMC UM8498F & UM8496 chipset), Aquarius Systems/Bcom Technology, 1994

AT motherboard for Intel 80286 processors (16 MHz), manufactured by Aquarius Systems/Bcom Technology in the early 1990s. Based on the UMC UM8498F chipset (memory/cache controller) and UM8496 (system chipset), it supports up to 16 MB of RAM, features 16-bit ISA slots, and includes integrated floppy and IDE controllers. It comes equipped with an RTC clock, serial/parallel ports, and an AT keyboard connector. The industrial design incorporates jumpers for CPU and memory configuration. Intended for embedded systems or budget workstations from the DOS/OS-2 era, this board represents a IBM PC AT-compatible clone built around UMC components—known for their reliability but with limited market penetration compared to mainstream brands.

