$info=md6802
$mame
0.170 [Joakim Larsson Edström]

Mikrodator 6802, Didact AB, 1983

Didact Laromedelsproduktion was started in Linkoping in Sweden by Anders Andersson, Arne Kullbjer and Lars Bjorklund. They constructed a series of microcomputers for educational purposes such as "Mikrodator 6802", Esselte 100 and the Candela computer for the swedish schools to educate the students in assembly programming and BASIC for electro mechanical applications such as stepper motors, simple process control, buttons and LED:s. Didact designs were marketed by Esselte Studium to the swedish schools. The Candela computer was designed to be the big breakthough and was based on OS9 but lost the battle of the swedish schools to the Compis computer by TeleNova which was based on CP/M initially but later both lost to IBM PC (source: MAME driver).

DRIVER:
skeleton/didact.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Good
Color: Good
