$info=mega10k
$mame
0.269 [hap, Sean Riddle]

Mega 10.000: L'Encyclopédie Électronique, Jeux Nathan, 1980

Portable educational console "Jeux Nathan Mega 10,000: The Electronic Encyclopedia," produced by Nathan (Editis Group) for the French market in the 2000s. Book-shaped design featuring a monochromatic LCD screen, an alphanumeric keypad, and navigation buttons. It contains over 10,000 questions and pieces of information organized into school-related categories (science, history, geography, language, mathematics), with interactive quiz modes, educational games, and a text-based mini-encyclopedia. Battery-powered, intended for children aged 8–14 as a playful learning tool and for reviewing school material. It has no external connectivity or expansion capabilities—all content is integrated into the ROM. This device represents a typical example of pre-smartphone European educational consoles, focused on curriculum-based content and independent educational entertainment.

