$info=mekd4
$mame
0.214 [68bit]

MEK6802D4, Motorola, 1980

Development board for the Motorola MC6802 microprocessor, released in the early 1980s as part of the MEK6800D4 system. It includes an MC6802 CPU with 128 bytes of internal RAM and a 1 MHz clock, a resident ROM monitor for basic debugging, parallel and serial I/O ports, connectors for bus expansion, and external power supply. Designed for engineers and hobbyists to learn the 6800 architecture, develop firmware, and test embedded circuits. Used with a serial keyboard and video terminal; programming is performed in assembly language via the integrated monitor. This board represents a key educational tool in the pre-microcontroller era for systems based on the Motorola 6800 family.

