$info=mentor16
$mame
0.263 [hap, Berger]

Mentor 16, Novag Industries / Intelligent Heuristic Programming, 1989

The Mentor 16 was launched by Novag in 1989; the programmer is the "usual" David Kittinger. It is a tabletop sensory chessboard (27.3 x 27.5 x 2.8 cm) equipped with an 8 Mhz processor, 16 Kbytes of ROM and 256 bytes of RAM. An opening library of 8000 half-moves is provided. There are 48 game levels available, and the playing strength (Aktiv list) is 1537 ELO points (source, translated from Italian: https://museoscacchi.wordpress.com/2011/02/19/novag-mentor-16/).

