0.282 [Berger]

Mephisto (set 1), Hegener + Glaser, 1980

It is a dedicated chess computer released in 1980, designed for serious players and amateur competitions. Based on an 8-bit microprocessor, it offers multiple difficulty levels, position analysis, an opening book, and an LED display for move visualization. Integrated into a compact design with a mechanical keyboard and physical chessboard, it uses an advanced game engine for its time, establishing itself as one of the first commercial systems capable of challenging intermediate-level players with precision and reliability.

