$info=mephisto1x
$mame
0.219 [Berger, blitzchess.fr]

Mephisto 1X, Hegener + Glaser, 1981

The Hegener + Glaser Mephisto 1X is an electronic device dedicated to the game of chess, produced by the German company Hegener + Glaser AG, known for developing a long series of portable and tabletop chess computers in the 1980s and 1990s. The Mephisto series is one of the most famous brands in the chess computer scene at the time. The designation "1X" seems to indicate an entry-level version or a particular edition of the basic model within the Mephisto range, although it is not an extremely well-known model like the "Mephisto Berlin" or the "Mephisto MM II," which were based on very strong chess software (such as the Rebel or Kramer engines ).

