$info=mephisto2b
$mame
0.268 [Berger]

Mephisto II (set 3), Hegener + Glaser, 1981

The successor to Mephisto, Mephisto II, was released at the end of 1982. The program was based on the experimental version that triumphed at the MCCT (Second Stockholm Micro Computer Chess Tournament) in Stockholm in 1980 and at the CPWTIPC (Chess Programs World Tournament in Personal Computers) in Paris in 1981. The playing strength could be increased and the opening library also became much more extensive with ~300 variations. The first version of the Mephisto II ran at 3.5 MHz. From September 1982, the Mephisto II (original with basic unit I, 1802 with 3.5 MHz) was upgraded with higher-quality components (basic unit II, 1802 with 6.1 MHz), without the model name changing (source, traslated from Geraman: https://www.schach-computer.info/wiki/index.php/Mephisto_II).

