0.268 [hap, Berger]

Mephisto ESB II (ESB II board), Hegener + Glaser, 1981

ESB II was the name given to the program module for the Mephisto II basic device, which made it possible to control the ESB II, ESB 3000 and ESB 6000 magnetic sensor boards. The first version corresponds mainly to the Mephisto II program with the opening library increased from 300 to 350 variants and was launched at the same time as the simple Mephisto II basic unit at Christmas 1981. Like the Mephisto II, it ran with a 3.5 MHz base unit. With the introduction of the 6.1 MHz base units (Briquette), a new ESB IIb module was launched, which runs in the ESB 3000/6000 boards. The software of this module is said to be improved once again, especially the playback behavior. This version can also be found in the later Mirage module (source, traslated from German: https://www.schach-computer.info/wiki/index.php/Mephisto_ESB_II).

