0.144u5 [Miodrag Milanović]

Meritum I (Model 2) (network), Mera-Elzab, 1985

The Meritum was a Polish home computer esteemed as the forerunner of the Polish computer industry and the first home computer produced in Poland. Nevertheless, the machine was really a clone of the TRS-80 Model I (with a Polish BASIC Level II version in ROM). Mera-Elzab made two versions of Meritum and a third was announced and exhibited in a computer fair in 1986, but was never produced (vapourware). The Meritum I was launched in 1983, with 16 KB of RAM, text mode of 32x16 lines, and semi-graphic (32x16, 64x16 or 128x48 pixels); monochromatic display and limited expansion capabilities (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mera-Elzab_Meritum#Meritum_I).

