$info=microkorg
$mame
0.223 [DBWBP]

microKORG Synthesizer/Vocoder, Korg, 2002

The microKORG contains the same DSP synthesis as Korg's MS2000B (2 oscillators), but offers many more waveforms. For Oscillator 1,71 waveforms are available: including analog classics like sawtooth, pulse, sinus and noise, but also new things like Vox Wave and Cross Wave. This would create a great deal of variation, but you can also modulate these waveforms in depth. In addition you have 64 unique DWGS waveforms, the classic Korg DW8000, so that the microKorg is also suitable as an imitator. This produces bells, pianos, guitars, basses, etc., which are difficult to simulate with analog waveforms. With the additional use of Oscillator 2 you can also synchronize and use (source, traslated from Italian: https://www.amazon.it/Korg-MICROKORG-microkorg/dp/B0000WS0SC).

DRIVER:
korg/microkorg.cpp

