Micron, Tangerine, 1980

The Microtan 65 was a 6502 based single board microcomputer which could be expanded into what later became the ORIC, ATMOS and later computers. The basis of all these highly integrated machines can be seen in the Microtan, and although the detail of the I/O addressing varies between the M65 and the ORIC etc, the fundamental method of keyboard addressing, tape I/O (source: https://web.archive.org/web/20081024034120/http://oric.ifrance.com/microtan_hardware.txt).

