The PAiA midi2cv8 is an interface device designed by PAiA Electronics, a US company renowned for its DIY (Do-It-Yourself) electronic kits and modular musical instruments. The midi2cv8 is specifically designed to convert MIDI signals to analog control voltage (CV) and gate/trigger voltages, enabling the integration of modern MIDI devices with analog modular or semi-modular synthesizers. This device is especially useful for musicians and synthesis enthusiasts who want to combine modern digital technologies with contemporary vintage analog or modular systems.

