$info=midifex
$mame
0.282 [m1macrophage, Peter Pearson]

MIDIFEX, Alesis, 1986

A stereo digital effects unit designed for musicians and home recording studios. It offers 63 preset configurations of delays, reverbs, and doubling effects, all controllable via MIDI for real-time program switching. Housed in a half-rack (1U) chassis, it features stereo RCA inputs/outputs, a Mix control, and MIDI In/Thru ports. Characterized by a simple interface and affordable price, it combines professional-quality effects with an intuitive design, inspired by the success of the contemporary Alesis Midiverb. Valued for its versatility in enhancing vocal tracks, drum machines, and MIDI instruments, it became a classic of the analog-digital era.

