MiniB Computer, Sprow, 2002

The MiniB is a complete 6502 based microcomputer, measuring just 3.5"x3.1", with all the resources on board to implement a compact controller finding applications in burglar alarm systems/embedded control/and other such places. Where possible it has been designed with more modern, easy to obtain, surface mount components offering not only considerable space savings but cost savings too. Architecturally the microcomputer is based heavily on the BBC Microcomputer series, and indeed a lot of software which will run on a BBC micro will also run on MiniB - including the original unmodified BASIC language (source: http://www.sprow.co.uk/bbc/minib.htm).

