Minitel 2 NFZ 400, Philips, 1989

Minitel terminals basically consisted of four parts: Keyboard, monitor (in black and white with eight shades of gray or in color, with eight colors), modem for standard communication ( ASCII standard) and motherboard. France Telecom imposed minimum quality and functionality requirements that manufacturing companies (Philips, Matra, Alcatel) had to meet. As a result of this policy, different terminals that met the requirements were put on the market. One of them was the Philips Minitel 2 that had the possibility of putting a password and had a directory of ten numbers (source, traslated from French: https://retroordenadoresorty.blogspot.com/2016/04/terminal-philips-minitel-2-france.html?m=1).

