$info=mk1forth
$mame
0.230 [AJR]

Mark 1 FORTH Computer, Andrew Holme, 2003

This computer has no microprocessor. The CPU is discrete TTL logic. I bought my first TTL data book in 1979. I was learning 6502 machine code at the time and dreamt of building a simple TTL CPU. I sketched some circuit ideas; but that was as far as it went. Now, 25 years later, I've finally done it! Working evenings and weekends, the Mark 1 took a month to design, 4 months to build and a month to program (source: http://www.aholme.co.uk/Mk1/Architecture.htm).

