0.140 [Ralf Schaefer]

Mephisto MM II (set 1, v4.00), Hegener + Glaser, 1985

A dedicated chess computer module for Mephisto module systems by Hegener & Glaser launched in 1985 with a Plymate based program by Ulf Rathsman. The Mephisto MM II ran on a 65C02 CPU at 3.7 MHz inside a 32 KiB ROM using 4 KiB of RAM. Based on the MM II, the Mephisto B&P (Blitz- and Problemsolving) appeared in the same year (source: https://www.chessprogramming.org/Mephisto_MM_II).

