0.282 [mickihamster]

Mephisto MM II (set 7), Hegener + Glaser, 1985

It is a dedicated chess computer released in 1985, designed for advanced players and competitive play. Based on an 8-bit microprocessor with an accelerated clock, it offers multiple difficulty levels, deep analysis, an extensive opening book, and an LED display for move visualization. Integrated into a compact design with a physical chessboard and pressure sensors, it employs a powerful game engine for its time, capable of challenging expert players with precision and sophisticated strategy.

