$info=mm5
$mame
0.119 [Dirk Verwiebe, Cowering]

Mephisto MM V (v5.1), Hegener + Glaser, 1990

In 1990, the Mephisto MM V program appeared on the market and is still one of the most popular modules! There are several reasons: Firstly, it is the last module of Hegener and Glaser, which can also be operated in the mobile and thus Mephisto "pocket-portable" is. Secondly, it is because of his playing style. But the program itself has other undeniable qualities: failed the narrow opening repertoire for which a circumference of 8000 half moves is specified. But at least all transpositions are detected. To compensate you can access opening to the HG 550 module that expands the scope of nearly 20,000 half moves, but in the mobile / slot can not be operated (source, traslated from German: http://www.schach-computer.info/wiki/index.php/Mephisto_MM_V).

