$info=mm6
$mame
0.288 [hap, Berger, Mr. Lars]

Mephisto MM VI, Saitek, 1996

Portable electronic chessboard Saitek Mephisto MM VI, part of the renowned Mephisto series designed for serious players. Compact design features a physical chessboard with capacitive sensors, an alphanumeric LCD display, and a keypad for advanced input. Powered by an 8/16-bit processor with optimized chess firmware, it offers deep analysis, an opening library, tournament mode, adjustable difficulty levels, and educational features. Operates on battery power or an external adapter. It does not include voice synthesis or graphics—the interface is text-based. Intended for clubs, amateur tournaments, and intermediate to advanced enthusiasts as a reliable tool for independent study and practice, it represents the pinnacle of pre-computer modern chess hardware, focused on precision and performance without connectivity.

DRIVER:
hegenerglaser/mm6.cpp

