MicroMainFrame 9000 (Sweden/Finland), Commodore Business Machines, 1981

This was a computer professional of the Commodore, was marketed in Europe by this name (Micro MainFrame 9000) while in America was known as SuperPET. I bought it in 1996 for 2,000 pounds (yes, there is an error, two thousand pounds) from a former Commodore service center who wanted to reduce inventory from the point of view because the administrative cost was too high. Then, along with two friends, I spent some hours in this store to choose what to take away / not to overdo it though / with a fixed price of 2,000 lire each. We found a cartridge, some devices, and MMF 9000 to head (source, traslated from italian: http://www.vecchicomputer.com/2008/01/commodore-mmf-9000-superpet-9000/).

