$info=mpc200sp
$mame
0.155 [Wilbert Pol]

MPC-200SP (MSX1, Spain), Sanyo, 1985

Computer MSX1 Sanyo MPC-200SP, the Spanish/European version of the MPC-200 produced in 1985. Based on the MSX engine Toshiba T7775 (a Z80A-compatible processor running at 3.58 MHz) with 64 KB of RAM, expandable up to 256 KB. It uses the Toshiba T6950 VDP for standard MSX graphics, features two cartridge slots, a cassette port for storage, and a video output for TV or monitor (PAL 50Hz). Its compact white plastic design is typical of MSX home computers from that era. Intended for the Spanish and European educational and domestic markets for BASIC programming, games, and productivity applications. It represents one of Sanyo's early OEM MSX1 implementations before the transition to the MSX2 standard.

