0.218 [Marc Capdeville]

Microprofessor II, Multitech, 1982

I bought my Microprofessor II (MPF-II) at a local flea market in Singapore in 2000 for S$10 not knowing whether it still works or not. Of course some keys on the keyboard are a little sticky but functional after some pounding. The casing had sustained some minor damage, discoloration and the video color output doesn't show up too well either. This little gem actually has 64K of ram, 16K rom, 1 expansion slot, printer port, external keyboard port, AV and RF out and the cassette in and out ports. Read the review here. Having owned a Apple][+ clone (Base-64A) and a Apple //e computer, I have to set things right with this petite computer (source: http://mpf-ii.blogspot.com/).

