0.279 [David Haywood, TeamEurope]

Mission: Paintball, Hasbro / Tiger Electronics, 2004

This is a video game for television consoles, launched in 2004, inspired by the theme of paintball and set within a tactical mission context. The gameplay combines arcade-style action and adventure, featuring shooting mechanics and movement across scrolling or third-person environments. Designed for a young audience, the title stands out for its dynamic gaming experience, centered around challenges, objectives to complete, and progression through various missions. With graphics typical of the era and an accessible approach, it delivers immediate fun and role-playing elements inspired by the adrenaline-fueled excitement of paintball—all packaged in a format perfectly suited for home consoles from the early 2000s.

