MPS-1000 Printer, Commodore Business Machines, 1986

The MPS-1000, released in the mid-80's, was born into a new era. The CBM Serial port was no longer king, and dot-matrix quality was getting old. Into that was the MPS-1000 born. Commodores first CBM Serial AND Centronics printer (so that Amiga and Commodore 8-bit computers could use it). This printer also featured bi-directional printing, as well as an NLQ (Near Letter Quality) mode (source: http://www.zimmers.net/cbmpics/plserial.html).

