0.136 [Curt Coder]

Victory MPT-02 Home TV Programmer (Austria), Soundic, 1978

The Soundic Victory MPT-02 is a clone of one of the first home videogame systems, the RCA Studio II. In opposition to the Studio II, the Victory MPT-02 has detachable controllers. Those controllers are composed of 10 buttons labeled from 0 to 9. More surprising, the Victory MPT-02 is the only Studio II clone system to offer alternative joysticks: real ones, with a stick and a fire button. More practical for action games (source: http://www.old-computers.com/museum/computer.asp?st=2&c=1221).

