$info=mpx16
$mame
0.214 [rfka01]

MPX-16, Micromint, 198?

Single-board computer Micromint MPX-16, based on a 4.77 MHz Intel 8088 processor, produced in the early 1980s. Its architecture is not fully compatible with the IBM PC but can run MS-DOS 1.25 and software written in 8088 assembly language. It includes ISA-compatible expansion slots, a base RAM capacity of 64 KB that is expandable, and onboard serial and parallel ports. The modular design targets hobbyists, educators, and embedded developers for prototyping and learning about the x86 architecture. Detailed documentation was published in technical magazines of the era to facilitate do-it-yourself assembly. This computer represents one of Micromint's earliest ventures into the microcomputer market before its eventual specialization in industrial embedded systems.

