$info=msx_cart_video80
$mame
0.277 [F. Ulivi]

MSX Cartridge - VIDEO80, <unknown>, ????

The MSX Cartridge VIDEO80 is a type of cartridge for MSX computers, a standardized home computer system launched in the 1980s, mainly in Europe, Japan, and South America. This particular cartridge is not a program or game, but an optional hardware device that allows an MSX computer to display 80 columns of text (instead of the standard 40 columns) on CRT screens. This feature was very important for professional applications such as word processors, spreadsheets, and more advanced programming environments.

DRIVER:
devices/bus/msx/cart/video80.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Good
Color: Good
Sound: Good
Graphics: Good
Save State: Unsupported

WIP:
- 0.277: F. Ulivi added 'MSX Cartridge - VIDEO80' device.

ROMSET:
None required.

$end
