$info=mt440
$mame
0.263 [Bitsavers]

Micro-Term 440, Micro-Term, 1986

Comp-Sultants’ Micro 440 might have been first 4040-based kit. An entry-level system for hobbyists, its processor had only a 4-bit word length, as opposed to the Intel 8080 8-bit length, so the system was limited even by the day’s standards. Partial kits were sold, so it’s possible to find Micro 440 components in other home-made systems. Having very limited capabilities, Micro 440 had a tuff time competing agains other "more powerfull" 8-bit systems (source: https://oldcomputermuseum.com/micro-440.html#).

