$info=mu15
$mame
0.263 [Matt, Olivier Galibert]

MU15, Yamaha, 1998

Internally, the MU15 is identical to the older MU10XG and MU50, with 16‑part multitimbrality, 32‑voice polyphony, General MIDI and Yamaha's extended GM (XG) compatibility. The GM/XG sound set, using Yamaha's established AWM2 (Advanced Wave Memory) technology, provides 480 sounds and 11 drum kits. Some of the instrumental voices are made up of two 'elements' and use up more of the available polyphony. Three onboard effects processors are available: two global processors provide reverb and modulation effects, while the third 'Variation' processor can be configured as an 'insert' effect, applied to one part, or as an extra global effect (source: https://www.soundonsound.com/reviews/yamaha-mu15).

