0.270 [buffi]

MU90B, Yamaha, 2005

Yamaha MU90B is a sound module designed for use in music production. It is a multi-timbral, 16-voice polyphonic synthesizer with a wide range of sounds and effects. It has been used by many professional musicians, producers, and composers, including the likes of Daft Punk, Skrillex, and Deadmau5. The MU90B features a variety of sound sources, including samples, waveforms, and virtual analog synthesis. It also has a built-in sequencer, arpeggiator, and effects processor. It has a wide range of parameters that can be adjusted to create unique sounds and textures. Additionally, it has a USB port for connecting to a computer and a MIDI interface for connecting to other MIDI-compatible devices (https://synthpedia.net/yamaha/mu90b/).

