ADDS Multivision, Applied Digital Data Systems, 1981

The Multivision offered superior raster graphics capabilities compared to the standard alphanumeric terminals of the time, with a resolution of up to 512×512 monochromatic pixels. It was used in CAD applications, scientific data visualization, and industrial automation. It featured an RS-232 serial connection to mainframes/minicomputers (VAX, PDP-11). The display included a 14- to 19-inch CRT with an optional optical pen for direct interaction. It represented a professional solution prior to the advent of modern graphic workstations—a typical example from the pre-PC era for specialized technical visualization.

