$info=mvme147
$mame
0.174 [Joakim Larsson Edström]

Motorola MVME147, <unknown>, ????

The MVME147, a single-board computer (SBC), was the first system from Motorola to implement a 68030 CPU. The MVME147 itself is a single-height 6U VME board. This board was equipped with most of the I/O needed for full computer functionality, including RS232, Ethernet and SCSI. The external I/O was implemented via the P2-VME connector at the back of the board which became standard in the following MVME1x7 CPU boards. Several breakouts were available, Motorola's 712 boards were the most widely used ones. The MVME147 boards and also clones were popular and widely used. The board configuration and component will vary depending on the generation (source: http://www.m88k.com/mvme147.html).

