0.139 [Angelo Salese]

MZ-2000, Sharp, 1982

Another strange MZ family member. At the moment, we have no information about it. It seems to be a "super MZ 80B" (that's what the badge says, anyway), but we are not sure it was compatible with it. To our knowledge, the MZ-2000 was never regularly exported outside Japan. A "16 Bit Bord Kit" was sold in April 1983 to expand the 8-bit computer to a 16-bit' system. Price: $327 (source: http://www.old-computers.com/museum/computer.asp?st=1&c=415).

