$info=mz5500
$mame
0.279 [Anna Wu]

MZ-5500, Sharp, 1984

This is a high-end personal computer produced in the late 1980s, part of Sharp's MZ series. Featuring a 16-bit architecture, it included a built-in floppy disk drive and a monochrome monitor, designed for advanced professional and home use. The machine supported programming languages such as BASIC and CP/M, and was particularly praised for its graphics capabilities and text-processing features compared to contemporary home computers. With its compact yet robust design, it offered a versatile solution for office work, academic study, and technical applications, standing out for its reliability and seamless hardware-software integration.

