0.279 [sharpmz.org, Anna Wu]

MZ-6550, Sharp, 1985

This is a personal computer from the late 1980s, part of a series designed for both advanced home and professional use. Featuring an integrated design with a monochrome LCD monitor and built-in floppy disk drive, it delivers solid performance for its time thanks to a 16-bit architecture. It supports operating environments like CP/M-68K and programming languages such as BASIC, making it suitable for document management, software development, and technical applications. Designed for reliability and efficiency, it combines compactness with ergonomics, offering a versatile solution for office and academic use.

