$info=n8810m15
$mame
0.210 [rfka01]

8810 M15, Nixdorf Computer AG, 1987

Business computer system produced by Nixdorf Computer AG in the early 1980s. A compact desktop computer based on the Zilog Z80 processor, part of the 8800 series introduced in 1979–1980. The M15 represented a specific configuration featuring an integrated monochrome CRT display (typically green or amber), a dedicated keyboard, and a 5.25-inch floppy disk drive for storage. Designed for office automation applications—word processing, file management, and light accounting—in European business environments (especially Germany). It ran the proprietary Nixdorf BS2000/BCS operating system with a text-based menu interface. Characterized by a distinctive design with a dark gray metal-plastic chassis and an ergonomic layout optimized for extended use in office settings. It represented an all-in-one integrated solution prior to the advent of standardized IBM-compatible PCs.

