0.132 [Miodrag Milanović]

NANOS, Ingenieurhochschule fur Seefahrt Warnemunde/Wustrow, 1985

The Engineering College of Maritime Affairs in Warnemünde developed along with several other companies about 1985 a platinum record and power supplies for an 8-bit computer system, which leaned on the K1520 system and plug side compatible with him. Compared to the K1520 boards the NANOS boards had only half the height. K1520 in the usual link bus system was omitted, and if necessary implemented individually on separate jacks (source, traslated from german: http://www.robotrontechnik.de/index.htm?/html/standorte/fh-warnemuende.htm).

DRIVER:
ddr/nanos.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Preliminary
Color: Good
Sound: Preliminary
Graphics: Good
Save State: Supported

SOFTWARE LIST:
-

RESOURCES:
Snap, Title, Icon, machine picture (in "Cabinet" collection) and PCB.

WIP
- 0.132: Miodrag Milanović added skeleton driver of 'Ingenieurhochschule fur Seefahrt Warnemunde/Wustrow NANOS' system.

ROMSET:
4480 bytes in 3 files / 2.67Kb packed

$end
