The NC200, was the last model of the NC series which was comprised of the NC 100 and NC 150. The NC200, appeared in late 1993, featuring a 3?" floppy disk drive able to read/write MS-DOS-formatted double density disks, 128 KB RAM, some extra software / most notably a spreadsheet and three Tetris-like games / and a larger, backlit screen. However, this change required much greater power use, using 5 C cell batteries. The disk drive could only be used at near full-charge, which meant that it could only be used a few hours after putting in new batteries. However, the laptop could function for considerably longer than this without using the disk drive (source: http://www.computinghistory.org.uk/det/18431/Amstrad-NC200/).

