$info=ncd19c
$mame
0.218 [Don Maslin Archive]

19c, Network Computing Devices, 1991

The NCD19c uses 72 pin, 80 nS fast-page-mode SIMMs. The SIMMs *must* be fast-page-mode SIMMs. In the NCD19c, space in the Video RAMs is broken up into 1024 segments of 768 bytes each. Each scan line in the NCD19c is 2048 bytes long, but only 1280 bytes are used for display. The remaining 768 bytes after each displayed scan line can be used by the server. A 36 bit SIMM can not be use in the NCD19c, because this generates additional heat and because the 36-bit SIMMs also have 50% more DRAMs on the SIMM (24 instead of 16), causing the loading on the address and clock lines to go up by 50%. At this increased loading, we cannot guarantee that the critical timings are met (source: http://bio.gsi.de/DOCS/NCDWARE/ftp.ncd.com/pub/ncd/Archive/NCD-Articles/NCD_X_Terminals/Memory_specs/NCD_88k_family_memory_specs).

