$info=ndpbj
$mame
0.275 [David Haywood, TeamEurope]

Dontore da bei - Donbei-kun to Training (Japan), Nissin / SSD Company LTD, 2007

The "SSD Dontore da bei - Donbei-kun to Training" is an electronic educational device produced by the Japanese company SSD (Silicon Sound Design) . This product is part of a series of interactive toys designed for children's learning and enjoyment, with a special focus on music education. The name "Donbei-kun" refers to the device's main character, who serves as a virtual mascot to guide children through various activities. The device combines playful and educational elements, using music and rhythm as the main tools to engage young users. It is particularly suitable for preschool or school-age children who are learning the fundamentals of music, motor coordination, and creativity.

