0.279 [David Haywood, TeamEurope]

Dontore da bei 2 - Ouchi de, Minna de Fitness! (Japan), Nissin / SSD Company LTD, 2008

This is a home console video game designed for fitness and family-friendly physical activity, featuring a playful and inclusive approach. Through a series of guided exercises and workouts, the game encourages players to move, dance, and work out by following the on-screen movements. Designed for both solo and group play at home, it combines upbeat music, mini-games, and motivational feedback to make exercise fun and accessible for all ages. With a strong emphasis on social interaction and overall well-being, it serves as a gamification tool for physical activity—typical of Japanese titles focused on active, lifestyle-oriented experiences.

