$info=nectk85
$mame
0.148u1 [Robbbert, Nama]

TK-85, NEC, 1980

The NEC TK-85 was a 8085 CPU based microprocessor trainer which followed in the footsteps of the famous 8080 based NEC TK-80. The operation of micro trainers such as the TK-85 is very simple. In general data is entered into the machine via a small HEX keypad. This code is entered into specified address locations and can then be 'run'. Programs are displayed on a small 8 segment LED display. Any program can later be edited and re-run if desired. Two audio jacks allow the program to be saved and loaded via cassette. Although this description is very simplistic, there really isn't much more to the general operation of this machine (source: http://www.neoncluster.com/home/tk85.html).

DRIVER:
trainer/tk80.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Good
Color: Good
Sound: Good
Graphics: Good
Save State: Supported

SOFTWARE LIST:
-

RESOURCES:
Snap, Title, Icon and machine picture (in "Cabinet" collection).

WIP:
- 0.148u1: Robbbert and Nama added 'NEC TK-85' system.

ROMSET:
2048 bytes in 1 file / 1.50Kb packed

$end
