$info=neopad
$mame
0.282 [David Haywood, TeamEurope]

Shogakukan no Zukan NEO Pad - Ikimono-hen (Japan), Takara Tomy, 201?

It’s a plug-and-play console released in Japan in the 2010s, designed to connect to a television. Based on the Zukan franchise, it offers an interactive educational experience featuring content about the animal kingdom. The player uses a pen- or stylus-shaped controller to explore images, listen to sounds, and answer quizzes. Audio and video are output via composite connection, targeting preschool-aged children with an intuitive approach to learning about nature through familiar characters.

