$info=nes_apu_vt
$mame
0.226 [David Haywood]

XOP APU, <unknown>, ????

DRIVER:
devices/sound/nes_apu_vt.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Good
Color: Good
Sound: Good
Graphics: Good
Save State: Unsupported

WIP:
- 0.261: It claims to be GPL, then it can't have a GPL-incompatible license restriction [hap].
- 0.242: Don't zero DPCM channel output when disabled (fixes some audio popping). Removed register read-back, corrected length counter table, and cleaned up code [kmg].
- 0.241: Added 'noise channel period table for PAL systems. Fixed a value in the parallel NTSC table for the largest period (lowest freq). Fixed a value in the counter length table (for all channels but DMC). Improved triangle channel emulation, reducing audible popping [kmg]. Improved mixing, clamping, duty cycles, and interaction between channels [cam900].
- 0.240: Added 'DPCM period table for PAL systems [kmg].
- 0.226: David Haywood added 'XOP APU' device.

ROMSET:
None required.

$end
