$info=nes_sharpcass
$mame
0.248 [kmg]

Sharp Cassette Interface AN-300SL, <unknown>, ????

An alternative to the Nintendo released Data Recorder. Unlike the Data Recorder, which plugs into the Famicom Keyboard via audio jacks, this Sharp Cassette Interface plugs directly into the expansion port and connects to any cassette deck via two audio jacks. The Sharp and Nintendo cassette interfaces are software incompatible. This device is used by the built-in Graphics/Note program of the Sharp My Computer Terebi C1 for saving/loading.

DRIVER:
devices/bus/nes_ctrl/sharpcass.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Good
Color: Good
Sound: Good
Graphics: Good
Save State: Unsupported

WIP:
- 0.248: kmg added 'Sharp Cassette Interface AN-300SL' device.

ROMSET:
None required.

$end
