$info=netbook
$mame
0.288 [Nigel Barnes, Bs ()Dd]

netBook, Psion, 1999

The Psion netBook is an iconic subnotebook computer released by Psion in 1999, designed specifically for the business and professional markets. This historic device holds a special place in the history of technology: its brand name coined and anticipated the term "netbook" by many years, before Intel officially reintroduced it to the market in 2008 to identify low-cost portable PCs. As with the devices discussed previously, its historical significance and collector’s value have led to its digital preservation through the emulation of its components.

