0.135 [Olivier Galibert]

NeXT Computer, Next Software Inc, 1987

NeXT's first workstation was officially named the NeXT Computer, although it was widely referred to as 'the cube' because of its distinctive case, a 1 ft x 1 ft x 1 ft magnesium cube, an edict of Jobs' designed by Apple IIc case designer Frogdesign. Prototype workstations were shown to standing ovations on October 12, 1988. The first machines were tested in 1989, after which NeXT started selling limited numbers to universities with a beta version of the NeXTSTEP operating system installed (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NeXT).

