$info=ngen
$mame
0.156 [Al Kossow, Barry Rodewald]

NGEN CP-001, Convergent Technologies, 1983

The system appears to be based on the Burroughs B20 to B26 workstations with the BTOS operating' system. For example the Burroughs B20 was also sold as the Convergent Technologies C20. Burroughs B25 model was used by Convergent Technologies for the NGEN model. The NGEN was known to Burroughs users as the B25, to Prime as the "Prime Producer 200", and was included the Intel 80186 CPU chip (source: https://www.computinghistory.org.uk/det/2964/Convergent-Technologies-AWS-NGEN-Workstation/).

