$info=ngen386
$mame
0.282 [Bitsavers]

NGEN 386, Convergent Technologies, 199?

It is a workstation released in the early 1990s, based on the Intel 80386 processor. Designed for professional and industrial environments, it integrates a smart terminal with a proprietary architecture, featuring an alphanumeric or graphical display, an integrated keyboard, and serial/parallel ports. It runs dedicated firmware for managing PBX systems, office automation, and business communications. Characterized by ruggedness and reliability, it is intended for integration into local networks and critical operational settings, representing the evolution of CT terminals from the previous era.

