$info=nms801
$mame
0.128 [Wilbert Pol]

NMS-801 (MSX1, Italy), Philips, 1989

The NMS-801 was one of the last MSX machine made by Philips. This economical computer was a true MSX machine. The official MSX logo was although replaced on the case by the "MSX Compatible" mark because the MSX standard required a cartridge slot, which the NMS-801 had not (source: http://www.old-computers.com/museum/computer.asp?st=1&c=1084).

