$info=nms8245
$mame
0.79 [Sean Young]

NMS 8245 (MSX2, Europe), Philips, 1987

The New Media Systems (NMS) 8245 is the last MSX2 model produced by Philips. This machine integrates the computer and the keyboard in one' device. Compared to its close cousin, the Philips VG-8235, the 8245 has a double sided disk drive, on the right, but lacks the adjustable keyboard. The second cartridge slot is optional as it is closed off by default but can easily be enabled by screwing the supplied cartridge holder onto the computer. The computer shipped with the office suite Ease and the drawing program Designer Plus (source: http://www.msx.org/wiki/Philips_NMS_8245).

