$info=nms8250
$mame
0.81 [Jirou Kaneda]

NMS 8250 (MSX2, Europe), Philips, 1987

The NMS 8250 is an MSX2 model released in 1986 by Philips. The abbreviation NMS stands for New Media Systems. The computer is a desktop model with a modern and business-like design and features one built-in disk station. The main board was designed by Sanyo. The NMS 8250 was a very popular model in Europe. The computer shipped with the office suite Home Office 2 and the drawing program Designer Plus. The NMS 8250 is closely related to the Philips NMS 8255 which is essentially the same computer but features 2 disk drives (source: http://www.msx.org/wiki/Philips_NMS_8250).

