NMS 8280 (MSX2, Europe), Philips, 1987

The NMS (New Media Systems) 8280 is the MSX2 top model released by Philips in 1986. While it looks very similar to the NMS 8250 and NMS 8255, the 8280 is an entirely different beast, as it features a video digitizer and super impose functionality. The computer features sliders to control the video, audio mix and digitize levels and an extra button to select the input source (source: http://www.msx.org/wiki/Philips_NMS_8280).

