$info=noki3410
$mame
0.170 [Sandro Ronco]

Nokia 3410, Nokia, 2002

The Nokia 3410 is a mobile phone made by Nokia which was released in early 2002, being the successor of the Nokia 3310. The 3410 was the first Java phone by Nokia. The phone features a monochrome display. It is also the first cellphone outside Japan to have 3D graphics on mobile phones, before Symbian and OpenGL ES. The 3410 is a compact, but somewhat heavy phone (weight:114 g, battery included). It employs up and down buttons for menu navigation. The on/off/profile button is a stiff black button located on the top of the phone (source: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nokia_3410).

