Nokia 8850, Nokia, 1999

The Nokia 8850 was launched in the market in 1999 and was the most expensive model in Nokia's home that year. The design was developed by Frank Nuovo, a Finnish designer arrived at home after studying at the Art Center College of Design in Pasadena. This series of high-end phones (8810, 8850 and 8910) was probably one of his best creations (source, traslated form Italian: http://www.borto.net/nokia_8850.htm).

