$info=nsnovaa
$mame
0.264 [Berger]

Super Nova (Novag, set 2), Novag Industries / Intelligent Heuristic Programming, 1990

In April 1990, the Super Nova appeared, a device in the Super series that replaced the Supremo and was part of the Super System with its serial interface. It was a pressure sensor device for battery (approx. 50 h) and mains operation for DM 449.00 (€ 249.50), in black, white and green and with a different design to the previous range of devices. The keypad and display, a four-digit seven-segment LC display with some special characters, are no longer located to the right of the 20 x 20 cm playing surface, but in front of it. Inside this mid-range device is a single-chip computer clocked at 16 MHz with a program of 32 kByte and a working memory of 8 kByte (source, tradotto dal Tedesco: https://www.schach-computer.info/wiki/index.php/Novag_Super_Nova).

