$info=o2
$mame
0.204 [Ryan Holtz, NekoChan]

O2, Silicon Graphics Inc., 1996

The O2 was an entry-level Unix workstation introduced in 1996 by Silicon Graphics, Inc. (SGI) to replace their earlier Indy series. Like the Indy, the O2 used a single MIPS microprocessor and was intended to be used mainly for multimedia. Its larger counterpart was the SGI Octane. The O2 was SGI's last attempt at a low-end workstation (source: https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/SGI_O2).

