It is a famous desktop chess computer: in the development of this iconic standalone electronic device, Perfect Technology was the Hong Kong-based industrial manufacturing subsidiary responsible for assembling the printed circuit boards (PCBs) and casings on behalf of Novag. Intelligent Heuristic Programming, on the other hand, refers to the heuristic logic and mathematical algorithms of the chess engine programmed into the ROM memory to allow the machine to calculate moves “intelligently” by simulating a human opponent.

