$info=osbexec
$mame
0.141 [Wilbert Pol]

Executive, Osborne, 1982

The Osborne Executive was the planned successor of the already commercially successful Osborne 1 portable computer by Osborne Computer Corporation. The Executive was a collection of the good features from the Osborne 1 and fixed some of its predecessor's flaws. The Osborne Executive, like the Osborne 1, came with application software. The WordStar word processor, SuperCalc spreadsheet, and the CBASIC and MBASIC programming languages -all software packages that were the leading applications in their respective niches at the time- had a retail value of more than $2495 (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Osborne_Executive).

