Oui-Oui - Pocket Dream Console (VideoJet, France), Conny / VideoJet, 2008

The Conny / VideoJet Oui-Oui – Pocket Dream Console, launched in 2008, is a themed and localized version of the portable PDC30 Pocket Dream Console system, produced by Conny and also sold under the VideoJet brand. This device is an example of an unofficial (clone) portable console that combines generic hardware with content dedicated to a children's television character, in this case Oui-Oui, known in Italy as Noddy, the friendly storybook character created by Enid Blyton.

