$info=p2000t
$mame
0.36RC1 [Paul Daniels]

P2000T, Philips, 1980

The Philips P2000T home computer was Philips' first real entry in the home computer market, after the Philips Videopac G7000 game system (better known in the U.S. as the Magnavox Odyssey?) which they already sold to compete with the Atari 2600 and similar game systems. There was also an P2000M version with an additional 80-column card for use with a monochrome monitor. This version shipped with a monitor cabinet also housing a dual 5?" floppy drive (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philips_P2000).

