$info=p500p
$mame
0.147u1 [Curt Coder]

P500 (PAL), Commodore Business Machines, 1983

he P500 is a rare machine of the CBMII series. It's a CBM600 with VIC-II (40 Col. color graphic) and two joyports. It looks like a C64. But the P500 is able to use more than one 64KB bank. The 6509 CPU uses with bank-switching 256KB and extern up to 968 KB RAM. The CPU is an upgraded MOS6502. The P500 has build in the fast IEEE488 and a RS232-Interface (source: http://www.cbmhardware.de/cbm2/p500.php).

