$info=p8000
$mame
0.135 [Matt Knoth, Fabio Priuli]

P8000 (8bit Board), EAW electronic Treptow, 1989

The P8000 consits of an 8bit and a 16bit microcomputer and was an universal all-purpose programming and developing system for multi-user / multi-task applications as workstation. It was produced by EAW in the GDR. To make a big application area accessible, there where 3 operation systems implemented for the P8000. WEGA which is a System III compatible UNIX, UDOS which is compatible to Z80-RIO and OS/M which is a CP/M compatible OS. WEGA which was implemented on the 16bit part of the P8000 demonstrated, regarding to its capability and usability, a new quality compared to other operating systems in that era (source: http://www.pofo.de/P8000/).

