Partner 1F/G, Iskra Delta, 1987

Iskra Delta Partner was a computer developed by Iskra Delta (Slovenia) in 1983. A family of desktop computers that were created to be small business and/or development systems. The Operating System was CP/M 3+ and  it had built in monochromatic monitor, there were three versions of the computer: 1. WFG - graphical microcomputer PARTNER with winchester disk and one disk unit. 2. 2FG - graphical microcomputer PARTNER with two disk units. 3. 1FG- graphical microcomputer PARTNER with one disk unit (source: https://8bithardware.wixsite.com/website/post/iskra-delta-partner-rom).

