$info=pasogo
$mame
0.125 [Peter Trauner]

PasoGo, KOEI, 1996

The Koei PasoGo. A contraction of Pasocon (personal computer) and Go (Go) the PasoGo (See how that works?) is a personal Go thing. It has a 2-colour low-contrast EyeStrain-O-Vision screen. The system was released in 1996, which if you'll recall, is the same year Nintendo was shopping around the Atlantis, released a milleia later as the GameBoy Advance. Seriously, this system was released when the GBA was finished. For shame, Koei. Two buttons, a power switch and a 4-way pad on the front, power + contrast on top, and a cartridge slot as well. Three softs were released. They're shown below, the titles all include the word 'Go' (source: http://nfggames.com/games/pasogo/).

