MOS 8364 "Paula", <unknown>, ????

The Paula chip, designed by Glenn Keller, from MOS Technology, is the interrupt controller, but also includes logic for audio playback, floppy disk drive control, serial port input/output and mouse/joystick buttons two and three signals. The logic remained functionally identical across all Amiga models from Commodore (source: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Original_Chip_Set#Paula).

