Pocket Computer 1360, Sharp, 198?

The Sharp PC-1350 is a small pocket computer manufactured by Sharp. It can also be considered as an electronic calculator. The PC-1350 was introduced in 1984 and was used by engineers, and favored by programmers for its decent programming and graphical capabilities. It was superseded in 1987 by the PC-1360, which featured one additional RAM expansion port, improved BASIC, Floppy disk capability and a faster CPU (source: http://www.computinghistory.org.uk/det/5004/Sharp-PC-1360/).

