$info=pc6001mk2sr
$mame
0.132 [Angelo Salese]

PC-6001mkIISR (Japan), NEC, 1984

This is another enhanced version of the original PC-6001 and later PC-6001 MK2. Two Basics languages (N66 & N66SR) are built-in. The computer is still compatible with the N60-Basic and N60-Extended Basic modes from the original PC-6001. The Basic N66 offers a 320x200 graphic mode (in 4 colors) and the new N66SR-Basic offers new text and graphic resolutions, the maximum being 640x200 with 15 colors. There is a ROM holding 1024 chinese characters. The PC-6001 MK2 SR offers optional speech synthesis features. There were 2 floppy disk drive types that were incompatible with each other, known as B and BE (source: http://www.old-computers.com/museum/computer.asp?st=1&c=394).

