$info=pc8001
$mame
0.132 [Fabio Priuli]

PC-8001, NEC, 1979

n 1979, the NEC PC-8001 was an excellent machine, offering 8 colors when most of its competitors were still monochrome. There is even a (low) graphic resolution of 160 x 100 dots. It could display capital and small letters. The PC-8001 had great success with Japanese businesses, where it was widely used. At the time, NEC claimed that the PC-8001 represented at least 45% of their home japanese market. This is when the PC serie from NEC and MZ serie from Sharp started competing! (source: http://www.old-computers.com/museum/computer.asp?c=178).

