$info=pc9801m2
$mame
0.283 [anonymous]

PC-9801M2, NEC, 1984

Desktop computer released in 1984 as part of the PC-9801 family, featuring a 16-bit architecture, a built-in monochrome high-resolution display (720×512), and support for 5.25" floppy disks. Designed for the Japanese market, it offered an advanced environment for productivity, programming, and gaming, complete with a proprietary operating system and extensive software compatibility within its own ecosystem.

