$info=pc9801uv2
$mame
0.277 [Mike Stedman]

PC-9801UV2, NEC, 1986

The NEC PC-9801UV2 is a variant of the famous PC-9801 computer system, developed and manufactured by NEC (Nippon Electric Company), one of the largest computer manufacturers in Japan. The PC-9801 series was launched beginning in 1982 and played a dominant role in the Japanese personal computer market until the late decade of the 1990s. The specific model PC-9801UV2 is part of the long line of hardware upgrades and variants introduced during the life of the system, probably referring to a configuration with an improved or expanded video unit (hence the suffix "UV," which could stand for Video Upgrade or Video Unit ).

