0.132 [Angelo Salese, Carl]

PC-9821 (98MULTi), NEC, 1992

PC-9821 series, the NEC had been sold until 1992 and 2003 personal computer is the name of the product group. It was the main models of NEC's consumer PC product in about four years from around 1993 until the fall of 1997. PC-9800 series it is upward-compatible product. Only the part "21" out of '9821' in the product name has become a white character, meaning that it is put 'PC-9800 series for the 21st century'. However, without waiting for the new series I 21st century PC98-NX released. (English version release of Windows 3.0 Windows 3.x era of 1990 Japanese edition / May 1991 Mon 2, Windows 3.1 is the English version in 1992 Japanese edition / April 1993 May), the major In addition to the corresponding business applications to Windows in succession, DOS / V With the advent of Compaq inexpensive while corresponding to Japanese products such as PC / AT compatible offensive by is now one after another, machine manufacturers domestic Japanese The companies were being forced to respond to these (source, traslated from japanese: http://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/PC-9821%E3%82%B7%E3%83%AA%E3%83%BC%E3%82%BA).

