$info=pcd2m
$mame
0.234 [Predator99, rfka01]

PCD-2M, Siemens, 198?

The Siemens PCD family was a product line AT -compatible personal computer that Siemens made from 1986 and sold before finally in 1996 was replaced by the Scenic Pro product line. During the production time of the first generation, the office PC department of Siemens merged with Nixdorf to form Siemens-Nixdorf. The M model was a compact desktop PC. It offered three free slots for expansion cards as well as three slots for 3.5? drives, two of which can be operated. The M systems also had a key switch with keyboard and boat lock as well as mechanical locking of the housing, but no drive cover. An external 5?? drive was offered as an accessory. The PCD-2L was an inexpensive variant of the PCD-2M without a hard disk, but with otherwise the same technical data (source: https://second.wiki/wiki/siemens_pcd-familie#PCD-2L/2M/3M/4M).

