PC-G850V, Sharp, 2001

The Sharp PC-G850V is a pocket computer of Sharp. He is possibly the last model of this kind, and was, like his predecessors, produced for the Japanese education market. He is a direct descendant of the Sharp PC-G850S and belongs to a line of hand-held computers with Z80 processor which started with the PC-E200. The PC-G850V has an alphanumeric keypad and a graphical LCD display with 144 × 48 pixels, on the six lines of text can be displayed and compared with the previous models, offers a higher contrast. The computer is a Z80-compatible processor operates at 8 MHz (source, traslated from german: http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sharp_PC-G850V).

