$info=pcw9256
$mame
0.37b5 [Kev Thacker]

PCW9256, Amstrad plc, 1991

The PcW 9256, was introduced in 1991, together with the PcW 9512+, and its housing was a complete redesign, resembling none of the earlier PCW's. It is a quite elegant design, with a printer platform on the monitor: perfect for small sized desktops. The keyboard is an 8000-style one, only the case has been modernised and curves and roundings have been added 'to match the printer in a more modern fashion. The monitor has rather large 'margins' to the left and the right so that, while working with it, it may look like that the monitor is not placed at the proper angle, but I checked it thoroughly and it is located properly (source: http://www.fvempel.nl/9256.html).

