$info=pdc30p
$mame
0.278 [David Haywood, Sean Riddle, TeamEurope]

PDC30 - Pocket Dream Console (Pink version) (VideoJet, France), Conny / VideoJet, 2008

The Conny/VideoJet PDC30 – Pocket Dream Console is a portable Plug & Play system produced by Conny (a well-known Chinese brand of electronic gadgets) and also marketed under the name VideoJet, launched in 2008. It presents itself as a mini portable console promising to offer hundreds of classic games in a pocket-sized format, but it actually falls into the category of unofficial "TV Games" or clone systems, which were common during those years. The PDC30 (Pocket Dream Console) is an affordable portable console with an integrated LCD screen, designed for playing retro games without the need for a TV or PC. It is similar to many "Dendy Handhelds" or "Game Keys" of the time, but with a more refined design and a greater variety of games.

