$info=pdcj
$mame
0.280 [David Haywood, TeamEurope]

PDC - Pocket Dream Console (Japan), Conny / Takara, 2006

Portable cartridge-based console, launched in the early 2000s, designed to deliver a pocket-sized gaming experience with both original and adapted titles. Featuring a color LCD screen, directional controls, and action buttons, it includes features like state-saving and volume adjustment. Powered by batteries, the console stands out for its compact, colorful design tailored for a younger audience. It supports a limited yet carefully curated library of games, often inspired by genres such as adventure, puzzles, and light-action titles. Despite its modest hardware, the device represents an attempt to compete with the portable consoles of its time, emphasizing affordability and portability.

