$info=pdp11ub
$mame
0.142 [Miodrag Milanović]

PDP-11 [Unibus](M9301-YA), Digital Equipment Corporation, 197?

The PDP-11 was a series of 16-bit minicomputers sold by Digital Equipment Corporation (DEC) from 1970 into the 1990s, one of a succession of products in the PDP series. The PDP-11 replaced the PDP-8 in many real-time applications, although both product lines lived in parallel for more than 10 years. The PDP-11 had several uniquely innovative features, and was easier to program than its predecessors with its use of general registers. Its successor in the mid-range minicomputer niche was the 32-bit VAX-11 (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PDP-11).

