$info=pet2001j
$mame
0.285 [Curt Coder]

PET 2001-4 (Japan), Commodore Business Machines, 1977

Personal computer launched by Commodore in 1977, a Japanese variant of the base model featuring only 4 KB of RAM. It came with a compact case housing a 9-inch monochrome CRT monitor, a cassette tape drive (Datasette), and a chiclet-style keyboard. Based on a 1-MHz MOS 6502 processor, it was primarily intended for educational use and small offices. The Japanese version included adaptations for the local character set and was marketed in limited quantities, making it particularly rare today among collectors of vintage home computers.

