$info=phc64
$mame
0.130 [Dirk Best]

Mephisto PHC 64 (Germany), Intelligent Software / Hegener + Glaser, 1985

A British home computer in a very unusual design (what the computer given the nickname "Knetgummilache"). The black case is very discreet and above all comfortable flat, the colorful buttons but look rather funky. Particularly noteworthy is the built joystick, when the Enterprise replaces the cursor keys. That may seem playful (can also be used to play fine), but is really handy / in comparison to conventional cursor keys move the stick goes by really fast by the hand (source, traslated from german: http://www.zock.com/8-Bit/D_Enterprise64.HTML).

