$info=pickytlk
$mame
0.264 [QUFB]

Super Picky Talk - Forest of Gurutan, Casio, 1998

The Super Picky Talk, released in 1990 functions like a PDA, with a stylus, but is tailored to the children's market, with a dog or a cat at start up for instance. Features are a notepad, calculator, clock and stopwatch, a drawing pad, with a feature for basic animation. There are also a few simple games accessed from a toy shelf on the left of the desktop screen. An infrared system can be used to link up the system with other Picky Talk Users. The system is regarded as a PDA rather than a games console, as no more titles can be put on the machine, though the games are a bit more involved than the usual PDA ones (source: https://www.computinghistory.org.uk/det/60825/Casio-Super-Picky-Talk/).

