P/ECE (2 MB Flash), Aquaplus, 2001

An early preview of the P/ECE referred to the P/ECE as a portable game console though the water was somewhat muddied by the fact that one of the built in apps, Picket, was a PIM (Personal Information Manager). This means it was often referred to as a PDA. It has a d-pad, start and select buttons, and you can play games on it — that makes it a console in my eyes. But a console where each unit could be used as a development device by connecting it to a desktop computer (source: https://blog.gingerbeardman.com/2021/08/19/aquaplus-piece-vs-panic-playdate/).

