$info=piet1
$mame
0.287 [QUFB]

Electronic Tool PI-ET1, NEC, 1990

NEC "PI-ET1" embedded development system (Personal Intelligent - Electronic Tool 1), a hardware/software prototyping and debugging platform based on NEC V25/V35 microprocessors (x86-compatible architecture compatible with Intel 80186/8086). Designed in the 1990s for electronic engineers, it includes in-circuit emulators, built-in debuggers, ROM monitors, and slots for interchangeable CPU modules. It was used to develop firmware, industrial controllers, and real-time systems prior to the widespread adoption of modern tools. Featuring a modular design with rack-mountable chassis, connectors for logic probes, and a serial interface for connection to a host PC, the PI-ET1 represents a professional tool from the pre-JTAG era for embedded development on NEC’s proprietary x86 architectures.

