$info=pilot5k
$mame
0.130 [R. Belmont]

Pilot 5000, U.S. Robotics, 1996

The pilot was in Germany for the first time presented at the CeBIT '96. In this context it is interesting that U.S. Robotics has previously entered only as a modem manufacturer in appearance. The operation is done with the included stylus on the touch surface. The character recognition is performed on a zone divided in the lower third of the screen. A 'training' the recognition routines is not possible, but the PDA requires a special notation. In a pinch, however, can also be an on-screen keyboard and use Show. To software includes among others, the pilot Notebook, address book and calculator (source, traslated from german: http://palmtopmagazin.de/produktkatalog/19.php3).

