$info=piopxv60
$mame
0.155 [Wilbert Pol]

PX-V60 (MSX1, Japan), Pioneer, 1986

The Pioneer PX-V60 is a MSX1 computer, aimed at the Japanese market. It was meant for attaching to a LaserDisc player, and as such has superimpose capabilities. Compared to other Pioneer MSX1 computers, it lacks LaserDisc system control-in, RGB output, headphone out and the sliders for volume and mixing-level that the other Pioneer MSX machines feature. It also has a completely different keyboard connector, the separate keyboard has the reference AAX-476. It was provided with a demo cassette (source: https://www.msx.org/wiki/Pioneer_PX-V60).

