$info=pm5644g00
$mame
0.281 [stonedDiscord, Matthew Millman]

PM 5644 color pattern generator (PAL-G 4:3 Colour Circle), Philips, 1989

It’s a professional color video signal generator used for calibrating and testing television and broadcast equipment in the PAL-G format (the European standard). It produces a test pattern known as the "Colour Circle" (or "Circle Pattern"), consisting of color bars, grids, sync pulses, and other geometric elements, used to verify chrominance, luminance, linearity, and synchronization in monitors and broadcast systems. Designed for TV engineers and lab technicians, it features composite and/or RF outputs, high signal stability, and compliance with EBU standards. It was widely used in television studios, transmission facilities, and repair workshops until the advent of digital broadcasting.

