$info=pm5644g913
$mame
0.281 [stonedDiscord, Matthew Millman]

PM 5644 color pattern generator (PAL-G 4:3 Indian Head), Philips, 1989

It’s a professional color video signal generator used for servicing and calibrating television equipment in the PAL-G format (the European standard). Unlike the more common “Colour Circle” version, this variant outputs the classic “Indian Head” test pattern—originally developed in the United States for NTSC but here adapted to the PAL system. The signal includes test elements for evaluating resolution, contrast, geometry, and synchronization, and it was primarily used in technical labs, broadcast stations, and repair workshops. Equipped with composite and/or RF outputs and compliant with EBU standards, it represents a specialized solution for analog testing in professional environments prior to the transition to digital broadcasting.

