$info=pm5644g924
$mame
0.281 [stonedDiscord, Matthew Millman]

PM 5644 color pattern generator (PAL 16:9 Colour Circle Rev 1), Philips, 1989

It’s a professional color video signal generator introduced in 1989 for calibrating television equipment in the PAL format with a 16:9 aspect ratio, anticipating the transition to widescreen displays. It produces an updated version of the well-known “Colour Circle” test pattern, adapted to verify parameters such as geometry, horizontal/vertical linearity, chrominance, and synchronization in widescreen format. Equipped with composite and/or component outputs, it complies with EBU standards and is designed for broadcast engineers and lab technicians. Although released at a time when 16:9 was not yet a broadcast standard, it represents a pioneering tool for the development and testing of advanced video systems prior to the advent of digital HDTV.

