It’s a professional color video signal generator designed for calibrating television equipment in the PAL format with a 16:9 aspect ratio. Compared to Revision 1, this version features enhancements to the “Colour Circle” test pattern, with optimized elements for more accurately evaluating widescreen geometry, chroma response at screen edges, linearity, and sync stability in panoramic format. Equipped with composite and/or component outputs and compliant with EBU standards, it was used by broadcast engineers during the development and testing of advanced displays and video systems, serving as a reference tool in the analog era before HDTV.

