$info=pofo2
$mame
0.283 [Nigel Barnes, derkom]

Portfolio 2, Atari, 1990

Handheld computer released in 1990, featuring a compact plastic chassis with a built-in QWERTY keyboard and an 8-line monochrome LCD display. Based on an architecture compatible with the IBM PC, it uses a 5.78 MHz CMOS 80C88 processor and comes equipped with 128 KB of RAM, expandable up to 640 KB via PCMCIA cards. Powered by three AA batteries, it offers extended battery life. The device includes integrated applications for word processing, spreadsheet, calendar, and calculator, and supports connection to printers and PCs via serial ports. Designed for mobile professionals, it represents one of the earliest truly compact solutions that were compatible with PC software of the time.

