$info=poly880
$mame
0.132 [Miodrag Milanović]

Poly-Computer 880, VEB Polytechnik Karl-Marx-Stadt, 1983

The Polycomputer 880 in the GDR was a widespread computer-based learning the microprocessor U880. The computer was from 1983 produced by the state-owned enterprise VEB Polytechnik Karl-Marx-Stadt for use as machine learning in general education schools and higher education institutions. The device is installed and ready for operation in a diplomatic pouch (48x38x12cm) delivered and had a total weight of 5 Kg to enter data possessed the Polycomputer a hexadecimal keyboard and some function keys. The issue was made over an 8-digit seven-segment display. The status of all lines of the data and address bus could have been read by LEDs. The operating system of Polycomputers was on a 4-kbyte ROM for data storage was 1 KByte RAM provided. Due to incomplete address decoding was an upgrade to the full 64 KB memory not possible. For external data storage was a cassette tape recorder can be connected via a DIN connector. To print over a loudspeaker connector was a teletype connected. A driver for the loop current of the telegraph was already installed (source, traslated from german: http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polycomputer_880).

