Mephisto Portorose 68030, Hegener + Glaser, 1989

A year had passed since the Micro World Cup in Almeria, Spain, and the new location was Portorose (today's Slovenia). As in previous years, Hegener & Glaser (Mephisto) had relied on the same successful duo Richard Lang / Ossi Weiner - and rightly so. Everything should, and measured against the high expectations, it got better. The "new" started with "commercial hardware" that had it all: a Motorola 68030 with 36 MHz, 2 megabytes for hash tables, available for "cheap" 15,000 DM. Ordinary people were allowed a.) Their Almeria `s send to Munich for retrofitting or b.) stock up with the" cheap "68020 (32 bit) + 68000 (16 bit) module sets (source, traslated from German: https://www.schach-computer.info/wiki/index.php/Mephisto_Portorose_68030).

