$info=positron
$mame
0.238 [Binary Dinosaurs, Nigel Barnes]

Positron 9000, Positron Computers Ltd, 1982

This is quite a beast of a machine, from 1982. Based around a 1MHz 6809, optionally 2MHz, it supports up to 512k RAM (with the use of 8 MMU chips). The OS is in ROM: OS9 or optionally Flex. There's a version with 40x24 text or 240x240 colour graphics and also a headless version, and supposedly supporting multiple users - 4 serial lines expandable to 8. Oddly, it can output to a monitor or a TV (source: https://retrocomputingforum.com/t/the-positron-9000-multiuser-6809-system-from-the-uk/1905).

