Powerpack In-Circuit Emulator PP-SW+ PIII, Microtek, 1999

The Microtek Powerpack In-Circuit Emulator PP-SW+ PIII is a hardware and software development tool used primarily by embedded systems engineers and developers to test, emulate, and debug code during the design phase of microprocessor- or microcontroller-based devices. This device belongs to the category of In-Circuit Emulator (ICE), which allow to simulate the behavior of a microprocessor inside the real circuit in which it will be installed.

