Pravetz were Bulgarian computers, manufactured mainly in the town of Pravetz. Some components and software were produced in Stara Zagora, Plovdiv and other Bulgarian cities. (IMKO-2) / 82 is model year. BASIC interpreter, RAM/ROM / 48/12 Kb; CPU Synertek 6502 /1 MHz. The storage is improved due to one or (optional) two 5?" floppy disk drive(s) (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pravetz_computers).

