0.128 [Miodrag Milanović]

Primo C-64, Microkey, 1984

Primo is a Hungarian developed hobby/game computer. The Microkey Research Development Production Partnership was formed in 1983 by SZTAKI az Elektomodul and "Új Élet" MgTsz in Sárisáp. After a year of development work, the association announced to the public in the spring of 1984 that it would begin manufacturing a simple and inexpensive home computer. This computer was the Primo. Until the end of production in 1986, a total of about 7,000 units were made, of which 1,000 units had a real keyboard (source, traslated from Hungarian: https://hu.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Primo).

