PROF-181X, Conitec Datensysteme, 1992

The Conitec Datensysteme PROF-180X (often identified or associated with industrial variants such as the PROF-181X) is a sophisticated single-board computer (SBC) and professional development system based on the Eurocard architecture, released by the German company Conitec Datensysteme GmbH in the late 1980s. The system represents a direct evolution of the earlier PROF-80. It was designed not as a consumer computer, but as a powerful standalone industrial and test machine for engineers, laboratories, and embedded control systems.

