$info=prophet2
$mame
0.279 [anonymous]

Prophet 2, Busicomputers, 1983

This is a computer clone of the Commodore 64, produced in Italy during the first half of the 1980s. Built around the MOS 6510 architecture and equipped with 64 KB of RAM, it was compatible with most of the C64's software and games—though it did feature some hardware and interface differences. Designed for home and recreational use, it supported programming languages like BASIC and could be connected to TVs or monitors via RF. Marketed at a competitive price, it emerged as an affordable alternative to the original computers, appealing to families and computing enthusiasts during the golden age of home computing.

