$info=prophet5r30
$mame
0.281 [DBWBP]

Prophet 5 (Model 1000) Rev 3.0, Sequential Circuits, 1980

It’s a 5-voice polyphonic analog synthesizer released in 1980, renowned for its warm and versatile sound. Featuring two oscillators per voice, a resonant analog filter, and full modulation capabilities (LFO, envelopes, pitch bend), it was the first synth to include digital memory for presets. Revision 3.0 introduced a hybrid architecture with digitally controlled oscillators (Curtis CEM3340) and an analog filter, improving tuning stability and reliability. It became a studio standard in pop, rock, and electronic music production.

