$info=prpht600a
$mame
0.287 [Siftware]

Prophet-600 (set 2), Sequential Circuits, 1983

Hybrid analog/digital synthesizer Sequential Circuits Prophet-600, released in 1983. The world's first synthesizer with built-in MIDI (initial implementation was non-standard but could be upgraded via firmware). Six-voice architecture featuring digitally controlled DCO oscillators, a 4-pole analog filter (Moog-style), LFO, and ADSR envelope generators for modulation. Compact design with a 61-key semi-weighted keyboard, a 3-digit LED display, and front-panel knobs for direct editing. Warm and versatile sound, widely used in synth-pop, new wave, and experimental music of the 1980s. This synthesizer marks a milestone in the history of musical synthesis by introducing MIDI to a commercial synthesizer, paving the way for interoperability among digital musical devices.

