0.189 [Dirk Best, rfka01]

PSI98, Kontron, 1984

The Kontron PSI98 (also known by the symbol PSI Ψ 98) is a sophisticated 8-bit professional and industrial microcomputer introduced in the early 1980s (around 1984) by Kontron Mikrocomputer GmbH, a German company based in Eching, near Munich. Designed as a high-performance evolution of the previous and successful PSI80 model, the PSI98 is a "compact desktop" (Tischgerät) machine or one that can be integrated into 19-inch industrial racks, tailored for scientific tasks, factory automation, laboratory applications, and complex data management tasks (such as hospital billing for anesthesia departments).

