Series 3mx (Dutch), Psion, 1998

This is a high-end, portable electronic organizer developed in the late 1990s, part of a series of handheld devices designed for both professional and personal use. Equipped with an LCD display, a full physical keyboard, and a proprietary operating system, it allows users to manage appointments, address books, notes, text documents, and spreadsheets. Powered by batteries, it offers impressive battery life and is designed to synchronize data seamlessly with a computer. With its compact yet rugged design, it stands out for its reliability, efficiency, and durability—making it ideal for business users and professionals who need a lightweight, functional tool to boost productivity on the go. The Dutch-language version features a localized interface and software tailored specifically for the Dutch market.

