$info=psion5mx_fr
$mame
0.288 [Nigel Barnes]

Series 5mx (French), Psion, 1999

The Psion Series 5mx is a famous handheld computer (Personal Digital Assistant – PDA) released by Psion in 1999. It represents a direct and enhanced evolution of the original 1997 Series 5. While retaining the same iconic exterior design, it features a completely redesigned motherboard, a much faster processor, and double the memory. The Keyboard Mechanism The most famous feature of the Psion Series 5mx is its revolutionary sliding clamshell mechanism. When the user lifts the screen, the physical keyboard automatically slides forward, extending from the body. This engineering solution shifts the device’s center of gravity to prevent the display from tipping over, while offering a mechanical keyboard of exceptional quality for mobile typing—still considered among the best ever made in this product category. Specifically, this is the version for the French market.

