Series 5mx PRO, Psion, 1999

The Psion Series 5mx PRO is a rare, enhanced variant of the famous Series 5mx handheld, released by Psion starting in 1999. This model represents the British company’s engineering pinnacle in the clamshell handheld computer sector. It was designed primarily for advanced professional users, developers, and the enterprise market (particularly the German market). While retaining the iconic exterior design and the famous anti-flip sliding keyboard, it introduces a radical change in the management of the system architecture.

