$info=pt581392
$mame
0.214 [rfka01]

386 motherboard using the Forex FRX46C402 + FRX46C411 + SiS 85C206 chipset, <unknown>, 199?

The combination of the Forex FRX46C402, Forex FRX46C411, and SiS 85C206 chips identifies a very specific chipset architecture used on various motherboards for Intel 386DX processors (and AMD/Cyrix clones) manufactured between 1991 and 1992. This hardware transition represents the golden age of high-performance "multi-chip" motherboards, before the industry standardized on chipsets integrated into just two or three main chips (Northbridge/Southbridge).

