$info=ptc100
$mame
0.205 [Dirk Best, rfka01]

PTC-100, Grundig, 198?

The PTC 100 is nothing more than a differently colored Mupid 2. The original is black with a gray keyboard, the PTC 100 comes in a very old-fashioned brown-beige. Technically, the PTC 100 is a classic home computer. It was launched in 1984, the Mupid 2 was available a year earlier. In the basic configuration, the device was restricted to use as a BTX terminal. There is a connection on the device for the "DBT-03" modem provided by the Deutsche Bundespost for BTX customers at the time. The connection to a TV set is made via a scart socket (source, traslated from German: https://www.homecomputermuseum.de/sammlung/detailansicht/comp/Computer/show/ptc-100/).

