$info=pyuutajr
$mame
0.143u8 [Anonymous source, Robbbert]

Tomy Pyuuta Jr., Tomy, 1983

In 1982, Tomy of Japan decided totry their hand in the computer market. They introduced the Tomy Pyuuta (pronunced PYOOO-ta and means computer dude'). It garnered moderate success and appered on both European (GrandStand Tutor) and US shores (Tomy Tutor) in 1983. However due to fierce competititors (MSX, Commodore, Atari, Texas), the console did better in its native home of Japan (source: http://www.videogameconsolelibrary.com/pg80-pyuuta.htm#page=reviews).

