$info=qx10
$mame
0.132 [Mariusz Wojcieszek]

QX-10, Epson, 1983

The Epson QX-10 is a microcomputer running CP/M or TPM-III (CP/M-80 compatible) which was introduced in 1983. It was based on a Zilog Z80 microprocessor, running at 4 MHz, provided up to 256K of RAM organized in four switchable banks, and included a separate graphics processor chip (?PD7220) manufactured by NEC to provide advanced graphics capabilities. In the USA, two versions were launched; a basic CP/M configuration with 64 K RAM and the HASCI configuration with 256 K RAM and the special HASCI keyboard to be used with the bundled application suite, called Valdocs. The European and Japanese versions were like the CP/M configurations. TPM-III was used for Valdocs and some copy protected programs like Logo Professor (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Epson_QX-10).

DRIVER:
epson/qx10.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Preliminary
Color: Good
Sound: Good
Graphics: Good
Save State: Unsupported

SOFTWARE LIST:
qx10_flop.xml

RESOURCES:
Snap, Title, Icon, machine picture (in "Cabinet" collection), Control Panel, Flyer, pdf Manual and Marquee.

WIP:
- 0.272: Add checksums for multifont rom dumps (#12910) [Brian Johnson].
- 0.249: Added YM2149-based sound card. Added hard disk support for the Epson QX-10 (IDE and ComFiler CR-1510 option boards) [Brian Johnson].
- 0.242: Implement floppy motor on timer. Install software timer interrupts. Add multifont option card [Brian Johnson].
- 0.233: Add centronics printer port (#8034) [Brian Johnson].
- 0.149: Added 'floppy software list [Curt Coder].
- 0.147u4: Downgrade floppies to DD [Olivier Galibert].
- 0.143u8: Added 'proper ROM dumps [F.J. Kraan].
- 0.135: Driver boots and load CP/M from floppy image [Mariusz Wojcieszek].
- 0.132: Mariusz Wojcieszek added skeleton driver of 'Epson QX-10' system.

ROMSET:
8192 bytes in 3 files / 3.78Kb packed

$end
