0.245 [Sean Riddle, David Haywood, Peter Wilhelmsen, Kamaal Brown]

Play TV Jr. Construction, Radica / Takara / SSD Company LTD, 2002

Flashing Lights on console show your child where to start. Battery operated and hooks straight to your TV and cords are included. Menu button allows you to chose games. Very nice starting hand/eyes cordination console. Some kids can't get enough of tractors, cranes, bulldozers and dump trucks. The interactive Play TV Junior Construction Game puts them in the action. Just plug it in to your TV or VCR, pick your job and get to work! Build a house or playground, dig a train tunnel, pave the road or catch fish! Control the action on-screen with realistic steering wheel, shifters, buttons and gears. Uses 4 C batteries, not included. Ages 4 and up. Game plugs into standard TV or VCR "audio/video in" ports with supplied RCA cables. Most TVs made after 1994 have these ports—double check yours to make sure (source: https://www.searchamateur.com/product/Power-Junior-Construction.htm)

