$info=rad_rsgp
$mame
0.206 [Sean Riddle, Peter Wilhelmsen]

Connectv Real Swing Golf (set 1), Radica / FarSight Studios, 2005

In Radica's all-in-one sports game series, I'd like to say Golf! In fact, there are two of them. Golden Tee Golf uses a track ball to hit shots on the green. Here, with Real Swing, you'll actually have a golf club in your hands. This is one of the first games in Radica's connecTV range. The box is bulky, but contains very little: the console and a golf club. The console takes the form of a sort of mine, incorporating a sensor that determines your shot. For once, the box is easy to open, as it's classic cardboard with no transparent plastic built in. The game can be unpacked very quickly, and once you've plugged in the two RCAs and inserted the four batteries, you can start playing. The cable is very long, so you can stand well away from the TV to avoid any problems (sourcem traslated from French: https://www.obsolete-tears.com/radica-connectv-real-swing-golf-machine-401.html).

