Street Fighter II: Special Champion Edition [Ghouls'n Ghosts] (Radica, Arcade Legends) (UK), Radica / Capcom / Sega, 2004

Radica continues its momentum by proposing us a new console of the series Arcade Legends all in one based on the hardware of the Megadrive of Sega. As its name suggests, it is of course the illustrious Street Fighter II that is in the spotlight. On this subject, one can easily wonder why to have used the version Megadrive, certainly excellent, but all of not even a hair under the Super Nintendo version. The reason is obviously a question of rights, especially hardware, Nintendo being very picky about the adaptation of its consoles and Radica already having the Megadrive on hand. Regulars of the two previous models of Arcade Legends Megadrive will not be out of place: we find the mini CPU in the form of Megadrive as cute as impractical. However, this time, two joysticks are provided. When you know the potential of Street Fighter II to many, this choice seems obvious. The controllers are not the original ones of the 16-bit Sega, but the six-button versions that had already been released when the game was released in 1993. The comfort is therefore total (source, translate from French: http://www.obsolete-tears.com/radica-arcade-legends-street-fighter-ii-machine-340.html).

