$mame
0.194 [Team Europe, Sean Riddle]

Space Invaders [Lunar Rescue, Colony 7, Qix, Phoenix] (Radica, Arcade Legends TV Game), Radica (licensed from Taito), 2004

Retro fashion continues with this Space Invaders from the Arcade Legends Collection. Manufactured by Radica and marketed in France by Nobilis, this console in a joystick is aimed rather at nostalgic thirties, since the games on offer are classics of the 1980s. The machine is in the form of an arcade controller. The photos allow to imagine something quite voluminous, but it is not so. The controller is a little bigger than others like the Megadrive version or the PacMan of Lansay, but nothing much different in the end. Pleasantly, both right-handed and left-handed can take pleasure: the typical arcade stick is present in the middle, and the buttons A and B are replicated to the right and left. Everyone to take the position that is most comfortable. Unlike many of its counterparts, this mini-console can be connected to the mains via a very conventional 6 Volt adapter. As it does not consume much, we can prefer the four AA type batteries. To connect to the TV, an RCA cable is secured to the machine, and the scart tip is provided in the box (source, translate from French: http://www.obsolete-tears.com/radica-arcade-legends-space-invaders-machine-329.html).

