0.196 [Sean Riddle, Peter Wilhelmsen]

ConnecTV Snowboarder (Blue) (PAL), Radica / SSD Company LTD, 2001

The price is quite high compared to other machines of this type. With an object costing almost twice that of a classic joystick-type machine to plug into the television, we might have expected something a little more chiadé. To simplify, it's actually an eight-way controller that is handled with a board. The board itself is made of wood, small in size – we can imagine that this game is made for children, with a fairly nice design, but absolutely nothing to explain such a high selling price. Power is supplied by four LR06 type batteries, or by an AC adapter in the classic 6 vol format (not supplied). Regarding the connection to the television, it is always two same RCA: a composite for the video, and another for the mono sound. The hardware is obviously totally identical to that of the other Radica machines (source, traslated from French: https://www.obsolete-tears.com/radica-connect-tv-snowboarder-machine-355.html).

