The Radio-86RK (Russian: ?????-86??) is a build-it-yourself home computer designed in the Soviet Union. It was featured in the popular Radio (Russian: ?????) magazine for radio hams and electronics hobbyists in 1986. The letters RK in the title stands for the words Radio ham's Computer (Russian: ?????????????????? ?????????). Design of the computer was published in a series of articles describing its logical structure, electrical circuitry, drawings of printed circuit boards and firmware. The computer could be built entirely out of standard off-the-shelf parts. Later it was also available in a kit form as well as fully assembled form (source: https://www.wikiwand.com/en/Radio-86RK).

