$info=rbitgen
$mame
0.218 [Porchy]

Generations (Retro-Bit), Retro-Bit, 2016

The Retro-Bit Generations is a simple glossy black plastic box with red highlights on the top. You might compare it with the Sega Genesis if you squint, but it doesn't really look like much of anything beyond a box with two USB ports on the front and a power button on the top. The back of the system holds an HDMI output, a composite video output, an SD card slot for saving game states, and the power connector. In theory, the Generations far surpasses the NES Classic by including two controllers with nine-foot cables instead of just one with a too-short two-foot cable. Unfortunately, the controllers are simply not very good. They're USB gamepads modeled after the six-button Sega Genesis controller, black plastic crescents with a direction pad, a Start button, and two rows of red buttons on the face. A Mode button sits on the top edge, serving as a Select control for most games and accessing the system's menu by pressing it while holding down on the direction pad (source: https://www.pcmag.com/reviews/retro-bit-generations).

DRIVER:
tvgames/actions_atj2279b.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Preliminary
