$mame
0.268 [Giulio Zausa]

RD-500 Digital Piano, Roland, 1994

Roland RD is a series of professional stage instruments launched in the 80's. RD-500 is one of the successful digital instruments with recorded samples of pianos, organs, harpsichords, strings, as well as synthesizers, bass and percussion instruments. The total number of timbres of musical instruments included in RD-500 is 121. At the same time, the digital piano allows its users to change and save the recorded sounds, which is of great importance when creating musical compositions. RD-500 features a 28-voice polyphony (source: https://synth.market/en/catalogue/roland/rd_500/).

