$info=rdqa
$mame
0.230 [hap, Sean Riddle]

Reader's Digest Q&A: Computer Question & Answer Game, Selchow & Righter, 1980

This 1980 game was donated to the Museum by the manufacturer Selchow & Righter in 1981. The plastic case is 26cm long x 20.5cm wide x 4cm high, with a screen 19cm x 14cm. There are 20 keys on the keyboard. The 10 round beige keys are numbered 0 through 9. Five red oval keys are lettered A though D. Five additional red oval keys are labeled Score, Wrong, Right, Pass, Clear, Enter. On the lower right side of the plastic case is an 4 position switch marked: Off, On, Single, Double. In the rear of the case a back plate held by 5 screws holds a 9volt battery (source: https://healthy.uwaterloo.ca/museum/VirtualExhibits/electronic/handheld/word/index.html).

