0.119 [Dirk Verwiebe]

Mephisto Rebell 5,0 (set 1), Hegener + Glaser, 1986

Hardly a program has been very eagerly awaited as at the time of the rebel Mephisto 5.0, the foundation stone was laid in this computer-WM 1986 WCCC in Cologne. During the tournament rebel had several competitors that ran on mainframes, beaten and impressively in the last round, the chance to win with a victory over the American program Be-Be for the world title. Unfortunately the program Schröder resist in a profitable position in fatal Pawn not finished and finally the 5th Place (source, traslated from german: http://www.schach-computer.info/wiki/index.php/Mephisto_Rebell_5.0).

