$info=renaissa
$mame
0.221 [hap, Berger]

Kasparov Renaissance (set 1), Saitek / Heuristic Software, 1989

The Renaissance board, like the Leonardo or Galileo, is comparable to the modular series from Hegener & Glaser (Mephisto). Compared to the soulless Mephisto boards, the Modular Series from Saitek are full-fledged chess computers, i.e. A basic program is already included in the various boards. With 52 x 52 cm (playing field 38 x 38 cm), the Renaissance has an extremely generous wooden board that also houses a small LCD chess board. This can be used to check the position, visually demonstrate the main variants or automatically play back and forth entire games. When it comes to ease of use, the Renaissance leaves nothing to be desired: a 16-digit display that can be controlled directly with a button shows the main variant, ratings, nodes, times and much more. It has four recessed but clearly visible LEDs in each corner of the field, which is very helpful to the eye. Furthermore, it can be connected to a PC by means of an interface, which considerably increases its possible uses. Since its sensitive magnetic sensors (flash board) also register figure movements that are not quite clean, it is particularly suitable from a technical point of view for flash and fast games. But the built-in chess program of the Renaissance is in stark contrast to the fantastic equipment and has a level of play that is completely unacceptable for its price range. Fortunately, it can be easily upgraded due to the modular expansion option (source, traslated from German: https://www.schach-computer.info/wiki/index.php/Saitek_Renaissance).

DRIVER:
saitek/renaissance.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Good
Color: Good
Sound: Good
Graphics: Good
Save State: Supported

SOFTWARE LIST:
-

RESOURCES:
Snap, Title, Icon and machine picture (in "Cabinet" collection).

WIP:
- 0.265: Changed manufacturer to 'Saitek / Heuristic Software'.
- 0.261: Add NVRAM [hap].
- 0.246: Correct ACK output [hap].
- 0.233: Use input_merger for stb [hap].
- 0.232: Machine promoted to working [hap].
- 0.221: hap and Berger added 'Saitek Kasparov Renaissance (set 1)' system.

