The Psion Revo is a sleek 32-bit handheld computer (PDA) released by the British company Psion in November 1999. This model represents a milestone in European technological design at the turn of the millennium. It was designed with the goal of packing the full software power and architecture of the Psion Series 5mx into an ultra-slim, lightweight, and extremely pocket-friendly chassis, designed to slip into the pocket of a business suit jacket. Version for the French market.

