$info=rocksock
$mame
0.278 [David Haywood, Sean Ridle, TeamEurope]

Rock 'Em Sock 'Em Robots (TV Game), Mattel, 2006

The Mattel Rock 'Em Sock 'Em Robots (2006) is an updated reissue of the classic mechanical tabletop game first launched by Mattel in 1966. This version, released in 2006, combines the iconic design of the original with modern electronic elements, such as LED lights, electronic sounds, and combat sound effects, making it more appealing to children of the 21st century while retaining the playful and competitive spirit of the original game. The Rock 'Em Sock 'Em Robots (2006) is an interactive two-player tabletop game where each participant controls a robot (the Red Rocker or the Blue Bomber) and tries to defeat their opponent by repeatedly hitting them until the head of the opponent's robot pops off — the famous "knockout." This edition was designed to modernize the gaming experience by adding visual and auditory stimuli that were absent from the purely mechanical versions of the '60s and '80s.

