$info=rt1715lc
$mame
0.140 [Miodrag Milanović, Robbbert]

Robotron PC-1715 (latin/cyrillic), Robotron, 1986

The PC 1715 or 1715, robotron. Following its introduction in 1985, the standard computer in the GDR in the 1980s He also was among the SKR-CM code exported in 1904 in the USSR and other CMEA countries. The PC used was a 1715 U880 chip with a 2.5 MHz processor, which was identical to the Z80 processor ZILOG. (Another U880 was found in the corresponding keyboard as a controller for the same.) Other facilities included 64 KB RAM, 2 KB of ROM and 2 floppy drives, each 5.25 inches with initially each 160 KB and later devices, depending on the operating system, to each 800 kilobyte (source, traslated for german: http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/PC_1715).

