$info=rx15
$mame
0.239 [DBWBP]

RX15 Digital Rhythm Programmer, Yamaha, 1984

Budget version of the RX11, priced at 449 pounds compared to the 799 that Yamaha was asking for its big brother. Same exact box, but some features together: fewer sounds, slightly limited memory, and no individual output for instruments. The ease of use and the quality of the digital sounds are the same, making it a good drum machine for professionals on a budget. The all-plastic body, the large dimensions compared to the features offered and the technological limitations (including a non-backlit LCD) make this first series of RX today a not very good choice compared to subsequent models, today still easy to find (source, traslated from Italian: https://yamahablackboxes.com/it/collezione/yamaha-rx15-batteria-elettronica/).

