$info=rz1
$mame
0.196 [Arashikage, Dirk Best, R. Belmont]

RZ-1, Casio, 1986

Casio's RZ-1 came out in 1986 and in its time, it was pretty good. It has 12 PCM sampled drum sounds - basic sounds, and nothing to get excited about either. They included 3 toms, kick, snare, rim, open/closed hh, ride, crash, cowbell and clap. They don't sound like real drums, but they do sound electronic and maybe a little different than more common Roland and Linn drum machines. They have been used in lots of Hip Hop and House tracks.
A real special feature (for its time) was on-board sampling designed to let you create up to four of your own percussion sounds. Now, the sampling specs are pretty bad with just a 20kHz sample rate and only 0.2 seconds of sample time per each of the four sample pads (or one 0.8 second sample). Its a very lo-fi sound, which may be a good thing. The only editing you can do with your samples is a simple low-pass tone adjust (source: http://www.vintagesynth.com/casio/rz1.php).

DRIVER:
casio/rz1.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Good
Color: Good
Sound: Imperfect
Graphics: Good
