$info=s3000
$mame
0.283 [R. Belmont]

S3000, Akai, 1993

Professional sampler introduced in 1993, featuring a 16-bit architecture with support for up to 32 MB of sample memory (expandable). It boasts an improved user interface compared to earlier models, with a larger display and simplified navigation. The device includes two 3.5" floppy disk slots, full MIDI connectivity, balanced audio outputs, and options for hardware expansions such as additional filters or external AD/DA converters. Designed for professional studios, it offers advanced editing tools—including LFO modulation, multidimensional envelopes, precise looping, and sophisticated sample management—all delivered with reliable audio quality and reduced loading times.

