$info=s330
$mame
0.288 [DBWBP]

S-330 Digital Sampler, Roland, 1988

The Roland S-330 Digital Sampler is a legendary rack-mount (1U) digital music sampler introduced by the Japanese company Roland in 1988. Originally conceived as a compact and affordable version of the top-of-the-line Roland S-550, the S-330 became an icon of electronic music production in the late 1980s and 1990s, particularly prized for its characteristic “warm and gritty” tone, ideal for genres such as hip-hop, ambient, techno, and vintage jungle.

