$info=sabavpl2
$mame
0.130 [Juergen Buchmueller, Frank Palazzolo, Sean Riddle]

SABA Videoplay 2, SABA, 1978

Play the video console of Saba is a clone of the Fairchild Channel F, the first video game with interchangeable modules. As revolutionary as the idea of the interchangeable games in the appearance of the console also had (previously there was only consoles with built-in software, usually Pong), the technique of video play could not keep up with the short time later put on the market Atari VCS. There are two different models of Saba, and Video Play Video Play 2 Both, however, differ only marginally from each other, the most noticeable change is the stick (see picture above, the left controller from the video channel, the right channel on the video 2). Otherwise see both consoles from the same, it was already found devices that are labeled as outside and inside and play video play video second (source, traslated from german: http://www.zock.com/8-Bit/D_Videoplay.HTML).

DRIVER:
fairchild/channelf.cpp

