$info=sacstate
$mame
0.142 [Robbbert]

SacState 8008, SacState, 1973

A while back we looked at the Altair, one of the first mass produced “personal?? computers. Before Altair, though, something had to advance computer technology to a point where the Altair could be successful. That computer is the SacState 8008. As the 1970s dawned, the rate of development and advancement in computer technology seemed to be gaining speed exponentially. The transition from tubes to transistors was measured in decades, but the transition from transistors to integrated circuits was merely years. Then came very large scale integrated (VLSI) circuits. These circuits would contain all that was necessary to make them behave as one type of circuit in one case, but another type of circuit in another all by changing the instructions on the ROM (source: http://atomictoasters.com/2011/11/before-the-altair-the-sacstate-8008/).

DRIVER:
skeleton/sacstate.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Preliminary
Color: Good
Sound: Good
Graphics: Good
Save State: Supported

SOFTWARE LIST:
-

RESOURCES:
Snap, Title, Icon and machine picture (in "Cabinet" collection).

WIP:
- 0.146u5: Added 'comments. Fixed input ports [Robbbert].
- 0.142: Robbbert added skeleton driver of 'SacState 8008' system.

ROMSET:
2048 bytes in 8 files / 1.69Kb packed

$end
