$info=sagafoxf80
$mame
0.232 [Alessandro Liberalato]

Saga Fox/F80, Sistemi Avanzati Gestione Aziendale, 1980

Among the various CP/M computers on the market in the eighties there is one of Italian production that is rather interesting and curious, also thanks to its resemblance to the American Intertec Superbrain ... it is the SAGA Fox F80. The SAGA Fox is a computer manufactured by S.A.G.A. of Milan, whose acronym stands for "Advanced Systems for Business Management" which in 1980 released this CP / M computer dedicated precisely to business users and companies. It is not the only computer they produced, in fact, although less widespread, there was also the SAGA Bip, released two years later, which was completely the same as the SAGA Fox in terms of electronics, but with a detachable keyboard. The Bip computer case looked a lot like the DMD 900 case, another computer that we will see in another article. The SAGA FOX, on the other hand, is an all-in-one with a monitor, keyboard, transformer and two floppy drives in a single rugged case (source, traslated from Italian: https://www.apuliaretrocomputing.it/wordpress/?p=8824).

DRIVER:
