$info=saikyopc
$mame
0.280 [TeamEurope, David Haywood]

Manabi no Sai-Kyo-Oh ni Nare! Sai-Kyo-Oh Zukan PC (Japan), Bandai, 2020

It’s a portable educational device designed for children, combining learning with play through an interactive interface and an engaging design. Equipped with an LCD screen and a simplified keyboard, it offers quizzes, challenges, and educational activities covering subjects like math, science, language, and general knowledge—complete with a reward system that motivates progress. The "Sai-Kyo-Oh" (Supreme King) theme turns studying into an adventure, where players "level up" by answering questions correctly. The device also features voice recording capabilities and audio feedback to make the experience even more immersive. Powered by batteries, it’s durable and ideal for everyday use at home or in school. Launched in Japan in 2020, it targets young audiences with a playful, stimulating approach to learning.

