SAPI-1 ZPS 1, Tesla, 1985

The SAPI-1 was a computer produced in the former Czechoslovakia by Tesla since 1980. It was designed by Eduard Smutný (hardware) and his brother Tomáš Smutný (software), and based on the Intel 8080/2 MHz clone (and later Z80). The SAPI-86 was also developed as a 8086 clone of the PC (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SAPI-1).

