$info=sapizps3a
$mame
0.151 [Robbbert]

SAPI-1 ZPS 3 (terminal), Tesla, 1985

The SAPI-1 was a computer produced in the former Czechoslovakia by Tesla since 1980. It was designed by Eduard Smutný (hardware) and his brother Tomáš Smutný (software), and based on the Intel 8080/2 MHz clone (and later Z80). The SAPI-1 ZPS 3 ROM contains CP/M booting sequence, CP/M is booting from 8" Shugart floppy disk drives. Position of VideoRAM was moved from 3800 to E800 to allow CP/M running. The "Z" version of SAPI-1 ZPS 3 used Z80 processor clone instead of 8080 clone, video with 64 characters per line instead of 40 (source: https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/SAPI-1).

