StrongARM Risc PC, Acorn, 1997

In September 1996 Acorn launched the StrongARM RiscPC. The StrongARM RiscPC is similar to the RiscPC 700, but has a 202MHz StrongARM CPU and RISC OS 3.70. The main differences between the models were increasing memory, larger hard discs and, optionally, CD_ROM drives (source: http://chrisacorns.computinghistory.org.uk/Computers/SARiscPC.html).

