$info=saturn
$mame
0.113 [R. Belmont]

Saturn (USA), Sega, 1994

The Sega Saturn is a 32-bit fifth-generation video game console that was first released by Sega on November 22, 1994 in Japan, May 11, 1995 in North America, and July 8, 1995 in Europe. The system was discontinued in North America and Europe in 1998, and in 2000 in Japan. The Saturn sold 9.5 million units worldwide. While its installed base in the United States ended at 2 million, its installed base in Japan was more than 6 million units. While it was popular in Japan, the Saturn failed to gain a similar market share in North America and Europe against its main competitors: Sony's PlayStation and later the Nintendo 64. In 2009, video game website IGN chose the Saturn to be their 18th best video game console of all time, out of their list of 25 (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sega_Saturn).

DRIVER:
sega/saturn.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Preliminary
Color: Good
Sound: Imperfect
Graphics: Good
Save State: Unsupported

SOFTWARE LIST:
saturn.xml, photo_cd.xml, sat_cart.xml

RESOURCES:
Snap, Title, Icon, machine picture (in "Cabinet" collection), Control Panel, Flyer, pdf Manual, Marquee and PCB.

WIP:
- 0.249: Replaced abbreviated country names with full names in descriptions in 'saturn.xml' [ArcadeShadow].
- 0.247: Remove some residual debugging stuff [AJR].
- 0.234: Improved metadata for several items and updated metadata (name; year) in 'saturn.xml' [ArcadeShadow].
- 0.195: Encapsulated existing CD-ROM emulation as device [AJR].
- 0.180: Various changes: Worked around VDP1 timings in Sega Saturn, fixes regression with Batman Forever gameplay speed. Added Rotation Parameter read control register, fixes at least Riddler stage ROZ positioning in Batman Forever [Angelo Salese].
- 0.164: Added 'preliminary CD-DA routing to SCSP EXTS parallel port, fixes CD-Rom player equalizer in Sega Saturn [Angelo Salese].
- 0.151: Added 'dump of Ultraman support cart in soft list [Team Europe].
- 0.148u3: Converted carts to be slot devices and enabled battery RAM carts support [Fabio Priuli].
- 0.143u4: Inputs to use PORT_CONDITION instead of PORT_CATEGORY [Fabio Priuli].
- 0.143u2: Added 'cycle remainder for FRC in SH-2, fixes a tight loop in Astal. Implemented IRQ pending and SCU IRQ enable register mechanism, allowing Choice Cuts to boot up to the title screen [Angelo Salese].
- 0.142u5: Verified saturn BIOS 1.01 labels [ElBarto]; moved intback command inside a timer and hooked up SMPC direct mode inputs in Sega Saturn, allows it to load the CD menu and makes the diagnostic cart to be operational. Added PAL timing support for Sega Saturn Implemented CART DRAM emulation in Sega Saturn [Angelo Salese].
- 0.126: Added 'ROM cartridge support. Fixed mem_mask regressions [R. Belmont].
- 0.115: Preliminary CDROM, backup, & input support. Fixed sound. Still marked NOT_WORKING as only a few games do anything [R. Belmont].
- 0.113: R. Belmont readded Sega Saturn (USA) (not working)' system.
- 0.112: Saturn driver back up to date so it starts up and shows the boot screens properly [R. Belmont].
- 0.37b15: Added 'SEGA Saturn' system. Many fixes. The driver now boots up and displays splash screen, but it's still non-functional [James Forshaw].

ROMSET:
1048576 bytes in 2 files / 891.46Kb packed

$end
