$info=sb2m600b
$mame
0.36RC1 [Paul Daniels]

Superboard II Model 600 (Rev. B), Ohio Scientific, 1978

The Superboard II, also called Model 600, was quite the same board as the british clone Compukit UK-101. It came fully assembled and did not featur neither power supply (user had to build or buy a 5V external power supply), / nor RF modulator to display video output on a standard TV, but only a composite video output. A 40 pin IC socket allowed an expansion board and OSI bus to be connected, giving access to memory expansion (up to 64 KB) and floppy drive controller (source: http://www.oldcomputermuseum.com/superboard_2.html).

