Schachcomputer SC 2, VEB Funkwerk Erfurt, 1981

Schachcomputer SC 2, a dedicated chess computer manufactured from 1981 until 1983 by VEB Funkwerk Erfurt, in 1983 renamed to VEB Mikroelektronik „Karl Marx“ Erfurt. The SC 2 ran on an 8-bit U880 CPU, which was an unlicensed Z80 clone, and had 9 KB ROM and 1 KB RAM. The chess program was an apparently re-engineered, slightly modified clone of Ron Nelson's program of the Chess Challenger 10 C manufactured by Fidelity Electronics (source: https://www.chessprogramming.org/SC_2).

