$info=schess
$mame
0.221 [hap, bataais]

Sensor Chess, SciSys / Heuristic Software, 1981

Released in 1981 the Sensor Chess was SciSys's bid for a slice of the rapidly growing tabletop press sensory market. This model was in direct competition with the Fidelity's Chess Challenger Voice Sensory and the Novag Super Sensor IV. The Sensor Chess was released in two versions, in grey (see below) and in the plastic simulated wood finish. The chess computer is unusual in that the LEDs on each square and the keypad are located below the chessboard surface, which is translucent (source: http://www.chesscomputeruk.com/html/sensor_chess.html).

