$info=scpchess
$mame
0.221 [hap, Sean Riddle]

Sensor Computachess (1985 version), Newcrest Technology / CXG Systems / Intelligent Chess Software, 1985

CXG Sensor Computachess, a dedicated chess computer with integrated travel sensory pegboard. It was the first own computer under the brand name CXG, manufactured by White and Allcock, the forerunner of Newcrest Technology. It was in 1981, when Eric White started to collaborate with David Levy and Kevin O'Connell on the software for the dedicated units. Levy and O'Connell were just in the process to loosen their relationship with SciSys, and their company Philidor Software was about to become Intelligent Software at that time (source: https://www.chessprogramming.org/CXG_Sensor_Computachess).

