$info=scpchessa
$mame
0.221 [hap, Sean Riddle]

Sensor Computachess (1981 version), White and Allcock / CXG Systems / Intelligent Software, 1981

The Advanced Portachess is a portable electronic chessboard (17.7x14.1x2.6 cm) launched on the market by Newcrest Technology in 1982. The moves are inserted with pressure sensitive contacts, while the chessboard announces its moves using 16 LEDs. The power supply is battery (4 x AA) or from the mains, with a 9V power supply. There are 8 game levels and 150 opening half-moves. The processor is a 4-bit HD44801 C89, with a clock frequency of 1 MHz. There are 2.5 KByte of ROM and 128 Byte of RAM (source, traslated from Italian: https://museoscacchi.wordpress.com/2011/03/27/newcrest-advanced-portachess/).

