$info=sdk80
$mame
0.164 [Nigel Barnes]

SDK-80, Intel, 1975

The 8080 System Design Kit (SDK-80) of 1975 provided a training and prototype vehicle for evaluation of the 8080 microcomputer system (MCS-80), clocked at 0.5 MHZ (1.95 uS instruction cycle time). The SDK-80 allowed interface to an existing application or custom interface development. A monitor ROM was provided. - RAM 256 bytes expandable to 1 KB - ROM 2 KB expandable to 4 KB - SIZE / WEIGHT 12 (W) x 0.5 (D) x 6.75 (H) inch - I/O PORTS Parallel (24 lines expandable to 48 lines), Serial 4800 baud (source: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intel_System_Development_Kit#Intel_SDK-80).

