$info=sdtora
$mame
0.273 [Mr. Lars]

Sphinx Dominator (v2.04), Newcrest Technology / CXG Systems, 1989

Older versions do not necessarily play weaker, but they do contain some unpleasant program errors that have cost the Dominator many a half or full point. The following trick makes it easy to determine which program version you are dealing with: Hold down the knight and pawn keys and simply switch on the device. The two four-digit displays will then show "Test" and the respective version number. The following report describes the development of the chess program first used in the CXG Sphinx Galaxy and later in the Dominator (source, traslated from German: https://www.schach-computer.info/wiki/index.php/CXG_Sphinx_Dominator).

