$info=se3010
$mame
0.280 [anonymous]

SE3010 Teletext Editing Terminal, Softel Electronics, 1987

This is a professional terminal designed specifically for creating and editing Teletext pages, primarily used by television broadcasters in the 1980s. Based on dedicated hardware and featuring a monochromatic text-based interface, it allowed operators to compose, format, and transmit simple text and graphic content—such as news, weather updates, or TV schedules—in the standard Teletext format (Ceefax/ORACLE). Equipped with an extended keyboard offering quick-access functions and control codes, it was engineered for intensive use in broadcast environments. While it lacked advanced graphical capabilities, it delivered precision and reliability in managing data transmitted via television signals. It served as a crucial tool in the pre-web era for disseminating digital information over the airwaves.

