0.288 [DBWBP]

SE 41, Orla, 198?

The "Orla SE 41" is a rare vintage standalone MIDI sound module and arranger, designed and manufactured in Italy by Orla, a company based in the Marche region (headquartered in Castelfidardo, the famous musical instrument district). This device was primarily developed as an accompaniment instrument for MIDI accordions and electronic keyboards. In terms of sound, it functions as a combination of a synthesizer, organ, string machine, and drum machine, all housed in a single standalone module.

