$info=se440bx2
$mame
0.286 [The Retro Web]

SE440BX-2 "Seattle 2", Intel, 1998

Intel SE440BX-2 "Seattle 2" ATX-form-factor motherboard (307×198 mm), second-generation model based on the Intel 440BX chipset (codename "Seattle"). Designed to facilitate the transition from the previous SE440BX, it supports Slot 1 Pentium II, Pentium III, and Celeron processors with a 100 MHz system bus. It features an AGP slot for accelerated graphics cards, three PCI slots, one ISA slot, and one shared PCI/ISA slot for expansion. The motherboard supports up to 768 MB of PC100 SDRAM memory via three DIMM slots. Some versions include integrated onboard audio. Aimed at entry-level workstations and business-oriented desktop PCs in the late 1990s, this platform offered a stable and high-performance solution for the Windows 98/NT era prior to the introduction of later chipsets such as the i810/i820. It features a typical Intel industrial design with high-quality components ensuring prolonged reliability in professional environments.

