Mocchiri Pet Mocchimaruzu (2018 version, set 1), Sega Toys, 2018

It’s a portable electronic toy released in 2018, inspired by the Mocchiri Pet franchise. Designed for children, it simulates caring for a virtual pet through tactile interactions: the device responds to touch, movement, and pressure with sounds, lights, and animations. It has no screen, but a soft, rounded design that makes it a cuddly object. Battery-powered, it offers a reassuring sensory experience focused on affection and playful responsibility, typical of modern virtual pets.

