0.165 [David Haywood]

Picture Magic, Sega, 1996

The Sega Picture Magic is a graphic tablet released in 1996 in Japan designed for use with the Sega Digio SJ-1 and the Sega PriFun. The PMagic can be used to overdraw, squeeze, reshape, and/or enhance photos taken off the SmartMedia Card. The output is A/V (composite) and the tablet is 22 x 18 cm and comes with a plastic pen. The system is based on the Sega 32X hardware. It accepts 5V SmartMedia cards (source: http://segaretro.org/Sega_Picture_Magic).

