$info=sgx
$mame
0.120 [Wilbert Pol]

SuperGrafx, NEC / Hudson Soft, 1989

The SuperGrafx is video game console created by NEC. It is an upgraded version of the PC Engine (known as the TurboGrafx-16 in North America), released exclusively in Japan, primarily in response to the Super Famicom (Super Nintendo Entertainment System outside of Japan) by Nintendo. Originally announced as the PC Engine 2, the machine was purported to be a true 16-bit system with improved graphics and audio capabilities over the original PC Engine. Expected to be released in 1990, the SuperGrafx was rushed to market, debuting several months earlier in late 1989 with only modest improvements over the original PC Engine (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SuperGrafx).

