3072 bytes in 3 files / 2.86Kb packed

$end
$info=shredmjr
$mame
0.217 [Sean Riddle, David Haywood]

Shredmaster Jr (NTSC), dreamGEAR, 2007

The dreamGear Shredmaster JR is a game controller that is designed to look like a real guitar, but is made of lightweight materials so kids can use it for long periods without it getting too heavy. The Shredmaster JR includes AV cables and connects directly to any TV that has AV inputs. The game runs from the guitar and features 10 licensed songs to allow your kids to shred away. The song list includes some well known rock classics including Smoke on the Water, I Love Rock and Roll, Iron Man, You Give Love a Bad Name, Billion Dollar Babies, Hotel California, Paradise City, Smells Like Teen Spirit, Paranoid, and Master of Puppets. The game also allows kids to make up their own music (source: https://www.i4u.com/16391/dreamgear-shredmaster-jr-micro-plug-n-play-guitar).

DRIVER:
