$info=siena_us
$mame
0.288 [Nigel Barnes]

Siena (US), Psion, 1996

The Psion Siena, launched on the global market in 1996, never received a modified hardware variant or a name change specifically for the U.S. market, unlike the Psion Revo, which was released years later (and marketed in the U.S. as the Diamond Mako). However, the version distributed in the United States featured specific customizations in terms of software localization, firmware, and packaging to adapt to overseas standards.

