$info=sixtrak
$mame
0.281 [DBWBP]

Six-Trak (Model 610) Rev B/C, Sequential Circuits, 1984

It’s a 6-voice polyphonic analog synthesizer released in 1984, notable for being one of the first to feature an integrated sequencer and multitimbrality (up to 6 parts). Built around one oscillator per voice, an analog filter, and full modulation capabilities, it allows layering sounds or assigning them to separate sequencer tracks. Designed for composers and solo musicians, it combines compact size, versatility, and a distinctive analog sound. Its straightforward interface and affordable price made it popular in 1980s synth-pop and experimental music.

