$info=sixtraka
$mame
0.283 [m1macrophage]

Six-Trak (Model 610) Rev A, Sequential Circuits, 1984

Monophonic analog synthesizer (with multitimbral mode) released in 1984, featuring six-voice polyphony and an architecture based on a voice oscillator with selectable waveforms (sawtooth, square, pulse, and noise). It includes a 24 dB/octave low-pass filter, ADSR envelopes, a modulatable LFO, and a 100-step sequencer capable of storing patterns and real-time automations. Designed for composers and performers, it offers an intuitive workflow thanks to its front panel with dedicated controls and the ability to layer up to six different timbres, making it a versatile tool for sound design and music production of the era.

