$info=slegend
$mame
0.285 [hap, Berger]

Sphinx Legend, National Telecommunication System, 1992

The Sphinx Legend chess program was created by the Hungarian programmer Guyla Horvath and is based on his “Pandix” program that won the amateur world championship in 1987. The normal out of the box playing style is a little passive but you do have the ability to change its play in 9 styles ranging from ultra-cautious play when the program is WHITE and ultra-aggressive play when it is BLACK (style number 1), to ultra-aggressive play when the program is WHITE and ultra-cautious play when it is BLACK (style number 9). The normal style is style number 5 (source: https://www.spacious-mind.com/html/sphinx_legend.html).

