$info=smastmind
$mame
0.230 [hap, Sean Riddle]

Super-Sonic Electronic Master Mind, Invicta, 1979

Invicta's Super-Sonic Mastermind is founded on the original game of the same name. 1-4 players are trying to guess a combination of numbers that has been randomly selected by the computer. When a guess is entered, a response is returned indicating how many digits are correct and how many digits are correct but in the incorrect position. Depending on the difficulty level, players have a limited number of guesses to find the correct "code". The "Super-Sonic" in the name is for an upgrade of the original Invicta Electronic MasterMind that has added 'a timer and sound effects (source: https://boardgamegeek.com/boardgame/6906/electronic-master-mind).

