$info=smkcatch
$mame
0.280 [TeamEurope, David Haywood]

Sumikko Gurashi - Sumikko Catch (Japan), San-X / Tomy, 2021

It’s a portable electronic toy launched in Japan in 2021, inspired by the sweet, character-filled world of Sumikko Gurashi. Resembling a small, pocket-sized device with an LCD screen, it simulates a "catching" and collecting experience: using a simple aiming or motion-based mechanism, players "chase" and "capture" the various Sumikko characters that appear on the screen—like stepping into a mini virtual treasure-hunting game. Each character has its own unique personality and reacts with adorable animations and gentle sounds when found. The gameplay is relaxed and irresistibly charming, focusing on discovery and collection rather than competition. With its soft, colorful design staying true to the original aesthetic, the toy features large, intuitive buttons perfect for little hands. Powered by batteries, it’s designed for kids and fans of the series, offering a cozy, portable, and utterly kawaii-filled experience.

