$info=smsbr
$mame
0.175 [Enik Land]

Master System III Compact (Brazil), Tec Toy, 1992

The Master System 3 is a console released by Tectoy exclusively in Brazil in 2008. It is a continuation of the long-running Sega Master System line was it was seen in the country, succeeding the line of "Master System 3 Collection" consoles (which in turn followed the "Master System III Compact"). This Master System 3 has a shorter name and lacks a cartridge slot, relying solely on built-in games. It also opts for a radically changed design over previous consoles, presumed to be unique to Tectoy products. The Master System 3 comes with 131 built-in games (or so it claims), the same number as the last Master System 3 Collection console to be released. It also comes with two Sega Mega Drive-style six button control pads which plug into two DE-9 ports, although most of the buttons on the pads are redundant as the console has no built-in Mega Drive games (source: http://segaretro.org/Master_System_3).

