$info=snotecut
$mame
0.278 [TeamEurope, QUFB]

Super Note Club µ teen's time (Japan), Bandai, 1999

The Bandai Super Note Club µ teen's time, launched in Japan in 1999, is a portable electronic device produced by Bandai, designed as a digital organizer for teenagers, featuring calendar functions, reminders, simple games, and content related to the youth culture of the time. The full name—Super Note Club µ teen's time—clearly reflects its target audience: Japanese boys and girls aged 12 to 18, interested in fashion, music, school, and social life. The symbol "µ" (micro) suggests compactness and modernity, while "teen's time" explicitly highlights its focus: the time and life of teenagers.

