$info=snspell
$mame
0.157 [hap, Lord Nightmare, Kevin Horton, Sean Riddle]

Speak & Spell (US, 1980 version), Texas Instruments, 1980

The Speak & Spell line is a series of electronic handheld child computers created by Texas Instruments that consist of a speech synthesizer, a keyboard, and a receptor slot to receive one of a collection of ROM game library modules (collectively covered under patent US 3934233). The first Speak & Spell was introduced at the summer Consumer Electronics Show in June 1978, making it one of the earliest handheld electronic devices with a visual display to use interchangeable game cartridges (source: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Speak_%26_Spell_(toy)).

DRIVER:
ti/snspell.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Good
Color: Good
Sound: Imperfect
Graphics: Good
Save State: Supported

SOFTWARE LIST:
snspell.xml

RESOURCES:
Snap, Title, Icon, machine picture (in "Cabinet" collection), pdf Manual, PCB and Artwork Preview.

WIP:
- 0.157: hap and Lord Nightmare, Kevin Horton, Sean Riddle added 'Texas Instruments Speak & Spell (US set 1)' system.

ROMSET:
41483 bytes in 6 files / 34.74Kb packed

$end
$info=snspellc
$mame
0.170 [hap, Sean Riddle, Lord Nightmare, Kevin Horton, plgDavid(David Viens)]

Speak & Spell Compact (US, 1982 version), Texas Instruments, 1982

Think about the original Speak & Spell without a display. A slightly different version was sold in United Kingdom as Speak & Write. The Speak & Spell project was started in the year 1976 and created with the TMC0280 the first one-chip LPC speech synthesizer. Later refinements to the Speak & Spell chips resulted in the TMS5100, 5200 and 5220 Voice Synthesis Processors (VSP) for use in commercial products needing synthetic speech voice output from digitally-stored words and phrases. Speech data was stored in in up to sixteen 128K ROM chips (TMC0350) (source: http://www.datamath.org/Speech/SpeaknSpell_Compact.htm).

DRIVER:
ti/snspellc.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Good
Color: Good
Sound: Imperfect
Graphics: Good
Save State: Supported

SOFTWARE LIST:
snspell.xml

RESOURCES:
Snap, Title, Icon and machine picture (in "Cabinet" collection).

WIP:
- 0.170: hap, Sean Riddle, Lord Nightmare, Kevin Horton and plgDavid(David Viens) added 'Texas Instruments Speak & Spell Compact (US, 1981 version)' system.

ROMSET:
19664 bytes in 4 files / 17.67Kb packed

$end
