$info=snspellfr
$mame
0.157 [hap, Sean Riddle]

La Dictée Magique (France), Texas Instruments, 1981

La Dictée Magique (Speak & Spell in English) is an educational electronic game produced by the company Texas Instruments, in 1978. In France, it is the linguist Jacques Capelovici, then known for his role as referee, Master Capello, at the Games  of 20 hours, which participates in the development of the basic library of 142 words, divided into 4 levels of difficulty, and later those of additional modules, including one devoted to words deemed difficult (source, traslated from French: https://fr.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Dict%C3%A9e_magique).

