$info=softbox
$mame
0.148u5 [Curt Coder, Mike Naberezny]

SoftBox, Small Systems Engineering, 1981

The SoftBox from Small Systems Engineering Ltd. (SSE) adds CP/M capability to Commodore PET/CBM computers. It is a Z80-based single board computer with 64K RAM and 4K ROM BIOS, designed to run CP/M 2.2. Rather than mounting internally, the SoftBox is an external unit that connects to the IEEE-488 bus. Over IEEE-488, it can use the Commodore computer as its terminal and use the Commodore floppy drives under CP/M (source: http://mikenaberezny.com/hardware/pet-cbm/sse-softbox-z80-computer/).

