$info=sp3e8bit
$mame
0.128 [Kevin Thacker]

ZX Spectrum +3e 8bit IDE, Amstrad plc, 2002

The ZX Spectrum +3 looked similar to the +2 but featured a built-in 3-inch floppy disk drive (like the Amstrad CPC 6128) instead of the tape drive, and was in a black case. It was launched in 1987, initially retailed for ?249 and then later ?199 and was the only Spectrum capable of running the CP/M operating system without additional hardware (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ZX_Spectrum#ZX_Spectrum_.2B3).

