$info=spc4000
$mame
0.137 [Peter Trauner, Manfred Schneider, Robbbert]

Super Play Computer 4000, Grundig, 1979

The Interton VC4000 was the first and only gaming console that is built entirely in Germany. A very attractive price-performance ratio (advanced controller with continuously operating analog joysticks, two fire buttons and additional twelve function keys, less than the price as the main rival Atari 2600) could be the console, especially in the German market claiming for several years, to graphic and sound of other vendors were significantly exceeded. The identical with the Grundig Superplay 4000 computer console was built from 1974 to about 1982, the sale was not until 1978, however, with a price of around 500 at that time DM (source, traslated from german: http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interton_VC4000).

