0.128 [Kevin Thacker]

ZX Spectrum 80K, <unknown>, 1987

Mythical expansion 80k! Indeed, it seems that some were fitted with the Spectrum RAM 4164 rather than '4132. A small logic circuit it enabled the 32k of RAM in unused 4164. In practical use of the expansion in Basic you had to lower the RAMtop 32768 available so having two banks of 32k (enabled with the out) (source: http://www.freelists.org/post/zxspectrum/Esapnsione-80k).

