$info=specnext_ks1
$mame
0.287 [holub]

ZX Spectrum Next: KS1, SpecNext Ltd., Victor Trucco, Fabio Belavenuto, 2020

The retrocompatible ZX Spectrum Next model KS1, developed by SpecNext Ltd. with key contributions from Victor Trucco and Fabio Belavenuto. Based on a Z80 architecture running at 3.5/7/14 MHz, it features an ARM Cortex-M4 co-processor for advanced functionality. This model extends the original ZX Spectrum standard (1982) with 256-color graphics, hardware layers, sprites, enhanced AY/YM/ZX Beeper audio, a built-in SD card, HDMI and VGA outputs, optional Wi-Fi, and full compatibility with software and classics from the Sinclair ZX Spectrum. The KS1 model (KickStarter 1) is the first limited-edition release, produced in 2017–2018 for Kickstarter campaign backers. It comes with a black ABS plastic case and membrane keyboard. This project represents an open-hardware initiative aimed at retrocomputing, classic gaming, and educational development on an evolved platform that remains true to the spirit of the original Spectrum.

