$info=sq80
$mame
0.146u1 [R. Belmont]

SQ-80 Cross Wave Synthesizer, Ensoniq, 1988

The Ensoniq SQ-80 is a synthesizer from Ensoniq. It was basically an update to the original Ensoniq ESQ-1. Compared to the ESQ1, the SQ80 includes 43 additional waveforms (including 5 drumkits), an enhanced sequencer, and a floppy disk drive for storing patches and sequences. Synthesis-wise, the SQ80 introduced the so-called 2nd Reverb, a low-cost solution to simulate reverb-like effects. As with the first Ensoniq product, the SQ80 not only offers MIDI In and Out, but also a MIDI Thru jack. The SQ80 was the first Ensoniq product to feature their patented Polypressure Keyboard technology. Unlike the ESQ1 and Mirage, the SQ80 keyboard offers channel pressure and polyphonic pressure (aftertouch) as well as programmable hardness (velocity). Since the keyboard does not use mechanical sensors for detecting velocity and pressure, it is immune to contact problems (which ESQ1 and Mirage suffered from) and pressure sensor wearout (like conventional keyboards) (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ensoniq_SQ-80).

