$info=starwbc
$mame
0.157 [hap, Kevin Horton]

Star Wars: Electronic Battle Command Game, Kenner, 1979

Star Wars Electronic Battle Command Game, a hyperspace dogfight simulation that you can play by yourself or against three other players, the screen is a
grid made up of LED's (Light Emitting Diodes) which shows the coordinates. You can zoom into a particular coordinate as you search for other player's ships, there are basic, intermediate and advanced levels each with their own teaching modes, all accompanied with simulated battle sounds as you play (source: http://www.oocities.org/starwarstrader_nz/rare.html).

