$info=stepone
$mame
0.193 [Fredrik Ohrstrom]

Step/One, Ericsson, 1984

This is Ericsson's first attempt to get into the new and fully exploding PC market. The computer manufactured by Panasonic in Japan received a Swedish exterior design in the Ericsson light brown color. Ericsson's first computer was introduced in 1983 and claimed to be IBM-PC compatible. It had a special version of MS DOS ver 1.25 as an operating' system. It was argued that the ergonomics were something outstanding on this computer, nobody really understood how. Compatibility was a little bit so and that was probably the reason why step one never became a real success. Most DOS programs must be customized to run on Step/One (source, traslated from Swedish: http://www.pc-museum.com/ericsson/index.htm).

DRIVER:
matsushita/myb3k.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Good
Color: Good
Sound: Good
Graphics: Good
Save State: Unsupported

SOFTWARE LIST:
stepone_flop.xml

RESOURCES:
Snap, Title, Icon, machine picture (in "Cabinet" collection) and Marquee.

WIP:
- 0.194: Clone promoted to working. Refactored graphics circuit, added 'color in 320x200 mode, fixed text scrolling, and added '80-character 640*200 mode. Fixed speed issue by reducing CPU clock by 50% as suggested by RAM waitstates in the schematics. Added support for -ramsize with 128K option and 256K default. Emulated the INT7 pull down and up for the keyboard, and added 'support for three keyboard variants. Added high-resolution 640*400 mode, and added 'crude cursor support for 40-character mode. Added monochrome monitor support with palette to match the 525Nm P39 phoshor used in the Ericsson DU4721 monitor. Added printer support. Completed interrupt support, including jumper settings. Fixed crude support for 36*25 color text mode, and added 'graphics mode 0 (resolution depends on monitor used) [Edstrom, Fredrik Ohrstrom].
- 0.193: Fredrik Ohrstrom added 'Ericsson Step/One' system.

ROMSET:
16384 bytes in 2 files / 8.13Kb packed

$end
