$info=storio
$mame
0.206 [ClawGrip]

Storio (GB, English, 2011-10-17), VTech, 2011

The VTech Storio is constructively a good product, assembled well using a hard plastic, which allows it to withstand accidental drops and small impacts, and thanks to the transparent rigid plastic cover that closes like a book also reduces the risk of damaging the screen . The colorful and rounded design indicates from the first glance that it is a device designed for children. The screen has a decent resolution and good brightness, 3.5 inches are not many and in some contexts it turns out to be a little small, but the response to the touch is still very good. The Storio is also equipped with a Qwerty keyboard, a very interesting choice because it allows children to become familiar with the standard used by normal PC keyboards. Another interesting addition is the microSD slot, which allow you to upload songs, photos and videos to the Storio, which can then also be retouched and modified by children, adding fun effects (source, traslated from Italian: http://www.tabletperbambini.it/vtech-storio-console-rosa/).

DRIVER:
vtech/storio.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Preliminary
Color: Good
Sound: Preliminary
Graphics: Good
Save State: Unsupported

SOFTWARE LIST:
vtech_storio_cart.xml

RESOURCES:
