0.143u4 [Miodrag Milanović]

Sun 3/110, Sun Microsystems, 198?

Sun-3 was the name given to a series of UNIX computer workstations and servers produced by Sun Microsystems, launched on September 9, 1985. The Sun-3 series were VMEbus-based systems similar to some of the earlier Sun-2 series, but using the Motorola 68020 microprocessor, in combination with the Motorola 68881 floating-point co-processor (optional on the Sun 3/50) and a proprietary Sun MMU. Sun-3 systems were supported in SunOS versions 3.0 to 4.1.1_U1 and also have current support in NetBSD and Linux. The Sun 3/110 as a codename: 'Prism' (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun-3).

