SPARCstation IPC (Sun 4/40), Sun Microsystems, 1990

SPARCstation IPC is a workstation sold by Sun Microsystems. It is based on the sun4c architecture, and is enclosed in a lunchbox chassis. The SPARCstation IPC incorporate a Fujitsu MB86901A or a LSI L64801 25 MHz processor. The SPARCstation IPC is limited to use as a single-processor machine. Has twelve DSIMM slots for memory expansion. Slots can be filled individually giving a maximum of 48Mb memory. Can hold one internal 50 pins, single ended, fast-narrow SE SCSI drives and a floppy. It also supports external SCSI devices. There is no IDE/ATAPI support (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SPARCstation_IPC).

