$info=sun4_60
$mame
0.144u1 [Miodrag Milanović]

SPARCstation 1 (Sun 4/60), Sun Microsystems, 1989

The SPARCstation 1, or Sun 4/60, is the first of the SPARCstation series of SPARC-based computer workstations sold by Sun Microsystems. It had a distinctive slim enclosure (a square 3 inch high 'pizza box') and was first sold in April 1989, with Sun's support for it ending in 1995. Based around a LSI Logic RISC CPU running at 20 MHz, with a Weitek 3167 (or 3170) FPU coprocessor it was the fourth Sun computer (after the 4/260, 4/110 and 4/280) to use the SPARC architecture and the first of the sun4c architecture. The motherboard offered three SBus slots and had built-in AUI ethernet, 8 kHz audio, and a 5 MB/s SCSI-1 bus. The basic display ran at 1152x900 in 256 colours, and monitors shipped with the computer were 16 to 19 inch greyscale or colour (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SPARCstation_1).

