The Dick Smith Super-80 was a Zilog Z80 based kit computer developed as a joint venture between Electronics Australia magazine and Dick Smith Electronics. It was presented as a series of construction articles in Electronics Australia magazine's August, September and October 1981 issues. Many Super-80 owners chose to modify their machines to address the limitations of the original machine. The El Graphix kit added 'the ability to display lower case characters and 'chunky' graphics (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dick_Smith_Super-80_Computer).

