$info=supr200
$mame
0.280 [TeamEurope, David Haywood]

Supreme 200 (handheld), Fizz Creations, 201?

It’s a plug-and-play TV console controller designed to connect directly to your TV via AV or RF cable. It doesn’t have a built-in screen—instead, the game is displayed on your TV’s monitor. The device features an 8-way joystick, action buttons, and a simple digital display (either LED or a small LCD) for quick information. It comes preloaded with several games—often more than 100—including classic arcade titles, sports, and puzzle games, accessible from a main menu. Powered by batteries or an external power adapter, it operates independently without requiring a PC or gaming console. The design is durable, with large, easy-to-use buttons, making it perfect for kids and retro gaming enthusiasts alike. Introduced in the 2000s as an affordable alternative to traditional gaming systems, it delivers an instant, content-rich gaming experience.

