Supremo, Novag Industries / Intelligent Heuristic Programming, 1988

A wide range of features and an elegant SENSOR CHESSBOARD assure lasting playing pleasure. Choose between 48 levels of difficulty to match your skill. Special Blitz, Speed and Tournament levels. Very strong 32K Byte program and a new 16 MHz micro computer with 8K RAM. Take Back up to 124 half moves. 15,000 pre-stored openings from Master Chess. Offers the ability of complete game recall and its superb brain can solve up to mate-in-14 moves. A multitude of features can be chosen and displayed via the cleverly arranged Liquid Crystal Display. One other MAJOR FEATURE is an RS232 link to the NOVAG SUPER SYSTEM which enables you to connect your chess computer to a PC (most types), a domestic color TV or the beautiful NOVAG auto-sensory wooden tournament chess board for ultimate luxury. Plays with one set of 6 x AAA alkaline batteries or a special mains NOVAG adapter 8210 (source: http://www.spacious-mind.com/html/supremo.html)

