$info=sv8000
$mame
0.153 [ranger_lennier, Charles McDonald, Wilbert Pol, Robbbert]

Super Vision 8000, Bandai, 1979

The Bandai Super Vision 8000 is a video game console released by Bandai in 1979 belonging to the second generation. The console can be directly connected to a TV. This console was the last of the Bandai TV Jack console series but was completely different from the other consoles of the series. The Super Vision 8000 had a central CPU. The other consoles belonged to the first generation: they didn't feature a microprocessor, and were based on custom codeless state machine computers consisting of discrete logic circuits comprising each element of the game itself (Pong-style console) (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bandai_Super_Vision_8000).

DRIVER:
bandai/sv8000.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
