$info=svi728es
$mame
0.250 [openMSX]

SVI-728 (MSX1, Spanish), Spectravideo, 1984

Spectravideo was a American company that was selling MSX computers in many countries. The SVI-728 was one of the most popular MSX1 models in many countries. Looks almost identical to its predecessor, the pre-MSX SVI-328. The main chips also are same but its architecture is very different from MSX. The power supply is external and a little bit big (source: https://www.msx.org/wiki/Spectravideo_SVI-728).

