$info=svmu
$mame
0.147u4 [Sandro Ronco]

Visual Memory Unit, Sega, 1998

The VMU, or Visual Memory Unit is a memory card peripheral for the Dreamcast. Its official name was changed by Sega for each of the three key regions:
- Japan = Visual Memory System (VMS)
- North America = Visual Memory Unit (VMU)
- Europe = Visual Memory (VM)
The name was changed from VMS to VMU for the NA market as the name VMS was already owned and in use by the Digital Equipment Corporation for their VMS operating' system. It is not known why the name was changed again to VM for the European market, however the name VMU was commonly used in the UK (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/VMU).

