$info=swtpc09
$mame
0.153 [Robert Justice]

swtpc S/09 Sbug, SWTPC, 1980

When Motorola came out with the MC6809 microprocessor SWTPC came out with a new series of computers. These had a new case to reduce the radio frequency interference that was common among early personal computers. The new computers came in two versions. The SWTPC 69K which had the MP-B3 mother board that supported 56K of memory. The SWTPC S09 (shown here) had the MP-MB mother that supported a 20-bit address bus for a total of 768K OF RAM. I had several SWTPC 6800 systems so I just ordered a new 6809 CPU board and modified a old mother board for 20-bit addressing and expanded I/O addressing. I also got 2 extended addressing memory boards so I could have 112K of RAM (source: https://deramp.com/swtpc.com/6809/My_S09_Index.htm).

DRIVER:
swtpc/swtpc09.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Good
Color: Good
Sound: Good
Graphics: Good
Save State: Unsupported

SOFTWARE LIST:
-

RESOURCES:
