0.250 [openMSX]

SX-100 (MSX1, Japan), Yamaha, 1985

The SX-100 is a small MSX computer designed for gamers. It has a single cartridge slot on the right side. The power supply is external - see Yamaha VB03770. This model was sold in black (SX-100 DB), white or dark blue. It was aimed at the Japanese market and features a Japanese keyboard. The same model was also sold in Japan as the Victor HC-30 in black or red (source: https://www.msx.org/wiki/Yamaha_SX-100).

