$info=sx240
$mame
0.223 [DBWBP]

SX-240 8-Voice Programmable Polyphonic Synthesizer, Kawai Musical Instrument Manufacturing, 1984

The Kawai SX-240 is an eight voice, fully programmable polyphonic analog synthesizer released in 1984 as a follow up to the Kawai SX-210. It was manufactured by Kawai but originally released under the Teisco brand-name in Japan when Kawai bought out Teisco. The Kawai SX-240 and the Kawai SX-210 never got much attention due to entering the market during the time of the digital revolution and poor marketing. Its main analog competitors of the time were the Korg Polysix and the Roland Juno 6/60 (source: http://www.vintagesynth.com/kawai/kawai_sx240.php).

