$info=sy019s
$mame
0.286 [Angelo Salese]

SY-019S (UMC UM8498F & UM8496 chipset), Soyo, 199?

Soyo SY-019S AT-form-factor motherboard based on the UMC chipset (UM8498F northbridge + UM8496 southbridge), manufactured in the mid-to-late 1990s. It supports Socket 7 processors: Intel Pentium/Pentium MMX, AMD K5/K6, and Cyrix 6x86/6x86MX. The industrial design features predominantly 16-bit ISA slots, one or two PCI slots for limited expansion, support for 30-pin SIMM modules for DRAM up to 128 MB, integrated floppy/IDE controllers, and onboard serial and parallel ports. Power supply is AT type (with P8/P9 connectors). Typical of entry-level workstations and home PCs from the Windows 95/98 era. The UMC chipset offered an affordable alternative to the Intel/VIA chipsets of the time, delivering modest performance but sufficient for general-purpose use. It represents a widely used OEM solution in Asian PC clones prior to the transition toward the ATX architecture and more advanced chipsets in the late 1990s.

DRIVER:
umc/pc486vl.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Preliminary
Color: Good
Sound: Good
Graphics: Good
Save State: Unsupported

SOFTWARE LIST:
-

RESOURCES:
Snap and Title.

WIP:
- 0.286: Angelo Salese added 'Soyo SY-019S (UMC UM8498F & UM8496 chipset)' system.

