$info=sys80
$mame
0.36b16 [Juergen Buchmueller]

System-80 (60 Hz), EACA Computers Ltd, 1980

EACA produced a range of machines from about 1980 to 1983. While re-branding in different parts of the world was common, the "Genie" name seems to be EACA's itself. I've deduced this from the fact that where the "Genie" name appears, the EACA brand and name also appears, whereas in its other guises only the trademark (and name) of the distributor is present (e.g. the Dick Smith System 80) (source: http://www.classic-computers.org.nz/system-80/hardware_eaca.htm).

