- 0.271: Moved BK0010 floppy drive controller to a card device, and fixed disk writes [Sergey Svishchev].
- 0.269: Changed PC display to octal. Improved interrupt handling on 1801VM1, misc fixes (#12646). Allows bus error handlers on BK to deal with interrupt from STOP key (causes a HALT-mode IRQ and triggers access to unmapped region at 177674) [Sergey Svishchev].
- 0.266: Reuse Z80 daisy chain code for vectored interrupts; reuse z80_daisy_chain for QBus vectored interrupts; forward INIT signal to all cards on QBus (#12290) [Sergey Svishchev].
- 0.264: Improved trace trap processing, and added basic interrupt processing to the K1801VM1 [Sergey Svishchev].
- 0.263: Ignore least significant bit of PC when fetching opcodes. Corrected MTPS and MFPS to be byte-wide. Reject instructions not implemented by each variant. Fixed MTPS/MFPS data width and improved emulation of differences between variants. Added basic support for the K1801VM1 [Sergey Svishchev].
- 0.239: Power fail trap is NMI, added 'bus error trap [hap].
- 0.218: Changed disassembler and register display to use octal number format, and fixed disassembly of SOB instruction [AJR].
