$info=talkingbb
$mame
0.210 [hap, Kevin Horton]

Starting Lineup Talking Baseball, Parker Brothers, 1988

In?Starting Lineup Talking Baseball, one or two players take on the role(s) of Major League Baseball managers. Each player tries to out manage his opponent using teams made of up of actual MLB players. On defense, the manager can choose the pitch type and location. He can also choose to intentionally walk a player or to bring his infielders in to increase the chances of getting a runner out at home (source: https://boardgamegeek.com/boardgame/22585/starting-lineup-talking-baseball).

DRIVER:
handheld/talkingbb.cpp

