$info=tanodr64
$mame
0.109 [Phill Harvey-Smith]

Tano Dragon 64 (NTSC), Dragon Data Ltd / Tano Ltd, 1983

Released in the autumn of 1983, about a year after the Dragon 32 launch, the Dragon 64 offered both a 32K "compatibility mode" as well as a 64K enhanced mode. The 64 also added 'a RS232C serial port to it's specifications, making it one of the first computers ever with both serial and parallel ports. The 64's main advantage was the possibility to run the multi tasking operating system OS-9 by Microware, but delays in the release of the disk drive system crippled the 64 at it's launch (source: http://www.dragonwiki.com/wiki/index.php?title=Dragon_64).

