$info=teradrive3
$mame
0.280 [McRetro.net]

Teradrive (Japan, Model 3), Sega / International Business Machines, 1991

It’s a unique hybrid of a personal computer and a console, launched in Japan in 1991, that integrates an IBM PC-compatible system (featuring an Intel processor and MS-DOS) along with a motherboard derived from a well-known Sega console, allowing it to run both PC software and console games—even simultaneously in some cases. Designed for both home and professional use, it includes standard PC peripheral ports (keyboard, mouse, floppy drive) and cartridge slots for the built-in console. The goal was to unify entertainment and productivity into a single device, appealing to tech-savvy users or enthusiasts passionate about both worlds. Despite its innovative concept, it achieved limited commercial success, but today it’s regarded as a rare and fascinating collector’s item—a symbol of an ambitious experiment during the era of digital convergence.

DRIVER:
pc/teradrive.cpp

