$info=tesa6240
$mame
0.163 [Retroport]

Etikettendrucker 6240, Tesa Etikett, 1984

As a laptop, the portable C64 home computer can not be called because firstly no battery is present (only an integrated power supply, which is connected via an IEC connector) and secondly the computer weighs around 11 kg. The detachable keyboard that also acts as a dust cover is connected via a special cable to the SX-64. In the empty compartment on the floppy drive some floppy disks or when rolled the Tasturkabel and Kaltegrätestecker can be kept. For the Tesa 6240 label printer also a Beiersdorf Company, various modifications to the standard SX64 were the Hamburg-based company ACOS, made. So the color monitor was replaced by a green monitor, the sound chip SID removed and the basic, Char and Kernalroms replaced with special Tesa versions. On the SX 64 Tesa thus runs to create labels and print to a printer not a normal C64 software more, but only a program. The Tesa 6240 version was produced in a limited edition for field staff of scotch, as well as for industrial companies. The selling price was more than 10,000, - DM, but then with an additional suit the system label printer. Unlike normal SX64 is available at the Tesa 6240 no label settings for the monitor. Here the entire control board has been removed. The modifications to the Commodore SX64 are continued even on the nameplate of the back (source, traslated from german:http://retroport.de/SX64Tesa.html).

