$info=test410
$mame
0.146 [Curt Coder]

T410 test suite, T400 uController project, 2008

The T400 ?Controller is an implementation of National's 4-bit COP400 microcontroller family architecture. It is intended to be used as a replacement for the original chip in SOCs recreating legacy systems. Its final target is to provide design variants that are compatible with the COP420/421 and COP410L/411L family members. All of them derived from the common t400_core design. Such a sample system has been implemented in several FPGA families (source: http://opencores.org/project,t400).

