TI-1250 (1975 version), Texas Instruments, 1975

Introduced three month later than the TI-1200 the TI-1250 was the "fully loaded" design. Basically both calculators were identical, most important was the higher sales margin during the price wars due to the additional memory. The later TI-1450 was nothing else than a cosmetically enhanced version of the TI-1250. Don't miss the colorful TI-1255 and the rare CONCEPT II (source: http://www.datamath.org/BASIC/TI-1200/TI-1250.htm).

