0.154 [Felipe Corrêa da Silva Sanches]

TI630 telephone, Intelbras, 1999

The 630 Intelligent Terminal is a device developed exclusively for the Intelbras Modulare, 4015, 6020, 10040 and 16064 exchanges. Its performance makes it possible to add to the normal function of a telephone device a series of operational facilities of the PABX to which it is connected. In this way, using the Terminal, it is easier and more practical to operate the various functions of the PBX. The Intelligent Terminal has a liquid crystal display that makes it possible to visualize all the procedures for using the facilities that will be shown step by step. This terminal leaves the factory with its default label, which can be used with any PBX from those mentioned above, and, to provide greater convenience, you also receive five specific labels for each PBX model (figures 2, 3, 4, 5 and 6), which can replace the standard label as needed (source, traslated from Portuguese (Brazilian): Original Manual do Usu?rio).

