$info=tibusan
$mame
0.157 [hap, Sean Riddle]

TI Business Analyst, Texas Instruments, 1976

The Business Analyst-I was introduced 1979 as a facelifted low-budget version of the Business Analyst. The rechargable battery pack was replaced by a simple 9V cell and the usage of a metal key plate gave a more modern appearance. Battery consumption of the Business Analyst-I was horrible, marketing guys from TI invented the after market sales of "Rechargable Kits"  RK2. They used two AA-cells and a step-up converter to generate the 9V of the calculator (source: http://www.datamath.org/Sci/MAJESTIC/Business-Analyst-I.htm).

