$info=tisr16ii
$mame
0.161 [hap, Sean Riddle]

SR-16 II, Texas Instruments, 1975

The SR-16 II followed soon in the steps of the rare and wonderful SR-16. It uses a very similar housing to the SR-50A but gave a cheap appearance with the few black keys and the printed keyplate. The rare SR-40 prototype was sandwiched between the SR-50A and SR-16 II. This calculator gave a first view into the future of Texas Instruments - the TI-30 (source: http://www.datamath.org/Sci/WEDGE/sr-16-ii.htm).

