$info=tk3000
$mame
0.155 [R. Belmont]

TK3000 //e, Microdigital, 1986

Despite the large amount of clones of the Apple II, we have some difficulties to find. This MicroDigital directly imported from Brazil is particularly cool. It is well built, the famous manufacturer of Hi Fi Brazilian who used to make good quality products. This machine has to be seen in the economic context of the mid-80s political power wants to protect its economy particularly threatened in electronics and computer skills. Local constructions will be promoted to the fullest. In 1996, domestic production of personal computers is still 65%. A policy of shamelessly cloning was introduced. It seems quite difficult to determine if it is was conducted in accordance with the cloned firms (Apple, Tandy Sinclair) Nothing is less certain. The second TK 3000 is an evolution of TK 2000 As the name suggests, this new machine is more modern, cloning the Apple Enhanced second. It is presented to the computer fair in Sao Paolo. The next evolution (1987) will be the TK 3000 Compact that includes 128 or 320 KB of RAM, a serial port and controller floppies in a smaller package (source, traslated from french: http://www.silicium.org/oldskool/apple/clones/tk3000.htm).

