$info=tku5s
$mame
0.286 [Angelo Salese]

U5S-TK-V03A (UMC UM8498F & UM8496 chipset), TK, 1994

Motherboard TK U5S-TK-V03A, in AT/ATX form factor, based on the UMC chipset (UM8498F northbridge + UM8496 southbridge), manufactured in the mid-to-late 1990s. It supports Socket 7 processors: Intel Pentium/Pentium MMX, AMD K5/K6, and Cyrix 6x86. The design features predominantly 16-bit ISA slots, one or two PCI slots, support for 30-pin SIMM modules for DRAM up to 128 MB, integrated floppy/IDE controllers, and serial/parallel ports. Power supply options include AT (P8/P9) or ATX, depending on the revision. Typical of entry-level workstations and home PCs running Windows 95/98. The UMC chipset represented an affordable alternative to Intel/VIA, offering adequate performance for general-purpose use. This OEM solution was widely used in Asian PC clones before the transition to ATX and advanced chipsets in the late 1990s.

