$info=tmc2000e
$mame
0.128 [Curt Coder]

Telmac 2000E, Telercas Oy, 1980

Telmac 1800 was a simple CDP1802 system introduced here in Finland around 1977. It was designed by Osmo Kainulainen, who built his own computer using RCA CDP1801, that he already knew from his job. It was an improved version over Telmac 1800, but I don't know who actually designed that one and how mane were made. 2000 had PAL version video chip (1864) with color also supported and more RAM, board could hold 16k bytes (source: http://www.hobbylabs.org/telmac.htm).

