$info=to16
$mame
0.217 [rfka01]

TO16, Thomson SIMIV, 1987

The Thomson TO16 is a PC compatible computer marketed by the French company Thomson SIMIV from September 1987. This machine exists in four basic versions: 1. TO16 PC: 1 5 "1/4 floppy drive of 360 KB, 2 ISA expansion ports. 2. TO16 PCM: TO16 PC with an integrated Kortex KX-Tel 2 modem (occupies one of the two ISA ports). 3. TO16 XPDD: 2 floppy drives, 4 ISA expansion ports, perpetual calendar. 4. TO16 XPHD: 1 floppy drive, 4 ISA expansion ports (one occupied by the hard disk controller card and one occupied by the EGA card), perpetual calendar, 1 20 MB hard disk, EGA display. The EGA graphics card is a GB100, officially from Thomson, but in reality designed and produced by Renaissance GRX for Thomson. The TO16-PC and TO16-PCM can optionally receive a second external floppy drive. The operating system supplied as standard is MS-DOS version 3.21, with MS-DOS Manager and GW-BASIC (source, traslated from French: https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomson_TO16).

