TO8, Thomson, 1986

TO8 is a computer created by the French company Thomson-SIMIV and released in 1986. It replaces its predecessor, the TO7/70 while remaining essentially compatible. New features (more memory, better graphics modes) are common to the whole range of third generation (MO6, and TO8 TO9 +). It has a tape drive and the BASIC 512 BASIC 1.0 and Microsoft integrated ROM and offers external floppy drive. An improved version, the TO8D, further includes a floppy drive 3 1/2 "integrated (source, traslated from french: http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomson_TO8).

