Nihon Isshuu - Boku wa Plarail Untenshi (Japan), Tomy / SSD Company LTD, 2004

Boku wa Plarail Unten-shi: Shinkansen & J?kikikansha-hen, loosely translated to "I am a Plarail Driver: Shinkansen & Steam Locomotive Edition" is a train driving game developed and digitally released by Tomy for the Wii (as a WiiWare title) exclusively in Japan on January 5, 2010. Based on Tomy's Plarail line of electric toy train sets, Boku wa Plarail Untenshi has players driving two trains: the N700 Series Shinkansen and the C12 Steam Locomotive. Intended for children, the game takes place on a fictional rail line made up of the toyline's signature blue plastic tracks, with a simplistic art style resembling a toy set (source: https://steam-games.org/game/87102/boku-wa-plarail-untenshi-shinkansen-j-kikikansha-hen/).

