ThinkPad 600X, IBM, 1999

It’s a business laptop released in 1999, part of the renowned ThinkPad series. Based on an Intel Pentium III processor (up to 650 MHz), it offers up to 192 MB of RAM, a 13.3" color TFT display, a hard drive up to 12 GB, and full connectivity (USB, serial, parallel, modem, and optional Ethernet/Wi-Fi). Designed for mobility and reliability, it features an ergonomic keyboard with TrackPoint and a long-lasting battery. It represents the pinnacle of 1990s ThinkPad design—combining durability, performance, and compactness for professionals on the go.

