$info=triplec
$mame
0.283 [DBWBP]

Triple-C Stereo Channel Multiband Compressor & Envelope, TC Electronic, 2000

Rack-mount audio processor released in 2000, designed for stereo multiband compression with advanced control over the signal envelope. It divides the signal into three independent frequency bands (low, mid, high), each equipped with dedicated parameters for threshold, ratio, attack, and release, enabling precise and transparent dynamic shaping. The unit features high-quality analog circuits and a “True Bypass” architecture to preserve the integrity of the original sound. Designed for sound engineers and producers, it is ideal for mastering, mixing, and processing stereo bus signals, offering both subtle adjustments and more pronounced dynamic interventions, with a clean and versatile character.

