$info=trs80m4
$mame
0.125 [Robbbert and unknown others]

TRS-80 Model 4, Tandy Radio Shack, 1980

The TRS-80 model 4 (ref 26-1068/69) was one of the last models of the TRS-80 series (and perhaps the less known). It ran at 4 MHz and displayed 80 columns x 24 lines in Model 4 mode, but was fully compatible with the TRS-80 model 3 and in Model 3 mode actually displayed 64x16 and ran at the Model 3's 2 MHz. It had 64 or 128 KB RAM, the 64 upper KB being used as a RAM disk. It had one or two 5?" floppy disk (184 KB each) and ran under TRSDOS 6.0 or 1.3, LDOS or CP/M (source: http://www.old-computers.com/museum/computer.asp?c=244).

