$info=ts1500
$mame
0.132 [Robbbert, Miodrag Milanović]

Timex Sinclair 1500, Timex Sinclair, 1983

The TS1500 was a slightly-upgraded development of the TS1000. Because of the big problem built around TS1000 in the US (keyboard and RAM Pack mainly), Timex Sinclair (TMX Portugal) designed TS1500 and offered it to Timex Corporation to solve the problems (RAM pack connection) and use the TS2000 (ZXSpectrum) silver case that were never used because they launched TS2068. It replaced the earlier machine's ZX81-like case with a ZX Spectrum-like case (in Silver), the same ZX Spectrum rubber keyboard, a custom ULA (it does not have the Ferranti ULA) and increased the onboard RAM to 16 KB (for more info see: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timex_Sinclair_1500#Timex_Sinclair_1500).

