$info=ts2068
$mame
0.37b2 [David Robertson]

TS-2068, Timex Sinclair, 1983

The Timex Sinclair 2068 (TS2068), released in November 1983, was Timex Sinclair's fourth and last home computer for the United States market. It was also marketed in Portugal and Poland, as the Timex Computer 2068. A variant of the machine was later sold in Poland under the name Unipolbrit Komputer 2086. The TS2068 was based on the ZX Spectrum and followed Timex's ZX81-based TS1000 and TS1500, and the Spectrum-based TC2048. Like the TS2048 was announced as a 40K memory machine (16K RAM + 24K ROM), so the 2068 was announced as a 72K machine (48K RAM + 24K ROM). (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timex_Sinclair_2068).

