$info=ts30a
$mame
0.285 [The MacDat Network]

TS30A, Compal, 1994

The laptop ODM released by Compal in 1994, designed for rebranding by various manufacturers. The base model features a 9.4-inch passive-matrix monochrome display with a resolution of 640x480 pixels. It is powered by either an Intel or Cyrix 486 processor (ranging from 25 MHz to 100 MHz depending on the configuration) and includes a Socket 3 slot. The system comes with proprietary 4 MB of RAM, expandable up to 20 MB. It boasts a compact design with an integrated trackball replacing the touchpad, a plastic chassis typical of the era—known for its fragility—and a CMOS battery soldered directly onto the motherboard. This model was marketed under several brands, including Epson ActionNote 650/660, Targa, MidWest Micro SoundBook, and Viglen Dossier 486 ST.

