TS30AS, Compal, 1994

The laptop ODM, released by Compal in 1994 as an evolution of the TS30A, was designed for rebranding by various manufacturers. This enhanced version features a 9.4-inch passive-matrix color display with a resolution of 640x480 pixels. It is based on either an Intel or Cyrix 486 processor (ranging from 33 MHz to 100 MHz) and includes a Socket 3 slot. The laptop comes with proprietary 4 MB of RAM, expandable up to 20 MB. It boasts a compact design with a built-in trackball, a plastic chassis, and a CMOS battery soldered directly onto the motherboard. It was marketed under various brands, including the Epson ActionNote 760C and other European and Asian OEMs, serving as an affordable alternative to business notebooks of that era.

