$info=ts30at
$mame
0.285 [The MacDat Network]

TS30AT, Compal, 1994

The laptop ODM, released by Compal in 1994 as part of the TS30 series, was designed for rebranding by various manufacturers. This variant was equipped with the Chips & Technologies 65540 graphics chipset and either 512 KB or 1 MB of VRAM, depending on the configuration. It optionally included the ESS AudioDrive 488 audio chip, along with mono or stereo speakers and a built-in microphone in "sound" models. The system was based on either an Intel or Cyrix 486 processor (up to 100 MHz with a DX4 multiplier) and featured a Socket 3 slot. It came with proprietary 4 MB of RAM, expandable up to 20 MB. The design was compact, featuring a 9.4-inch display (monochromatic or color passive-matrix, depending on the version), an integrated trackball instead of a touchpad, and a CMOS battery soldered directly onto the motherboard. It was primarily marketed as the Epson ActionNote 650/660 Series and also sold by other OEMs such as Targa and Midwest Micro.

