$info=tsfight2
$mame
0.193 [hap, Sean Riddle]

Street Fighter II (Tiger), Tiger Electronics, 1993

A stripped down version of the Coin-Op SFII, made to fit on a portable unit. You have two 'game types', basically whether you want to control either the character on the left or the character on the right. The player on the left could choose between Ryu, Ken and Guile, while the right-hand character could be one of Blanka, E. Honda and Zangief. Players could control the characters on a 'simplified layout' (ie. two buttons). Although special moves exist, keep in mind it's an LCD game - there aren't many (in fact Ryu and Ken are the only characters with two moves) (source: https://www.arcade-history.com/?n=street-fighter-ii&page=detail&id=100585).

