$info=tunixha
$mame
0.137 [Manfred Schneider, PeT, Paul Robson]

Tunix Home Arcade, Monaco Leisure, 1982

Emerson family console. Released in New Zealand. Greg Cook reports that two console versions existed; the earlier one had a wood grain look to it, while the later version was just black. The controllers had slightly different writing on them. One note of interest is that unlike most of the other Emerson family game collections, the Tunix library never used the short cart style; all of their carts were always the longer version. Cart packaging would vary in minor ways such as letter fonts, from batch to batch. The thin vacu-formed plastic trays used to hold carts securely in their boxes were apparently never used in Tunix boxes, perhaps to cut costs. The rear labels on Tunix carts were rarely consistent even on one game; they may have been colored in white or silver, or were simply not used at all. No one seems to know exactly why, but given the cost-cutting of most families, that likely explains it (source: http://guide.digitpress.com:8080/DP/cmf/game.cmf?gameid=33099).

DRIVER:
arcadia/arcadia.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Good
Color: Good
Sound: Imperfect
Graphics: Good
Save State: Unsupported

SOFTWARE LIST:
arcadia.xml

RESOURCES:
Snap, Title, Icon and machine picture (in "Cabinet" collection).

WIP:
- 0.137: Manfred Schneider, PeT and Paul Robson added 'Tunix Home Arcade' system.

ROMSET:
None required.

$end
