$info=turbos24k
$mame
0.263 [hap, Berger]

Kasparov Turbo S-24K, SciSys / Heuristic Software, 1986

Your KASPAROV TURBO S-24K is an advanced chess computer that automatically registers the moves you make on its built-in sensor chessboard. It has triple-colored LED’s that make it especially easy to operate. There are 32 different levels of skill and two digital chess clocks to show you the elapsed time for each side. It can take back any number of moves, replay games, announce mate, and display its thought processes. It also has a unique user-programmable library that allows you to store games, positions and openings in its permanent memory. These features make the KASPAROV TURBO S-24K one of the most versatile chess computers available. Your KASPAROV TURBO S-24K chess computer has a total of 32 different levels of skill. They include levels for casual play, tournaments, speed chess, analysis, problem solving and eight special junior levels for beginners. Remember that just like a human being the computer becomes stronger when it has more time to about its moves (source: original SciSys manual).

