$info=tvc64
$mame
0.132 [Miodrag Milanović, Sandro Ronco]

TVC 64, Videoton, 1985

The TV Computer (TVC) was a home computer made by the Hungarian company Videoton around 1986. The computer was based on the ZiLOG Z80 microprocessor and had a built-in BASIC interpreter. Programs could be loaded via tape or floppy. It had a built-in joystick, and a keyboard with Hungarian letters and nine function keys. TVC 64 had 64Kb of memory (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TVC_(computer)).

