$info=uniap2ti
$mame
0.166 [Felipe Corrêa da Silva Sanches]

Unitron AP II+ Teclado Inteligente, <unknown>, ????

Unitron Ap II was one of the first Brazilian microcomputer fully compatible with the Apple II US, had the internal and external form almost identical with single cabinet, integrated professional keyboard, CPU on a single board, eight expansion sockets, built armored source the cabinet, video monitor and other peripherals separate. In 1984, Unitron launched a version of Ap II called IT (Intelligent Keyboard), aiming to word processing in English, uppercase and lowercase letters. This was a variation of the original PC (source, translated from Portuguese: http://www.mci.org.br/micro/outros/apii.html).

