$info=unitron
$mame
0.146u1 [rbanffy]

Mac 512, bootleg (Unitron), 1985

The Mac 512 of the Brazilian company Unitron Electronics was the first Macintosh clone produced worldwide. The machine was an almost exact copy of Fat Mac (Macintosh with 512 KB of RAM released in September 1984) and its development began in 1985, ie, just one year after the original release of Mac. Never came into commercial production by interference of Apple Computer and the U.S. government, who complained of copyright infringement by the Brazilian government (source, traslated from portuguese: http://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unitron_Mac_512).

