$info=unsp
$mame
0.150

SunPlus u'nSP (ISA 1.0), <unknown>, ????

DRIVER:
devices/cpu/unsp/unsp.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Good
Color: Good
Sound: Good
Graphics: Good
Save State: Unsupported

WIP:
- 0.288: Use default constructor for compiler_state [Vas Crabb].
- 0.222: Fixed unsp20 ASR instruction. Fixed an unsp20 opcode decode priority bug that caused an ASR instruction to decode as a MUL [David Haywood].
- 0.220: Added 'individual members for FR status flags. Added Ext A6 support, and implemented Fraction on/off, SECBANK on/off, IRQNEST on/off, and move to/from FR. Fixed shift instructions and cleaned up GOTO MR. Respect interrupt enable flag. Disabled DRC for the time being [Ryan Holtz].
- 0.219: Implemented MULS and FIR_MOV operations [Ryan Holtz, N. Gilbert, smf]
- 0.217: Implemented goto mr, mul su, lslor, exp, jvc and jvs instructions. Added stubs for u'nSP 2.0 unimplemented extended instructions and registers [David Haywood].
- 0.210: Changed description to 'SunPlus u'nSP (ISA 1.0)'.
- 0.209: Fixed signed multiplication in recompiler (fixes controls in jak_pooh) [Ryan Holtz].
- 0.206: Implemented a recompiler with timing matching the interpreter. Added direct accessors for interrupt inputs and data segment with a view to more integrated SoC implementation. Improved logging [Ryan Holtz]. Improved S flag calculation for additions (fixes background scrolling in vsmile pooh) [Vas Crabb, Ryan Holtz].
- 0.196: Changed description to 'SunPlus u'nSP' [Angelo Salese].
- 0.150: Added 'u'nSP' device.

ROMSET:
None required.

$end
