$info=upd765a
$mame
0.149u1

NEC uPD765A FDC, <unknown>, ????

DRIVER:
devices/machine/upd765.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Good
Color: Good
Sound: Good
Graphics: Good
Save State: Unsupported

WIP:
- 0.287: Let the controller idle during soft reset [Curt Coder].
- 0.284: Add support for machines that have non-standard TS (two-sided) line hookups [R. Belmont].
- 0.282: upd72069 data rate control [cracyc].
- 0.281: Corrected recalibrate steps for Intel N82077 FDC (#14150). As documented in the datasheet it should be 80 for this FDC [Brice Onken].
- 0.272: Also set ST0_SE when seeking not ready drive (verified on real hardware) [cracyc].
- 0.270: Don't bail immediately when a sector address crc failure fixes ea interlock copy pro [cracyc].
- 0.268: Drive busy bits should not be cleared until a SIS is executed (#12585). The upd765 does not clear the drive busy bits until you issue a sense interrupt status command. Without this fix CP/M Plus on the QX-10 gives disk I/O errors because it expects the busy bit to stay set until it has a chance to issue the SIS command. Only clear drive busy bits on executing sense interrupt status command [Brian Johnson].
- 0.253: Minimally add some auxcmd commands to the 72069 (need docs!) [Olivier Galibert]. Turn back down excessive default verbosity level [cracyc].
- 0.252: Handle read/write completion interrupts the same way as any other interrupts [Carl].
- 0.251: Don't raise data interrupt on abnormal command termination [Angelo Salese]. Revert data_completion change and clear data_irq in fifo_r/w. Also disable clearing data_irq in msr_r. Clear wc if the found sector has the correct cyl in the address field [cracyc].
- 0.244: If waiting for additional command bytes, treat a data register read as an open bus write (tested on real hardware) and always trigger the DRQ line even if in nodma mode [Carl, Miodrag Milanović].
- 0.240: Check write protect line on write and format commands [SomeRandomGuyIdk]. Improved SRA and SRB signal generation, and added 'DP8473 reset interrupt [Sergey Svishchev].
- 0.237: Use the command sector size not the address size in read track and set the correct bit in st2 to indicate data crc error [cracyc].
- 0.209: Improved drive selection logic: Deselect drives upon reset, or select drive 0 for older controllers with multiplexed select lines. Deselect other floppies when using set_floppy [AJR].
- 0.208: Made Read ID return command if execution phase is reached but ID is not found [AmatCoder]. Changed ND flag behaviour to fix Speedlock copy protection regression [Michael Zapf].
- 0.201: Discard write FIFO data pushed when write command fails to find sector [Michael Zapf].
- 0.199: Clear ST1.ND on ID scan failure, implemented head load delay, and improved logging [Michael Zapf].
- 0.190: Added support for i82072 including sense interrupt status logic and motor on/off logic [Patrick Mackinlay].
- 0.186: Changed description to 'NEC uPD765A FDC'.
- 0.149u1: Added 'UPD765A' device.

ROMSET:
None required.

$end
