$info=uts20
$mame
0.132 [Robbbert]

UTS-20, Sperry Univac, 1980

Professional workstation based on Sperry Univac’s proprietary architecture, introduced in the early 1980s as an intelligent terminal for business and government environments. It integrates a bit-slice processor or custom microprocessor, a dedicated real-time operating system, and support for connecting to Univac Series 90/1100 mainframes via a proprietary network. The design is compact, featuring a built-in high-resolution monochrome display, an ergonomic keyboard with dedicated function keys, and options for external floppy disk drives or hard disks. It was used for data-entry applications, document management, and centralized database access in sectors such as finance, healthcare, and public administration. This pre-PC enterprise solution focused on security, reliability, and integration with legacy Univac infrastructures.

