Visual 100, Visual Technology, 1980

The Visual 100 was the first of the second series of display terminals released by Visual Technology. (The Visual 200 and Visual 210 made up the first series.) It was followed by the Visual 110 (which emulated the Data General Dasher series rather than the DEC VT-100) and the "top of the line" Visual 400. The second 8251 and 8116T seem to have been typically  populated. However, the program does include routines to drive these components, which probably would be installed to provide the optional serial printer interface (source: MAME driver).

