$info=v1050
$mame
0.133 [Curt Coder, rbramante]

Visual 1050, Visual Technology Inc, 1983

The Visual 1050 was an 8-bit desktop computer sold by Visual Technology in the early 1980s. The computer ran under the CP/M operating system and used 2 400KB, 5 1/4, SSDD, 96tpi floppy disk drives (TEAC FD-55E) for mass storage with an optional 10Mb external Winchester hard disk drive. In addition to the Zilog Z80 processor clocked at 4 MHz, the Visual 1050 also included a MOS Technology 6502 used as a graphics coprocessor (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Visual_1050).

