$info=vax785
$mame
0.146u5 [Miodrag Milanović]

VAX-11/785, Digital Equipment Corporation, 1984

The VAX-11 was a family of minicomputers developed and manufactured by Digital Equipment Corporation (DEC) using processors implementing the VAX instruction set architecture (ISA). The VAX-11/780 was the first VAX computer. The VAX-11/785, code named "Superstar", was introduced in April 1984. It was essentially a faster VAX-11/780, with a CPU cycle time of 133 ns (7.52 MHz) versus the 200 ns (5 MHz) CPU cycle time of the VAX-11/780. The memory subsystem was also upgraded to support higher capacity memory boards (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/VAX-11#VAX-11.2F785).

