$info=vcc
$mame
0.137 [Kevin Horton, Jonathan Gevaryahu, Sandro Ronco]

Voice Chess Challenger (set 1), Fidelity Electronics, 1979

Your VOICE SENSORY CHESS CHALLENGER is Fidelity's first thinking chess game that talks ... and sees every move you make. The most advanced state-of-the-art technology provides you with an amazing computerized opponent that plays chess with skill and cunning, yet allows you to control the levels of difficulty. Your VOICE SENSORY CHESS CHALLENGER is not a contrived chess board that has been gimmicked with lights and pushbutton keys - CHALLENGER is, in every sense, a versatile and talented computerized chess playing opponent. The voice feature is not a tape recording, but a computer created voice capability that talks in response to CHALLENGER'S thoughts or to a move made by the human player. A vocabulary of over fifty words will verbalize play action such as which piece was moved or captured, illegal moves, when your King is in check, etc., and it will tell you when it is verifying the locations of the pieces on the board (at your request) (source: https://www.spacious-mind.com/html/voice_sensory_challenger.html).

DRIVER:
fidelity/vcc.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Good
Color: Good
Sound: Good
Graphics: Good
Save State: Supported

SOFTWARE LIST:
-

RESOURCES:
Snap, Title, Icon, machine picture (in "Cabinet" collection), pdf Manual and Marquee.

WIP:
- 0.262: Changed description to 'Voice Chess Challenger (set 1)'.
- 0.208: Changed description to 'Voice Chess Challenger'.
- 0.137: Kevin Horton, Jonathan Gevaryahu and Sandro Ronc added 'Fidelity Electronics Talking Chess Challenger (model VCC)' system.

ROMSET:
40960 bytes in 7 files / 29.80Kb packed

$end
