$info=vdogdeme
$mame
0.187 [David Haywood]

V-Dog (prototype, earlier), VRT, 200?

Prototype of an interactive toy robot shaped like a dog, developed by VRT in the early 2000s. Modular design with a plastic body, rudimentary motion/touch sensors, and a motor for basic movements (head and legs). Battery-powered, featuring limited mono audio and no artificial intelligence—reacts to external stimuli through preprogrammed sequences. No wireless connectivity or PC connection; autonomous but highly basic functionality. This represents an experimental stage preceding the commercial launch of the V-Dog, focused on simple mechanics and basic behavioral feedback to gauge market interest in robotic household pets.

DRIVER:
nintendo/nes_vt02_vt03.cpp

