$info=vec1200
$mame
0.132 [Miodrag Milanović]

Vector 1200, <unknown>, 1987

The Vector 1200 industrial embedded system, introduced in 1987 for real-time automation and control applications. Based on a 10-MHz Intel 80186 processor with a proprietary architecture, it features 512 KB to 2 MB of RAM, EPROM for firmware, RS-232/422 serial ports, isolated digital I/O, and slots for custom expansion modules. The system runs a dedicated real-time operating system (often VRTX or OS-9) and is programmed in C or assembly language. It has been widely used in CNC machinery, electronic test systems, and process controllers thanks to its high reliability and deterministic response times. The rugged design includes a metal chassis, passive cooling, and an industrial 24VDC power supply. This system represents a pre-PC professional platform for critical applications where stability and timing precision were prioritized over graphics or user interface capabilities.

