$info=vector4
$mame
0.253 [Eric Anderson]

Vector 4, Vector Graphic, 1982

Vector Graphic?s Vector 4 was one of the first such dual-processor systems, introduced in 1982. It kept the S-100 bus but added an 8088 CPU. CP/M was still the standard operating system with MS-DOS available as an option. In 1984, the Vector 4-S appeared, which could read PC-format floppy disks. Introduced: 1982 (Vector 4), 1984 (Vector 4-S). Original Retail Price: $3,295 to $9,995 (4-S). Base Configuration: Z-80 and 8088 CPUs, CP/M (4)/CP/M-86 with GSX-86 (4-S); two S-100 slots (4-S); 128K RAM (256K max) (source: https://classictech.wordpress.com/2021/08/26/vector-graphic-vector-4-dual-processor-system/).

