$info=vegaplus
$mame
0.280 [Andrew Bickers]

ZX Spectrum Vega+, Retro Computers Ltd, 2018

It’s a retro portable console launched in 2018, inspired by the legendary British home computer of the 1980s. Featuring a modern yet nostalgic design, it comes with a built-in controller equipped with a simplified keyboard and a small LCD screen, crafted to faithfully recreate the gaming experience of original ZX Spectrum titles. The device includes hundreds of pre-installed games, easily selectable from an intuitive menu, and also allows users to load additional games via a microSD card. Despite being marketed as a plug-and-play solution for TVs (with HDMI output) and as a handheld gaming device, the project faced significant setbacks due to delays, manufacturing issues, and controversies—so much so that many units were never delivered to backers of the crowdfunding campaign. Today, it’s highly sought after by collectors as a symbol of an ambitious—but ultimately unfinished—tribute to the golden age of British gaming.

