$info=vg8235
$mame
0.81 [Jirou Kaneda]

VG-8235 (MSX2, Europe), Philips, 1986

The Philips VG-8235 belongs to the MSX 2 standard. For its release, Philips presented the VG-8235 as the first link of their audio-video-micro concept, being able to use the newly announced CD-i system, but few VG-8235 were actually seen connected to a CD-i. It was the successor of the the short-lived VG 8230, wich only had 64K RAM and a single sided disk drive (source: http://www.old-computers.com/museum/computer.asp?c=251).

