$info=vgpocket
$mame
0.188 [BeckieRGB]

VG Pocket (VG-2000), Performance Designed Products / JungleTac, 2005

Portable plug-and-play console with a built-in LCD screen, marketed in the 2000s as an affordable device featuring "100+ games." Compact design with a miniaturized analog joystick, A/B buttons, and a mono speaker. The games are simplified variations of classic arcade titles (such as Breakout, Snake, and Space Invaders), running on 8-bit embedded hardware—not actually based on the Atari 2600 architecture; the label "VG-2000" is purely evocative and marketing-driven. It lacks cartridge slots or expansion capabilities—all software is permanently soldered onto an internal ROM. Powered by AAA batteries. Intended for children and discount markets as casual entertainment, typical of pocket-sized TV game consoles from the pre-smartphone era.

