VIC-10 / Max Machine / UltiMax (NTSC), Commodore Business Machines, 1982

VIC-10, or MAX or Ultimax is presented at the Hannover Fair in the spring of 1982 along with the Commodore 64, with whom he shares the CPU. The VIC10 is thought of as the 'brother' less than the VIC20, a personal low cost targeted especially home entertainment. Aesthetically similar to the VIC20 but with a membrane keyboard (like the first Sinclair computer), the budget is quite minimal: 2Kb of RAM and a graphics resolution of 320 x 200pxl (source, traslated from italian: http://www.storiainformatica.it/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=286:commodore-vic-10&catid=22:commodore&Itemid=172).

