0.155 [Wilbert Pol]

HC-95 (MSX2, Japan), Victor, 1986

The Victor HC-95 MSX2 was made by JVC (Japan Victor Company) and released in 1986. The HC-95 is a personal computer with a 3.58 MHz Zilog Z80A processor, 64KB RAM, running on MSX Basic 2.0. It included two 3?" floppy disk drives and conformed to the graphics specification of the MSX-2 standard. The second CPU HD64180 is actually a Z180 clone. Contrary to populair belief, the HC-90 has the same specifications as the HC-95, but lacks the second floppy disk drive (source: http://www.msx.org/wiki/Victor-HC95).

