$info=videoart
$mame
0.261 [hap, Sean Riddle, Phil Bennett]

VideoArt, LJN Toys, 1987

It's a system for drawing/coloring pictures on the tv, not a video game console. The cartridge ROMs contain no executable code, only data for a title screen and vector pictures. On the title screen, press CLEAR to start drawing (no need to wait half a minute). Drawing with the same color as the picture outline is not allowed. To change the background color, choose one from the color slider and press CLEAR (source: https://github.com/mamedev/mame/blob/master/src/mame/misc/videoart.cpp).

