$info=virusrck
$mame
0.189 [R. Belmont, absence]

Virus Rack (Ver. T), Access, 2001

The Access Virus Rack is an Analog Modeling synthesizer with 2 oscillators and one sub-oscillator. Software Version 2.0 adds an additional 512 presets by replacing the demo song included in the original software version. There is also a noise generator, ring modulator, two multi-mode filters, two envelopes, a stereo VCA, and a saturation stage for cascade filtering, tube, and distortion effects. Two external inputs allow processing of external devices through the filters, gates and lo-fi effects. External audio sources can also be used to modulate frequency and ring modulation. The Virus Rack was first released in 2001 by Access Music of Germany (source: http://www.musicalbox.com/Sito2010/articolo.aspx?sez=CATALOGO&cat=000003%7C000028%7C6845432163&art=ACVIRUSR).

