$info=vis
$mame
0.177 [Carl, Sly DC]

Video Information System MD-2500, Tandy/Memorex, 1992

The Memorex/Tandy?VIS was a "Visual Information System" that also doubled as a gaming machine. The machine was only sold at Radio Shack, and the games released for the system were mostly educational. The system is notable for it's operating system, Modular Windows. A special embedded version of Windows 3.1, it acts as a precursor to the modern Windows CE. While there were plans to use Modular Windows in other devices like televisions, it appears that the VIS was the only released platform to actually use it (source: https://www.giantbomb.com/memorex-md-2500-vis/3045-153/).

