$info=vsmaxtx2
$mame
0.226 [David Haywood, Sean Riddle, Kev (FBN), Kamaal Brown]

Vs Maxx TX-2 50-in-1, Senario / JungleTac, 200?

Economic multi-game console marketed by Senario (under the alternative branding "JungleTac Vs Maxx") in the early 2000s. This TV game device features 50 built-in games based on a simplified NES/Famiclone hardware platform. It boasts a compact plastic design with two wired controllers integrated into the chassis, an RF/composite video output for connection to a television, and power supplied via an external adapter. The games are simplified variations of classic titles from the 8-bit era, often featuring reduced graphics and audio compared to the originals. Targeted at discount markets and low-cost retail outlets (e.g., supermarkets, toy stores), this console offered an affordable solution for home entertainment prior to the advent of modern digital consoles. Its construction reflects the essential design typical of budget TV games of that era, emphasizing affordability over premium hardware quality.

DRIVER:
