V.Smile Pro, VTech, 2007

The V.Smile Pro is a video game console released in 2007, designed and marketed by VTech. Thought for children aged 6 to 11 years, it relies on being educational. The console to a more rectangular appearance compared to the one before, the V.Smile and opens on top. The console is available in blue and silver sold with Scooby Doo, or pink and silver sold with the game Disney Princesses. Compared to its predecessor, it can display 3D graphics, while the V.Smile games are 2D. With its CD player, V.Smile Pro can also play audio CDs. The controller has an analog stick on the left side, 4 buttons on the right side, and 4 central buttons (Source traslated from French: https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/V.Smile_Pro).

