0.133 [Miodrag Milanović, Jonathan Gevaryahu]

VT220 (Version 2.3), Digital Equipment Corporation, 1983

The VT220 was a terminal produced by Digital Equipment Corporation from 1983 to 1987. The VT220 improved on the earlier VT100 series of terminals with a redesigned keyboard, much smaller physical packaging, and a much faster microprocessor. To meet the needs of various national regulatory agencies, the VT220 was available with CRTs that used white, green, or amber phosphors (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/VT220).

