$info=vt240
$mame
0.162 [Matt Burke, Balrog, Lord Nightmare]

VT240, Digital Equipment Corporation, 1983

The DEC VT240 terminal is a graphics terminal supporting DEC's ReGIS graphics commands as well as the Tektronix 4010 graphics commands. It was introduced in January, 1984. It was discontinued in April, 1987. The terminal base unit supports both grayscale and color monitors. When configured with a VR201 grayscale monitor, the terminal was sold as a VT240. When configured with the VR241 color monitor, the terminal was sold as a VT241 (source: http://terminals.classiccmp.org/wiki/index.php/DEC_VT240).

