The VT320 can work with standard American National Standards Institute (ANSI) functions. Set-Up: the VT320 has a series of set-up screens that list the operating features of the terminal. You can display these screens and change feature settings from the keyboard. For example, the VT320 has an On-Line/Local feature. You can only set this feature from set-up. When you use the "On-Line" setting, the VT320 can communicate with your host' system. To enter set-up, you press the Set-Up key. Chapter 4 describes set-up (source: http://dec.vecmar.com/products/productpage.asp?pid=3610-DEC_VT320_Terminal).

DRIVER:
dec/vt320.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Preliminary
Color: Good
Sound: Preliminary
Graphics: Good
Save State: Unsupported

SOFTWARE LIST:
-

RESOURCES:
Snap, Title, Icon, machine picture (in "Cabinet" collection), pdf Manual and Marquee.

WIP:
