$info=vz300
$mame
0.36b11 [Juergen Buchmueller]

VZ-300 (Oceania), Dick Smith Electronics, 1984

Dick Smith released the VZ-300 (same model as the VTech Laser 310) in 1985. It was basically a VZ-200 with 16K RAM (the VZ-200 had 8K RAM), a slightly updated BASIC ROM and a better standard keyboard. The 16K cartridge could be plugged into the VZ300, as well as a new 64K version, but it only gave a total of 34 KB. Only language machine programs could take advantage of the extra 32 KB thanks to the Z80 bank switching facility (source: http://www.old-computers.com/museum/computer.asp?st=1&c=980).

