$info=wangpc
$mame
0.144u7 [Anna Wu]

Wang Professional Computer, Wang Laboratories, 1985

The Wang Professional Computer is one of the first generation of competitors to the IBM PC: an MS-DOS machine that isn't compatible with the IBM at a hardware level. The case is roughly the size of an IBM XT, sideways on, but taller. At the front are two full-height 5?" drive bays; the right-hand one holds a 5?" floppy drive, and the left-hand one holds a Quantum Q540 hard drive, formatted to 32Mb (the boot ROM refers to this as a 'Winchester', as this page will from now on). From the design of the case, a twin-floppy configuration would also be possible (source: http://www.seasip.info/VintagePC/wangpc.html).

DRIVER:
wang/wangpc.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Good
Color: Good
Sound: Good
Graphics: Good
Save State: Supported

SOFTWARE LIST:
wangpc.xml

RESOURCES:
Snap, Title, Icon, machine picture (in "Cabinet" collection), Control Panel and Marquee.

