$info=wfcentro
$mame
0.224 [ClawGrip, Sean Riddle, David Haywood]

Centro TV de Diseno Artistico (Spain), WinFun, 200?

Console TV game plug-and-play WinFun "Artistic Design TV Center," marketed in Spain as a device for drawing and creativity. Compact design with a pen-shaped/stylus-like controller that interacts with the screen via your TV. Includes built-in artistic mini-games: free drawing, coloring, visual puzzles, and simple creative activities featuring basic 2D graphics. Composite/PAL video output for European TVs; power supplied via an external adapter. Designed for children aged 4–10 as an entry-level educational entertainment tool to help develop basic artistic skills. An inexpensive OEM product without official licenses, typical of discount markets in Spain and Europe during the 2000s–2010s.

