$info=wicat
$mame
0.150 [Al Kossow, Robbbert]

Wicat System 150, Millennium Systems, 1982

WICAT set a new standard of price performance with thè introduction of thè System 100. Nowthe System 150, packaged neatly within a CRT housing, offers even greater price performance. Included in a single, trim, desktop unit is thè processor, memory, CRT, Storage and Storage backup. A graphics version of thè System 150 is also available. Thè processor for thè WICAT System 150 is thè Motorola 68000, which runs at 8 MHz and executes approximately one million instructions per second. Although this processor has a 16-bit external data path, internally it supports 32-bit operation. Memory rangesfrom 256 Kbyte of dynamic RAM up to 1.5 Mbyte (source: original brochure).

