Wizzard (Oceania), Dick Smith Electronics, 1982

Dick Smith is a maker of pong systems, cheap computers, and clone game systems. They made this Creatavision copy in  addition to several PC 50X and 1292 machines. Pretty much the same thing as the OG version except for minor color variations and this console being a PAL unit, of course. There are also several add-ons that turn this machine into a makeshift computer, including disk drives, printers, modems, etc. Games came on Cartridges and tapes. Machine is compatible with the Colecovision via adapter (source: http://ultimateconsoledatabase.com/others/dick_smith_wizzard.htm).

