$info=wmbullet
$mame
0.140 [Curt Coder]

Bullet, Wave Mate, 1982

The Wave Mate Bullet was a Z80 single-board computer from the late 1970's and early 1980's which used the CP/M operating' system. This computer is rarely seen now but has historical value as an early microcomputer pioneer. It was sold in Australia, the USA and Europe and was apparently popular in academic settings. The Wave Mate Bullet runs CP/M 3.0 and CP/M 2.2 is available. It is available in many configurations but typically is found in a small chassis with two 96 tracks per inch 5?" floppy disk drives. The 5?" disks were formatted on both sides with five 1024 byte sectors per track with 80 tracks per side for a total of 800K per disk (source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wave_Mate_Bullet).

