X1 Twin (CZ-830C), Sharp, 1987

The Sharp X-1 Twin was a weird combination unit, featuring the X-1 computer (a Z80-based precursor to the X68000) and an integrated PC Engine. I use the term integrated loosely, the two systems shared the same shell, but little else. It's more like an Amstrad MegaPC than a Sega/IBM TeraDrive (source: http://nfggames.com/forum2/index.php?topic=2089).

