$info=xavaero
$mame
0.272 [TeamEurope, David Haywood]

XaviX Aerostep J-Mat (XaviXPORT, Japan), SSD Company LTD, 2005

Interactive fitness system for the XaviXPORT platform, developed by SSD Company Ltd. It includes an aerobic step platform equipped with pressure sensors connected to the XaviX console via cable, used for exercise games synchronized with video content displayed on a TV. The system is based on a proprietary 8/16-bit processor and comes with ROM cartridges containing dedicated software. It tracks steps, rhythm, and accuracy, seamlessly integrating real-world movement with on-screen action (e.g., jumping over obstacles, following choreographed routines). Designed for home users seeking light cardiovascular training, typical of the “exergaming” approach popular in the early 2000s. Requires specific XaviXPORT hardware—does not work on other consoles.

