PowerKIDS Jr. (XaviXPORT, Japan), SSD Company LTD, 2007

The PowerKIDS Jr. manufactured by SSD Company LTD is an educational computer system dedicated to children, launched in China and some Asian markets in 2007. It is not a traditional computer, but a hybrid electronic device, similar to VTech series educational toys or JAKKS Pacific's Plug & Play TV Games, designed to introduce children to the use of computers in a simple, colorful and interactive way. While never commercialized in Europe or North America, the PowerKIDS Jr. has gained some notoriety among retro technology collectors and nostalgic children's educational technology enthusiasts.

