0.286 [TeamEurope]

PowerKIDS (XaviXPORT, Japan), SSD Company LTD, 2007

The console TV game, developed by SSD Company LTD under the "PowerKIDS" brand for the XaviXPORT system, was released in Japan in 2007. It is part of the XaviX platform (sixth generation), which focuses on motion-based gaming and sports activities. The game uses dedicated peripherals—such as mats or sports equipment—connected to the console to detect the player’s real-world movements and translate them into actions on the screen. Primarily aimed at children, it combines educational elements with light physical exercise in interactive mini-games. The "PowerKIDS Jr." version (2007) represents a simplified edition designed for younger users. SSD Company Limited, a Japanese manufacturer specializing in fitness gaming devices, developed this title in collaboration with Jupiter Corporation for the Japanese educational and family market, anticipating concepts that would later become popular with Wii Fit and Kinect.

