$info=xbase09
$mame
0.222 [DBWBP]

XBase 09 Midi Controlled Analogue Drum Module, JoMoX, 1997

The XBase 09 is serious about emulating the Roland TR-909. Like the 909, it is an analog drum machine, and it sounds just like the 909, and more! It offers the same types of analog controls that the TR-808 and TR-909 did such as tuning, level, decay, snap, etc. However it provides more of these controls for more sounds than the originals ever did and has MIDI implementation and Patch memory making the XBase 09 a much more versatile machine than those originals (source: http://www.vintagesynth.com/misc/xbase09.php).

