$info=xd88_01
$mame
0.268 [CJ Reha]

XD88/01, Tektronix, 1990

The Tektronix XD88/01 graphics workstation, introduced in the early 1990s as a professional CAD/CAM system, was based on a 25-MHz Motorola 68030 processor with a 68882 coprocessor, featuring 8–32 MB of RAM, up to 500 MB of SCSI hard disk storage, and a proprietary graphics controller for high-resolution displays (up to 1280×1024). The system ran UNIX System V with a customized X Window graphical environment. It included RS-232 serial ports, a Centronics parallel port, an Ethernet network interface, and a VMEbus expansion slot. The XD88/01 was widely used in engineering, electronic design, and scientific research for 2D/3D modeling and complex data analysis. Its compact desktop design featured a dark-gray case and integrated power supply. As a pre-PC high-end solution, it catered to technical applications requiring precise graphics, UNIX stability, and seamless integration with Tektronix instrumentation.

