$info=xm200
$mame
0.256 [AJR]

XM200 Orchestra Module, Orla, 1990

Professional sound module Orla XM200, produced in the 1990s as a rack-mount unit for generating automatic orchestral arrangements. Based on sample-based synthesis with an internal ROM containing acoustic instruments (strings, winds, percussion, pianos), it offers "auto-accompaniment" style accompaniments featuring rhythmic patterns and harmonic variations synchronized to MIDI input. It includes MIDI input/output, stereo audio outputs, an LCD display, and controls for style, tempo, volume, and musical sections (intro, fill, ending). Designed for live musicians and home studios as a compact alternative to full-fledged workstations—without a built-in keyboard or sequencer. It embodies the Italian philosophy of modular arrangers from that era, focused on realistic sounds and rapid integration into existing setups.

