$info=y805128r2
$mame
0.155 [Wilbert Pol]

YIS805/128R2 (MSX2, USSR), Yamaha, 1986

The Yamaha YIS-805 comes with a separate keyboard and in 2 versions: The /128 version has only 128kB RAM and 1 disk drive by default, but there's a location planned for the addition of a second disk drive. The /256 version has 256kB RAM, 2 disk drives and a RS-232C interface. Both versions have an expansion bus at the back, reserved for a digitizer, also known as 'video enhancer'. It's the last computer released by Yamaha for the MSX system and the only one with a built-in floppy drive. It has still a special slot for specific Yamaha modules (source: https://www.msx.org/wiki/Yamaha_YIS-805).

DRIVER:
