$info=yis503f
$mame
0.143u3 [Wilbert Pol]

YIS503F (MSX1, French), Yamaha, 1984

The YIS503F is a signed Yamaha MSX fairly uncommon, where a lack of information on this machine. It is found in France, Scandinavia, Germany and Japan. Like all MSX machines, the Yis-503E is built around a Z80, an Intel 8255 PPI (Programable Peripheral Interface), a 9918A or 9928A Texas Instruments Video Display Processor (characterized by a smart manager sprites with its own memory the VRAM) and finally a General Instrument AY-2-8910 Programmable Sound Generator. The machine has 16 KB RAM, 16 KB of video RAM and 32 KB of ROM (source: http://www.obsolete-tears.com/yamaha-yis-503-f-machine-152.html).

