$info=z8536
$mame
0.149u1 [Curt Coder]

Zilog Z8536 CIO, <unknown>, ????

Zilog Z8036/Z8536 Counter/Timer and Parallel I/O Unit. Much like the SCC, two alternate versions of this peripheral were developed by Zilog. The Z8036 (Z-CIO) was compatible with the Z8000's address-latched Z-Bus and could write to any register directly, while the Z8536 interfaced to a generic bus using two address bits, requiring sequential writes to its control register in order to access any of the internal registers besides the three for port data. Both versions of the CIO can be reset through hardware as well as software, despite that neither provides a dedicated RESET pin. Pulling AS and DS active low at the same time resets the Z8036, and Z8536 is reset by activating RD and WR simultaneously.

DRIVER:
devices/machine/z8536.cpp

DRIVER STATUS:
Emulation: Good
Color: Good
Sound: Good
Graphics: Good
Save State: Unsupported

WIP:
- 0.288: Take into account data path polarity on port writes and bit matching [Curt Coder].
- 0.280: Fix counter/timer enable and interrupt error clear; fixed reading from Port C nibble registers [Curt Coder].
- 0.235: Better daisy chain support, fix port assignment when writing data. Avoid magic numbers [Dirk Best].
- 0.186: Changed description to 'Zilog Z8536 CIO'.
- 0.149u1: Curt Coder added 'Zilog Z8536' device.

ROMSET:
None required.

$end
