Z9001 (KC 85/1.10), Robotron, 1984

The Z9001 is a home computer from the GDR. He was a self-development, but based on a replica of the famous in the West as the Z80. Conceived as a home computer, the device is still used primarily in companies and schools / universities. After a while the computer was in KC85 / 1 and 1987 was renamed the successor KC87 presented. It differed mainly due to the built-in Basic interpreter, which previously had to be purchased as a module. During the building work of the family computer Robotron could never satisfy the huge demand despite horrendous prices (source, traslated from german: http://www.homecomputermuseum.de/comp/111_de.htm).

