SuperSport, Zenith Data Systems, 1987

The SuperSport is an older laptop with a 286 or 8088 processor (depending upon the specific model) and one or two 3?" disk drives. They can still be found on eBay.com occasionally (usually under $50), and you might find one in a garage sale or thrift store. According to obsoletecomputermuseum.org, it has a built-in 2.4kbps modem and an LCD display. 286 computers are capable of running DOS or an early version of Windows for an operating' system. Windows 1.x or 2.x would probably be preferable to any newer version (Windows 3.x would likely run at too slow a speed) (source: http://www.lesswaiting.com/info4.html).

