$info=zdz150
$mame
0.216 [rfka01]

Z-150 Series, Zenith Data Systems, 198?

The Zenith Z-150 is a plate mounted linear Alps SKCL series keyboard from Zenith. The keyboard features excellent build quality with very thick plastic construction and a metal plate back cover. A thick non detachable cable is also included. It was bundled with multiple Zenith computer systems from the 1980's. Keys use either Alps SKCL Green or Alps SKCL Yellow. The spacebar can sometimes use Alps SKCL Cream or Alps SKCL Grey depending on the year in which the keyboard was made. The keycaps are either doubleshot ABS or dye sublimated PBT. Spacebars are always ABS. All versions of the Z-150 have a internal speaker which makes a beep noise when typing on the alpha keys. To disable/enable the beeper use the key combo Alt + Esc (source: https://deskthority.net/wiki/Zenith_Z-150).

