$info=zdz160
$mame
0.216 [rfka01]

Z-160 Series, Zenith Data Systems, 198?

Believe it or not, the Zenith Z160 was considered a "portable" machine. It was larger and heavier than most desktops, but it did include an internal monitor and *could* be carried around. It's an odd design with the disk drives popping up from a panel in the top of the machine. Internally, it has a passive backplane, with the CPU, Memory and other traditional "mainboard" resources located in removable cards. Donated by Mike Kenzie (source: http://classiccmp.org/dunfield/pc/index.htm).

