BX98 (VIA Apollo Pro chipset), Zida, 1998

The Zida BX98 is a well-known PC motherboard manufactured starting in 1998 by the Taiwanese company Zida Computer Technologies, which is extremely famous in the consumer and low-cost clone markets of the retro-hardware era thanks to its renowned "Tomato Board" product line. hw-museum.czThis specific model represents a key budget transition solution for the late 1990s: despite bearing the "BX" designation (which typically referred to the prestigious and expensive Intel 440BX chipset), the board circumvented licensing costs by adopting the budget-friendly VIA Apollo Pro alternative.

