$info=zon32bit
$mame
0.218 [Team Europe, David Haywood]

Zone 32-bit Gaming Console System (Family Sport 41-in-1), Ultimate Products (HK) Ltd / Senca, 200?

Zone?is a brand name for inexpensive consoles with built-in games that are marketed by?Ultimate Products Ltd.. Most of the Zone consoles superficially resemble the?Wii?but have a 16 or 32-bit architecture. Ultimate Products even claimed that the Zone consoles are not meant to compete with 7th generation consoles, and are therefore sold at a lower price. The game developers for the consoles vary; for example,?Waixing?made the games on the Zone 40,?Senca?made the games on the Zone Interactive, and?JungleTac?made the games on the Zone 60. In the United States some Zone consoles (such as the 40, 60, and 3D) were available at?CVS Pharmacy. In the UK the Zone 40 is common in discount stores, but other models are only affordable from TV shopping channels (source: https://bootleggames.fandom.com/wiki/Zone).

