$info=zonemini
$mame
0.223 [Sean Riddle, David Haywood]

Zone Mini, Ultimate Products Ltd. / Waixing, 200?

An affordable handheld device released in the 2010s, often sold under various brands such as "Zone Mini." Based on a simplified and compact hardware design, it came with a fixed selection of preinstalled retro games (typically unofficial clones of classics like Tetris, Snake, or Pac-Man). Equipped with a small monochrome LCD screen, a membrane keypad, and battery power, it was intended for casual, low-cost, portable entertainment, primarily targeting younger audiences or serving as a promotional gadget. Despite its name "Waixing" (a well-known Chinese developer of NES cartridges), the device wasn't technically related to classic consoles but rather tapped into nostalgia for vintage titles in a pocket-sized format.

