0.133 [Robbbert]

ZRT-80, Digital Research Computers, 1982

An 8-bit architecture-based computer system developed for educational and basic applications in the field of programming. Equipped with a Z80 processor, it includes a BASIC environment permanently stored in ROM, a video interface for connecting to monitors or TVs, and storage capabilities via cassette tapes. Designed specifically for learning computer science, it features a functional keyboard and expansion ports, providing a hands-on, educational experience for using computers in either school settings or as a hobbyist's tool.

