$info=a7800.cpp
$drv
0.36b6 [Dan Boris, Fabio Priuli, Mike Saarna, Robert Tuccitto]

WIP:
- 0.288: Updates and cleanups (#15140): Use bool type for Boolean values, made some variables const, reduced duplication; fixed debugger and save state issues, use BIT helper to extract bits; use a memory view for BIOS ROM overlay, cleaned up code [cam900].
- 0.286: (a7800.xml) Added 21 working Inufuto homebrews (#14885) [Ectoplasm].
- 0.278: Update 1on1 comment again [hap]. PCB type and proper rom names for most entries. (a7800.xml) Big documentation update. Corrected ROM label for rampage. More PCB and ROM label updates [Guru]. Redumped and corrected ROM labels for foodfu, karatekau, polepos2u. Added PCB values for some more sets [Guru]. Verified dump and improved documentation for aceoface [Guru].
- 0.266: Changed years from copyright years to years of release in 'a7800.xml' [kmg].
- 0.259: Verified ROM code for PAL BIOS [Guru].
- 0.250: Pass phase 2 clock to cartridge slot – fixes PAL add-on chip clock rates [kmg].
- 0.246: Placed driver in the sub-folder "atari/".
- 0.187: BugFIX #06612 [Interface] (a7800.cpp) a7800.ccp: Machine inputs broken [Ivan Vangelista].
- 0.168: BugFIX #06060 [DIP/Input] (a7800.cpp) a7800 [1on1u]: Cannot start a game in One-On-One Basketball [David Haywood]. More accurately reflect '0x02XX' map per hardware documentation and testing [Mike Saarna, Robert Tuccitto].
- 0.166: More accurate representation of the Activision cart hardware for utilized hotspots. Rampage no longer crashes when P1 selects Lizzy [Mike Saarna].
- 0.164: Fix 0x2800 mirroring behavior [Mike Saarna, Robert Tuccitto].
- 0.155: Various update: split video emulation (Atari MARIA chip) into a separate' device. Rewritten cart emulation to use slot devices. Removed POKEY chip from the main unit since it was inside the carts (of course it gets enabled when you launch a game who contained it in its cart). Added support for the High Score cart as a passthru cart: when you mount hiscore, a -cart2 switch will become available to mount the game you want to play. Properly implemented XBoarD and XM expansions as passthru carts as well, so that new syntax to run dkxm.a78 is mess a7800 -cart xm -cart2 path\to\games\dkxm.a78 High Score support for XM shall work as well. Big clean up of the driver, simplifying memory map, removing writes to ROM, etc. Fixed YM2151 clock in XM expansion, thanks to info from tep392 and GroovyBee. Added support for homebrew boards MegaCart+ and VersaBoard by CPUWIZ (ROM respectively up to 512K and 256K + 32K of RAM). Misc cleanups [Fabio Priuli].
- 0.154: Brought initial Maria cycle counts inline from measurements taken with logic analyzer/tests [Mike Saarna/Robert Tuccitto]. Added interrupts to DMA cycle eating. Updates to LL, OL, and spin accounting for HALT behavior [Mike Saarna].
- 0.153: BugFIX #05347: (a7800.c) a7800 [digdugu]: Line of garbage graphics on game screen. BugFix#05448: (a7800.c) a7800 [xeviousu]: Line Below Score Display under Xevious. BugFix#05450: (a7800.c) a7800 [hattricku]: Grey Line At Top Of Playfield under Hat Trick. BugFix#05451: (a7800.c) a7800 [midnightu]: Line at Bottom of Playfield under Midnight Mutants. BugFix#05453: (a7800.c) a7800 [planetsmu]: Difficulty selection text improved but some corruption still present. BugFix#05454: (a7800.c) a7800 [ddragonu]: Corrupted scanline in score display still present but moved up from previous position. BugFix#05455: (a7800.c) a7800 [commandou]: Corrupted text improved but still there on title/difficulty selection screen. BugFix#05456: (a7800.c) a7800 [plutos]: Line glitch at top of screen below score display, and towards the bottom of the gameplay field. BugFix#05457: (a7800.c) a7800 [1on1u]: 'Shot' clock & 'Game Time Remaining' clock countdown too fast; makes game unplayable [Tafoid]. Corrected joystick buttons assignment & minor palette notes cleanup. Positional description for difficulty switches added. Added more details and clarification regarding the potentiometer [Robert Tuccitto]. Support for >128k cart formats and banked RAM and added bit 4 & bit 5 notes while standardizing 'super' description listing. Fixed number of scanlines to accurately reflect hardware testing and schematics (262-->263 NTSC and 312-->313 PAL). Additional fix to timing of Maria cycles and comments. Fixed INPTCTRL register implementation to match hardware Diagnostic Test Cart now works. Corrected ROM_FILL. Proper calibration per Diagnostic cart. PAL RIOT fixed. Corrected SYNC timing to match later GCC tech doc and measurements against real HW. Fix to bug that causes skip to first DLL if its 1 scanline tall. Fixed total horiz pixels to better match hw testing results and tech docs. Fixed rendering to ensure DMA stolen cycles. Fixes reading of controller port behavior when held high by RIOT chip. Fixed DMA regarding startup, shutdown and cycle stealing which fixes numerous recorded MAMETester bugs. Bug fixed and fine tuned the DMA timing. Corrected RIOT timing [Mike Saarna]. Normalize horizontal frequency while maintaining same net cycles [Robert Tuccitto]. Fixed a few remaining issues while keeping to documented tech specs and ranges. Correct fix to Maria cycles regarding DMA Shutdown short/other line shutdown [Mike Saarna/Robert Tuccitto].
- 0.152: Added Atari 2600, 5200, and 7800 palette notes [Robert Tuccitto].
- 0.151: Added Phase Shifts 24.7, 25.2, 26.2, 27.2. Phase Shifts 24.7 through 27.7 degrees with 0.5 degree increments documented. Phase Shift 26.2 degrees made active. Fixed typo under 26.77$. Cleanup of address maps, high score maps added [Robert Tuccitto].
- 0.150: Normalized contrast and brightness, providing a standardized grayscale and adjusted color values. Green miscalculated proportions fixed. Stored data for 26.7 & 27.7 phase shifts with corrections and label for 25.7 values. Made 26.7 (medium) default. Phase shifting falls outside the realm of video controls and hope to implement a selectable toggle hardware option similar to Donkey Kong TKG02/TKG04 [Robert Tuccitto].
- 0.149u1: XM/XBoard POKEY support. 'Bentley Bear - Crystal Quest' & 'Donkey Kong XM' now work, while maintaining support for original library titles, Commando and Ballblazer [Robert Tuccitto].
- 0.148u5: Red and Blue miscalculated proportions fixed [Robert Tuccitto].
- 0.148u3: Corrected rotation values and errors including duplicate entries for palette. Address map locations for the XBOARD added to get the ball rolling on support for it. Stripped palette to raw video output values removing YIQ/YUV infer data [Robert Tuccitto].
- 0.148u2: Fixed color clip in $1 & $F. Improved and corrected NTSC (a7800) and PAL (a7800p) palettes. Palette rebuild due to misaligned data references. Corrected PAL color sequence order [Robert Tuccitto].
- 0.147u4: Adjusted colorburst/tint/hue of entire palette to closer reflect default hardware configuration setting of ~180 degrees [i.e. $17 = 179.92706396 & $18 = 179.927063726] [Robert Tuccitto].
- 0.128: Incog added Atari 7800 Prototype driver.
- 0.94: Add keys to toggle switches. New keyboard mappings are: (1) Select, (2) Reset, (3) Toggle Left Difficulty switch, (4) Toggle Right Difficulty switch, (C) Toggle Black & White switch (a2600 only), (]) Toggle Pause switch (a7800 only) [Christopher Stone].
- 0.36b6: Dan Boris added a7800.cpp driver.

$end
$info=aa310.cpp
$drv
0.132 [Angelo Salese, R. Belmont, Juergen Buchmueller]

WIP:
- 0.280: Added support for HFE floppy format to all machines. Added another romset for the A500 [Nigel Barnes].
- 0.263: Configured Acorn R225 with discless bootstrap. Configured Acorn A4 to auto-start !BatMgr. Reduced ROM region size, and mirrored. Removed RISC OS 3.19 from BIOS options, was only available in German A3010. Corrected ROMs in Acorn M4  [Nigel Barnes].
- 0.246: Placed driver in the sub-folder "acorn/".
- 0.228: Replaced i2cmem with pcf8583 RTC device [Nigel Barnes].
- 0.182: Over 30 games (some protected), and many apps in archimedes.xml [Nigel Barnes].
- 0.180: Renamed (a310.cpp) to (aa310.cpp). Fixed horizontal display position and cursor position in VIDC [Sandro Ronco]. Added new NOT WORKING machines Archimedes 305, Archimedes 440, Archimedes 3000, Archimedes 410/1, Archimedes 420/1, Archimedes 440/1, Archimedes 540, Acorn A5000, Acorn A4, Acorn A4000, Acorn A5000 Alpha. Renamed a310->aa310 to avoid conflict with Amiga machines. Added all missing OS releases Arthur 0.30, RISC OS 2.01, RISC OS 3.00, RISC OS 3.10, RISC OS 3.19 (German). Made all machines default to the OS (Arthur, RISC OS 2, RISC OS 3) they were shipped with. Corrected ROM labels/locations. Added default CMOS to boot to desktop. Mapped Acorn A4 Power Management extension [Nigel Barnes].
- 0.157: Added softlist for Archimedes disks [Riley110, Fabio Priuli].
- 0.132: Added a310.cpp driver.

$end
