$info=apollo.cpp
$drv
0.145u1 [Hans Ostermeyer, R. Belmont]

WIP:
- 0.246: Driver placed in the sub-folder "apollo/".
- 0.237: BugFIX #08111 [Crash/Freeze] (apollo.cpp) dn3500 and clones: Apollo machines cannot load programs from tape [AJR].
- 0.217: Fixed failures in DEX DISP7C tests 170 and 210 and self-test TE [Hans Ostermeyer].
- 0.208: Updates and resurrection: Fix typo'd constant in m68kmmu that prevented trapping user accesses to kernel space. Removed need for intrusive m68k modifications, fixed crash in 3c505 networking, and fixed Domain/OS booting in Normal mode [Hans Ostermeyer].
- 0.185: Fixed SIO regression [Hans Ostermeyer].
- 0.180: Enabled creation when non-existent image name is supplied for omti8621 and sc499 [Hans Ostermeyer].
- 0.178: Eliminate logerror spam on unmapped ISA access [Hans Ostermeyer].
- 0.177: BugFIX #06331: [Crash/Freeze] (apollo.cpp) dn3500_19i, dsp3000, dsp3500, dsp5500: Crash/Exception on start [Osso].
- 0.176: Changes: Keyboard mapping adjusted to fit current MAME. Fixed screen raw parameters. Fixed disp.dex Test 20 (Video SYNC Gen. Add. Test) for color displays [Hans Ostermeyer].
- 0.175: Install the unmapped handler in the correct post-trampoline range [Olivier Galibert].
- 0.171: Unified logging format in associated devices. Use correct raw video modes [Hans Ostermeyer].
- 0.169: Cleanups and enhancements: Split OMTI8621 ISA device into PC and Apollo versions (Apollo doesn't have a BIOS extension ROM, PC does). Cleaned up OMTI8621 logging. Forced slot # of OMTI board so we can look it up and auto-set the node ID. Adjusted mouse sensitivity [Hans Ostermeyer].
- 0.167: Changes: Fixed the Apollo floppy disk emulation. Added the media option -node_id resp. -ni to set the node ID from a node ID ROM image file. Fixed the unmapped ISA Bus access to return 0xff instead of 0x00. Removed excessive log entries from unmapped ISA Bus access. Fixed date (and some other issues) in mc146818 (new in MAME 0166) [Hans Ostermeyer].
- 0.164: Improved mouse emulation [Hans Ostermeyer].
- 0.157: Added apollo_ctape softlist [Riley110]. Made possible to load cartridge tapes from softlist, by dealing with these images like it's done for cassettes and floppies [Fabio Priuli].
- 0.154: Updates: Fixed ISA bus endianness, it's the same as other 680x0 systems with ISA. Improved logging in several places. "20 years ago" option updated to now-necessary "25 years ago". Fixed ISA high IRQ routing. Fixed 3c505 to have a 16 bit ISA interface. Fixed omti8621 and sc499 to have correct-endian ISA interfaces. Minor Apollo cleanups & removal of no-longer-supported options, plus data format fix for systems using a serial terminal [Hans Ostermeyer].
- 0.153: Start modernizing/cleanup. Old 68681 is gone. Apollo keyboard now speaks diserial. Headless configs use the serial terminal' device. More cleanup, devlegcy.h now gone. Cleaned up PIC8259 usage. Converted to use real ISA bus. sc499 cartridge tape converted to ISA. Separate 3c505 out into an ISA16 card [R. Belmont].
- 0.152: Correct MC146818 clock [Hans Ostermeyer].
- 0.149u1: Fixed disk and tape DMA, improved logging. Fix out-of-bounds framebuffer access crash on OS X [Hans Ostermeyer].
- 0.148: BugFIX #05068: [Crash/Freeze] (apollo.c) All sets in apollo.c: [debug] Assert: src/emu/render.c, Line 2466 [Firewave]. Apollo fixes: Fixed MLOG: machine -> machine(). Use the correct address space for DMA (supplied space parameter is wrong; why?). Minor fix for 64 Bit Ubuntu. Block_set_filemark() failed to set the filemark buffer; memcpy will now use 64 bit words (i.e. 8 byte chunks) for copying [Hans Ostermeyer].
- 0.146: Properly reset all motherboard devices on a 68k RESET instruction; makes the PROM "RE" command work properly [Hans Ostermeyer].
- 0.145u7: Add alternate layouts for a better experience on XGA (1024x768) and WXGA (1280x800) displays [Hans Ostermeyer].
- 0.145u5: Do bounds checking on Ethernet packets [Hans Ostermeyer].
- 0.145u4: Various cleanups [Hans Ostermeyer, R. Belmont].
- 0.145u1: Hans Ostermeyer and R. Belmont added apollo.cpp driver.

$end
