- 0.162: Rewrote driver and removed lots of cruft: Remove custom 6845 emulation and use our standard core. Use the slot system for the parallel interface, fix and implement the joystick as a slot device and create a printer slot' device. Add support for the RS-232 port. Add support for the Break key (causes NMI) [Dirk Best].
- 0.36b14: Changed the cgenie driver to use the opbaseoverride() to load a .cas file from the command line. This works for unprotected, binary *.cas files only, though. From inside the emulation you can still load binary images with the SYSTEM command and BASIC files with CLOAD"<letter> [Juergen Buchmueller]. Fixed some minor cgenie problems, like loading *.cas files from inside the emulation with names shorter than 6 characters [Juergen Buchmueller].
