$info=coco12.cpp
$drv
0.36b11 [Nathan Woods]

WIP:
- 0.265: Fix light gun offset (#12242) [Tim Lindner].
- 0.263: Dumped ROMs for Deluxe Color Computer and promoted it to working [Brian Wiesler, Tim Lindner]. Cleaned up some rot. In particular, use object finders in machine configuration rather than defining tag macros, and avoid unnecessary device_replace to just slightly alter device configuration [Vas Crabb].
- 0.255: Added BIOS options for Color Computer 1 and 2. Add -bios options to Color Computer 1 & 2. Removed drivers that existed only to select BASIC versions (coco2), (coco2h), (cocoe) and (cocoeh) [Tim Lindner].
- 0.251: Moved real-time clocks to slot cards where they belong (addresses MT08416) [Tim Lindner].
- 0.246: Driver placed in the sub-folder "trs/".
- 0.243: Increase dynamic range of Radio Shack hi-res joystick interface [Tim Lindner].
- 0.240: Create peripheral screens after the main screen [Nigel Barnes].
- 0.238: Audited save state support and marked it as supported for systems [Tim Lindner].
- 0.237: Added initial RPK format support for CoCo ROM cartridges [Nathan Woods]. Added support for the ILCE / SEP Micro-SEP 1600 [Tim Lindner].
- 0.235: BugFIX #08045 [Misc.] (coco12.cpp) coco, coco2, dragon32: 32K machines present with one byte missing (c478e4e) [Nigel Barnes].
- 0.233: Fix for MT 07305 [AJR].
- 0.230: Set proper tri-state value for keyboard PIA port B (fixes MT07701) [Tim Lindner].
- 0.227: Added Speech Systems Stereo Composer cartridge. Improved behaviour of high-resolution joystick interface. Removed IRQ trampolines. Fixed SSC TMS7000 busy flag and reset handling (fixes speech in Pegsaus and the Phantom Riders). Added Speech Systems Symphony Twelve cartridge. Added CoCo and Dragon MIDI cartridges [Tim Lindner]. [Tim Lindner]. Cleaned up CoCo cartridge slot configuration code [Nathan Woods].
- 0.222: Disabled Becker Port by default (it conflicts with cartridge devices) [Tim Lindner].
- 0.210: Added handlers for CTS region $C000-$FEFF, allowing cartridges to implement devices in this region [Nigel Barnes].
- 0.207: Removed some MCFG macros [cam900].
- 0.202: Use CLEAR or CTRL as second shift, allowing more punctuation to be typed in natural keyboard mode [Tim Lindner].
- 0.198: BugFIX #06982 [Gameplay] (coco12.cpp) Other Coco related drivers: 1bit audio DAC issue [AJR].
- 0.177: BugFIX #05823 [Core] (coco12.cpp) -ramsize does nothing for emulation although it does change the .ini file [Nathan Woods]. Fixed configurable RAM sizes: Changes the 6883 SAM implementation to assume memory bank lengths smaller than available space are not mirrored [Nathan Woods].
- 0.192: BugFIX #06771 [Compiling] (coco12.cpp) coco3, dragon, etc..: Genie failing to determine the nested dependency of coco_t4426 on mc14411 [hap]. Fixed metadata fro Brazilian CoCo clones, and renamed LZ Color64 ROMs to document labels and PCB locations [Felipe Corrêa da Silva Sanches].
- 0.191: BugFIX #06719 [Core] (coco12.cpp) coco12, coco3, other 6809?: SBCB instruction returns the wrong result [hap]. Added support for multiple PORT_CHAR() bindings, and adopted in the CoCo driver [Nathan Woods].
- 0.186: Made 6883 SAM control the root device clock, and changed CoCo devices to use derived clocks [Nathan Woods]. Added support for Games Master Cartridge developed by John Linville as slot device [Tim Lindner].
- 0.185: Further cleanups in cartridge slot signal handling: Attempts to make signals on the CoCo cartridge slot (CART, NMI, HALT) more standardized, particularly the practice of Program Paks tying the CART line to Q. Should fix some outstanding bugs in how these signals were passed around when using the CoCo Multi-Pak interface [Nathan Woods].
- 0.178: CoCo and Dragon FDC code overhaul. Split CoCo and Dragon FDC code. Added save state support. Fixed regression introduced on the Dragon FDC from 0.154 [Nathan Woods].
- 0.177: BugFIX #05823: [Core] (coco12.cpp) -ramsize does nothing for emulation although it does change the .ini file [Nathan Woods]. Fixed configurable RAM sizes: Changes the 6883 SAM implementation to assume memory bank lengths smaller than available space are not mirrored [Nathan Woods].
- 0.159: BugFIX #05844 [Core] (coco12.c) all coco drivers: Crash to desktop when slot device Multi selected [Osso].
- 0.156: BugFIX #05660 [Misc.] (coco12.c) Coco 1, 2, 3: Implement virtual "Becker Port" for DriveWire support [R. Belmont]. BugFix#05694: [Sound] All sets in coco12.c and coco3.c: audio output level incorrect when Cassette/Cartridge selected on SC77526 chip.
- 0.154: BugFIX #05541 [Core] (coco12.c) coco2b and coco3/3h: coco2b and coco3/3h will not run correct versions of NitrOS-9 [Osso].
- 0.148: BugFIX #04894 [Core] (coco12.c) All sets in coco12.c: RTC option is missing. BugFix#05037: [Misc.] (coco12.c) Request for change in mess/drivers/coco12.c. BugFix#05031: [Graphics] (coco12.c) coco2: The video timing in the program MCPaint 2.10 trashes program [npwoods].
- 0.144u1: Renamed (coco) to (coco12).
- 0.143u3: Added better dump for Canyon Climber in coco_cart.xml [Tim Lindner].
- 0.140: Added bi-directional bitbanger support. Needs further core changes to be fully implemented. Fixed delays in when propagating interrupts signals from the floppy disk controller to the CPU. Added a small pool of timers to allow overlapping interrupt signals [Tim Lindner].
- 0.134: Bug #1839 fixed [Miodrag Milanović].
- 0.91: Fixed a bug that caused problems when dealing with double sided disk images (bug #633) [Nate Woods].
- 0.37b8: Added support for printer. Optimized graphics emulation [Nate Woods].
- 0.37b5: Converted the Dragon driver to use an include file, moved PAK loading code into a new src/mess/formats directory [Nate Woods].
- 0.36b16: Far better disk support in the COCO drivers [Paul Burgin, Stewart Orchard, Nate Woods].
- 0.36b11: Nathan Woods added coco.cpp driver.

$end
$info=coco3.cpp
$drv
0.144u1 [Nathan Woods]

WIP:
- 0.288: Fix CoCo 3 Keyboard interrupt (#15349) [Tim Lindner].
- 0.283: Enable GIME vertical text scroll register (#14503) [Tim Lindner].
- 0.278: Change order of GIME initialization (#13764) [Tim Lindner].
- 0.270: Extend display from 639 to 640 pixels (#12780). Corrected visible display width to 640 pixels (fixes MT08903) [Tim Lindner].
- 0.263: Cleaned up some rot. In particular, use object finders in machine configuration rather than defining tag macros, and avoid unnecessary device_replace to just slightly alter device configuration [Vas Crabb].
- 0.254: BugFIX #06797 [Core] (trs/coco3.cpp) MC6809 handles invalid instruction $10?$4F incorrectly [Tim Lindner].
- 0.251: Moved real-time clocks to slot cards where they belong (addresses MT08416) [Tim Lindner].
- 0.246: Driver placed in the sub-folder "trs/".
- 0.243: Increased range of high resolution joystick axis inputs [Tim Lindner].
- 0.242: Added ILCE / SEP Micro-Sep Model 3 (Mexican Color Computer 3 clone) [Barry Nelson, Tim Lindner].
- 0.240: Create peripheral screens after the main screen [Nigel Barnes].
- 0.233: Improve timer calculation (#8223) [Tim Lindner].
- 0.231: Set port B tristate value of 0xff to the first PIA (fixes MT07701) [Tim Lindner].
- 0.222: BugFIX #07526 [Crash/Freeze] (coco3.cpp) MAME exits without error or with error when trying to format a HxC .HFE image [kkaempf]. Enabled Becker Port by default for coco3dw1. Fixed jostick button labels [Tim Lindner].
- 0.212: BugFIX #06880 [Crash/Freeze] (coco3.cpp) All machines in coco12.cpp, coco3.cpp: UI/MAME crash when configuring MPI options [AmatCoder].
- 0.209: BugFIX #05291 [Sound] (coco3.cpp) All drivers in coco.c: ORC90 emulation has no sound output [Nigel Barnes].
- 0.207: Removed some MCFG macros [cam900].
- 0.203: Added workaround to show only one screen by default [Tim Lindner].
- 0.202: Use CLEAR or CTRL as second shift, allowing more punctuation to be typed in natural keyboard mode [Tim Lindner].
- 0.193: BugFIX #06785 [Interface] (coco3.cpp) Any driver that allows one to browse the host file system: Can't change into directories that have a "." prefix in their name [cuavas]. BugFix#06779: [Crash/Freeze] (coco3.cpp) Mounting Zenix Floppy Disk crashes MAME with floating point exception error [Duke].
- 0.186: BugFIX #06560 [Crash/Freeze] (coco3.cpp) All sets in coco12.cpp, coco3.cpp: Loading cartridges from softlists locks up emulator [Nathan Woods].
- 0.177: Fixed some MC6847 low resolution video modes: Fixed a bug from where video data was sampled that could cause too many samples to be loaded in low resolution video modes * On the CoCo, this fixes some low resolution video modes used by Project Nebula and some other games [Nathan Woods].
- 0.156: BugFIX #05694 [Sound] All sets in coco12.c and coco3.c: audio output level incorrect when Cassette/Cartridge selected on SC77526 chip.
- 0.153: Added some new dumps in coco_cart.xml [k1w1].
- 0.148: BugFIX #05037 Removing VHD from 'coco' driver [Robert Gault].
- 0.146: BugFIX #04811 [Gameplay] (coco3.c) coco3, coco3h: RTC emulation is not working [Miodrag Milanović].
- 0.144u1: Nathan Woods added coco3.cpp driver.

