$info=esq1.cpp
$drv
0.134 [R. Belmont, Olivier Galibert]

WIP:
- 0 .281: Add my name to (c) holders list on Ensoniq ESQ-1 driver (#14128). And remove old comment (the keyboard scanning was already implementented). Adding internal interactive artwork for the Ensoniq ESQ-1 (#14049) [Felipe Corrêa da Silva Sanches]. Fixed previously commented code that had rotted (as it always does) [Vas Crabb].
- 0.246: Driver placed in the sub-folder "ensoniq/".
- 0.211: Improved emulation of sq80 allowing it to boot and play [R. Belmont, Jariseon, R. Buchty].
- 0.146u2: Various documentation improvements for the 16-bit Ensoniqs including correct CPU speed and other details [R. Belmont, Christian Brunschen].
- 0.134: R. Belmont and Olivier Galibert added esq1.cpp driver.

$end
$info=esq5505.cpp
$drv
0.146 [R. Belmont]

WIP:
- 0.287: Add support for the Ensoniq VFX OS version 2.30 ROMs (#15080). UART is an mc68681_device, not an scn2681_device (#15114) [Christian Brunschen].
- 0.284: Change VFX-family buttons from IPT_KEYBOARD to IPT_KEYPAD (#14565) [Christian Brunschen]. (sd132_flop.xml) Lower case on descriptive media storage. Lower case on descriptive media storage. vfxsd_flop.xml: Lower case on descriptive media storage. (ibm5170_cdrom-xml): Fixed typo on (acatari2) set description. (sd132_flop.xml), (sd1_flop.xml), (vfxsd_flop.xml) Metadata cleanings (#14604) [ArcadeShadow].
- 0.283: Add software lists for the Ensoniq VFX-SD, SD-1 and SD-1/32 keyboards (#14498). Add software lists for the Ensoniq VFX-SD, SD-1 and SD-1/32 keyboards. Each can also use the floppy disks for its predecessor, mainly because there are demo songs on the earlier OS disks that are not on the later ones, but which still work perfectly well and sounds great; the SD-1/32 software list also includes four demo disks; a demo disk specifically for the SD-1/32; a demo disk for the SQ-series of keyboards with 32 voices This contains System Exclusive files foro use with 32-voice SQ series keyboards; two multi-product demo disks These contain both sequencer files for the SD-1/32 and System Exclusive files for use with the SQ and KS series of keyboards. Add VFX-family ROM & EEPROM Cartridge support, and improve floppy support (#14444). Second attempt, simpler and hopefully better; when the floppy is active (i.e., when the motor is actually on), also indicate this on the LED on the panel layout; only create writeable cartridge images. The user can always rename a writable (.eeprom, .sc32) image to .rom or .cart to mark it as read-only; restore the previous behaviour when creating a cartridge image - even ones created with the filetypes that indicate a read-only image are effectively write-once. Also normalize the spelling of to "writeable". Also support HFE format flopppy images (#14504). Ensoniq VFX family layouts (#14518). Specify the bounds for each group; this fixes an issue where the VFX (non-SD)'s button area is stretched vertically, because it does not have the "System" label at the top, leaving an empty space [Christian Brunschen].
- 0.282: Route es5505 bus to a separate 'aux' stereo output (#14333). The VFX-SD and later keyboards in the family have not only a main stereo output, but also a second 'aux' stereo output that bypasses effects processing and has separate output jacks from the keyboard. This allows some sound to be routed for separate effects processing or recording. Make the VFX family of keyboards' RAM non-volatile (#14341). Add VFX-family ROM and EEPROM Cartridge support, and improve floppy support (#14331) [Christian Brunschen].
- 0.280; Clean up interrupt handling [Patrick Mackinlay].
- 0.246: Driver placed in the sub-folder "ensoniq/".
- 0.219: Added PCB layout for SQ-2 [Guru].
- 0.188: Added an external panel for the Ensoniq VFX family of keyboards, with a websocket interface and an HTML/Javascript implementation that can be served over HTTP [Christian Brunschen].
- 0.150: Sorted out BIOSes for the SD-1 family: newly dumped 3.0 for 21-voice, allow selecting 4.02 or 4.10 for 32-voice [Christian Brunschen, R. Belmont].
- 0.148: More documentation and other fixes from schematics [R. Belmont].
- 0.147u4: Updates: Fixed up clocks for 21 vs. 32-voice models. Added ROMs for the 12-bit sample region on the SD-1 and SD-1 32-voice. Minor cleanups [Christian Brunschen, R. Belmont].
- 0.146u1: Add floppy side select control and EPS/EPS-16+'s 68450 DMAC. EPS OS now boots and says "ERROR 129" instead of crashing. Added ubiqitous 2x40 line VFD display. Hooked up floppy drive and controller on VFX-SD, SD-1, SD-1 32, and EPS-16. Fixed battery level readback on all 16-bit Ensoniqs and respond correctly to keyboard calibration command. EPS-16 ROMs turned out to be plain EPS [R. Belmont].
- 0.146: R. Belmont added esq5505.cpp driver.

$end
