$info=fmtowns.cpp
$drv
0.132 [Barry Rodewald]

WIP:
- 0.286: Better serial IRQ handling. Also cleanup [Vas Crabb].
- 0.278: (fmtowns_cd.xml) Added 23 items (twenty working) and replaced three items with better dumps (#13651) [r09].
- 0.275: (fmtowns_cd.xml)  Bulk replace "fmt_cdrom" interface with "cdrom" [AJR].
- 0.264: (fmtowns_cd.xml) Metadata cleanup: Fixed cloneof relationships. "mbomberd" cloneof "mbomber" "mmorphd" cloneof "mmorph" "psydetf2d" cloneof "psydetf2" "psydet2d" cloneof "psydet2" / "psydet2r" cloneof "psydet2" "psydet1r" cloneof "psydet1" "psydet3r" cloneof "psydet3" "psydet4d" cloneof "psydet4" / "psydet4r" cloneof "psydet4" "psydet5r" cloneof "psydet5" "sherlockd" cloneof "sherlock" "simfarmd" cloneof "simfarm" "chasehqd" cloneof "chasehq" "dagaind" cloneof "dagain" "wyattd" cloneof "wyatt". Lowercase on descriptive words. Lowercase on descriptive words ("Demo") "indycrusd" cloneof "indycrus". Marked demos as clones and use lowercase for descriptive text in descriptions [ArcadeShadow].
- 0.250: Get rid of the rest of the leftover code. Use MSX controller slots for pad ports [Vas Crabb].
- 0.248: (fmtowns_flop_misc.xml) Cleaned up descriptions [ArcadeShadow].
- 0.246: Driver placed in the sub-folder "fujitsu/".
- 0.233: Fix missing controller return value and cdda status [cracyc].
- 0.232: Adjusted PCM/CD-DA sound balance [r09].
- 0.231: Fixed off-by-one calculation in CDDA track length. Added fourteen new dumps, sixteen replacements, and four missing floppies and added 29 entries, replaced 13 entries with better dumps, and added one missing floppy image [r09].
- 0.230: (fmtowns_flop.xml) Split into separate lists for original, cracked and miscellaneous software, and added seven entries. Added thirteen entries, replaced twelve entries with better dumps, and added five missing floppies [r09].
- 0.226: Added support for SCSI card slot and FMT-121 card used on first-generation models [r09].
- 0.222: (fmtowns_cd.xml) Added eight entries, and replaced five entries with better dumps [redump.org, r09].
- 0.218: Updated notes on sound chips used [cam900].
- 0.217: (fmtowns_flop.xml) Added Japanese titles for most entries [r09].
- 0.215: Removed SCSI controller from first-generation models and the Marty as these machines lack it. Corrected CPU types for FM-Towns II SJ and FM-Towns II MX. Corrected user-selectable RAM size options. Mapped packed video RAM at 0x00b00000 for 386SX-based models (fixes graphical issues on FM-Towns II UX and FM-Towns Marty). Configured FM-Towns Marty with one floppy drive and 2MB of RAM. Fixed crashes when 1MB ROM or a single floppy drive is selected. Dumped and added ROMs from a first-generation FM-Towns Model 2. Replaced a number of entries with better dumps from the redump.org database, added parent/clone relationships for Windows 3.1 revisions and updated the list of missing dumps in "fmtowns_cd.xml" [r09].
- 0.212: Fixed CD-DA start/end position (should be relative to beginning of table of contents). Fixed crash on out-of-bounds palette writes in 16-color mode [r09].
- 0.202: (fmtowns_cd.xml) Dumped Branmarker 2 Extra Disc [DamienD, Tokugawa Corporate Forums].
- 0.199: Fixed speaker output level [cam900].
- 0.198: Implemented stereo output, fixed PCM output level, and reduced code duplication [cam900].
- 0.194: FM Towns improvements: Fixed horizontal wrap for bitmap layers. Refactored line drawing, with support for zoom up to *16, and better wrapping. Added support for all sixteen horizontal zoom levels supported by the hardware instead of just 5 (used in Misty and Rayxanber). Simplified the line wrap detection code and added support all use cases including vertical scrolling and layer 1 with sprites. Doubled line size when in single-layer plus high color mode. Made the line wrapping code aware of VRAM page selection. Fixed misplaced bottom lines. Fixed vertical sync flag read from port 0xcff86 - Birdy Soft games now boot. Implemented horizontal sync read from 0xcff86 - later 4th Unit games now boot (based on Barry Rodewald's implementation). Fixed missing pixels in single-layer modes. Fixed CD-ROM regressions that caused some games not to boot (e.g. Emerald Dragon or Indiana Jones and the Last Crusade). Replaced 3dgolfha floppy dump with HxC MFM format dump, allowing copy protection check to pass. Documented all non-working software list items [r09].
- 0.193: Improved horizontal scrolling/positioning. Fixed mouse cursor moving on its own in Data West games. Implemented half-size sprites and sprite rotation. Fixed kana input and identified missing keys [r09].
- 0.192: Fixed kanji ROM offset calculation and scrolling in 16-color mode. Kanji in fixed ROM font now displays correctly, making boot messages intelligible. Scrolling imperfect but better than before - fixes scrolling/positioning issues in multiple games [r09].
- 0.189: improvements: Added support vertical zoom greater than x2 (fixes Evolution). Improved graphic layer placement - games with different-sized layers now display better. Added preliminary RS232C port support [Barry Rodewald]. (fmtowns_cd.xml) Update undumped list, merged the Towns and Marty list [r09].
- 0.180: Addded support for IC Memory Card images. Limited to 16MB in size until software that supports more can be found [Barry Rodewald].
- 0.178: Switched off layer debug keys by default [Barry Rodewald].
- 0.177: New dumps in fmtowns_cd.xml [rzero9]
- 0.175: (fmtowns_cd.xml) Added more info, based on Breiztiger's research. Added a new software list for floppy-only FM Towns games (boot disks for CDs remain in the CD list, for easier launching). Many thanks to r09 and Breiztiger for help with info and images [Fabio Priuli]. Completed addition of known dumps [r09, Breiztiger].
- 0.154: Added clone FM Towns II FreshTV [caius, Barry Rodewald].
- 0.132: Barry Rodewald added fmtowns.cpp driver.

$end
