$info=hp9k_3xx.cpp
$drv
0.157 [R. Belmont, Al Kossow]

WIP:
- 0.246: Driver placed in the sub-folder "hp/".
- 0.230: Initialized some variables which were causing incorrect behaviours in drvnoclear debug builds [Ivan Vangelista].
- 0.227: Fixed uninitialized variables in a number of devices used by the HP9000/300 series systems [Sven Schnelle].
- 0.224: (hp9k3xx_cdrom.xml, hp9k3xx_hdd.xml) Added HP-UX CD-ROMs and installed hard disk image for HP9000/3xx [Davide Cavalca].
- 0.204: Use correct memory map for HP9000/360. Fixed RTC data corruption bug (initial state of latch clock was unsafe) [Sven Schnelle].
- 0.203: Converted to use delegate timers [Sven Schnelle]. Moved sound, GPIB, keyboad and RTC to human interface DIO module. Cleaned up DIO configuration. Use 98543 DIO card for video output on HP9000/320 and HP9000/332, replacing driver code for the latter [Sven Schnelle].
- 0.199: Improvements: Fixed keyboard microcontroller part number. Removed BASIC ROM cards from the default configuration as booting from floppy works now. Hooked up NMI line to keyboard controller. Split out common machine configuration [Sven Schnelle].
- 0.198: Improvements: Added internal TMS9914 GPIB, clocked at 5MHz. Added HP 46021A (ITF) HIL keyboard, and changed h9k_3xx to use this' device. Added “topcat?? ASIC used on HP900/300 graphics cards, and hooked up to HP98544. Fixed PTM6840 hookup – clock 2 is driven by output of timer 1 [Sven Schnelle].
- 0.197: Improvements: Added 98644 asynchronous serial card. Added workaround for double exception during read/modify/write operations confusing the boot ROM. Added dummy GPIB read/write handlers (BASIC crashes if not present). Added fallback bus error handler for model 340 and later (used by BASIC to probe hardware configuration) [Sven Schnelle].
- 0.190: Hooked up keyboard/sound to HP9000/332, added 98603 ROM card [Sven Schnelle].
- 0.187: Preliminary working DIO/DIO-II bus implementation and 98544 video card. Hooked up i8042 I/O microcontroller comms to main CPU. Support medium-res built-in video on 9000/332 [R. Belmont].
- 0.158: Support 9000/370 (same bootrom as 330,340) [Al Kossow].
- 0.157: R. Belmont and Al Kossow added hp9k_3xx.cpp driver.

$end
