$info=interpro.cpp
$drv
0.183 [Patrick Mackinlay]

WIP:
- 0.279: Add missing PLDs and PROMs to ip2700 and correct some info [ArcadeHacker] (#13948) [ClawGrip].
- 0.247: Driver moved to "intergraph/" sub-folder. (intellect02.xml) Don't use title case in software list description [ArcadeShadow].
- 0.246: Driver placed in the sub-folder "interpro/".
- 0.201: Improved emulation, allowing headless configurations to be used. Fixed serial DMA and added missing control lines. Added 60x0 CLIX root floppies to software list [Patrick Mackinlay].
- 0.200: Improved to the point where CLIX boots on the ip2000. Includes re-written IOGA interrupt and DMA handling, and fixes for CPU and MMU issues [Patrick Mackinlay].
- 0.198: Slowed down CPU – fixes graphical glitches and keyboard detection. Added low-level keyboard emulation (key mapping is incomplete) [Patrick Mackinlay].
- 0.196: Various improvements, culminating in the ability to boot the "blue screen" rebuild floppy. Nearly boots CLIX - hangs trying to mount the filesystems. Refactored CPU/MMU memory access, added alignment faults, and added support for DMA virtual addressing. Implemented most C400 instructions, and fixed wait instruction. Removed broken forced interrupt handling [Patrick Mackinlay].
- 0.195: Improved graphics emulation - basic bit blit and line drawing work well enough for now [Patrick Mackinlay].
- 0.193: CPU and MMU improvements. Implemented most clipper CPU and MMU exceptions. Completed C300 instructions, adjusted for C400. Improved CAMMU dynamic translation and added faults. Refactored C300 CAMMU into separate instruction/data instances. Configurable IOGA and SR bus memory access [Patrick Mackinlay].
- 0.192: Added basic support for the system bus variously referred to as SR, SR bus, SRX and CBUS. Added initial GT graphics card implementation sufficient to boot the diagnostic monitor in graphics mode. Added high-level emulation of the InterPro keyboard with US English layout. Added support for InterPro 20x0, 24x0 and 27x0 systems. Added support for Ethernet, mouse, and serial DMA. Improved timer, interrupt and DMA handling. Improved comments/documentation.
- 0.188: Got SCSI working and other improvements: Reworked DMA, added eth registers. Improved 5390 device, removed legacy 539x SCSI stuff. Passes all iogadiag tests if bus error hack is enabled. Implemented basic serial DMA. Switched to ncr53c94. Initial preparation for Ethernet implementation. Implemented timer-based DMA [Patrick Mackinlay].
- 0.187: Added skeleton for srarb. Improved mcga/fmcc skeleton and fixed mcga/fmcc detection. Expanded cammu skeletons. Added support for "new" SCSI. Added clock-based ioga interrupts. Added forced NMI handling. Improved SCSI DMA. Removed broken caching. Added Clipper CPU ID support. Added enum masks and unknown registers, disabled bus errors. Made RAM configurable and improved system registers. Added initial implementation of unmapped memory handler. DMA/IRQ changes, serial DMA registers. Added 7-segment diagnostic LED. NMI and DMA improvements - NMI boot diagnostics pass. Made floppy DMA read and write work. Improved logging [Patrick Mackinlay].
- 0.183: Patrick Mackinlay added interpro.cpp driver.

$end
$info=intv.cpp
$drv
0.37b10 [Nathan Woods, Frank Palazzolo]

WIP:
- 0.266: (intvecs.xml) Metadata cleaning (#12315): Added manufacturer's name in software list name. Lowercase on descriptive word ("Unreleased") [ArcadeShadow].
- 0.263: (intv.xml) Use lowercase for things that aren't proper nouns [ArcadeShadow].
- 0.246: Driver placed in the sub-folder "mattel/".
- 0.157: Fix loading of very large .rom carts like D2K Arcade [R. Belmont].
- 0.149: Added support for save states to all systems of this driver [Fabio Priuli].
- 0.143u7: Changed driver to use modern memory map [Huygens]. Added cart RAM support (used in Chess, Triple Challenge, Land Battle, Game Factory). Added ECS and ECS controller support (extra hand controllers, keyboard, piano). Turned down ay-8914 volume to inprove intellivoice / console volume balance. Fix incorrect masking of register writes on ay-3-8914, fixes wrong envelope amplitude on games which use hardware enveloping on Intellivision/2 (Thunder Castle, etc) [Huygens].
- 0.143: Some corrections to the Intellivision hash file in intv.hsi [John Rieman].
- 0.37b10: Nathan Woods and Frank Palazzolo added intv.cpp driver.

$end
$info=ip12.cpp
$drv
0.96 [Ryan Holtz]

WIP:
- 0.258: Driver (indigo.cpp) splitted to (ip20.cpp) and (ip12.cpp). Refactor and WIP. Added int2 and pic1 devices. Refactor hpc1 device, add ethernet support. Refactor 4dpi into ip6 and ip12 variants. Refactor indigo into ip12 and ip20 variants. Rework 4dpi3x based on hpc1, int2 and pic1. ip6 and ip12 mostly working (will run irix 4.0.5 and 5.3 except for graphics issues and missing audio) [Patrick Mackinlay].
- 0.246: Driver placed in the sub-folder "sgi/".
- 0.233: Added indigo4k boot PROM version 4.0.5G revision B as BIOS option [Henry Bent, Davide Cavalca]. Add new ROM revision for indigo4k [Davide Cavalca].
- 0.214: Switched indigo4k to use the new R4000 CPU core [Ryan Holtz].
- 0.207: Converted LG1 "Light" graphics to a device for sharing with other systems [tyfighter].
- 0.204: Separated indigo3k and indigo4k state classes. Hooked up RS-232 ports. Switched to new Zilog SCC implementation, and added PIT8254 device (uses incorrect clock value to work around hang). Fleshed out SCSI and started fleshing out HPC1 implementation. Hooked up new DP8573 real-time clock implementation. Improved RAM layout. Added stubs for DSP RAM and Entry-Level Graphics (LG1/LG2). Implemented LG1 palette setup, block drawing, pattern drawing, frame buffer copy, and remaining commands used by PROM monitor. Removed unused screen' device. Expanded logging and converted to use logmacro, and renamed variables to meet MAME coding standards [Ryan Holtz].
- 0.201: Fixed ROM loading [Olivier Galibert].
- 0.169: Renamed (ip20.cpp) to (indigo.cpp).
- 0.96: Ryan Holtz added ip20.cpp driver.

$end
