$info=mdconsole.cpp
$drv
0.114 [David Haywood]

WIP:
- 0.288: (megadriv.xml) Added 40 working items + 2 not working (#15254) [ArcadeShadow]. (megadriv.xml) Fix illmore cart type; actually fix illmoore cart type [Angelo Salese].
- 0.286: (megacd.xml) Demote batmanrn to partial [Angelo Salese]. (megadriv.xml) "release" info element is supposed to be an unambiguous ISO date [Vas Crabb]; added 39 working items + 5 not working (#14824) [ArcadeShadow]; update (galahad) and (telebrad) notes [Angelo Salese].
- 0.283: (megacd.xml) Mark missing index images as baddump [Angelo Salese].
- 0.282: (megadriv.xml) Change rockmnx3b slot type (boots in teradrive) [Angelo Salese]. (megacd.xml) Marked the re-release of The Secret fo Monkey Island as a clone of the original (#14227) [ArcadeShadow].
- 0.281: (megacd.xml) Added six items (five working) (#14041) [David 'Foxhack' Silva]. (megadriv.xml) Added 41 working items + 1 not working (#14163) [ArcadeShadow]. 68k access to z80 delays by 1 cycle, fix MT09222 [Angelo Salese].
- 0.280: (32x.xml) Refine QA, pre-emptively demote wwfraw. (megacd.xml) Perform QA pass. (megadriv.xml) Fatalrew doesn't boot with NTSC machines, make it supported=partial [Angelo Salese]. (megadriv.xml) Added 21 working items (#14063) [ArcadeShadow].
- 0.279: (megacd.xml) Use conventional phonetic 'zu' reading rather than 'du' in 'Kanzume' [Naoki Saito]. Moved a few sets from mdconsole.cpp to megadriv_rad.cpp as they're clearly the same SoC as we have partial support for in there, and will help build a better picture of the features that SoC has [David Haywood]. Perform various 32x changes: Fix regressed stereo sound routing; remove _32X_SWAP_MASTER_SLAVE_HACK (fifa96 doesn't mind anymore); rewrite commsram read/write to use scheduler synchronize; fix soulstar missing layer by mirroring DRAM area; make set_maximum_quantum more deterministic; (32x.xml) Perform a QA pass [Angelo Salese].
- 0.278: (megadriv.xml) Added 27 working items + 1 redumped + 1 removed (#13765) [ArcadeShadow].
- 0.277: Added 6 working items (#13485) [ArcadeShadow]. Fixed trailing spaces in attributes [Vas Crabb].
- 0.276: (megacd.xml) Metadata cleanups (#13436): Added parent/clone relationship between "Blackhole Assault (Europe)" / "Black Hole Assault (Japan)"; lowercase on descriptive words "Night Trap (USA, re-release)"; replaced country abbreviation "Cadillacs and Dinosaurs - The Second Cataclysm (Brazil)" [ArcadeShadow].
- 0.275: (megacd.xml) Mark the US version of Eternal Champions - Challenge from the Dark Side as a clone of the PAL version (#13306) [jflatt]. Bulk replace scd_cdrom -> cdrom [Angelo Salese].
- 0.274: (megacd.xml) Combined the Mega CD and Sega CD software lists (#13199). sega/mdconsole.cpp: Added compatibility filters for CD-ROM media [Mike Swanson]. Use conventional phonetic 'zu' reading rather than 'du' in 'Kanzume' [Vas Crabb].
- 0.272: Corrected two bad bytes in ESPN National Hocky Night cartridge dump in 'megadriv.xml' [Don Jones]. Added a dump of Sonic the Hedgehog CD (USA) with R4C ring code (#12996). Also updated the descriptions to include the ring codes of the existing dumps of different pressings in 'segacd.xml' [David 'Foxhack' Silva].
- 0.270: Added 4 working items (#12650). Added language and compatibility info [ArcadeShadow]. Added four working prototypes [Hidden Palace, Gaming Alexandria, ArcadeShadow].
- 0.267: Replaced abbreviated country names in descriptions to 'megadriv.xml' [ArcadeShadow].
- 0.266: Added 2 working items, replaced bad dump (#12190). Bad Dump replaced with verified one. Férias Frustradas do Pica-Pau (Brazil) (fixes GitHub Issue https://github.com/mamedev/mame/issues/11950) [MARCSLASH, arthurthekidboy]. Fixed some descriptions, added some notes (#12171) and updated descriptions for some Sonic The Hedgehog games, and added notes in 'megadriv.xml' and added three working items [ICEknigh7].
- 0.265: Added and corrected info on the Sega Game Toshokan games (#12172). Added a list of missing Sega Game Toshokan games to the header comment. Updated years to match Sega's web site. Use Hepburn romaji for "Game Kanzume" and clarified which release games are ripped from in 'megadriv.xml' [ICEknigh7].
- 0.264: Added HeartBeat PGA Tour Golf II [Vas Crabb]. Also changed "SegaNet" to "Sega Game Toshokan" and "16 Ton" to "16t" in descriptions in 'megadriv.xml' [ICEknight].
- 0.263: Add rom_sram to cavestory entries in 'megadriv.xml' [Angelo Salese].
- 0.262: Fixed Genesis Nomad compatibility filter. Added compatibility filters for cartrdige software list [Vas Crabb].
- 0.260: Replaced unnecessary abbreviations in descriptions in 'megacdj.xml' and 'mdconsole.cpp' [ArcadeShadow].
- 0.251: Further broke up base Mega Drive class. Created a light-weight base class with just the core functionality, used for "Genie" hardware (Puckman Pockimon). Moved built-in controller emulation to a derived class so it isn't lurking underneath the consoles with pluggable controllers. Moved the Sun Mixing Mega Drive bootlegs to their own source file - they're substantially different, not using the I/O blocks for input [Vas Crabb].
- 0.246: Renamed (megadriv.cpp) to (mdconsole.cpp) and placed in the sub-folder "sega/". BugFix#08231 [Sound] (mdconsole.cpp) genesis and clones [ejim2u]: Slight differences in YM2612 emulation [Aaron Giles].
- 0.239: Mega Drive is written with a space [Vas Crabb].
- 0.235: Added mega-cd euro v2.11 bios. Dumped BIOS from a late-model UK Mega CD with smaller, Sony-made PCB [TwistedTom].
- 0.231: Added notes on SVP chip [Javier de Silóniz Sandino]. Corrected metadata for eleven entries in 'megadriv.xml' [ArcadeShadow].
- 0.222: Added notes about games that should be re-dumped in 'megadriv.xml' [ICEknight].
- 0.218: Added handheld variants, and added machine configuration for variants with YM3438 integrated in ASIC [cam900]. Added Mega-CD Japan BIOS version 1.11 [Fredrik Nyqvist].
- 0.213: Corrected screen refresh rate and added notes. Added support for Z80 VDP access, and corrected VDP sound balance [cam900].
- 0.211: Dumped MegaCD Japan BIOS revision 1.00C [tmee].
- 0.203: BugFIX #07124: [Documentation] (megadriv.cpp) megadriv [rrash3]: Incorrect Title Name [Tafoid)]. BugFix#07123: [Documentation] (megadriv.cpp) megadriv [dstrike]: Incomplete title name [Tafoid].
- 0.177: BugFIX #06326: [Crash/Freeze] (megadriv.cpp) megadriv, 32x and clones: Selecting machine and game via softlist though internal menu results exception/crash [Osso].
- 0.174: Added custom X24C02 emulation to NBA Jam cart, making finally possible to save records at exit. Hopefully, this will help finding the problem in our core emulation [Fabio Priuli].
- 0.156: BugFIX #05252: [Crash/Freeze] (megadriv.c) genesis [madden98]: Madden 98 - black screen [David Haywood].
- 0.155: Added support for Game Genie as a passthru cart [Fabio Priuli].
- 0.148u5: BugFIX #05172: [Crash/Freeze] (megadriv.c) 32x and clones: [debug] Assertion `curlabel->m_codeptr == __null' failed [hap].
- 0.148u3: Removed drivers (gensvp), (mdsvp) and (mdsvpj): Virtua Racing can now be loaded directly in (genesis), (megadriv) and (megadrij) [Fabio Priuli].
- 0.148u2: BugFIX #05153: [Gameplay] (megadriv.c) genesis, megadriv, pico: Crash when loading a cart [Wilbert Pol].
- 0.147u1: Removed includes\genesis.h. Fix for crashes in MESS SEGACD clones [Miodrag Milanović]. Some Mega CD refactoring [David Haywood].
- 0.147: Added machine\mega32x.h, machine\lc89510.c/h and machine\megacd.h. Started making 32x a device, by creating a device and moving the CPUs there. Get all the handlers into the device state. Moved a bunch of other stuff into the device state involving 32x. There should be no real functional changes at this point. Made the genvdp a derived class of the newer SMS VDP because the genesis VDP has an sms compatibility mode where it basically operates as an sms VDP (with a few changes / limitations). In preparation for future work (basic device structure). Should have no functional change at this point (machine\megacd.c and machine\megadriv.c). Added LC89510 CD Controller dummy (skeleton) device file to start moving some CDC stuff into so that it can then be shared with NeoCD [David Haywood]. Fixed invalid partial update calls on negative scanlines [Aaron Giles]. Fixed remaining regressions [Miodrag Milanović].
- 0.114: David Haywood added megadriv.cpp driver.

$end
