$info=mips_i2000.cpp
$drv
0.283 [Patrick Mackinlay]

WIP:
- 0.284 Move MIPS boards into their own files. Since the I2000 (Rx2030) and R3030 (Rx3230) boards are so different, they really belong in their own files. I've kept the original mips.cpp file for common functions. There doesn't seem to be enough commonality at this time to make a common base class worthwhile, perhaps as more boards are implemented some will be found [Chris Hanson].
- 0.283: Move MIPS boards into their own files (#14472). Since the I2000 (Rx2030) and R3030 (Rx3230) boards are so different, they really belong in their own files. I've kept the original mips.cpp file for common functions; there doesn't seem to be enough commonality at this time to make a common base class worthwhile, perhaps as more boards are implemented some will be found. Distinguish boards from systems in state (#14451). Rename the state classes for MIPS systems to have a `mips_` prefix and rename them to represent the board (I2000 or R3030) rather than the system containing the board (Rx2030 or Rx3230). Add tape to supported SCSI devices (#14447) [Chris Hanson].
- 0.272: Added support for IDT R4650 multiply/accumulate instructions to the interpreter [Ryan Holtz].
- 0.255: Fixed MIPS3 PRID and memory controller RPSS issues [Jiaxun Yang].
- 0.254: Fixed memory access handling in the IDT MIPS R4650 core [Ryan Holtz].
- 0.246: Driver placed in the sub-folder "mips/".
- 0.244: Added TimerIntDis multiplexer to IPEX5 for R4000 [Brice Onken]. Mitigated performance impact of optional additional instruction checks [Ryan Holtz].
- 0.241: Replaced a std::function with a marginally more efficient delegate [Vas Crabb].
- 0.220: Added basic R5000 support to the r4000 interpreter [Ryan Holtz].
- 0.206: Allowed rx2030 to boot RISC/os from a pre-installed hard disk image (with FPU disabled) [Patrick Mackinlay].
- 0.204: Hooked up MAC address PROM, LANCE Ethernet controller, and floppy drive controller [Patrick Mackinlay].
- 0.283: Patrick Mackinlay added mips\mips_i2000.cpp driver.

$end
