$info=pet.cpp
$drv
0.36RC1 [Curt Coder]

WIP:
- 0.285: Started cleanup of legacy code; continued cleanup of legacy code. Pair DOS and FDC ROMs appropriately for the 8050 floppy drive. Floppy code cleanup. Fix loading on 8050/8250/SFD-1001 floppy drives [Curt Coder]. Add a few enters on long comment line from prev commit [hap].
- 0.269: Cleaned up descriptions in 'pet_rom.xml' [ArcadeShadow].
- 0.246: Driver placed in the sub-folder "commodore/".
- 0.233: Eliminate bus tag macros and legacy lookups; use finder arrays in some places [AJR].
- 0.201: Modernized machine configuration or many devices and systems [Ryan Holtz].
- 0.193: Fixed video RAM mirroring [Curt Coder].
- 0.175: Added Supermon (Toronto PET User Group); replaced bad dump of Side B of Squiggle, Big Time / Monitor (the m command in the monitor now works correctly) in pet_cass.xml [Ken White].
- 0.169: Added MONJANA/1 in pet_rom.xml [Ruud Baltissen].
- 0.165: Added French CBM 8032 ROMs. Added Edex (France, v4.4) in pet_rom.xml [Hervé Warin].
- 0.164: Added alternate Commodore SFD-1001 Test/Demo diskette in pet_flop.xml [Curt Coder]. Added disks in pet_flop.xml. Added tapes in pet_cass.xml [Dagarman].
- 0.162: Added BASIC Programmer's Toolkit for BASIC 2.0 in pet_rom.xml [Mike Naberezny]. Added SFD-1001 Test/Demo disk in pet_flop.xml [SPACETAXI].
- 0.161: Added McTerm 1.10 in softlist pet_rom.xml [Bo Zimmerman, Steve Gray, Mike Naberezny]. Added KRAM 2.0 in pet_rom.xml [Ville Laustela]. Refactored the Commodore 8050/8250/SFD-1001 to use the new floppy system [Curt Coder].
- 0.160: Added McTerm 0.95 in pet_rom.xml [Mike Naberezny].
- 0.156: Added many new images, including the Cursor tapes in pet_cass.xml [Dagarman].
- 0.154: Added user port diagnostic connector [Curt Coder]. Replaced bad D80 for Z-RAM in pet_flop.xml [Mike Naberezny]. Added InfoPro at pet_rom.xml [Paul Rickards and Mike Naberezny].
- 0.153: Software list update (pet_flop.xml): Fixed "set unit number" program on HardBox disks. Added Nestar Cluster/One CLO-1002-2 [Mike Naberezny]. Check out "No Pets Allowed" by Orb to see them and the new mc6845 functionality in action [Curt Coder].
- 0.152: Added hard disk software list with preformatted images for the Commodore D9060 and D9090 hard drives (pet_hdd.xml) [Curt Coder].
- 0.151: Added McTerm 1.20, BASIC Programmer's Toolkit for BASIC 4.0, POWER, Oracle 3.03, Command-O for 8032, SORT, WordPro 3, Waterloo Structured BASIC, and Paperclip 2.84 [Mike Naberezny]. Added McTerm 1.21 [Mike Naberezny, Stefano Santerini].
- 0.149u1: Fixed ROM signatures for Mator Shark hard drive. Added Z-RAM floppy [Mike Naberezny]. Added 8050 version of VisiCalc at soft list (pet_flop.xml) [Curt Coder].
- 0.149: Implemented SoftBox IEEE-488 peripheral mode, where a PET computer is used as terminal [Curt Coder, Mike Naberezny]. Removed (pet40on) 'PET 40xx (Basic 4, no CRTC, Normal keyboard)' machine.
- 0.148u1: Added add-on ROM software list [Curt Coder]. Removed (cbm30nor), (cbm40b), (cbm80hun) and (pet40n) machines.
- 0.144u5: Added skeleton for SSE SoftBox IEEE-488 peripheral [Curt Coder].
- 0.143u4: Added support for D80/D82 disk images with error information [Curt Coder].
- 0.137: Changed floppy drive to Commodore 4040 for 2001/30xx/40xx series. Changed floppy drive to Commodore 8050 for 80xx series [Curt Coder].
- 0.128: Refactored cartridge code to rely on MESS core functions. Disabled .crt support (.a0 and .b0 files working as before) since I doubt these computers used the same format as C64. More work when/if more documents will be available [Fabio Priuli]. Removed (cbm40) 'Commodore 40xx FAT (CRTC) 60Hz' (pet) 'PET2001/CBM20xx Series (Basic 1)' and.
- 0.121: Fixed keyboard regression introduced in 0.116 (bug #1405). Updated to use MAME's CRTC6548 implementation [Wilbert Pol].
- 0.102: Implemented RAM configuration support [Nate Woods].
- 0.36RC1: Peter Trauner added pet.c driver (Commodore PET2000/CBM2000).

$end
