$info=specnext.cpp
$drv
0.267 [Andrei I. Holub]

WIP:
- 0.288: Fixed postponed CTC timer update (#15217); forced more screen updated where required (#15130). Pulled up unmapped IO (#15125); implemented mouse dpi and buttons swap configuration (#15122). Added MIDI extension (#15150); simulated random state of the SIMM (#15151); refactored NMI handling (#15086); fixed CTC clock (#15190); duplicate palette workaround which doesn't allow color index escape (sprite) palette boundaries (#15167); simulated behaviour of Anti-Brick core working (#15208); I found the way to simulate flasher core bootrom. As of now if we load with Anti-Brick's bootrom it's waiting until core switch and loads requested coreId (Next the one we have) with corresponting BIOS and reboots; Forced more updates on tilemap writes; better handling DivMMC CS instant switch; pulled up unmapped value on 0x2ffd & 0x3ffd reads [holub]. Fixed video mode initialization; added notes regarding Anti-Brick core [David Haywood].
- 0.287: Emulated The Spectrum Next UART (#15058). Separated VRAM memory (#15117). The Next moved typical VRAM pages (bank5&7) from SRAM to internal FPGA BRAM. bank7 has only 0x2000 and it's mirrored to the second half - this is also covered in this implementation. KS1..3 variants as clones; Added v30204 BIOS options (#14997). "dot commands" loading issue with NextZXOS - switched back to safer sdcard implementation which not such sensitive to timings (#15066) [holub].
- 0.286: Cleaned up inherited unused driver's Configuration (#14798). Added raster offsets to save states (#14878). Also moved the setters to make it clearer that these can be changed on-the-fly; added initial implementation of KS3 features (#14880): Support for an additional 2MiB of RAM, SD swap bit; also disabled NMI in config mode (fixes existing bug). expansion bus control (#14328). Refactored INT/IRQ and implemented configuable DMA halt (delay) (#14739) [holub]. Added PS/2 Keyboard mapping (#14765) [Chris Taylor].
- 0.285: Added missing credits (#14734). Added missing save states (#14744) [holub].
- 0.284: Various fixes (#14683): Enabled timer-based steps for SPI; fixed visarea clipping; refactored video modes with blending; fixed ULA+ pen parser - GGGRRRBB instead of RRRGGGBB; renamed "Video" Machine Configuration option to less confusing "Captured Video Resolution" screen_ula.cpp; ULA+ palette matches original ULA+ specnext_layer2.cpp; revisited blending layers processing; fixed the layer clipping specnext_lores.cpp; added support of Radastan (4bpp) variant; fixed palette configured with offset parameter specnext_sprites.cpp; fixed drawing of sprites from negative offset position specnext_tiles.cpp; fixed "always on top" option; fixed priority in all variants of textmode. Various fixes (#14691). Deleay resolution change which simulates VGA/HDMI output sinclair/specnext_sprites.cpp: Fixed sprites clipping broken after refresh rate changed sinclair/*: Stylistic cleanups. Always route regs space r/w access through specific (#14614) [holub].
- 0.283: Various fixes (#14549). Added second SDCARD; route mono speaker to both channels; fixed typo in joystick mapping; missing screen updates sinclair/screen_ula.cpp: Fixed half pixel scroll; fix bug in rendering sinclair/specnext_tiles.cpp: Fixed scroll for different types of tiles. Various fixes (#14527). Fix line interrupt offset. Added Kempston/MD Pad inputs (#14509) [Andrei I. Holub].
- 0.282: Improved IRQ handling (#14340). Improved interrupts handling (#14399). Fixed few gfx bugs with screen update and overscaned area for layer2 (#14298). Improved blending modes (#14295). Fixed copper + tiles (#14221). Improved Copper timings. Configured cascading for CTC counters (#14363). Improved LoRes/ULA mode to support half-pixel rendering (#14354) [Andrei I. Holub].
- 0.281: Fixed copper offset direction (#14188). Added video output configuration (VGA/HDMI); refresh rate 50/60Hz; timings for all reference machines (#13992). Fixed uninitialized default for ula port #ff (#14183) [Andrei I. Holub].
- 0.279: Added extra memory read wait state at 28MHz (#13869) [Andrei I. Holub].
- 0.278: Removed imperfect graphics flag (#13787): All graphics features that are implemented are believed to be correct; some blending modes are not implemented, but they currently lack test cases [Andrei I. Holub].
- 0.267: Andrei I. Holub added sinclair\specnext.cpp driver.

$end
