$info=spg2xx_vii.cpp
$drv
0.136 [Curt Coder]

WIP:
- 0.246: Driver placed in the sub-folder "tvgames/".
- 0.218: Added hacks to zon32bit and mywicodx to select correct banks for all games. Split up the unwieldy vii.cpp into multiple source files [David Haywood]. Renamed (vii.cpp) to (spg2xx_vii.cpp).
- 0.216: Added preliminary LCD controller, UART and player input emulation for sentx6p. Added a hack to allow tvgogo to proceed further [David Haywood].
- 0.212: BugFIX #07362 [Crash/Freeze] (vii.cpp) jak_spdm, jak_pooh, others: [debug] DRC assertion failure [Ryan Holtz].
- 0.209: Moved SunPlus GC394 systems out of vii.cpp (it's a newer sytem-on-a-chip with more capabilities) [David Haywood].
- 0.208: Added basic inputs to dreamlif. Added inputs to icanpian and icanguit [David Haywood].
- 0.207: Identified difficulty-select bit for mattelcs [Ryan Holtz]. Corrected title for "Dora the Explorer - Nursery Rhyme Adventure (JAKKS Pacific TV Game, Game-Key Ready)". Previously misidentified as "Dora the Explorer - Race To Play Park (JAKKS Pacific TV Game, Game-Key Ready)" [David Haywood].
- 0.206: Mirrored JAKKS GameKey ROMs and added I/O allowing them to boot. Kludged handling of invalid DMA size writes to avoid trashing RAM and registers in jak_dora [David Haywood].
- 0.205: BugFIX #07172 [Gameplay] (vii.cpp) vii + vii software list entries: inputs no longer working in vii or the vii cartridges [Ryan Holtz].
- 0.203: Fixed titles and publishers. Ported current u'nSP 1.0 CPU core and serial EEPROM emulation from Unununium. Made u'nSP instructions that use post-increment/decrement addressing modes update segment register on rollover. Fixed road layer in several Zone 60 games. Added an optional visual debugger for audio (may be enabled with a preprocessor macro). Converted SPG24x and SPG28x SoCs to devices, added saturation and fade offset control, and implemented sound output. Added SPG24x/SPG28x chip select callbacks and rudimentary analog inputs. Hooked up walle NVRAM. Added preliminary V.Smile support - runs BIOS and boots games [Ryan Holtz].
- 0.195: Added I/O for skateboarder, and promoted to working with bad graphics/no sound; also modernised the code a bit [David Haywood].
- 0.194: Corrected parent/clone relationships and demoted to not working [David Haywood].
- 0.182: Updated software list: Split into three lists: regular V.Smile, V.Smile Motion, and V.Smile Baby (Motion and Baby lists not hooked up yet). Updated with a bunch of new-found carts and been restructured to indicate which carts are undumped. Documented cart internals more thoroughly - descriptions now list PCB types, chip placements/labels, etc. if available. Added previously missed dumps, fixed some typos [Fake Shemp].
- 0.177: Documented 3 diagnostic menu bugs in the Vii's BIOS [PressStartandSelect].
- 0.143u7: Modernised; BATMANTV connected X key, game is now playable; WALLE added details of alternate dump [Robbbert].
- 0.136: Curt Coder added vii.cpp driver.

$end
