$info=sun3.cpp
$drv
0.143u4 [Miodrag Milanović, R. Belmont]

WIP:
- 0.270: Adds a DIAG/NORMAL switch that affects how a Sun-3/60 (and other models) are configured at boot (#12734). Note that only sun4, not sun4c or other variants, has tape among the default devices; by that era, most installation and recovery was via CD-ROM (already in the default devices) rather than via tape [Chris Hanson].
- 0.246: Driver placed in the sub-folder "sun/".
- 0.176: Add high-level emulation of Sun type 3/4/5/6 keyboards: U.S.A, Great Britain, Sweden and Japan layouts for Type 5. Layout selection settings for Type 4 and Type 5. Identification selection for type 4. Adaptor for connecting to RS-232 port representing level translator. Hook up to sun3, sun4 and sun4c [Vas Crabb].
- 0.175: Split sun3 and sun3x archiectures, they're different enough. Sun3 MMU and unique hardware implemented, all models now POST including 3/2xx [R. Belmont].
- 0.169: Switch to new Z80SCC device, add RS232 ports (not functioning yet) [R. Belmont].
- 0.158: BugFIX #05758 [Crash/Freeze] (sun3.c) sun3_80: [debug] Assert shortly after start.
- 0.154: Work in progress on Sun 3/80. It now POSTs [R. Belmont].
- 0.143u4: Miodrag Milanović and R. Belmont added sun3.cpp driver.

$end
