$info=x68k.cpp
$drv
0.115 [Barry Rodewald, Carl]

WIP:
- 0.285: (x68k_flop.xml) laplacec is a cracked older version (#14787). No version numbers visible other than the one for the mouse driver [eientei95].
- 0.282: Subscribe to generic_flop_525.xml [Angelo Salese].
- 0.279: (x68k_flop.xml) Added 1 working items (#13275). Fix #8870 [Naoki Saito].
- 0.277: (x68k_flop.xml) Added/replaced 17 dumps from original disks (#13519) [r09].
- 0.276: Improve interrupt handling [Patrick Mackinlay].
- 0.275: (x68k_flop.xml) Added 1 working items (#13275) [Marc Roy]. Fix #8870 [Angelo Salese].
- 0.274: Add serial mouse [Patrick Mackinlay].
- 0.271: Further adjust vblank IRQ [cracyc].
- 0.270: Video registers are mirrored. Adjust vblank to fix lines at top and bottom in strider [cracyc].
- 0.263: Don't reset the adpcm timer when the rate is changed [cracyc].
- 0.262: (x68k_flop.xml) Use lowercase for descriptive text in descriptions [ArcadeShadow]. 'SoftBank' has no space.l [Vas Crabb]. Correct hash entries for akazopa to match provided image [ci].
- 0.259: Fix bg size again. Guess at scan rate for mode 25. Only set timer if op is set. Fix bitmap layer clear and sprite priority. Another tile layer-bitmap layer video mode mismatch special case [cracyc].
- 0.256: Slightly change pcg/text layer combining [cracyc]. Avoid dereferencing null pointers when fewer than 4 floppy drives are configured [AJR].
- 0.255: Hook up SCSI DMA channel [AJR]. Wait before setting gvram clear status bit. Fix bg layer positioning and another layer selection case [cracyc].
- 0.254: Switch to nscsi mb89352 implementation [Patrick Mackinlay].
- 0.253: Check for dma bus error first [cracyc].
- 0.247: BugFIX #08377 [Graphics] (sharp/x68k.cpp) keeper: Tree on title screen appears in front of Success logo. Do the final mix in a single loop per-pixel. Change layer drawing order and make pcg and text layers mask each other [cracyc].
- 0.246: Driver placed in the sub-folder "sharp/".
- 0.244: BugFIX #08305 [Crash/Freeze] (x68k.cpp) All machines in x68k.cpp: [debug] Assertion failed [AJR].
- 0.234: Slow down DMA channel 2 [cracyc].
- 0.233: Treat the nibbles in 8bit color mode as two separate planes. Seems pcg can set it's own vertical freq apart from the crtc. Adjust special priority mode and screen timings hd63450: correctly add link chain mode. Fill screen with color 0 if pcg disabled and make text color 0 transparent again. Fix 512 line double scan modes. Color 0 is only transparent if the crtc is not set for 16bit color mode [cracyc].
- 0.222: (x68k_flop.xml) Re-tested Sharp X68000 software and updated notes [Angelo Salese].
- 0.203: (x68k_flop.xml) Added and corrected many entries [Wayder].
- 0.200: Updates in x68k_flop: Organised and corrected entries, and replaced disk images with new dumps. Removed Ninin Battle (Alt) - it's a modified copy. Updated/corrected missing dumps, release years, and Japanese titles [Wayder].
- 0.197: BugFIX #06942: [Media Support] (x68k.cpp) x68000: Can't save game data to disk [crazyc].
- 0.196: Implemented ADPCM panning and corrected ADPCM timer [cam900].
- 0.180: Added keyboard LEDs to layout display * Among other things, this fixes the 'dancing keyboard' display when running Cotton [Barry Rodewald].
- 0.179: Added IPL ROM dumped from an early X68000 CZ-600CE, made default for the X68000 [The Dumping Union, Barry Rodewald].
- 0.170: BugFIX #06122: [Crash/Freeze] (x68k.cpp) x68000 [ffight]: Crashes with stack crawl [crazyc].
- 0.165: Added brightness controls, used for fade in/out effects [Barry Rodewald].
- 0.154: Compose the gfx and sprite/bg layers individually before drawing to the screen [Carl].
- 0.151: Make floppies work again [Carl].
- 0.148u5: Added missing sets from TOSEC, plus a lot of new disks dumped in the past seven years, plus lots of info [Ashura, mek1, wushu, Starscream the 2nd, cpt. Misumaru Tenchi, SuperDeadite, Anna Wu, Fabio Priuli].
- 0.148u1: BugFIX #05112: [Crash/Freeze] (x68k.c) x68030 access violation [Olivier Galibert].
- 0.145u8: Added clone X68000 Super (with its own internal SCSI ROM dump). Added internal SCSI ROM dump for the XVI [Anna Wu, Barry Rodewald].
- 0.143u6: Added basic expansion slot, and support for the Neptune-X NIC as a slot device [Barry Rodewald].
- 0.142: Refactored to use new MC68901 device [Curt Coder].
- 0.118: Added support for the Ricoh RP5C15 RTC, a few more memory size options, and the .2HD file extension for disk images [Barry Rodewald].
- 0.115: Barry Rodewald and Carl added x68k.cpp driver.

$end
$info=xavix.cpp
$drv
0.152 [Angelo Salese]

WIP:
- 0.286: Document ekara alternate input dip (#14866). BGM Down/Up buttons not affected, surprisingly [eientei95].
- 0.285: (ekara_cart.xml), (hikara.xml) Added 3 e-kara Web cartridges and 1 Hi-kara user cartridge. (#14847) [David Haywood].
- 0.284: Remove system timer disable hack, try some different logic (#14586). (audio tweaks, fix regression in rad_mtrk) (#14564). Remove the udance hack, it was stopping rad_mtrk going in game, and with the sample mode disabled elsewhere udance does't play garbage anyway; provide different 'tempo' defaults depending on machine, it isn't clear what's going on here as some match closest to hardware with 0x40, others with 0x80 [David Haywood].
- 0.282: BugFIX #09284: [Core] (tvgames/xavix.cpp) Some games in xavix.cpp: Games fail to boot due to memory or EEPROM errors [David Haywood]. Further XaviX sound improvements and code cleanups [ramacat] (#14335): Last remaining stuck notes bugs fixed; IRQ handling for audio engine rewritten to remove 10.3 magic number and to derive from the sequencer rate only; balls now line up perfectly on popira towards the end of the song; no more re-syncs between CPU and audio engine in hikara, which caused a lumbering feel to the music on each resync; sequencer rate calculated from hardware behaviours; WM1 (Noise Generator) corrected to better reflect hardware; various envelope logic bugs fixed; implement capacity limit for mixer with hardware accurate voice clipping; implement DAC broadcast and multiplex mixer modes; simplified pitch-bend stepping logic; WM0 waves are now read from RAM, as they are CPU modifiable; gain calculations adjusted to avoid clipping on worst case titles; lots of clean-up, de-duplication, better naming, and correctness fixes; detailed logging put in place; annotations added; use BIT helpers. Mostly sound (#14290): Attempted to improve XaviX audio emulation with hardware studies [ramacat]: Sample loop start positions are no longer being treated as left/right channel start positions; stop conditions are longer inverted, key-off no longer being treated as stop etc.; attempted to implement various envelope effects and more (some use wave in the ROM, others are fixed function); some things sound much better (taitons2 etc.) while at times some notes hang until a new sample is played in other games (popira for example). Added Save State support to the XaviX sound hardware emulation; fixed some regressions with SEEPROM handling in the driver [David Haywood]. Cleanup code, removing superfluous bankdev [AJR].
- 0.279: Removed the 'dumped' list from xavix.cpp for now, given that most titles are dumped and the list isn't entirely accurate [David Haywood].
- 0.278: (ekara_cart.xml) Added the last known Kids' Song 20 cartridge and twelve used e-kara Web cartridges (#13820) [David Haywood].
- 0.274: Clean up some machine-translated Japanese titles [Justin Kerk]. Begin to move towards a cleaner bus implementation without the memory bypass (as some later SuperXaviX games will need it) [David Haywood].
- 0.268: Added four TV games (not working) [TeamEurope, Peter Wilhelmsen, David Haywood].
- 0.266: New software list additions (ekara etc.), mostly XaviX (#12310). Comment cleanup [AJR]. Consolidated ekara form-factor carts into a single list with compatibility filters [David Haywood].
- 0.264: Hooked up controls for tomplc and tcarnavi, and promoted them to working. Also increased tomplc CPU clock frequency to 43MHz (avoids crashes). Corrected years for a couple of games [David Haywood].
- 0.263: (ekara_japan_d.xml) Restored unverified title information for dc0006 and dc0008  [David Haywood]. It's stylised "Hi-kara" (no capital K), software list already uses this capitalisation [Vas Crabb].
- 0.262: (ekara_japan.xml) Filled in title of EC0073-MKC (Mood Kayō Collection Volume 1) [David Haywood].
- 0.261: Treat taikodp drum input as digital to avoid issue with multiple hits registering [David Haywood].
- 0.251: (ekara_japan_a.xml) Added the final known un-dumped A series cartridge . Also added "Mermaid Melody" to titles for first three cartridges as it's on the title screen and cartridge label in gold text (it may be there for the others as well, but I haven't checked) [Vas Crabb].
- 0.246: Driver placed in the sub-folder "tvgames/". Corrected gcslottv system name [Vas Crabb].
- 0.244: Changed tomcpin EEPROM from 24C04 to 24C08 [Paul-Arnold].
- 0.218: Converted to direct RGB video output to allow support mid-screen palette changes [David Haywood]. Dumped internal ROM for Gachinko Contest! Slot machine TV (Japan) [Sean Riddle].
- 0.211: Store code bank in a private stack when on long calls (fixes crash on rad_hnt2 calibration screen) [David Haywood].
- 0.208: Fixed controls in popira2 and epo_guru, and mapped some missing inputs in ttv_mx [David Haywood]. Changed palette format to HCY and improved colors [Olivier Galibert].
- 0.207: Implemented global tile flipping [David Haywood]. Dumped XaviX Bass Fishing SEEPROMS containing I/O microcontroller code [Sean Riddle].
- 0.206: Split e-kara software list according to cartridge type as cartridges are compatible with multiple systems Associated appropriate lists with e-kara, Popira, Taiko De Popira, and Dance Dance Revolution Family Mat systems. Added logging function to calculate CRC shown in the header for Radica games to aid with verification. Added preliminary serial EEPROM support - saves correctly, but does not correctly reload. Implemented register read-back required by popira when pausing. Improved handling of raster interrupt enables. Added preliminary barrel shifter emulation (used by rad_guru in 3D sections). Implemented bitmap transparency (used by xavbaseb) [David Haywood]. Added notes about cameras [Sean Riddle].
- 0.205: Added support for building with clang on FreeBSD/NetBSD, and added a missing header to video/xavix.cpp [Thomas Klausner].
- 0.204: Don't set I2C memory page size (works around hanging in Namco/Taito Nostalgia games). Align palette base to natural boundary in modes with more than four bits per pixel. Moved e-kara cartridges to a software list. Added a crude timer implementation (frequency is fixed). Added preliminary wheel input for rad_mtrk, and ball input for rad_fb/rad_madf. Fixed opcode access in upper banks. Improved inputs for ekara and rad_rh. Fixed rad_rh tile addressing. Added preliminary sound emulation. Improved CPU emulation, improving ttv_mx road, showing graphics in ttv_sw, and playing music on ttv_lotr title screen. Improved sprite positioning. Improved Monster Truck tile flipping and rendering in inline header mode. Added a hack go allow epo_efdx to read its EEPROM and display a title screen [David Haywood].
- 0.198: Started looking at the extra opcodes in the SSD 2000 type XaviX chip [David Haywood].
- 0.197: Re-organised and tidied code, and updated notes [David Haywood].
- 0.195: Created derived 6502 type with far call/return instructions and banked data memory. Implemented graphics, including sprites, and packed 7bpp tiles. Monster Truck track outline and test mode work. Implemented multiplier chip [David Haywood].
- 0.152: Angelo Salese added xavix.cpp skeleton driver.

$end
